, 01:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T17:57:50-07:00","id":143984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=143118#post143118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Jack Kirby, brothers and sisters.<br /> <br /> Hail to the king, baby. /salute<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> The above image makes me want to read comic books.<br /> <br /> The above quote makes me glad I don't.<br /> <br /> *Sigh* One day, one day.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh. The Hawkeye book is more a particularly violent sitcom than a superhero comic ^__^ (nobody ever even appears in uniform and the gimmick is exactly &quot;what does Hawkeye do when he is not with the Avengers?&quot; )<br /> <br /> It is pretty funny and entertaining, but the competence downgrade (usually in the name of comedy) can be quite jarring. As I said, I actually really like the book, but I'm one of those terribly suffering individuals who expect consistency in comic books, so that aspect irks me at times XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T11:39:31-07:00","id":145857,"title":"","content":"In the new Buffy (#3) Xander has a patch on his shoulder, it's the BPRD symbol. Little things like that I love.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ortam + Malkavia makes a Requiem fun.<br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Posts in this colour are Persuasion.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">Posts in this colour are Seduction.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this colour are Intimidation.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/57-solomon-birch","name":"solomon birch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar57_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T17:40:20-07:00","id":147348,"title":"","content":"So, finally got the chance to read the whole Superior Spider-Man thing. I found it better than I expected, but less impressive than what all the hype I encountered for it indicated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T21:33:22-07:00","id":148373,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty much a comic extreme guy. Yet I'm weird in some respects as I tend to enjoy most changes done in the movies (loved IM3's take on the Mandarin for example.) Roleplay on one (about to be two) Super-Hero MU* as five different characters (nine technically.) And I pretty much get as many of the new releases that come out week to week as I can (try nearly every book for atleast five issues)<br /> <br /> Right now my favorite books are Amazing Spider-Man (formerly Superior), X-Men (no adjective), Mighty Avengers, She-Hulk, Guardians of the Galaxy, Harley Quinn, Wake and a new book called United States of Murder Inc,<br /> <br /> I used to love DC but I have found 90% of the new 52 to be unpalatable to me as most of it just feels like a bad copy rather than a new and fresh version of things. I really did love Animal Man, Aquaman and Justice League Dark for a long time but they slowly soured to me. Still reading Suicide Squad but that's ending. And really Forever Evil was just WAY too much and too long, It felt like the old days of Marvel where the crossovers were just so all encompassing and you needed everything like Infinity War and Infinity Crusade.<br /> <br /> Marvel is a really mixed bag for me now a days, it tends to be what I read the most of (see my favorite list) but I'm not entirely happy with Bendis's direction with the X-Men and absolutely hate his characterisation of Emma Frost and the relationship (ended by Bendis) of Emma and Cyclops. Though to be fair Kieron Gillen started the issues I had with it all with his seeming instance on an Emma/Namor OTP. I really hated AvX though I was glad that the event actually mattered it had consequences. So often in the Big Two, events have little repercussions outside of 'a single character died' or 'you don't like this guy anymore.' AvX did change the landscape for Marvel NOW and while I don't like all of that. I give it credit for doing that. The biggest problem I have with Marvel now these days is... and I never thought I'd say this, I miss when Marvel &quot;wrote for the trades&quot; when every story was done in 4-7 issues. Now Uncanny Avengers, New Avengers, Young Avengers(finished book) seem to be writing for longer stories. Yet, the stories instead drag on instead of the glory days of Claremont and Byrne where it was a built epic.<br /> <br /> Outside the Big Two I read very few books to be honest. I tried Zenoscope Wonderland books and Liked them until one time I was reading a trade for the second time and went &quot;This is pinup-art with a perverted horror theme. Pass.&quot; I'm reading the Star Trek ongoing book and the Doctor Who Comics. I adore the Walking Dead comic even though I'm starting to feel like Kirkman writes too much for the the shock value for the end of the issue, the story is still very good.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I'm a minor comic demi-god. And a walking wikipedia on the subject. I'm looking forward to talking more about it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2704-deimosmasque","name":"DeimosMasque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T23:01:37-07:00","id":148421,"title":"","content":"If you like super-heroes and the walking dead, and things having consequences and shaking up the status quo in your comics, you really should read Invincible (and once you get there in the timeline, possibly Guarding the Globe and Invincible Universe as well). Kirkman also sometimes abuses shock tactics and gore in there, but the story is great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T17:24:51-07:00","id":149033,"title":"","content":"I read Inhuman #1 last night. Decent start, but I hope they spend more time delving into this new aspect of the Marvelverse (well, not new but often overlooked).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T10:01:59-07:00","id":149462,"title":"","content":"I saw this video last night where Max Landis talks about Superman in general and what makes him a worthwhile hero:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aw_GlYve_Lg\" data-code=\"aw_GlYve_Lg\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/aw_GlYve_Lg/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> I felt like sharing it because it really expresses why I like Superman as a hero in a way that I hadn't been able to articulate. More broadly, it kinda covers why I'm sick of antiheroes and ambiguous/unhappy endings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T15:39:37-07:00","id":149760,"title":"","content":"I agree with Mr. Landis. One of the reasons I liked Winter Soldier was because, while it had plenty of action (SPOILER ALERT)<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Captain America, Black Widow, The Falcon and Nick Fury STOP the cataclysm from happening. As in, actually stop the badguys BEFORE they start killing everyone. And do the sensible thing and not perpetuate a system that was irrefutably proven to have been corrupted from the start.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Fittingly enough, Captain America put the Hero back into a Superhero movie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T16:18:39-07:00","id":149784,"title":"","content":"While I disagree with the video in a few specifics, I agree with the idea in general. That said, I do often find superman histories boring, because few writers know how to write a good story about an incredibly powerful hero with almost no moral failings. It is hard if you are trying to write something that is not super simplistic.<br /> <br /> Also, I agree with the praise for Winter Soldier, especially because they managed to save the day without Cap needing to compromise on his principles and instead inspiring others to action by his principles, leadership and charisma.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T16:21:22-07:00","id":149786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeimosMasque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=148373#post148373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IThe biggest problem I have with Marvel now these days is... and I never thought I'd say this, I miss when Marvel &quot;wrote for the trades&quot; when every story was done in 4-7 issues. Now Uncanny Avengers, New Avengers, Young Avengers(finished book) seem to be writing for longer stories. Yet, the stories instead drag on instead of the glory days of Claremont and Byrne where it was a built epic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't read anything by Marvel in a looong time. Last thing I read was X-Men: Schism when Lunatyk sent it my way.<br /> <br /> That said, I recently re-read Days of Future Past(since I was going to see the movie) and I forgot how much I missed that time. A time when one of the most popular and defining stories was only two issues long. Not some huge crossover, not an event, not even two issues of different comics. Just two issues of Uncanny X-Men. They told one of the best stories in two issues.<br /> <br /> So thats what I miss. I'm tired of stories that take months and months to tell, and that have to be some huge event crossover. I miss the smaller stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T16:21:58-07:00","id":149787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cielle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=149462#post149462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I saw this video last night where Max Landis talks about Superman in general and what makes him a worthwhile hero:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aw_GlYve_Lg\" data-code=\"aw_GlYve_Lg\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/aw_GlYve_Lg/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> I felt like sharing it because it really expresses why I like Superman as a hero in a way that I hadn't been able to articulate. More broadly, it kinda covers why I'm sick of antiheroes and ambiguous/unhappy endings.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm with you....not ever superhero needs to be dark.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T17:21:14-07:00","id":149861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=149786#post149786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So thats what I miss. I'm tired of stories that take months and months to tell, and that have to be some huge event crossover. I miss the smaller stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah...Spider-Man's introduction (including part of the supporting cast) and entire origin story: 11 pages. Superior Spider-Man storyline: 31 issues plus some extras.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":868,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","user":"danelsan","date":". 05-26-2014, 08:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T17:29:13-07:00","id":149863,"title":"","content":"Don't get me wrong, some stories can be told well and need a long time (Superior Spider-Man for examble isn't a single 31 issue story. It's a bunch of stories in 4 or 5 parts each that are part of a greater narrative, I like that stuff) But things like the Uncanny Avenger's story about the Death Twins has taken over 10 issues to tell... and half of it feels like filler that goes no where. That's when I kind of just roll my eyes and want to shout, &quot;GET ON WITH IT!&quot;<br /> <br /> I never thought I'd actually miss the practice of &quot;Writing for the trades&quot; but at least then stories were only six parts tops, allowing them to get wrapped up a lot faster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2704-deimosmasque","name":"DeimosMasque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T07:38:25-07:00","id":150324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=149786#post149786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I haven't read anything by Marvel in a looong time. Last thing I read was X-Men: Schism when Lunatyk sent it my way.<br /> <br /> That said, I recently re-read Days of Future Past(since I was going to see the movie) and I forgot how much I missed that time. A time when one of the most popular and defining stories was only two issues long. Not some huge crossover, not an event, not even two issues of different comics. Just two issues of Uncanny X-Men. They told one of the best stories in two issues.<br /> <br /> So thats what I miss. I'm tired of stories that take months and months to tell, and that have to be some huge event crossover. I miss the smaller stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will agree and disagree. It wasn't that they didn't have the long events and huge(depending on what you consider huge) crossovers, but that generally they still completed a smaller story while they occurred. You at least had some feeling of completion.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cielle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=149462#post149462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I saw this video last night where Max Landis talks about Superman in general and what makes him a worthwhile hero:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aw_GlYve_Lg\" data-code=\"aw_GlYve_Lg\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/aw_GlYve_Lg/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> I felt like sharing it because it really expresses why I like Superman as a hero in a way that I hadn't been able to articulate. More broadly, it kinda covers why I'm sick of antiheroes and ambiguous/unhappy endings.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with some of what he said. I think he was spot on about how Superman didn't have to be angsty to arrive at his need to be a hero and the fact that &quot;he will always make the right choice&quot;. I even agree that Superman shouldn't be allowing the city to be destroyed. Not that an unavoidable situation couldn't happen, but that really in MoS he was never allowed to try and stop it. The few times where the story allowed him to make a decision it was so he could make the wrong one. Then it would be all about getting to the next plot point. Its the difference in a story that tries to feel organic and one where it feels like it was written. It kind of the difference between Superman I and the Man of Steel.<br /> <br /> I disagree when he gets to the point of Superman killing and the killing of Zod is where I don't agree. To me it is the same situation as the rest of the movie. It didn't feel to me that he had no choice but to kill Zod, but that the writers were not going to give him any choice but to kill Zod. Nothing else he could do would be good enough yet he could still break his neck. He couldn't put his hand over his eyes, move in front of the beams, he couldn't try to fly them both out of there, and a hole host of other things. But he could break his neck. That is the thing about Superman, he is always looking for the alternative.<br /> <br /> This is why I still say that Superman vs the Elite is the best Superman story I've watched in years(I hadn't read the original comic run). He thought outside of the situation rather than give over his values. And that is really the most important aspect of the character. Not his powers but his vales. He comes from a set of values that might be more perfect than realistic, but ones that used to be believed in. I don't think they are gone just that media has decided that they are. That only this is the movie or story we want, but that realistically they are not giving us any other story.<br /> <br /> It is kind of like why so many stories that tried to follow Harry Potter or *shudders* the Twilight Saga for the most part did poorly. They decided that people like the formula and that isn't the case. If you could simply follow with the exact same thing or some formula then every story would be a hit. We pay money for the best of what we are offered, but that doesn't mean we wouldn't pay for something else.<br /> <br /> At the end of the video I agree with what he said about how many are stuck on the super and missing the HERO part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":787,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","user":"Sorwen","date":". 05-27-2014, 12:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T09:05:09-07:00","id":150411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorwen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=150324#post150324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will agree and disagree. It wasn't that they didn't have the long events and huge(depending on what you consider huge) crossovers, but that generally they still completed a smaller story while they occurred. You at least had some feeling of completion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yea. They did crossovers, and while the stories they did with were epic, it wasn't some company wide thing that went for months or years and that they made new titles for just to go along with it. Back in the day, the crossovers were shorter and more contained and felt epic. Like was said before, the ones now are huge, go on for month, and at the end nothing really matters or changes.<br /> <br /> So yea, I miss the way they used to do it. Especially with the smaller stories. Hell, they used to tell stories in one issue. Now it's at least 4 issues, if then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T11:47:32-07:00","id":150653,"title":"","content":"I think the real problem was the yearly imprint wide crossover model that Marvel and DC had going for a while. I'll give both credit that they backed off it for a little while and stuck to smaller crossovers, but after Forever Evil selling well it seems Marvel's following suit with thier own epically long imprint wide crossover called Original Sin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2704-deimosmasque","name":"DeimosMasque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T14:30:03-07:00","id":150794,"title":"","content":"I think one of the greatest sins of the huge crossovers was dragging along a number of books in which the writers had ongoing, self-contained stories with good potential that got ruined by having their stories derailed by the latest mega-event. I'm thinking Marvel in particular, but I imagine the same happened to some DC books too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T14:33:28-07:00","id":150796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=149786#post149786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I haven't read anything by Marvel in a looong time. Last thing I read was X-Men: Schism when Lunatyk sent it my way.<br /> <br /> That said, I recently re-read Days of Future Past(since I was going to see the movie) and I forgot how much I missed that time. A time when one of the most popular and defining stories was only two issues long. Not some huge crossover, not an event, not even two issues of different comics. Just two issues of Uncanny X-Men. They told one of the best stories in two issues.<br /> <br /> So thats what I miss. I'm tired of stories that take months and months to tell, and that have to be some huge event crossover. I miss the smaller stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>My reaction really speaks to how much the comics storytelling methods have changed. I just read <b>Days of Future Past</b> for the first time a week or so ago (I started reading X-Men comics, LITERALLY, the issue right after that), and I was <i>floored </i>that something that has had such a long-running impact on the X-Men storylines was <i><b>just two issues</b></i>!! I expected it to be drawn out for at least 5 or 6 and it felt like it was over in no time at all.<br /> <br /> But then I thought back to the other Marvel character I kept up with, Spider-Man. Gwen Stacy and the Green Goblin died in<i> just two issues</i>.<br /> <br /> Back in the day, JUST TWO ISSUES could change a character's whole life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T05:45:53-07:00","id":151222,"title":"","content":"Anyone here reading Ultimate Marvel?<br /> I'm not up to date there, since I started to buy the german translations for convenience, but they are six to nine months behind.<br /> <br /> In any case, I find the current stories unsatisfying in a way. That being <i>Ultimate Comics: The Ultimates</i> primarily, but also some of the <i>Ultimate Comics: X-Men</i>.<br /> In my opinion they lack depth, being full scale world changing super plots, that are super shallow. While Miles Morales as Spider-Man still has some light-heartedness, despite serious themes, the other series seem to just go off on cheap action elements, like 2nd rate action movies would.<br /> <br /> Maybe it has to do with the fact, that I get all the issues collected and have four to six US-issues in one book, when I can buy it?<br /> But still...<br /> <br /> It is true, that two issues could change a character's whole life, but they didn't have to.<br /> If a character was still the same after a couple of year (which could be decades in publication), it was okay. Now, everything changes regularly. I know Ultimate Marvel is about to. Those of you in the US might have already read Cataclysm and started with the new Ultimate series...<br /> <br /> In any case, I would wish for more basic stories, with stakes that are high, but not the world or reality every time....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T06:03:22-07:00","id":151230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=151222#post151222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone here reading Ultimate Marvel?</div> </div> </div> </div>A couple of books. I'll try to remember to talk about them after work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T07:49:06-07:00","id":151297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=150796#post150796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My reaction really speaks to how much the comics storytelling methods have changed. I just read <b>Days of Future Past</b> for the first time a week or so ago (I started reading X-Men comics, LITERALLY, the issue right after that), and I was <i>floored </i>that something that has had such a long-running impact on the X-Men storylines was <i><b>just two issues</b></i>!! I expected it to be drawn out for at least 5 or 6 and it felt like it was over in no time at all.<br /> <br /> But then I thought back to the other Marvel character I kept up with, Spider-Man. Gwen Stacy and the Green Goblin died in<i> just two issues</i>.<br /> <br /> Back in the day, JUST TWO ISSUES could change a character's whole life.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get a sense you're making fun of me... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T07:51:49-07:00","id":151298,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=151222#post151222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone here reading Ultimate Marvel?</div> </div> </div> </div>I read Ultimate X-Men for quite awhile when the Ultimate universe first started, maybe for 80 or 100 issues, but then I gave up on it. Just didn't do it for me. Last thing I really remember was the introduction of Cable, and how he was really Wolverine from the future...or something along those lines. Seemed weird..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T10:35:21-07:00","id":151447,"title":"","content":"I read Ultimate X-Men, the Ultimates and Ultimate Spider-Man for a long while. I stopped with Ultimates after they turned Captain America into a jingoist joke (so yeah after the first story) I stopped with X-Men after they brought Hank back from the dead and cured him of being blue. And I stopped Ultimate Spider-Man... never... still reading the comic to this day. Though if what I sense is going to happen is what's going to happen since the new series came out I might be stopping soon as I shake my fists in the air and scream &quot;DAMN YOU BENDIS!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2704-deimosmasque","name":"DeimosMasque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T11:25:59-07:00","id":151518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=151297#post151297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I get a sense you're making fun of me... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not in the least. Just agreeing and pointing out how a good, character-changing story didn't need to be a year long event. Just two issues can mean everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T12:33:07-07:00","id":151589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=151518#post151518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not in the least. Just agreeing and pointing out how a good, character-changing story didn't need to be a year long event. Just two issues can mean everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, cool. Wasn't quite sure. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But yea, I agree. I always liked it when they could do a story in one or two issues. They seemed to have moved pretty far away from that these days, and its one of the things that really keeps me away from them these days...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T12:49:07-07:00","id":151597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeimosMasque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=151447#post151447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I read Ultimate X-Men, the Ultimates and Ultimate Spider-Man for a long while. I stopped with Ultimates after they turned Captain America into a jingoist joke (so yeah after the first story) I stopped with X-Men after they brought Hank back from the dead and cured him of being blue. And I stopped Ultimate Spider-Man... never... still reading the comic to this day. Though if what I sense is going to happen is what's going to happen since the new series came out I might be stopping soon as I shake my fists in the air and scream &quot;DAMN YOU BENDIS!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I read X-men and spider-man. I stopped and then someone gave me the new series for x-men and when loeb stopped writing it (the issue with every loeb comic is that it's unequivocally bad) it was decent too bad that the writing change into their version of utopia scrapped a lot of good ideas but once I finished that I was done it felt over. Honestly so did spiderman once peter died so I don't know how you can keep reading it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T12:53:20-07:00","id":151599,"title":"","content":"I kept with USM because I wanted to give the new SM a chance. And found I really adored Miles Morales so that's how I kept going there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2704-deimosmasque","name":"DeimosMasque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T14:38:30-07:00","id":153008,"title":"","content":"Got through my New Release pile for this week and here's my in brief on them:<br /> <br /> Justice League Dark #31- Better than last months but the book is still trying to find itself in the wake of Forever Evil and it just doesn't seem to know what to do with itself. Introduction of Black Alice/Alice Walker felt a little weak as I expected it to. But the twist at the end gives me hope for next month<br /> <br /> Inhuman #2 - This was just great! Great follow up from the first issue and the things that are happening in the book seem like a good continuation of the after effects of the release of the Terrigan Gas. It's just too bad that its taken this long to get the new status quo of the Inhumans going. Also like the Nuhuman name for those who have just been changed. The conversations between Medusa and Captain America especially show how this can be an interesting game changer to the 616 universe<br /> <br /> Suicide Squad #30 - More Forever Evil follow up but hey Deadshot actually looks like Deadshot at last so that makes me happy. It was also cool to see a super-villain break out attempt get foiled by actual law enforcement, that's not something you see often in comics. I especially liked Black Manta in this book and the subplot of &quot;What's a supervillain supposed to actual DO when they get released from jail&quot;<br /> <br /> Wolverine #7 - I'm still bored with this whole &quot;going under cover as a bad guy to get to Sabertooth thing.&quot; Some cool moments but they have been doing this for 7 issues now with no real payoff.<br /> <br /> Avengers #30 - Okay so looks like the Avengers are going to be jumping ahead in time multiple times due to the shattering of the Time Gem, which does lead me to wonder why nothing similar to this happened when the other gems shattered. It just seems like an excuse to jump around in time. Which is fine, and the book itself is handling it well. I specifically liked Old Clint and Young Clint interacting.<br /> <br /> Thunderbolts #29 - This one was a mixed bag for me, after they killed off some major characters last book I knew there was going to be some great deus ex machina at the end to restore everything and here it was. It was just a really BAD one. However some really good moments with Deadpool and the Leader made this a good and entertaining read, despite the flaws.<br /> <br /> Guardians of the Galaxy #15 - Misleading cover is misleading. Don't advertise Captain Marvel on the cover if she's not anywhere in the book. And Bendis continues to show me that he is a good writer as long as it isn't Uncanny X-Men. I'm starting to think he just has too many books and too much clout at Marvel. The story itself was great, the humor was good and while it did feel a bit like filler, I was still entertained.<br /> <br /> Uncanny Avengers #20 - FINALLY THIS PLOT IS GOING SOME WHERE! The whole Death Twins story arch has been taking WAY too long to actually accomplish anything. It's been like fifteen issues since this plot started and just now they are getting somewhere, where it feels like it might actually end. More time travel though (Marvel seems to adore the concept right now, wonder if it has anything to do with a certain movie in theatres?) but I did like the part were Logan said that had to be sure to return before Rogue was killed or he was scuttle the entire mission. Shows his guilt for what happened to her like... 10 issues ago.<br /> <br /> All-New Invaders #5 - Great book is Great. Don't really have any more to say about this. The Invaders book has been very good, has had good dialogue between the characters and the writer seems to understand the characters motives and personalities. Read it.<br /> <br /> Fantastic Four #5 - Another great book. The Fantastic Four having to defend against charges of Negligence, Child Endangerment, etc is a good twist for the book and She-Hulk being their lawyer is a nice touch to it. The book references stories that have been told throughout the entire history of the F4 and even uses classic art where it can. A good read in general and a good jumping on point for the F4 specifically.<br /> <br /> Mighty Avengers #10 - Original Sin tie-in, but a good one. Deals with Blue Marvel's relationship with the Watcher and remembers that the FF book (previous to the current F4 book) gave the Watcher a wife who was pregnant. Also did a good job of making an alien pregnancy seem alien. <br /> <br /> Ms. Marvel #4 - Concept is still solid, book is still moving a bit on the slow side. Four issues in before we get into her origin far enough for her to make her own costume. Just feels like a book that is being held back for some reason. But Kamala and her supporting cast continue to be good and the interactions between them feel very real. <br /> <br /> Deadpool #29 - I still can't decide... 29 issues later if this book is awesome or bad. It just sort of jumps around between the two so much that it's hard to even view this as part of the 616 universe, even though it is supposed to be. But Deadpool being married to the Queen of the Monsters is pretty cool and having to now deal with Dracula might be fun.<br /> <br /> Iron Man #26 - Though the story with Maleketh wrapped itself up a bit too easily the journey to the end of it was fun and this kept that going. The Rings of the Mandarin story has been pretty awesome and I'm interested to see where its all going to lead to in the end.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And that's it from me. That's all I read this week.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2704-deimosmasque","name":"DeimosMasque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T02:09:02-07:00","id":153617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeimosMasque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=153008#post153008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Guardians of the Galaxy #15 - Misleading cover is misleading. Don't advertise Captain Marvel on the cover if she's not anywhere in the book. And Bendis continues to show me that he is a good writer as long as it isn't Uncanny X-Men. I'm starting to think he just has too many books and too much clout at Marvel. The story itself was great, the humor was good and while it did feel a bit like filler, I was still entertained.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>And so long as you don't know anything about the previous characters or their backstory.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeimosMasque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=153008#post153008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ms. Marvel #4 - Concept is still solid, book is still moving a bit on the slow side. Four issues in before we get into her origin far enough for her to make her own costume. Just feels like a book that is being held back for some reason. But Kamala and her supporting cast continue to be good and the interactions between them feel very real.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's very much a comic book manga. It's very slice of lifeish but that doesn't mean it's bad but it's meandering a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 05-30-2014, 05:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T05:11:57-07:00","id":153710,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeimosMasque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=153008#post153008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wolverine #7 - I'm still bored with this whole &quot;going under cover as a bad guy to get to Sabertooth thing.&quot; Some cool moments but they have been doing this for 7 issues now with no real payoff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Poor Wolverine, always trying to get to Sabretooth. :P<br /> <br /> I gave up on him and X-Men a long time ago. Makes me sad sometimes, but I just can't get into what they've done with ole Wolvy for the past 10 years or so...<br /> <br /> <br /> Speaking of that. I wanted to refresh myself on Apocalypse yesterday, so I loaded up Wikipedia, and there started a whole days worth of reading about various characters and how convoluted everything has become in Marvel comics. Seemed like for awhile they hit a wall and couldn't move any character forward, they retconned in lots of things into their backstories and such. It was crazy! And to hear about all the craziness with the uber-crossovers I don't how anyone could possibly keep up with it all...<br /> <br /> Or maybe it just seems confusing since I stopped reading it all years ago. Least when it comes to Marvel...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T12:46:52-07:00","id":154111,"title":"","content":"Yeah, confusing backstories, retcons, moving characters &quot;sideways&quot; because writers couldn't find a way to move them forward, messing things up trying to &quot;fix&quot; something the writer didn't like or that a previous writer had messed up, pet characters of a given writer becoming ultra-important Mary Sues then disappearing as soon as another writer takes helm of the book, bizarre editorial decisions and so on...none of that is new on comics.<br /> <br /> The longer existence of the characters, the dragged out storytelling and the more frequent mega-events have perhaps made these sorts of stuff more widespread or more common, I don't have enough data and impartiality to judge. Still, Donna Troy didn't happen last month.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T13:49:09-07:00","id":154162,"title":"","content":"There not really more or less common to be honest. Its just that its easier to discuss it now a days with the internet and all that. <br /> <br /> Also just like &quot;plot hole&quot; gets overused when discussing movies (plot hole then means thing in the movie I didn't understand or I didn't like) the term &quot;retcon&quot; gets used a lot when it means &quot;I don't like this change.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also in my general opinion I see that DC does the whole actual retcon thing more often than Marvel (at least on an imprint wide scale). Even before the New 52, the actual history of their characters had all been reset in the aftermath of Crisis on Infinite Earths in 1985. While Marvel's history has never gone through a global reboot with even hated events like Heroes Reborn being part of the wider canon of things. <br /> <br /> I also contend that the Internet makes it easier to follow comics than ever before. A character you don't know shows up in a book? Google him. An event is alluded to? Google it. It's easier than ever to follow what has happened in comics without having to read back issue after back issue after back issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2704-deimosmasque","name":"DeimosMasque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T14:44:55-07:00","id":154186,"title":"","content":"Oh, yeah. Thanks to google, everyone can play at being Mark Gruenwald XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T14:49:42-07:00","id":154189,"title":"","content":"*laughs* Who I had to google because I couldn't remember who he was. I recognized the name, just couldn't really think of what he was known for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2704-deimosmasque","name":"DeimosMasque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T14:56:10-07:00","id":154197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=154111#post154111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, confusing backstories, retcons, moving characters &quot;sideways&quot; because writers couldn't find a way to move them forward, messing things up trying to &quot;fix&quot; something the writer didn't like or that a previous writer had messed up, pet characters of a given writer becoming ultra-important Mary Sues then disappearing as soon as another writer takes helm of the book, bizarre editorial decisions and so on...none of that is new on comics.<br /> <br /> The longer existence of the characters, the dragged out storytelling and the more frequent mega-events have perhaps made these sorts of stuff more widespread or more common, I don't have enough data and impartiality to judge. Still, Donna Troy didn't happen last month.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yea, I'm with you. I'm known to not be hugely into the idea of a reboot...but occasionally, when done right, it can be a good thing, and I think Marvel is long overdo for one...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeimosMasque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=154162#post154162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also just like &quot;plot hole&quot; gets overused when discussing movies (plot hole then means thing in the movie I didn't understand or I didn't like) the term &quot;retcon&quot; gets used a lot when it means &quot;I don't like this change.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, tell me about it...and it happens alot it seems. What ever happened to keeping things in line with what other writers had done before? Seems alot of times new writers can't be assed to find out about a characters history, or just don't give a shit, and change things on a whim...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeimosMasque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=154162#post154162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also in my general opinion I see that DC does the whole actual retcon thing more often than Marvel (at least on an imprint wide scale). Even before the New 52, the actual history of their characters had all been reset in the aftermath of Crisis on Infinite Earths in 1985. While Marvel's history has never gone through a global reboot with even hated events like Heroes Reborn being part of the wider canon of things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, DC has done it quite a few times. And the first time, I think it was probably a good idea. But they just keep doing it...<br /> <br /> And Marvel hasn't ever done it that I'm aware of it...so it might be time...I dunno.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeimosMasque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=154162#post154162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also contend that the Internet makes it easier to follow comics than ever before. A character you don't know shows up in a book? Google him. An event is alluded to? Google it. It's easier than ever to follow what has happened in comics without having to read back issue after back issue after back issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats true...but, at least in my case, the more I started reading up on characters I had let slide, the more confused I seemed to become. But, that is a good point.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T15:00:53-07:00","id":154201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeimosMasque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=154162#post154162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There not really more or less common to be honest. Its just that its easier to discuss it now a days with the internet and all that.<br /> <br /> Also just like &quot;plot hole&quot; gets overused when discussing movies (plot hole then means thing in the movie I didn't understand or I didn't like) the term &quot;retcon&quot; gets used a lot when it means &quot;I don't like this change.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also in my general opinion I see that DC does the whole actual retcon thing more often than Marvel (at least on an imprint wide scale). Even before the New 52, the actual history of their characters had all been reset in the aftermath of Crisis on Infinite Earths in 1985. While Marvel's history has never gone through a global reboot with even hated events like Heroes Reborn being part of the wider canon of things.<br /> <br /> I also contend that the Internet makes it easier to follow comics than ever before. A character you don't know shows up in a book? Google him. An event is alluded to? Google it. It's easier than ever to follow what has happened in comics without having to read back issue after back issue after back issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both of them do it in different ways. You know why I basically said Guardians of the Galaxy sucks? Because bendis removed everything previously about them. He changed them up and after the ultimate sacrifice Starlord preforms, he's brought back with literally no explanation. Bendis' writing also doesn't work for anything but a street-level book like DD or spiderman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T15:03:14-07:00","id":154204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeimosMasque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=154189#post154189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*laughs* Who I had to google because I couldn't remember who he was. I recognized the name, just couldn't really think of what he was known for.</div> </div> </div> </div>You probably already found out but, in short, continuity guru and living encyclopaedia of jobber villains<br /> <br /> Edit: as for Marvel and full-line reboots, Ultimate Marvel makes it seem to me they prefer the idea of creating alternate lines with a rebooted universe than rebooting the main lines. I guess it seems less risky...<br /> <br /> As for Bendis' Guardians of the Galaxy and similar occurrences, I'm typically against completely ignoring continuity (especially character development) and/or completely changing a character's personality out of nowhere. That said, there have been a few times when I was glad some ridiculous shit was just ignored by further writers, especially considering that often trying to actually fix or undo the terrible stuff ends up bringing it back to the reader's attention unnecessarily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":868,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","user":"danelsan","date":". 05-30-2014, 06:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T02:00:50-07:00","id":156319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=154204#post154204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: as for Marvel and full-line reboots, Ultimate Marvel makes it seem to me they prefer the idea of creating alternate lines with a rebooted universe than rebooting the main lines. I guess it seems less risky...</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure, if that's the case.<br /> As far as I know, there are plenty of history altering and status-quo changing events in the main marvel universe. Spinder-Man's identity revealed, then removed from public knowledge, by sacrificing his relationship with MJ.<br /> Also House of M, Decimation.<br /> <br /> <br /> The <b>U</b>ltimate <b>U</b>niverse seemed to be a fresh new start in 2000. And I think in was good in the beginning, when any author still wrote a lot of story arcs without the need to finish off stuff in a big way. Also, there was Ultimate Team-ups, so there was a certain need, at least for Spider-Man to have a Status quo, so other authors could base the Team-ups on.<br /> <br /> But today, 14 years later, UXM seems overcrowded with Ultimate Versions of Classic Marvel characters, that don't get backstory or characterisation, since they are basically to illustrate the fight between Jean's and Kitty's respective nation. Same is true for the Ultimates / Ultimate Avengers.<br /> And all that is basically, because the stories are all to fast paced and aiming for a showdown, that has to be bigger than the last one, instead of a nice storytelling, within a status quo...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T17:27:13-07:00","id":165412,"title":"","content":"So, recently I've got the chance to read All-New X-Men, you know, the run in which the original X-Men are brought to current times. Overall, it entertaining enough but a bit too grim for my tastes, because the larger X-men and Marvel Universe in which they are inserted is too dark for me these days and it generally affects them negatively a bit more than them affect the world positively and, well, X-Men has always been an agsty book, but the direction this one is going is not my preferred one. Also, adult dudes fawning over 16-years-old Jean Grey gets creepy.<br /> <br /> That said, issue 15 is an aside in the series, even the artwork is different. It had a lot more levity and humor and was just plain fun and I would love if the whole series was like that. I still crack up every time a certain pair of characters* (spoilered below) come across each other and just keep going because it is super awkward ^__^<br /> <br /> Hey Marvel, make an All-New X-Men Adventures** book!<br /> <br /> *<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Young Jean Grey and her daughter-from-a-possible-future Rachel Summers</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> ** The adventures lines being the all-ages titles","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T07:27:15-07:00","id":165891,"title":"","content":"I'm still totally disappointed in All-New X-Men. They had the chance to really bring back the characters, but instead they used it as an opportunity to move them even further than before. They even continually screwed up details like age and the story up to the point they were taken from. Honestly I can only see it as another attempt for a writer to put their stamp on something. Seem totally ego driven.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T11:34:13-07:00","id":166127,"title":"","content":"Been out of comics for a while, only occassionally checking in to see what's going on, and...What The?!<br /> <br /> Marvel is doing a storyline other major super team leaders are discussing doing something borderline unethical. Captain America objects, so...the heroes overpower him and have Dr. Strange mindwipe this knowledge from his head. Also, Marvel is jumping some of their books almost a year ahead, to create tension as we see how the changes in those books came about as the others catch up with them. <br /> <br /> Sound familiar?<br /> <br /> Not that DC is in any position to complain: Apparently, the ending of the Forever Evil storyline saw Lex Luthor saving the day, for which he is rewarded by having his crimes officially expunged and being given some sort of authority over the JLA/superhuman activities! Yeah, because that worked out sooo well for Norman Osbourne...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> WTF is going on in comicland!? This *can't* be coincidence! Is blatantly ripping each other off just the fashion of the day at Marvel and DC now? Hell, I'm tempted to pick up some issues just to see how bold-faced it all is...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T07:19:05-07:00","id":166918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=166127#post166127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Been out of comics for a while, only occassionally checking in to see what's going on, and...What The?!<br /> <br /> Marvel is doing a storyline other major super team leaders are discussing doing something borderline unethical. Captain America objects, so...the heroes overpower him and have Dr. Strange mindwipe this knowledge from his head. Also, Marvel is jumping some of their books almost a year ahead, to create tension as we see how the changes in those books came about as the others catch up with them.<br /> <br /> Sound familiar?<br /> <br /> Not that DC is in any position to complain: Apparently, the ending of the Forever Evil storyline saw Lex Luthor saving the day, for which he is rewarded by having his crimes officially expunged and being given some sort of authority over the JLA/superhuman activities! Yeah, because that worked out sooo well for Norman Osbourne...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> WTF is going on in comicland!? This *can't* be coincidence! Is blatantly ripping each other off just the fashion of the day at Marvel and DC now? Hell, I'm tempted to pick up some issues just to see how bold-faced it all is...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's really nothing new.<br /> <br /> Stan Lee was told to create a team of superheroes (The Fantastic Four) because he boss was playing golf with one of the bosses over at DC who was bragging about how well Justice League was selling.<br /> <br /> DC's Swamp Thing and Marvel's Man-Thing were created nearly simultaneously and (according to internal rumors) it's because someone over at DC was roommates with someone at Marvel.<br /> <br /> Marvel's team of teenage superheroes (the X-Men) starts skyrocketing in sales and DC relaunches Teen Titans with an all-new cast.<br /> <br /> Marvel has Captain America. DC has The Guardian.<br /> <br /> Green Lantern Corps over at DC. Nova Corps over at Marvel.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><i>Jason Todd and Bucky Barnes.</i></b> nuff said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T08:09:10-07:00","id":166941,"title":"","content":"Except I didn't cheer when Bucky &quot;died&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ortam + Malkavia makes a Requiem fun.<br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Posts in this colour are Persuasion.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">Posts in this colour are Seduction.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this colour are Intimidation.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/57-solomon-birch","name":"solomon birch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar57_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T08:54:29-07:00","id":166967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solomon birch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=166941#post166941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except I didn't cheer when Bucky &quot;died&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't matter now, anyway, neither one <i>stayed </i>dead. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T15:25:06-07:00","id":171101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=166918#post166918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Marvel has Captain America. DC has The Guardian.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Guardian wasn't made to compete with Captain America, he was made as a sort of Ode to Joe Simon, who co-created Cap with Jack Kirby. I think he was also a co-creator of the Hulk, which probably explains what briefly happened to Jimmy in the beginning of the 4th World Saga.<br /> <img src=\"http://www.collectorsquest.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/kirby_5.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","user":"The Revenge of TV Head","date":". 06-18-2014, 03:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T10:01:24-07:00","id":172928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=166918#post166918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's really nothing new.<br /> <br /> Stan Lee was told to create a team of superheroes (The Fantastic Four) because he boss was playing golf with one of the bosses over at DC who was bragging about how well Justice League was selling.<br /> <br /> DC's Swamp Thing and Marvel's Man-Thing were created nearly simultaneously and (according to internal rumors) it's because someone over at DC was roommates with someone at Marvel.<br /> <br /> Marvel's team of teenage superheroes (the X-Men) starts skyrocketing in sales and DC relaunches Teen Titans with an all-new cast.<br /> <br /> Marvel has Captain America. DC has The Guardian.<br /> <br /> Green Lantern Corps over at DC. Nova Corps over at Marvel.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><i>Jason Todd and Bucky Barnes.</i></b> nuff said.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weeell...The FF is really nothing like the JLA, tho, besides being a group of people with superpowers; literally *everything* else is different! Marvel's true answer to JLA are the Avengers, who came along a little later. Agreed about the TT, however, that was a pretty blatant take off on the X-Men, as were the Nova Corps of the GLC (themselves allegedly a knock-off of the Lensmen!). <br /> <br /> But if you'll notice, the main difference is *characters* vs. *stories*. Maybe it's just a difference of degree, but it bugs me more when they start cribbing entire *storylines* from each other. Maybe it all started with your last example? Aside from being sidekicks, those two aren't similar at all, but the storylines that brought them back were...<br /> <br /> The funny thing is, I can't accuse the Big Two of lack of creativity, exactly, as they are also putting out some original storylines that do sound pretty good! I'm actually interested in this &quot;Who killed the Watcher?&quot; concept, and &quot;World War&quot; between Earths 1 &amp; 2 sounds like something only DC could really pull off...So, I'm kinda flabbergasted as to why they're doing this other stuff. Did they really think the fans, of all people, wouldn't notice? Or were they hoping we *would*?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T10:06:00-07:00","id":172941,"title":"","content":"Incidentally, although Marvel denies it, apparently it's true that they are stopping promotion of Fantastic Four characters (allegedgly even taking down FF art in the Marvel offices) in other media. Why? Because Fox's FF movie is about to kick off, and they (or the Disney higher ups, rather) don't want to encourage the success of their rivals...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, apparently, Warner Bros is moving DC headquarters from NY to LA, and while this is being done, DC may (or may not, I guess it's all up in the air) actually *cease publication of all titles* for a few months until they are settled in! Is the world ready for no Superman?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T15:26:14-07:00","id":173256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=172941#post172941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, although Marvel denies it, apparently it's true that they are stopping promotion of Fantastic Four characters (allegedgly even taking down FF art in the Marvel offices) in other media. Why? Because Fox's FF movie is about to kick off, and they (or the Disney higher ups, rather) don't want to encourage the success of their rivals...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thats pretty petty if they do that...for that reason anyway. If they stopped doing FF because they turned them into a bunch of asshole I don't care about(I hope they don't think I forgot that Reed Richards ran a concentration camp for supers during that whole Civil War thing) then I'd be fine with that. &quot;Fantastic&quot; my ass!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=172941#post172941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, apparently, Warner Bros is moving DC headquarters from NY to LA, and while this is being done, DC may (or may not, I guess it's all up in the air) actually *cease publication of all titles* for a few months until they are settled in! Is the world ready for no Superman?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, that'd be pretty shitty...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T19:52:00-07:00","id":173533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=172941#post172941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, apparently, Warner Bros is moving DC headquarters from NY to LA, and while this is being done, DC may (or may not, I guess it's all up in the air) actually *cease publication of all titles* for a few months until they are settled in! Is the world ready for no Superman?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe they should do another reboot. The last one didn't take so well.<br /> <br /> Or better yet, they should &quot;downsize&quot; the majority of the higher ups, get somebody in there with a modicum of decency who actually knows what they're doing...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T05:49:28-07:00","id":174003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=173533#post173533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe they should do another reboot. The last one didn't take so well.<br /> <br /> Or better yet, they should &quot;downsize&quot; the majority of the higher ups, get somebody in there with a modicum of decency who actually knows what they're doing...</div> </div> </div> </div>Really they need to get rid of the editorial and replace with a staff that knows the difference between editing and overriding creative control for their rather inane decisions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T07:07:07-07:00","id":174090,"title":"","content":"This <b>IS </b>how they're down-sizing. They're moving the offices, but they're only telling the staff they want to <i>keep </i>the address.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T08:22:23-07:00","id":174148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=173533#post173533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe they should do another reboot. The last one didn't take so well.<br /> <br /> Or better yet, they should &quot;downsize&quot; the majority of the higher ups, get somebody in there with a modicum of decency who actually knows what they're doing...</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=174003#post174003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really they need to get rid of the editorial and replace with a staff that knows the difference between editing and overriding creative control for their rather inane decisions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seeing as how at least 90% of the problem is because DC is controlled by artists/Writers (Jim Lee and Dan DiDio) I would say the problem is creative control gone amok. 52 and the main direction of each of the lines was mainly their baby. Your heroes the way they are right now was at their direction. The fact that most were half retconned and the major changes in direction was their warped brain child.<br /> <br /> For another DC Universe Online was Jim Lee's creation. He oversaw the whole creation of the game and was the lead writer and concept artist. There was more than just him doing it all, but he was man #1 on everything either through creation or approval. I'm sure if he knew programming he would have had his hand in that too.<br /> <br /> As to how controlling they are on each step of the individual stories I don't know. It has been said they do group summits like Marvel where each of the lines get together, but I don't know if that is for their input or for them to be dictated to. Though I doubt the latter because of who they've had working for them.<br /> <br /> That is Marvel's problem as well, the loonies have been allowed to take over the looney bin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T23:56:16-07:00","id":175025,"title":"","content":"Writers are an issue in Marvel. That is popular writers with large clout being allowed free reign of books while completely rewriting their personalities. Bendis and Loeb come to mind. To some extent terrible writers exist in both companies. The issue with DC editorial is that it more often then not takes away a project from a writer. Look at Earth 2 or the debacle with Green Lantern where they wanted to kill John Stuart. They make bad decisions and override everyone else to do it. A good editor can save bad writing. Good Writing can't save a bad edit.<br /> <br /> Dan Didio and Jim lee aren't just writers they are also editiors and publishers they are the upper management of DC. The real issue is that it's connections over talent that gets you a job in these fields.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 06-20-2014, 02:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T00:09:49-07:00","id":175028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=172941#post172941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, although Marvel denies it, apparently it's true that they are stopping promotion of Fantastic Four characters (allegedgly even taking down FF art in the Marvel offices) in other media. Why? Because Fox's FF movie is about to kick off, and they (or the Disney higher ups, rather) don't want to encourage the success of their rivals...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>There is not a single X-Men or FF member on their anniversary cover, but somehow B-Rated characters like Black Bolt, Falcon-something and a space raccoon manages to appear.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i1196.photobucket.com/albums/aa418/crimsonorigami/3843076-x-menless.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T06:55:21-07:00","id":175216,"title":"","content":"Wow...that sucks. Not even Wolverine made it...damn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T09:16:05-07:00","id":175285,"title":"","content":"Lol!<br /> It does make a statement though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T10:12:26-07:00","id":175329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=175028#post175028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is not a single X-Men or FF member on their anniversary cover, but somehow B-Rated characters like Black Bolt, Falcon-something and a space raccoon manages to appear.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i1196.photobucket.com/albums/aa418/crimsonorigami/3843076-x-menless.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>Rocky made it because of both Bendis and the new movie. Too bad Bendis' GotG is unreadable if you read the original series. It's also why Groot and starlord are there even though the look dumb as hell. Seriously the writer and the artist need to be taken off that book. I'm guessing Marvel figures that what made Comic Marvel such a big hit was a fluke that needs to be thoroughly run into the ground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T10:45:34-07:00","id":175382,"title":"","content":"Starlord's exposing-my-hair helmet does look pretty silly, isn't it ? I can not stop myself from laughting when watching the GoTG trailer, the part where he jump toward a cliff with his hair softly dangling on the helmet like some kind of bad CGI water brush effect, so narmy. And looking at that anniversary, Marvel still trying to push Ms.Marvel at their Wonder Woman, aren't they ? Too bad she probably will never be as popular as Wondy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T13:15:23-07:00","id":175501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=175216#post175216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow...that sucks. Not even Wolverine made it...damn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wolverine will be killed off in a month or two if he hasn't been already. Marvel's been advertising it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T14:25:33-07:00","id":175542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=175382#post175382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Starlord's exposing-my-hair helmet does look pretty silly, isn't it ? I can not stop myself from laughting when watching the GoTG trailer, the part where he jump toward a cliff with his hair softly dangling on the helmet like some kind of bad CGI water brush effect, so narmy. And looking at that anniversary, Marvel still trying to push Ms.Marvel at their Wonder Woman, aren't they ? Too bad she probably will never be as popular as Wondy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't seen the GoTG trailer. I'm not sure I can watch it being a fan of the 2007 run.<br /> <br /> She'd have to have a personality and charm for that to happen. She's honestly being written rather wooden and insufferable. Too bad they won't push Storm or Sue Richards due to not owning their movie rights. Storm is honestly someone I'd like to see back on a non-X-men series. I mean she was when she was married to black panther but that was a rather shitty period for her (writing wise).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T06:30:39-07:00","id":176943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=175542#post175542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Storm is honestly someone I'd like to see back on a non-X-men series. I mean she was when she was married to black panther but that was a rather shitty period for her (writing wise).</div> </div> </div> </div>I never understand why they pair her with Black Panther anyway, Storm's fans says that because Black Panther need a sale boost and Storm is the only black-female character who is an A-list so off her go to be someone trophy wife, though BP's fans insists that he has always been an A-list way before Storm come along.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T06:33:19-07:00","id":176948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=175501#post175501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wolverine will be killed off in a month or two if he hasn't been already. Marvel's been advertising it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heard that. They'll give that a month or two before he's back. They've killed him before....everyone in the marvel has been killed off at least once it seems.<br /> <br /> Not sure why they have to make a big event out of it all the time now...but whatever.<br /> <br /> We'll see how long they give this...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T11:34:50-07:00","id":177210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=176943#post176943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I never understand why they pair her with Black Panther anyway, Storm's fans says that because Black Panther need a sale boost and Storm is the only black-female character who is an A-list so off her go to be someone trophy wife, though BP's fans insists that he has always been an A-list way before Storm come along.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lets be honest. It was because they were both famous and black. BP less famous than Storm but it was shitty event. They never had any connection except a few times in over the few decades they were both around. It was a PR stunt that no one wanted. Even worse the writer for Black Panther was really bad so BP came off as insufferable during that time. It sucks that Priest seems to not be able to keep a book for too long because his BP run was really good and pretty much defined the character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T15:16:01-07:00","id":177378,"title":"","content":"I have never been a fan of Black Panther. There are some things I like about the character (like his role in Wakanda, and the mythology behind the character), and I respect his role in the evolution of mainstream comic books. That said, the character has never really peaked my interests. His marriage to Storm never felt right to me either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T16:59:36-07:00","id":177455,"title":"","content":"So does anyone else feel that Black Widow's head looks ridiculously large compared to her body in that pic?<br /> <br /> I found BP to be only slightly less insufferable than Namor. Guess that comes with being the ruler of a small, technologically advanced nation. Black Bolt seems to be the only character fitting that description that wasn't a dick, but I'd wager a guess that if he spoke the writer's would make him into an ass also. I wasn't a fan of the idea of he and storm getting married either. It seemed a bit of lazy writing, &quot;Hey you're an African superhero, so am I, let's get married.&quot; Meh. He also was never an A-list hero, regardless of what his fans might say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T17:11:07-07:00","id":177463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=176948#post176948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They've killed him before....</div> </div> </div> </div>Like in the X-Men annual where where he died and a drop of his blood hit the M'Kraan crystal, completely regenerated an entirely new body for him (including his adamantium skeleton, but managed not to unblock his memories). Not an example of their better writing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 06-22-2014, 08:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T12:47:49-07:00","id":178137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=176948#post176948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They've killed him before....</div> </div> </div> </div>He's been to hell and fights Azrael, the Angel of Death, every time he dies. He's literally past Bill &amp; Ted's Bogus Journey at this point. The last good Wolverine I read was Old Man Logan, an alternate future that was an awesome series.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ortam + Malkavia makes a Requiem fun.<br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Posts in this colour are Persuasion.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">Posts in this colour are Seduction.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this colour are Intimidation.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/57-solomon-birch","name":"solomon birch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar57_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T04:27:44-07:00","id":178786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=177463#post177463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like in the X-Men annual where where he died and a drop of his blood hit the M'Kraan crystal, completely regenerated an entirely new body for him (including his adamantium skeleton, but managed not to unblock his memories). Not an example of their better writing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solomon birch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=178137#post178137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's been to hell and fights Azrael, the Angel of Death, every time he dies. He's literally past Bill &amp; Ted's Bogus Journey at this point. The last good Wolverine I read was Old Man Logan, an alternate future that was an awesome series.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup and yup...<br /> <br /> I think I read some of Old Man Logan. I was getting disillusioned by that point and wasn't paying as good attention. I remember it being a pretty good story though.<br /> <br /> I'll just go ahead and admit this now. I wasn't a fan of the Origin comics, nor did I like how he magically regained his memories at the end of House of M. While I realize they couldn't do it forever, I liked him alot better when he had that mystery about his origins...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T06:37:37-07:00","id":178860,"title":"","content":"I don't read New52 Superman comic, but for anyone that do, can you confirm that he has indeed lost his eh.......&quot;hair brush/tail/ahoge&quot;.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.minus.com/ioLxwqLku95Da.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 06-24-2014, 09:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T06:45:11-07:00","id":178870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=178860#post178860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't read New52 Superman comic, but for anyone that do, can you confirm that he has indeed lost his eh...hair brush/tail/ahoge.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe the preferred term is &quot;spitcurl.&quot; I can't help you out with your request, though. I don't have any Nu52 Superman books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T10:05:26-07:00","id":179820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=177463#post177463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like in the X-Men annual where where he died and a drop of his blood hit the M'Kraan crystal, completely regenerated an entirely new body for him (including his adamantium skeleton, but managed not to unblock his memories). Not an example of their better writing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been a while, but I think that story was retconned within the story itself; the crystal wiped those events from reality, or something; so, not sure if that really counts...And that whole &quot;fighitng the angel of death&quot; nonsense was thankfully ended. It was an outgrowth of creators extending his healing factor to the point where it was essentially resussurection/regeneration, until someone finally realized that was pretty stupid and dialed it way back to where it was before. Supposedly the next time Logan dies will be final (I doubt if anyone at Marvel even remembers any of this, tho).<br /> <br /> Yeah, obviously, he'll be back, it's just a question of when. I'm sure it'll last longer than a couple of months, tho, maybe a year if we're lucky. Wasn't Cap dead for about two years?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T10:07:05-07:00","id":179821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=175028#post175028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i1196.photobucket.com/albums/aa418/crimsonorigami/3843076-x-menless.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, how is it 75 years?? Are they actually counting the Timely-Atlas years or something?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T10:07:12-07:00","id":179822,"title":"","content":"Death means nothing in ongoing franchise comics.<br /> <br /> Thanks Superman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T15:43:48-07:00","id":180130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=179822#post179822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Death means nothing in ongoing franchise comics.<br /> <br /> Thanks Superman.</div> </div> </div> </div>It started way before Superman he was just the reason the Crash happened in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T16:35:41-07:00","id":180161,"title":"","content":"At least they make fun of Jean Grey getting to return every other year.....<br /> <br /> Although best resurrection quote ever (although not from comics):<br /> &quot;Look what I found. Dr. Jackson is going to die if he sees this.&quot;<br /> &quot;What? again?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T16:50:37-07:00","id":180165,"title":"","content":"Jean Grey's resurrection was comic-books' death knell to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T18:10:37-07:00","id":180237,"title":"","content":"To emphasize the point, the X-Men's best ever run began with the intro of the new team way back in '75 and had Chris Claremont taking over the title with issue #94 and ran with it through The Dark Phoenix saga and the Days of Future Past. One of the best runs ever, bar none. But the emphasis is the Dark Phoenix saga where Jean Grey was written to be the hero she was always meant to be.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.covernk.com/Covers/L/X/X-Men%201963%20series/x-men1963series137.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> This was a classic! And it was ruined later by the introduction of X-Factor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","user":"Shadowflame","date":".  Spacing. 06-25-2014, 09:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T07:53:06-07:00","id":180805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=179821#post179821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, how is it 75 years?? Are they actually counting the Timely-Atlas years or something?</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as Captain America is on the roster, and the fact that Jack Kirby (one of Marvel's heavy-weights) was one of the co-creators, yeah.....they'll keep claiming a long lineage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T09:30:41-07:00","id":180907,"title":"","content":"Well, the original Human Torch and the Sub-Mariner were both created in 1939. Pity neither are in the pic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T11:28:13-07:00","id":181047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=180237#post180237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To emphasize the point, the X-Men's best ever run began with the intro of the new team way back in '75 and had Chris Claremont taking over the title with issue #94 and ran with it through The Dark Phoenix saga and the Days of Future Past. One of the best runs ever, bar none. But the emphasis is the Dark Phoenix saga where Jean Grey was written to be the hero she was always meant to be.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.covernk.com/Covers/L/X/X-Men%201963%20series/x-men1963series137.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.covernk.com/Covers/L/X/X-...3series137.jpg</a><br /> <br /> This was a classic! And it was ruined later by the introduction of X-Factor.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to disagree a bit. I agree that the Dark Phoenix saga is/was awesome. What I don't agree with is the end of it. It wasn't supposed to end that way and you can tell that it wasn't supposed to end that way. If it would have ended as it orginally was going to we would have had a lot less problems all around. Her death was one of the worst ones ever. She allows herself to die and it is done quickly and abruptly in the last few pages of the comic. It was more a &quot;lets get the bull shit out of the way&quot; kind of ending.<br /> <br /> If he had been allowed to follow through with the ending proposed then it would have totally negated some big opposition to both Jean and Cyclopes as characters from some fans and writers. The return of both of them in X-Factor would have had a better start as well. While it isn't the only stupid decision that has continued to hurt them over the years(some writers have specifically sited that instance as their decision for the later stories they wrote) it is a very pervasive one both from her death in the first place and her return because of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":787,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","user":"Sorwen","date":". 06-26-2014, 02:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T17:42:44-07:00","id":181469,"title":"","content":"From Jim Shooter's <a href=\"http://www.jimshooter.com/2011/06/origin-of-phoenix-saga.html\" target=\"_blank\">web site</a>;<br /> <br /> <i>I told Chris that the ending proposed in his plot didn't work. It wasn't workable with the characters, and in fact was a totally lame cop-out, storywise. I demanded a different ending. Chris--enraged--asked me just what that might be. I suggested that Phoenix be sent to some super-security interstellar prison as punishment for her crimes. Chris said that the X-Men would never stop trying to rescue (?!) her and that the story would become a loop. I said that then he should come up with an ending.<br /> <br /> I wasn't privy to Chris and John's conversations that night, but whatever.<br /> <br /> The next morning, Chris stormed into my office and said that there was only one answer--they'd have to kill Phoenix. I said fine.<br /> <br /> I don't think he expected me to say that, since killing characters just wasn't done in those days. Chris waffled a bit, but then I became insistent! She's dying. That's it.<br /> <br /> Chris left my office, obviously found a phone somewhere and, a few minutes later, I got a call from John that started with him asking me if I was insane.<br /> <br /> I insisted on the &quot;solution.&quot; It was done--brilliantly, if reluctantly--by Chris and John. And that's was the issue that propelled the X-Men to the top for, what, two decades?<br /> <br /> That's the story. Check it with Salicrup. Actually, Chris would probably corroborate it, too, though he'd make it seem that he was smarter and that I was a doofus. I'm okay with that. Chris doesn't get nearly enough credit for what he accomplished. I'm proud to be the doofus who helped to enable it.</i><br /> ------------------<br /> <br /> And Jim Salicrup comments on the bottom of that page;<i><br /> <br /> Yep, that's pretty much the story. Just a couple of nit picks-- I wasn't at that original dinner with Chris and Jim. I believe that was Roger Stern, who was still editor of UNCANNY X-MEN at the time the story was planned. I misunderstood the story all along, it seems, in that I thought an evil entity-- &quot;the Dark Phoenix&quot;-- had possessed Jean, and once that was gone, all would be well with the world. No moral problems, etc. The issue I edited was published, as the Untold Story or something like that, and we all talked about the behind-the-scenes evolution of the story in a text feature in that special edition. The actual Death of Dark Phoenix issue, was actually re-edited by the brilliant Louise Jones, as per Jim's instructions-- and it is indeed a classic! I always give the credit for killing Jean to Jim, and he deserves it. As do Chris, John, Terry, Tom, Glynis, and Louise, for the final, er, execution, and Roger Stern for getting it underway. </i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T07:31:43-07:00","id":181930,"title":"","content":"Claremont says pretty much the same. He was pissed because they had been building to Jean just becoming depowered and exiled since it was the Phoenix that went on a rampage. Her and Cyke would then leave the X-Men opening up others becoming the focus and the ability to bring them back later if they wanted. He talks about the, on his part, flippant remark about killing her off.<br /> <br /> Claremont differs just a little in that he says Jim wanted more than her just being locked up and was comparing her to Hitler. He wouldn't allow it to be the fault of the Phoenix Entity at all. That is when Chris says he got pissed and just said &quot;well lets kill her then&quot; because nothing else he said to Jim was acceptable. I think Claremont's comment is on his site.<br /> <br /> Cable would have been Jean's true son and while we would have lost out on the Goblin Queen we wouldn't have had to deal with a lot of the other shit. The clunky start to X-Factor, the Jean/Cyke/Logan triangle, the Cyke/Emma psychic affair, and probably a few other things I'm forgetting that was in one way or another attributed to that whole mess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T09:46:11-07:00","id":182059,"title":"","content":"Marvel should have kept her dead. Period.<br /> X-Factor was a crappy idea for a spin-off, made worse by cheapening the end of an incredibly successful run.<br /> The only good thing that came out of that mess called X-Factor was Apocalypse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T14:50:36-07:00","id":182243,"title":"","content":"I won't talk about why I hate <b>All-New Ultimates #4</b> enough to dump the title because my reasons touch on feminism and sexual politics, but yeah, I'm done with this book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T09:13:59-07:00","id":183857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorwen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=181930#post181930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Claremont says pretty much the same. He was pissed because they had been building to Jean just becoming depowered and exiled since it was the Phoenix that went on a rampage. Her and Cyke would then leave the X-Men opening up others becoming the focus and the ability to bring them back later if they wanted. He talks about the, on his part, flippant remark about killing her off.<br /> <br /> Claremont differs just a little in that he says Jim wanted more than her just being locked up and was comparing her to Hitler. He wouldn't allow it to be the fault of the Phoenix Entity at all. That is when Chris says he got pissed and just said &quot;well lets kill her then&quot; because nothing else he said to Jim was acceptable. I think Claremont's comment is on his site.<br /> <br /> Cable would have been Jean's true son and while we would have lost out on the Goblin Queen we wouldn't have had to deal with a lot of the other shit. The clunky start to X-Factor, the Jean/Cyke/Logan triangle, the Cyke/Emma psychic affair, and probably a few other things I'm forgetting that was in one way or another attributed to that whole mess.</div> </div> </div> </div>As fans of creative works and their creators, we are often predisposed to agree with the creators, esp against the &quot;big bad&quot; Authorities that force them to change their works. Sometimes it's hard for us (and esp for the creators) to see that those changes are...sometimes...for the better! In this case, if Claremont had made Jean headblind (a storyline he's been trying to tell for decades), I really don't think the Dark Phoenix storyline would have had anywhere near as much impact as it did (and Jean doesn't just &quot;allow&quot; herself to be killed, she actively does it herself!). Frankly, that alone makes a lot of what happened worthwhile, even if that followup wasn't all that great...<br /> <br /> Also, AFAIK, there was no concept of the &quot;Phoenix Entity&quot; until they came up with it to justify bringing Jean back later. At the time, it was simply Jean with ultimate power, which she couldn't handle. She had killed billions of people, some answer had to be made for that...<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200bI didn't know that Cable was going to really be Jean and Scott's son, but I do remember Claremont hinting that Wolverine was actually Rachel's father! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And, FWIW, Scott and Emma getting together was one of the best things that came from Morrison's run...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T09:16:11-07:00","id":183858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=179822#post179822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Death means nothing in ongoing franchise comics.<br /> <br /> Thanks Superman.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll just leave this here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0PlwDbSYicM\" data-code=\"0PlwDbSYicM\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/0PlwDbSYicM/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T20:43:01-07:00","id":184420,"title":"","content":"The first minute was so pretentious, I was annoyed and stopped watching it. If there was anything relevant in that whole 17 minute video could you summarize it for us?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T21:51:37-07:00","id":184520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=184420#post184420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first minute was so pretentious, I was annoyed and stopped watching it. If there was anything relevant in that whole 17 minute video could you summarize it for us?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's max landis for you. At least he made Chronicle which was surprisingly good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T08:14:35-07:00","id":184823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=184420#post184420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first minute was so pretentious, I was annoyed and stopped watching it. If there was anything relevant in that whole 17 minute video could you summarize it for us?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, it usually irritates me when people complain about things they refuse to watch in their entirety, but what the heck. He basically summarizes the storyline of The Death (Sleep?) and Return of Superman, and its impact, which is apparently a massive loss in sales for Superman's titles (at the time of the making of the vid, at least) and an onscreen list of the many, MANY characters to come back to life since then, concluding that the storyline didn't kill Superman, <i>it killed Death itself in comics,</i> which agrees with the poster that I posted the vid in response to.<br /> <br /> I thought the whole thing was very funny, but mileages vary. Epi implies that Max Landis is always like that, but I'd never heard of him before this, and haven't seen him in anything else, so I don't know if his persona is an act or how he really is. Maybe he'd annoy the hell out of me too if I saw him in more stuff...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":681,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","user":"Hand-of-Omega","date":". 06-30-2014, 11:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T09:27:09-07:00","id":184891,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=184520#post184520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's max landis for you. At least he made Chronicle which was surprisingly good.</div> </div> </div> </div>I look forward to the sequel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T09:46:34-07:00","id":184916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=182243#post182243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I won't talk about why I hate <b>All-New Ultimates #4</b> enough to dump the title because my reasons touch on feminism and sexual politics, but yeah, I'm done with this book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm curious. Especially since the UU is pretty much all I read these days.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T10:18:01-07:00","id":184931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=184891#post184891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I look forward to the sequel.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's gonna be one? Hm...<br /> <br /> There's been a similar rumor to the FF one going around, that Marvel (for similar movie related reasons), is doing a company wide reboot of sorts, that will permanently get rid of ALL mutants in the MU, and essentially replace them with the Inhumans (getting rid of Wolvie is apparently the first step to doing this). Marvel denies this, of course, and it's looking like it's probably unfounded...but we'll see...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T10:38:42-07:00","id":184949,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=184931#post184931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's gonna be one? Hm...</div> </div> </div> </div>The first movie had a $12 million budget, and grossed around $126 million. So, it's a thing. <a href=\"http://www.deadline.com/2014/03/fox-hires-scribe-for-chronicle-2/\" target=\"_blank\">Whether it's a good thing</a> with out the principals (director and writer) remains to be seen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","user":"Shadowflame","date":".  link fix 06-30-2014, 01:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T12:58:26-07:00","id":185004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=183857#post183857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As fans of creative works and their creators, we are often predisposed to agree with the creators, esp against the &quot;big bad&quot; Authorities that force them to change their works. Sometimes it's hard for us (and esp for the creators) to see that those changes are...sometimes...for the better! In this case, if Claremont had made Jean headblind (a storyline he's been trying to tell for decades), I really don't think the Dark Phoenix storyline would have had anywhere near as much impact as it did (and Jean doesn't just &quot;allow&quot; herself to be killed, she actively does it herself!). Frankly, that alone makes a lot of what happened worthwhile, even if that followup wasn't all that great...</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to disagree. In the first because as I said her death happens in like the last page or two pages of the story and that is it. Her death impacts the team peripherally and is only really shown in its affect on Scott. Who eventually disappears with Madelyne which is exactly what was supposed to happen with Jean any way. It all just caused a lot of unneeded bull.<br /> <br /> Second, I say allow because she senses she is about to be shot out of now where and just stands there and takes it. I don't see that as &quot;she actively does it herself&quot; really.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, AFAIK, there was no concept of the &quot;Phoenix Entity&quot; until they came up with it to justify bringing Jean back later. At the time, it was simply Jean with ultimate power, which she couldn't handle. She had killed billions of people, some answer had to be made for that... </div> </div> </div>Actually yes there was an Entity from the very beginning. The difference is originally she was possessed by it and it was rewritten that it cloned her instead when they decided to bring Jean back.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bI didn't know that Cable was going to really be Jean and Scott's son, but I do remember Claremont hinting that Wolverine was actually Rachel's father! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And, FWIW, Scott and Emma getting together was one of the best things that came from Morrison's run... </div> </div> </div>Order of events. Cable was made and then it was decided was Scott's and Madelyne's son. Can't say for 100% that they would have followed through if it was Jean instead it seems unlikely they wouldn't have because it was who the parents where and not just any mutant's son. They wanted to tie his origin in with Sinister who's plan had become joining Jean and Scott's DNA. Who can say though.<br /> <br /> As to Scott and Emma, meh. I can't argue your opinion, but I can't agree with it. It just made things even more fucked up in my opinion. And if it had been made totally pointless that doesn't mean a good story might not have came out of his run any way. Though I didn't care for most of Morrison's run even if you exclude that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=184823#post184823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, it usually irritates me when people complain about things they refuse to watch in their entirety, but what the heck. He basically summarizes the storyline of The Death (Sleep?) and Return of Superman, and its impact, which is apparently a massive loss in sales for Superman's titles (at the time of the making of the vid, at least) and an onscreen list of the many, MANY characters to come back to life since then, concluding that the storyline didn't kill Superman, <i>it killed Death itself in comics,</i> which agrees with the poster that I posted the vid in response to.<br /> <br /> I thought the whole thing was very funny, but mileages vary. Epi implies that Max Landis is always like that, but I'd never heard of him before this, and haven't seen him in anything else, so I don't know if his persona is an act or how he really is. Maybe he'd annoy the hell out of me too if I saw him in more stuff...</div> </div> </div> </div>I've seen it before and he does get some things wrong(among other things that Superman ruined death since they were already coming back however whenever). He talks about the Man of Steel movie as well. I partially agree with what he said in that, but I have a few problems with it as well.<br /> <br /> I agree it is funny though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T12:58:51-07:00","id":185007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=184931#post184931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's gonna be one? Hm...<br /> <br /> There's been a similar rumor to the FF one going around, that Marvel (for similar movie related reasons), is doing a company wide reboot of sorts, that will permanently get rid of ALL mutants in the MU, and essentially replace them with the Inhumans (getting rid of Wolvie is apparently the first step to doing this). Marvel denies this, of course, and it's looking like it's probably unfounded...but we'll see...</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't be surprised. Which is why I haven't bought the inhumans. It's pretty much mutants 2.0 which is dumb. The series isn't even all that compelling from what I've read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T13:12:16-07:00","id":185013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=185007#post185007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn't be surprised. Which is why I haven't bought the inhumans. It's pretty much mutants 2.0 which is dumb. The series isn't even all that compelling from what I've read.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would be because of how much money Marvel/Disney is throwing at mutants(both comics and games since they can't do movies) and re-birthing everything/everyone just about. I can't really see them saying &quot;Ah well its done lets fail with house of M 2.0&quot; subtitled &quot;Wanda gets it right this time&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T17:58:45-07:00","id":185271,"title":"","content":"How interesting; <a href=\"http://comicbookinformer.com/features/the-5-greatest-comic-storylines-of-all-time/\" target=\"_blank\">Five Greatest Storylines of All Time</a> <i> When it comes to the X-Men, the discussion pretty much starts and ends with Chris Claremont. Stan Lee may have created the team, but Claremont is the one that really developed the characters. Before Claremont took over, the book was failing, it had been publishing reprints for years. Look at it now, it\u2019s one of the most popular titles in Marvel\u2019s library. Much of that success can be attributed to the amazing success of Claremont\u2019s first major story arc, \u201cThe Dark Phoenix Saga.\u201d Jean Grey, one of the original X-Men, had become host of the super-powerful cosmic entity known as the Phoenix Force. As Phoenix, Grey had near limitless power, but her personality was becoming increasingly fragile. This made her a target for the Hellfire Club, a corrupt group of the world\u2019s social elite. The Inner Circle of the Club used mind control to trap Grey in a hallucination, making her believe she was their Black Queen, and allowing the Phoenix Force to grow corrupt. Enter the X-Men. They raid the Hellfire Club and are\u2026 soundly defeated. All would have been lost if not for the rise of Wolverine. You see, prior to this point, Wolverine was nowhere near the sensation he is today. In fact, the fans HATED him. The only purpose he served on the team was as an antagonist, constantly causing friction within the team. When the X-Men were defeated by the Hellfire Club, Wolverine was supposed to die. John Byrne, the artist for Uncanny, a Canadian (nobody\u2019s perfect), refused to let the one high-profile Canadian superhero die, and asked Claremont to give Wolverine one more chance. And so, Wolverine was unleashed.</i>.....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T06:47:55-07:00","id":185486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorwen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=185004#post185004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to disagree. In the first because as I said her death happens in like the last page or two pages of the story and that is it. Her death impacts the team peripherally and is only really shown in its affect on Scott. Who eventually disappears with Madelyne which is exactly what was supposed to happen with Jean any way. It all just caused a lot of unneeded bull.<br /> <br /> Second, I say allow because she senses she is about to be shot out of now where and just stands there and takes it. I don't see that as &quot;she actively does it herself&quot; really.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the page in question:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.judao.com.br/8/wp-content/uploads/2013/09/xmen10.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> So, this wasn't just some random antique gun that shot in her direction *for no reason*...She actively did it (to) herself with her powers. She decided to die and made it happen.<br /> <br /> And what does it matter if this was at the end of the issue or not? It's not like the overall series ends here, or that the characters and readers wouldn't be back next month to explore the ramifications! IIRC, the death of Supergirl happened at the end of that issue of Crisis on Infinite Earths, and that was certainly planned out well in advance (it even had a cover that could well be an homage to the Death of Phoenix cover!)...Why should a major character die at the beginning or middle of an issue, instead of at end (like Gwen Stacy also did), where the climax naturally is?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Actually yes there was an Entity from the very beginning. The difference is originally she was possessed by it and it was rewritten that it cloned her instead when they decided to bring Jean back.<br /> . </div> </div> </div>I've never seen or read any indication of this. From my reading, the Phoenix was originally just Jean Grey's natural powers enhanced to an awesome degree by mutagenic radiation (symbolized by a cool fire bird because John Byrne is *awesome*!^^). Later, when they needed to bring Jean back, they came up with the Phoenix entity to make her guiltless of its crimes (a trick DC would later use to get Hal Jordan off the hook for similar crimes). There was also some talk likening the Phoenix Force to the Force from Star Wars, as a universal field of psionic/cosmic energy that certain people (like Rachel) could tap into...<br /> <br /> It's clear that Jean wasn't possessed or anything back then, because if she were, then the obvious ending would be to &quot;exorcise&quot; the entity and kill IT for its crimes. And how come Xavier didn't notice another entity when he was locked in psychic combat with her? Why doesn't she mention it in the scene above, instead of taking personal responsibility for her own actions?<br /> <br /> The fact that one creator misunderstood (or misremembered) his impression of the story, as quoted earlier upthread, doesn't mean that that's what was really happening in it.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":681,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","user":"Hand-of-Omega","date":". 07-01-2014, 09:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T06:58:44-07:00","id":185488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=185271#post185271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How interesting; <a href=\"http://comicbookinformer.com/features/the-5-greatest-comic-storylines-of-all-time/\" target=\"_blank\">Five Greatest Storylines of All Time</a> [I] When it comes to the X-Men, the discussion pretty much starts and ends with Chris Claremont. Stan Lee may have created the team, but Claremont is the one that really developed the characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Stan may have created the original team and the concepts, but Claremont is the one who refined them into the huge franchise they are today. I was glad to see him get a cameo in the movies (even if it was X-Men 3)! <br /> <br /> John Byrne still takes credit saving Wolverine from the chopping block, if only because he wasn't gonna let them kill the only Canadian superhero at the time! I've seen recent evidence that Byrne actually did the lion's share of creative input into Kitty Pryde, as well...<br /> <br /> That sure was a fantastic run! Granted, some of its more memorable storylines were &quot;homages&quot; of what was going on in pop culture at the time (the Brood are obviously inspired by Alien, and Days of Future Past by Terminator (I'm unsure if Dragon Ball Z was ripping off Terminator or DoFP with its Trunks/Androids storyline)), but it was still great stuff...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T07:20:41-07:00","id":185498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=185486#post185486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><img src=\"http://www.judao.com.br/8/wp-content/uploads/2013/09/xmen10.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, maybe it's a product of its times that you had to be there for, because this is my first time reading those bottom three panels and I am <i>cringing</i> with embarrassment at that monologue. Hell, both of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T07:32:06-07:00","id":185506,"title":"","content":"You had to have read the series at the time. There was just so much going on, so much passion. The only thing that ever had such...impact before that was the death of Gwen Stacy back in the 70s. (The end of the Silver Age I believe) I don't believe that such emotion is well received these days in a more jaded society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T07:56:07-07:00","id":185513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=185506#post185506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You had to have read the series at the time. There was just so much going on, so much passion. The only thing that ever had such...impact before that was the death of Gwen Stacy back in the 70s. (The end of the Silver Age I believe) I don't believe that such emotion is well received these days in a more jaded society.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Also, the tastes of the times change...comics back then were written in a much more melodramatic, florid voice, unlike the attempts at &quot;realistic&quot; dialog today. <br /> <br /> But this impact is what I was getting at above: If Dark Phoenix had ended with Jean getting depowered and retiring (which I'm sure would have been undone in good time anyway), then that story would not have made anywhere near the impact it did or been remembered so fondly. So, sometimes, Executive Meddling can actually make things better, believe it or not!<br /> <br /> Similarly, Byrne got really pissed off at Claremont for changing his <a href=\"http://goodcomics.comicbookresources.com/2009/12/03/comic-book-legends-revealed-236/\" target=\"_blank\">Days of Future Past storyline</a>, but that change led to the character of Rachel, a personal favorite of mine, becoming a regular!<br /> <br /> (Careful with that site, btw; you can easily lose an entire day crawling around in there!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T12:22:01-07:00","id":186447,"title":"","content":"I just wanted to point out that Days of Future Past predates Terminator by a little over 4 years. It wasn't influenced by Terminator,.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T12:50:04-07:00","id":186455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno, maybe it's a product of its times that you had to be there for, because this is my first time reading those bottom three panels and I am <i>cringing</i> with embarrassment at that monologue. Hell, both of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The dialogue is terrible, but at least she didn't beg him to kill her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T13:22:33-07:00","id":186468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=186455#post186455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The dialogue is terrible, but at least she didn't beg him to kill her.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh, yeah, fair enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T13:49:29-07:00","id":186495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=186447#post186447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just wanted to point out that Days of Future Past predates Terminator by a little over 4 years. It wasn't influenced by Terminator,.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm surprised we never got a Terminator/X-Men crossover comic... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T20:55:49-07:00","id":187654,"title":"","content":"<br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><i> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Originally posted by <b>Darksider</b> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=186447#post186447\">View Post</a></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">I just wanted to point out that Days of Future Past predates Terminator by a little over 4 years. It wasn't influenced by Terminator,.</span><br /> </span><br /> </i></span><br /> <br /> <br /> Or maybe it was influenced by Soldier/Demon With A Glass Hand, the 1964 Harlan Ellison episodes of the Outer Limits that influenced Terminator!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm surprised we never got a Terminator/X-Men crossover comic... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Probably because the Terminator was too busy starring in stuff like:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://img1.wikia.nocookie.net/__cb20090428192238/terminator/images/b/bf/RobocopVTerminatorComic1.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> (Written by Frank Miller and drawn by Walt Simonson, if you can believe it!)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T23:04:11-07:00","id":187740,"title":"","content":"I am not a longtime comics reader, though I like the characters and try to pick up on what is going on in the comics every so often...<br /> <br /> Recently I decided to download one of the comics apps and have been picking up a few collections here and there.<br /> <br /> The first hellblazer collection was pretty cool... very strange, and in one issue I think I can see where the White Wolf writers might have gotten the idea for the Blood Brothers. Skinhead soccer hooligans...<br /> <br /> I am a fan of the underdog, so I have a soft spot for Aquaman. I picked up the first collection of that and I am liking it. Still not 100% sold on &quot;the others&quot;, I think they need a little more development before they feel like real superheroes. I am hoping to sink my teeth in a little more about atlantis and what that's all about...<br /> <br /> A few issues of Amazing X-Men as well. It strikes me as the new X-Calibur, given how they are putting Nightcrawler front and center and being just a tad silly, with the X-Mansion being filled with &quot;bamfs&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T09:26:44-07:00","id":188028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=187654#post187654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Probably because the Terminator was too busy starring in stuff like:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://img1.wikia.nocookie.ne