blr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 07-06-2014, 11:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T20:31:02-07:00","id":189888,"title":"","content":"Venom needs to bump into Thanos or someone very destructive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T23:29:24-07:00","id":191144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=189824#post189824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Carnage gonna appear in AXIS, I swear that if any of the X-Men loose to him.........<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> He is shipped to Guardians of the Galaxy ever since his book got canned, poor boy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being written by Bendis at moment is a fate worse than death. Especially with this &quot;Take everything that made Cosmic Marvel good and destroy it&quot; stance marvel has taken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T02:39:44-07:00","id":191264,"title":"","content":"Kyle: Giant Douche!<br /> Cartman: Shit Sandwich!!!<br /> Comic Industry: BOTH! BUY EXTRAS AND WE'LL DO CROSSOVERS AND ALTERNATE HISTORY ARCS!!!<br /> <br /> Anyway, I was looking around earlier and discovered that my digital (and now, only) copy of I, Joker has been mysteriously erased. Please excuse me while I go stab a random pedestrian.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T23:10:35-07:00","id":192083,"title":"","content":"Blond hair blue eyes hetero Captain America beat up Warpath, a native America X-men...............Okay, AvX was worse than I thought.<br /> <br /> Urrggh, I hate Military-type character who constantly calling everybody &quot;son&quot;.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://static.comicvine.com/uploads/scale_super/10/103530/2464841-3.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T14:55:50-07:00","id":195016,"title":"","content":"I'm torn about Batgirl.<br /> On one hand, I hated the new costume she will be wearing. Looks too much like normal clothing, which is something I detest in typical superheroes. And it is not like a leather jacket is more practical than the sci-fi &quot;bullet/cut/temperature/etc resistant spandex&quot; that the Bat-family usually wears. and boots with laces are more practical than heels, but less so than the boots she was wearing before these. Besides, the artist makes her look way too young.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if the writing does what it is proposing to do, it would be just the sort of story I'm looking for in comics these days.<br /> <br /> Though I can't help but notice that what it will try to do is pretty much what I already had with Steph as Batgirl before DC got rid of her in the reboot...no wonder DC gets so little of my money.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T15:05:51-07:00","id":195026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=195016#post195016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm torn about Batgirl.<br /> On one hand, I hated the new costume she will be wearing. Looks too much like normal clothing, which is something I detest in typical superheroes. And it is not like a leather jacket is more practical than the sci-fi &quot;bullet/cut/temperature/etc resistant spandex&quot; that the Bat-family usually wears. and boots with laces are more practical than heels, but less so than the boots she was wearing before these. Besides, the artist makes her look way too young.</div> </div> </div> </div>Overall I think it's an improvement, but it does give me a sort of 1930's hero vibe. Not that it's a bad thing, I know nothing about what stories they're telling or what style of hero they're going for, but that's the vibe I get.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T17:17:21-07:00","id":195118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=192083#post192083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blond hair blue eyes hetero Captain America beat up Warpath, a native America X-men...............Okay, AvX was worse than I thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, that's not the lens I try to see things, including comics, through...If Warpath isn't on Cap's fighting level (and from what I saw before, he's not), then he deserves to lose the fight, end of story. <br /> <br /> Granted, I have made similar statements about how DC got rid of the Asian Batgirl in favor of the blond, blue-eyed Batgirl, at the same time they killed off the one African-American member of the Bat team, so I'm not immune to such things. In fact, that's why I skipped Stephanie Brown's series as Batgirl (her horrible costume didn't help), until I finally read an issue...and had a blast! Of course, then DC cancelled it, to put Babs back in the suit, a decision I still disagree with with the fury of a thousand Unconquered Suns!<br /> <br /> So, yeah, I haven't read any of the current series. What's this about her getting a new costume?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T17:44:31-07:00","id":195134,"title":"","content":"New creative team. Her house will catch fire and she'll have to make a new costume because the current one is...I think the word the artist used is &quot;gazey.&quot;<br /> <br /> EDIT: <a href=\"http://www.mtv.com/news/1864359/batgirl-exclusive-dc-comics/\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a> is...not the link I was thinking of, but I swear to god the not-word &quot;gazey&quot; was involved somewhere. I'll keep looking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":271,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","user":"JimB","date":". 07-11-2014, 08:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T17:51:31-07:00","id":195137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=195118#post195118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, that's not the lens I try to see things, including comics, through...If Warpath isn't on Cap's fighting level (and from what I saw before, he's not), then he deserves to lose the fight, end of story.<br /> <br /> Granted, I have made similar statements about how DC got rid of the Asian Batgirl in favor of the blond, blue-eyed Batgirl, at the same time they killed off the one African-American member of the Bat team, so I'm not immune to such things. In fact, that's why I skipped Stephanie Brown's series as Batgirl (her horrible costume didn't help), until I finally read an issue...and had a blast! Of course, then DC cancelled it, to put Babs back in the suit, a decision I still disagree with with the fury of a thousand Unconquered Suns!<br /> <br /> So, yeah, I haven't read any of the current series. What's this about her getting a new costume?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spoiler and Batgirl were two different people. And they both worked together on multiple books and Cain was on Red Robin before the reboot. I'm just mad Barbra's out of her chair because she's terribly boring and she was a lot better as Oracle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T17:58:15-07:00","id":195148,"title":"","content":"Epimetheus, I gotta ask, do you even <i>like</i> comics? I don't see a single post where you talk about anything you like. This last one is the closest you've gotten, and even now you're only saying Oracle is better than a &quot;terribly boring&quot; character, not that you think Oracle is good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T18:33:16-07:00","id":195171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=195137#post195137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Spoiler and Batgirl were two different people. And they both worked together on multiple books and Cain was on Red Robin before the reboot..</div> </div> </div> </div>...Did you miss the storyline where Cassandra Cain gave up being Batgirl, and passed the mantle onto Steph? She was Batgirl for all of 12 issues or so, before the reboot.<br /> <br /> Cassie disappeared for awhile, then turned up in Hong Kong, as Batman's agent in Asia, now known as &quot;Black Bat&quot; (stupid name, but cool costume). It was in that identity that she helped Red Robin when he found her there. I don't know if she's turned up since the reboot, tho.<br /> <br /> DC has always had a funny attitude towards Cassie...I guess they never really knew what to do with her, or how to write her, and she has a large fandom that gets very upset whenever they try to write her out, which has happened at least twice now...<br /> <br /> Ah well, at least we'll always have <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Webcomic/CassToons?from=Main.CassToons\" target=\"_blank\">CassToons</a>!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T18:38:06-07:00","id":195173,"title":"","content":"Among the many, many...MANY reasons why Barbara becoming Batgirl again is such an awful idea (I'll spare you the whole rant), one of the more in-universe pressing ones is this: Leaving alone the fact that Babs did more good by effectively organizing the entire superhero community as Oracle than she can ever do leaping around buildings in tights, she now spends so much time being Batgirl that she can't BE Oracle anymore. How does the superhero community deal with that sudden, gaping silence where the voice that used to rally them so well used to be? <br /> <br /> Also, the very concept of Oracle was a really cool one that was something that Marvel never had, so that was an edge they lost against their competition right there...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T18:47:00-07:00","id":195180,"title":"","content":"I've just discovered this guy's column, and I'd really like to know what you fine folks think of <a href=\"http://comicsalliance.com/superman-characters-marvel-universe-ask-chris-171/\" target=\"_blank\">these</a> <a href=\"http://comicsalliance.com/dc-comics-marvel-golden-age-silver-age-comics-history/\" target=\"_blank\">articles</a>!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T19:18:43-07:00","id":195193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=195173#post195173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Leaving alone the fact that Babs did more good by effectively organizing the entire superhero community as Oracle than she can ever do leaping around buildings in tights, she now spends so much time being Batgirl that she can't [i]be[/u] Oracle anymore. How does the superhero community deal with that sudden, gaping silence where the voice that used to rally them so well used to be?</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I know, in Nu52 continuity, Barbara Gordon was never Oracle, so there is no voice to have gone silent. If I'm misinformed, please let me know and I'll retract the statement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=195180#post195180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've just discovered this guy's column, and I'd really like to know what you fine folks think of <a href=\"http://comicsalliance.com/superman-characters-marvel-universe-ask-chris-171/\" target=\"_blank\">these</a> <a href=\"http://comicsalliance.com/dc-comics-marvel-golden-age-silver-age-comics-history/\" target=\"_blank\">articles</a>!</div> </div> </div> </div>That guy is kind of full of crap. The particular article you've linked leaves out an event that I don't remember terribly clearly because it was happening when I first got into comics, but just after Bane let a bunch of supervillains out of superjail to wear down Batman such that someone had to take over the role, Spider-Man encountered a villain who let a bunch of supervillains out of superjail to wear him down, and shortly thereafter the Clone Saga saw Spider-Man's role taken over by a clone. And that's just a for instance.<br /> <br /> Marvel and DC have been ripping each other off for ages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T19:38:27-07:00","id":195200,"title":"","content":"I assume you're referring to Knightfall.<br /> <br /> <br /> He is sort of full of crap (For instance, Kirby requested to be put on Jimmy Olsen, because he didn't want to derail the work of anyone else by taking it over). But he is right about more or less about the distinctions between Marvel and DC, and DC's past policies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T20:37:43-07:00","id":195222,"title":"","content":"Hmm...Wikipedia's entry on Batgirl mentions that New 52 Babs was only in the chair for 3 years now, and she is a much younger character, in her early 20s who doesn't know as much (the main reason Gail Simone feels good about this approach); which does sound like Oracle has been retconned out of existence. DCs' wiki, however, *does* still mention her being Oracle...I honestly don't know if she was Oracle now or not. <br /> <br /> (Also, so far as I know, no explanation for Steph leaving the role of Batgirl was ever given, so she may well have been retconned out of that, too!)<br /> <br /> Regardless, at least part of my objection still stands: That was a unique part of a superhero universe that really set DC apart, and that DC is (imo) much poorer without, even if the heroes within it don't know it!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T20:47:22-07:00","id":195227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=195200#post195200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He is sort of full of crap (for instance, Kirby requested to be put on Jimmy Olsen, because he didn't want to derail the work of anyone else by taking it over). But he is right about more or less about the distinctions between Marvel and DC, and DC's past policies.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's one of the things that bugs me about Chris Sims. He gets some stuff right and some stuff wrong, and that makes his work really treacherous to navigate, in my opinion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=195222#post195222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm...Wikipedia's entry on Batgirl mentions that New 52 Babs was only in the chair for 3 years now, and she is a much younger character, in her early 20s who doesn't know as much (the main reason Gail Simone feels good about this approach); which does sound like Oracle has been retconned out of existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it mention her ever being Oracle?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=195222#post195222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DC's wiki, however, <u>does</u> still mention her being Oracle...I honestly don't know if she was Oracle now or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't trust DC's wiki. I went looking something up not too terribly long ago, and all the information seemed to be pre-Nu52.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=195222#post195222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regardless, at least part of my objection still stands.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T20:56:16-07:00","id":195230,"title":"","content":"Double Post. Edited by Darksider.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 07-12-2014, 12:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T21:28:34-07:00","id":195243,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Marvel and DC have been ripping each other off for ages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering &quot;The Problem&quot; opens with &quot;<span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">even though they share prominent creators and have influenced each other back and forth over the course of the last 50 years&quot;, I don't think he disagrees! </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=195227#post195227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's one of the things that bugs me about Chris Sims. He gets some stuff right and some stuff wrong, and that makes his work really treacherous to navigate, in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeh, I caught the Kirby on Jimmy Olson one, too. Even if I hadn't, I find that the responders at the bottom tend to catch these things, although his editor really should. Still, it encourages one not to take too much at face value...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does it mention her ever being Oracle? </div> </div> </div>Quite a bit; in fact, there's an extensive summary of the pros and cons of the debate about making her Batgirl again.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't trust DC's wiki. I went looking something up not too terribly long ago, and all the information seemed to be pre-Nu52. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, there is a funny &quot;non-linear&quot; quality to it; it looks like itcould really use better organization into the different &quot;eras&quot; of DCs history. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T21:36:46-07:00","id":195244,"title":"","content":"Sims doesn't get into it much in that article, but I think his comments around the end, about how &quot;grown up and mature&quot; DC wants to appear is really apparent in the movies they're making now. This desire has been passed on to Warner Bros, which seems to be what led one of their presidents to remark how a Green Lantern sequel would have to be &quot;darker and edgier&quot;...<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, the Dark Knight movies were such a success, that Warners' doesn't seem to realize that what goes for the DK does not automatically work for ALL their superheroes! Whether you call it trying to be like Marvel, or just trying to be &quot;dark and mature&quot;, that approach just does not fit those characters. <br /> <br /> Ironically, Marvel is, if anything, embracing the DC approach: Their movies are so successful now, I believe, because they are NOT dark and grim, but openly fun and (relatively) light-hearted! The Avengers, in tone, felt almost like a JLA story (notice how colorful the costumes were)! If DC/Warners really wants to compete, they should get back to their own basics...<br /> <br /> Of course, they'd probably misinterpret that, and go full-on Camp comedy or something...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Ugh, it's so frustrating, because it's SO easy for Warners to get these characters RIGHT, and yet they insist on driving them off a cliff instead...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T06:45:46-07:00","id":195467,"title":"","content":"The &quot;grown up and mature&quot; thing I believe was a comment about how Marvel tended to take a less kiddie view in comic books and grounded things in more emotional adult themes. When FF first came out the Thing had a huge chip on his shoulder and spent years dealing with his appearance, and the stories were never quite wrapped up so neatly at the end of every issue. And then there was the infighting between him and the Human Torch showing that the &quot;family&quot; was a bit dysfunctional at times. Such things didn't exist in DC in the 60s where most issues (I believe) where most issues ended in friendly laughter or a wink to the reader.<br /> And then there was the &quot;power&quot; problem. Marvel gave limitations as were seen in the strength category, which would later be referred to in the 80s as &quot;Class 100&quot; for those that can routinely bench press over 100 tons. (Marvel would undo that later it seems) But what were the limits in DC back then? The readership that DC aimed for were pretty much children, where as Marvel was shooting for an older demographic, one that can relate to heroes with personal problems, self-doubt and had their own...all too human failings.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T12:02:21-07:00","id":195644,"title":"","content":"That whole &quot;class&quot; system Marvel used was lifted from the old TSR Marvel Superheroes RPG. I remember being kind of excited about it when it came out but then disappointed it wasn't as complex as Mayfair's DC game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T12:34:41-07:00","id":195660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=195644#post195644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That whole &quot;class&quot; system Marvel used was lifted from the old TSR Marvel Superheroes RPG.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. I though Mark Gruenwald had come up with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T13:58:10-07:00","id":195730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=195467#post195467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;grown up and mature&quot; thing I believe was a comment about how Marvel tended to take a less kiddie view in comic books and grounded things in more emotional adult themes. When FF first came out the Thing had a huge chip on his shoulder and spent years dealing with his appearance, and the stories were never quite wrapped up so neatly at the end of every issue. And then there was the infighting between him and the Human Torch showing that the &quot;family&quot; was a bit dysfunctional at times. Such things didn't exist in DC in the 60s</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, but no.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.comics.pop-cult.com/A-G/images/DOOMP092.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Doom Patrol has pretty much everything the Fantastic Four had during it's initial run. Made in 1963. 2 Years after Fantastic Four was created.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, I wouldn't call DP a Ripoff of FF, but there are some pretty bizarre similarities. Specifically the fact that Cliff and Larry are almost always fighting, forcing Rita to make them stop.<br /> <br /> I'm actually amazed Sims didn't talk about Doom Patrol, because it's got the human failings, the foibles, the hard limits and LOTS of the self doubt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T01:28:48-07:00","id":198693,"title":"","content":"Rather than reintroduce Stephanie Brown they decided to go and make Batgirl into a hipster rather than oracle. Fuck DC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T07:47:18-07:00","id":198941,"title":"","content":"So.... no discussion about Thor being a title and/or the New Thor yet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T10:00:03-07:00","id":199070,"title":"","content":"I don't follow the book, so I have little to say except that I'm of mixed feelings on the new Thor being an original character. On the one hand, go ahead and infuse new blood into the world; on the other, Thor is the only superhero in the Marvel universe I know whose powers come with a minimum worthiness requirement, so it seems like a tacit condemnation of every existing female character that they had to make a new one to pick up the hammer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T10:05:47-07:00","id":199087,"title":"","content":"Odin-son...Odin-daughter...LOL","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T10:28:58-07:00","id":199099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=199070#post199070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't follow the book, so I have little to say except that I'm of mixed feelings on the new Thor being an original character. On the one hand, go ahead and infuse new blood into the world; on the other, Thor is the only superhero in the Marvel universe I know whose powers come with a minimum worthiness requirement, so it seems like a tacit condemnation of every existing female character that they had to make a new one to pick up the hammer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was it a condemnation of every male character when they had to make Eric Masterson the last time this happened?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href