d of the half mask-helm.</div> </div> </div> </div>See I was going to be a snide asshole but this post says what I wanted to say without being a dick. So. Yeah. This is basically why I don't like She-Thor's armor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>A Green Sun Destrier</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/77-kongurous","name":"kongurous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar77_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"417"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T03:37:41-07:00","id":201940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=201078#post201078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suppose you hate Harley Quinn, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>She got put in as an independent character. She didn't ALTER a character by her creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T19:45:59-07:00","id":203395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=201940#post201940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> She got put in as an independent character. She didn't ALTER a character by her creation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, except for *the Joker*...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> There's also the Batcave. IIRC, it first appeared in the original Batman movie serial that came out only a couple years after Batman himself. The reason why it was a cave? Because the studio had a cave set lying around and didn't want to build a new set for Batman's lab equipment!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":681,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","user":"Hand-of-Omega","date":". 07-20-2014, 10:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T19:56:15-07:00","id":203399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=199129#post199129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They reintroduced Stephanie Brown back in April.</div> </div> </div> </div>I heard that they (re?)introduced Carrie Kelley, the first female Robin from The Dark Knight Returns, building up fan anticipation that she may become the new Robin in official continuity...but then they introduced her as a little girl. True?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T20:06:46-07:00","id":203404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=195730#post195730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Doom Patrol has pretty much everything the Fantastic Four had during it's initial run. Made in 1963. 2 Years after Fantastic Four was created.<br /> <br /> Now, I wouldn't call DP a Ripoff of FF, but there are some pretty bizarre similarities. Specifically the fact that Cliff and Larry are almost always fighting, forcing Rita to make them stop.<br /> <br /> I'm actually amazed Sims didn't talk about Doom Patrol, because it's got the human failings, the foibles, the hard limits and LOTS of the self doubt.</div> </div> </div> </div>There was so much info there, I guess he had to leave some things out. <a href=\"http://comicsalliance.com/the-most-insane-moments-of-doom-patrol/\" target=\"_blank\">He has gone into the DP before, however.</a>. But I think he might argue that the truest attempt by DC to take on the Marvel style directly was <a href=\"http://comicsalliance.com/ask-chris-24-strange-sports-stories-and-celebrity-comics/\" target=\"_blank\">Metamorpho!</a><br /> <br /> Incidentally, I still think there's a killer cartoon series waiting to be made from the Doom Patrol! Guess I'll have to be satisfied with their appearances in Teen Titans and Batman TBATB...and keep my fingers crossed for a Metal Men show!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T20:11:27-07:00","id":203407,"title":"","content":"Finally saw Batgirls' new costume, or at least, a lot of fan renderings of it. There's elements I like and ones I don't. Is it terribly sexist of me to say that I see nothing wrong with a top that shows off the female form? It's not like her previous costume had a hole showing off her cleavage or anything (*coughPowerGirlcough*)!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Ah well, maybe our &quot;progressives&quot; will create a future world where all women are safely covered up so that no one looks at them as sex objects...and then wonder how their values somehow became identical to those of fundamentalist religions who want to cover women up for similar reasons.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T21:26:37-07:00","id":203475,"title":"","content":"Never mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":271,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","user":"JimB","date":". 07-21-2014, 12:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T22:30:43-07:00","id":203523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=203407#post203407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally saw Batgirls' new costume, or at least, a lot of fan renderings of it. There's elements I like and ones I don't. Is it terribly sexist of me to say that I see nothing wrong with a top that shows off the female form? It's not like her previous costume had a hole showing off her cleavage or anything (*coughPowerGirlcough*)!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Ah well, maybe our &quot;progressives&quot; will create a future world where all women are safely covered up so that no one looks at them as sex objects...and then wonder how their values somehow became identical to those of fundamentalist religions who want to cover women up for similar reasons.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>One of the reasons why I'm confused by Danel's opposition to normal clothes with superheroes is that, while I get the appeal of mythologizing the characters in every way, I like bridging the fantastic with the mundane and with characters doing things that make sense to me why still being big and grand.<br /> <br /> As such(even though I don't read American comics) I hope that when Batgirl isn't being Batgirl, she lives it up, embraces whatever clothing makes sense for her as a character outside of the costume. I'd be pleased if that resulted in an empowerment of femininty-let her rock the clothing that shows the female form off! But as Batgirl? I like the new design because it makes sense to me-it loosely resembles civilian casual armor(seriously, I can buy that coat and have a low grade of bullet proofing) that would be comfortable for doing the sort of movement she would have to while also protecting her.<br /> <br /> I don't think we're building to a puritanical state with progressivism here. We are building characters who are both relatable and epic, people who bridge the grand mythologies of DC to the reader's who enjoy them.<br /> <br /> Or in other words, I think it rocks, and I don't think it's for any particular agenda.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T23:49:33-07:00","id":203581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=203523#post203523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> resembles <b>civilian casual armor</b>(seriously, I can buy that coat and have a low grade of bullet proofing) that would be comfortable for doing the sort of movement she would have to while also protecting her.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the problems for me is, why would she use civilian casual armor for more than, like, a week (she got this new costume because all her other ones were destroyed in a fire or something like that) when she easily can get access to the superior stuff (effectively sci-fi fabrics or even high-tech armor) she wore before? Unless New52 Bruce Wayne is such a jerk that he wouldn't help her out, I guess.<br /> <br /> Besides, a leather jacket is not really confortable to spend hours in, swinging from gargoyles, jumping around in rooftops, doing acrobatics and fighting criminals.<br /> <br /> Also, as a clarification in case it seems otherwise, I have no problem with superheroes wearing normal clothing in normal situations or showing normal situations for the heroes to be in as part of the story (actually, a few of my favorite stories have a lot of mundane side of the hero's life in it). I don't like normal clothing when they are &quot;on the job&quot; only.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T23:53:55-07:00","id":203582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=203581#post203581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the problems for me is, why would she use civilian casual armor for more than, like, a week (she got this new costume because all her other ones were destroyed in a fire or something like that) when she easily can get access to the superior stuff (effectively sci-fi fabrics or even high-tech armor) she wore before? Unless New52 Bruce Wayne is such a jerk that he wouldn't help her out, I guess.<br /> <br /> Besides, a leather jacket is not really confortable to spend hours in, swinging from gargoyles, jumping around in rooftops, doing acrobatics and fighting criminals.<br /> <br /> Also, as a clarification in case it seems otherwise, I have no problem with superheroes wearing normal clothing in normal situations or showing normal situations for the heroes to be in as part of the story (actually, a few of my favorite stories have a lot of mundane side of the hero's life in it). I don't like normal clothing when they are &quot;on the job&quot; only.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a comic book-I gotta let some things slide, otherwise it's not a union between the fantastic and the realistic now, is it?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Although, again it must be stated that I just don't read many Western comics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T22:49:51-07:00","id":214423,"title":"","content":"Spoiler for Uncanny X-Men 24: <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Xavier is married to Mystique </span><br /> <br /> So Wolverine once again have sex with another man wife ( the wife of his boss, the only man who mattered, no less), and Iceman have sex with his surrogate father's wife.<br /> <br /> I can't even imagine the look on Nightcrawler's face.<br /> <br /> Also bonus point for Beast and Wolverine acting like bitter-Ex toward Cyclops.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T04:18:44-07:00","id":214529,"title":"","content":"You really shouldn't read X-men the writers just don't care or have the ability to write them well. Well for the most part. X-factor is really done well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T06:07:34-07:00","id":214585,"title":"","content":"Nah, I mostly want to watch the anti-Cyclops fan explode into a fountain of vitriol whenever a new Uncanny issue come out, I just started to collect a few recent issues since they are illustrated by the amazing Kris Anka.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T06:52:18-07:00","id":214614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=214585#post214585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah, I mostly want to watch the anti-Cyclops fan explode into a fountain of vitriol whenever a new Uncanny issue come out, I just started to collect a few recent issues since they are illustrated by the amazing Kris Anka.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. So basically 90% of people who read X-men (Cyclops has always been a rather lame and boring character Bendis trying to prop him up as something more doesn't change that). Really if you want to read a really good time for X-men go back to 2004-2011. Actually that's around when cosmic marvel was really really good. However, in the early 00's X-men started being good. This was after Chuck Austin, honestly probably one of the worst X-men writers, left the line. Then House of M happened. Which was a really shitty event. However, after that good writers tried to pick up the pace. When Endangered species ended and Utopia began it began to down spiral to what it is now. Cyclops or no. Bendis and Aaron can barely do their own Genres well and this is far from their genre as you could imagine. I'm kind of hoping Kyle and Yost can fix that but they do have terrible tendencies for deaths for shock value they also aren't really doing anything more than Amazing X-men.<br /> <br /> Also, bringing back the O5 instead of using a few of their DOZENS of Teen Superheroes is infuriating. As is proping up Quentin Quire over any of the New X-men. Which if you had to read only one Teen Superhero Comic book X-men Academy/New X-men probably the best one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 07-31-2014, 09:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T07:05:30-07:00","id":214617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=214529#post214529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You really shouldn't read X-men the writers just don't care or have the ability to write them well. Well for the most part. X-factor is really done well.</div> </div> </div> </div>its just not the same since Ellis left Uncanny.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T07:09:58-07:00","id":214619,"title":"","content":"This thread convinces me that getting out of comic-books when I did in the mid 90s saved whatever was left of my soul.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T07:34:40-07:00","id":214648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=214619#post214619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This thread convinces me that getting out of comic-books when I did in the mid 90s saved whatever was left of my soul.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly, that does seem to be the case. My attempts at reentering the field have proven disappointing. <b>Civil War</b> was just a mess. <b>Planet Hulk</b> was interesting, but not terribly satisfying. <b>World War Hulk</b> was a natural and unforced extension of that, and the only satisfying part was The Hulk beating on those who did that to him and should have been shown before to NOT be more powerful than The Hulk....because we all know, <b>NOBODY IS STRONGER THAN HULK!!</b> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Beyond that, yeah, nothing has been really worth the trouble.<br /> <br /> I was looking at one of the newer collections of Aquaman (2011-forward) because, <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/HeartIsAnAwesomePower\" target=\"_blank\">yes, I am one of those weirdos who believes that he's not as lame as they make him out to be</a>, but I just don't know if it's worth the effort.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T08:07:27-07:00","id":214680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=214648#post214648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sadly, that does seem to be the case. My attempts at reentering the field have proven disappointing. <b>Civil War</b> was just a mess. <b>Planet Hulk</b> was interesting, but not terribly satisfying. <b>World War Hulk</b> was a natural and unforced extension of that, and the only satisfying part was The Hulk beating on those who did that to him and should have been shown before to NOT be more powerful than The Hulk....because we all know, <b>NOBODY IS STRONGER THAN HULK!!</b> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Beyond that, yeah, nothing has been really worth the trouble.<br /> <br /> I was looking at one of the newer collections of Aquaman (2011-forward) because, <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/HeartIsAnAwesomePower\" target=\"_blank\">yes, I am one of those weirdos who believes that he's not as lame as they make him out to be</a>, but I just don't know if it's worth the effort.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> gotta go to indies man. much better stuff under publishers like Avatar Press. They typically aren't superheroes (unless you are talking about something like No Hero or some of the few other titles on avatar with a superhero facade) but you end up with stuff like Doktor Sleepless, Gravel, Crossed, Caligula, Neonomicon No Hero, Black Summer Freak Angels, Supergod.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","user":"cerealkiller","date":". 07-31-2014, 11:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T09:50:29-07:00","id":214753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cerealkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=214680#post214680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">gotta go to indies man. much better stuff under publishers like Avatar Press. They typically aren't superheroes (unless you are talking about something like No Hero or some of the few other titles on avatar with a superhero facade) but you end up with stuff like Doktor Sleepless, Gravel, Crossed, Caligula, Neonomicon No Hero, Black Summer Freak Angels, Supergod.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not so much about reading about <i>just </i>superheroes. These are the guys who were all over the TV when I was growing up. SuperFriends, Spider-Man &amp; his Amazing Friends, Incredible Hulk with Bill Bixby.....I know it's not the same as when I was under 10 years old, and it's never going to be, but I miss being able to read about these characters as they have (supposedly) matured somewhat with me. And then I read this stuff and I see it's still so much caught in the 90s crap of spectacle over substance that I couldn't get into anymore when I was in my early 20s.<br /> <br /> And I know that a lot of comics, especially superhero ones, are supposed to be that. They're over-the-top spectacles and mythologies and fantasies. But, lately, it seems they're falling rather short of that &quot;modern mythologies&quot; mantle that has been placed upon them. Maybe it's because I'm too world-weary to <i>need </i>the lessons they're hammering home. Maybe it <i>is </i>substandard writing. Maybe it's because the same bunch of goobers that were in the comic book stores with me are the putzes who are in charge now and writing the same crap they grew up with. I don't know.<br /> <br /> What I do know is that I miss the Spider-Man who was married and happy with MJ and didn't hang out with the Avengers and didn't brood over the fake parents who came back and tortured him or the fake Aunt May who died or the real Norman Osborn who didn't. I miss the Batman who responds to &quot;Who are you?&quot; with a simple and scary &quot;I'm Batman.&quot; and do not care for the one who says, &quot;I'm the goddamned Batman!&quot;. I miss Hulk Speak and HULK SMASH!. I miss Wolverine being a failed samurai who keeps trying and doesn't know jack about his past. I miss Green Arrow being a hot-headed malcontent and his buddy Green Lantern having to come save his ass regularly.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sorry, got off on a rant there. tl;dr......it's not the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T16:01:03-07:00","id":215263,"title":"","content":"Just because....<img src=\"http://img1.wikia.nocookie.net/__cb20080728001628/marveldatabase/images/thumb/c/c8/Avengers_Vol_1_164.jpg/300px-Avengers_Vol_1_164.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr c