class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T08:41:39-07:00","id":238222,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I don't have much respect for the artist to begin with simply because I don't know his work, but I don't think I'll ever be able to take him seriously after using the Gaza Defense (or more specifically, the variant Ferguson Gamble) to dismiss complaints about his art.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T09:27:47-07:00","id":238279,"title":"","content":"To a certain extent, this is Manara being Manara. Milo's work is very sensual, whoever hired such a well-known artist with those proclivities to do the cover of a woman who takes &quot;spider poses&quot; should have known what to expect. So, I get myself wondering: was this editorial incompetence at holding the artist in check, or was this done on purpose for the controversy and publicity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T12:24:56-07:00","id":238421,"title":"","content":"Saw that Spider-Woman cover the other day.... ::shakes head::<br /> <br /> <br /> So, whats this I hear about Superman becoming Doomsday or some such in the New 52?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T13:49:02-07:00","id":239541,"title":"","content":"Well, there's Superdoom, which is an Alternate Reality of Superman who was twisted to resemble a number of his infamous bad guys such as Doomsday and the Anti-Monitor. He goes around killing other Universes Supermen in a clear allegory to DC's treatment of competing comic companies back in the days of yore.<br /> <br /> <br /> Or you might be talking about to this particular caper:<img src=\"http://retconpunchdotcom.files.wordpress.com/2014/06/super-doom-gonna-punch-him-a-red-lantern.jpg?w=593&amp;h=376\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Wherein Superman is infected with a virus that transmogrifies him into a Superman/Doomsday hybrid (ala All Star Superman?). Kind of like those Silver Age Jimmy Olsen stories, but with Doomsday.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T15:25:49-07:00","id":239614,"title":"","content":"Ah. I just had someone telling me about it work and I wasn't sure what the deal is.<br /> <br /> In either case, weird. Thanks for the info though, I was wondering what was up. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I haven't really kept with much of the new DC stuff. They canceled the few books I was following, so I kind of tuned out...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T06:55:50-07:00","id":240239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=238221#post238221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spider-Woman #1 just feature a bikini witch doppelganger !<br /> <br /> And we get the same responds across comic board:<ul><li>I don't see what the problem is, she look HOT !</li> <li>There are more important stuffs to worry about like world hunger !</li> <li>You hate the woman body !</li> <li>There are worse cover out there, stop complaining !</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"http://www.comicbookresources.com/imgsrv/imglib/0/0/1/SPIDERWOMAN001Manara-a3461-ad504.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, in all fairness, they've probably had Spider-MAN in a &quot;butt in the air&quot; pose about 1,000 times by now. Perhaps not drawn with so much attention devoted to said butt, but that's probably more because they haven't had as many artists who like men's butts over women's butts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T07:27:20-07:00","id":240257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=240239#post240239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, in all fairness, they've probably had Spider-MAN in a &quot;butt in the air&quot; pose about 1,000 times by now.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was Todd McFarlane's entire career back in the nineties. Of course, the rebuttal* to this argument is the difference between idealization and objectification, but that argument scares me because I'm pretty sure it only loses friends, so I'm just going to bow out of this now.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T08:09:04-07:00","id":240303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=240257#post240257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was Todd McFarlane's entire career back in the nineties. Of course, the rebuttal* to this argument is the difference between idealization and objectification, but that argument scares me because I'm pretty sure it only loses friends, so I'm just going to bow out of this now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spiderman is sort of an odd duck comic that way, that having been said I've got more dislike over the fact that it's not an outfit so much as red body paint than the pose itself. <br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, yes it's an image/pose built primarily around sex appeal. It's also an alternate cover, so they're not trying to win new audience with it, they're trying to appeal to the obsessive collector of comics which the last I checked, still a primarily heterosexual male corner of their existing market. So they're targeting sex at the people that it is likely to appeal to, while at the same time generating a lot of press about it, thus working to ensure that sales of that alternate cover are high.<br /> <br /> <br /> And this is also where a bit of an issue crops up. Anything that is sold is depending on word getting out. Hell, until the cover thing happened I didn't even know they were doing a spider-woman thing. More press talking about something, even in a negative light, is going to result in more people buying it. This is the nature of advertising. So while there's something to be said for voting with your dollars and not supporting such products, with so much talk about the cover you're going to get far more people aware and buying the spider-woman comics (maybe not that specific variant but in general) than they would have otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T12:50:43-07:00","id":240519,"title":"","content":"Honestly in most popular comics you have to expect the art try an appeal as an object. Especially in a momentous volume(#1/Anniversary/Special Event/etc). Whether that be sex appeal or testosterone. There are generally no words so it has to appeal or catch the eye in some way through the art alone. What objectifies to me(women or men) in comics is what the writer has coming out of the speech or thought bubbles.<br /> <br /> I will that that back a little. She could be holding the magnum opus of intellectual conversations with someone, but if the artist has her doing it in nothing but bondage poses I would have to consider that objectification.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T13:40:17-07:00","id":240661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorwen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=240519#post240519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly in most popular comics you have to expect the art try an appeal as an object.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get what you're saying, but if you'll forgive me for taking your words literally for the sake of making a point: no, I don't. I don't have to expect that. I don't have to expect a weird, two-dimensional woman with no upper left arm presenting her ass like an open bun to lay a hotdog in, because as you say, it doesn't have words, but it <i>may as well</i> have a voice balloon reading, &quot;Hey guys! You can spank to this!&quot; No thank you, Marvel, and I'm disappointed that after books like <b>Ms. Marvel</b> and <b>Captain Marvel</b>, you haven't yet learned that I don't need or want those things in a book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T14:34:47-07:00","id":240751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=240661#post240661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get what you're saying, but if you'll forgive me for taking your words literally for the sake of making a point: no, I don't. I don't have to expect that. I don't have to expect a weird, two-dimensional woman with no upper left arm presenting her ass like an open bun to lay a hotdog in, because as you say, it doesn't have words, but it <i>may as well</i> have a voice balloon reading, &quot;Hey guys! You can spank to this!&quot; No thank you, Marvel, and I'm disappointed that after books like <b>Ms. Marvel</b> and <b>Captain Marvel</b>, you haven't yet learned that I don't need or want those things in a book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then let me ask this. What kind of non-sexual and wordless cover would you want to see that would apply to specifically to Spider-Woman's character? One that would try to catch the widest range of buyers? Or am I missing something and the aritst doesn't generally draw butts to appeal in that manner?<br /> <br /> Looking at 2014 #1 covers for the other two they seem just as much as they can be. Ms. Marvel is a teen now so they have to be careful there because there are different levels involved. Short of a camel toe I can't see how Captain Marvel could be more sexual and have a pose relevant to the character. I mean we are given a crotch angle view.<br /> <br /> For my part I agree I don't like heart shaped butts that look quite that open invitation, but I think that is more a artistic style choice than I percieve that no woman's butt would look that open. I've heard some comic artists still use models on poses so it is quite possible they had someone pose and came out with that. Honestly I would totally expect to see a lot of poses of Spider-Woman doggy style or crotch shots because she crawls and flies. It isn't like they don't do that for any of the male characters.<br /> <br /> Though I can't deny they could have been going for just a piece of meat so-to-speak as anything else. What would mean it to me is if we read it and she was as blatantly objectified as the New 52 Starfire was when that started. I still feel for a lot of fans on that one. I wouldn't be able to disagree if they had done Captain Marvel in such poses(cover or throughout the comic).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T14:48:39-07:00","id":240766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorwen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=240751#post240751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What kind of non-sexual and wordless cover would you want to see that would apply to specifically to Spider-Woman's character?</div> </div> </div> </div>At the risk of sounding like I'm trying to weasel here, I don't know. A good cover isn't just trying to sell a character, it's trying to sell a story arc, and I have no idea what this story will be about. Is it a continuation of the HYDRA/SHIELD double agent thing from a few years ago? Is it a new story? Or is it just Spider-Woman on a roof, ready to take it doggy-style from Superman?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorwen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=240751#post240751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Short of a camel toe I can't see how Captain Marvel could be more sexual and have a pose relevant to the character. I mean we are given a crotch angle view.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh, would you mind linking the image you're talking about? One of us is not thinking of the same cover the other one is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorwen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=240751#post240751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is quite possible they had someone pose and came out with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>If so, Milo Manara is a bad artist. The perspective is all fucked up, and parts of her body are just gone. <a href=\"http://www.themarysue.com/controversial-spider-woman-covers-redrawn/2/\" target=\"_blank\">Here is a link</a> to a story explaining what is wrong with the anatomy and/or perspective, if you're curious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/a