t I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":787,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","user":"Sorwen","date":". 08-26-2014, 10:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T09:07:15-07:00","id":241399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=240939#post240939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm told that the sexualization of female characters didn't really start until some time in the eighties.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and No. Early Wonder Woman comics were basically bondage porn, but until the art fidelity started advancing, there was little point. Early Superheroes wore their underwear on the outside because it was the easiest way to give their lower torso shape with the image quality they had at the time. Nowadays, it's not needed and therefore done less.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T10:47:23-07:00","id":241475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorwen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=241310#post241310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is the one I've seen. Maybe an alt?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that one. I don't think it's an alt; I think it's from a year or two ago. Dunno if you knew this, but Marvel has been rebooting all their series every time a given story arc concludes.<br /> <br /> As to the picture itself, eh, I can see your point but I'd argue a different interpretation. Yeah, the perspective lines seem to be at crotch level, but I think the intention is to make the reader feel like Captain Marvel towers over him, like he's looking up to her. And yeah, her legs are spread, but that's about showing a wide, firm, steady stance, not getting a look at her pussy; and I would guess her crotch is so black because the human eye tends to skip over black to look for easier colors to penetrate. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T12:33:39-07:00","id":241595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=241475#post241475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, that one. I don't think it's an alt; I think it's from a year or two ago. Dunno if you knew this, but Marvel has been rebooting all their series every time a given story arc concludes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah! Ok. It was the one people were showing on some other boards when talk about Ms/Captain Marvel. I've always been indifferent one way or another to her comics though I do like her as a character. I just can't bring myself to read current Marvel (or DC) comics. Right now to me they signify all that is wrong<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As to the picture itself, eh, I can see your point but I'd argue a different interpretation. Yeah, the perspective lines seem to be at crotch level, but I think the intention is to make the reader feel like Captain Marvel towers over him, like he's looking up to her. And yeah, her legs are spread, but that's about showing a wide, firm, steady stance, not getting a look at her pussy; and I would guess her crotch is so black because the human eye tends to skip over black to look for easier colors to penetrate. </div> </div> </div>You maybe totally right, but to me it isn't any different in intent. It was a way to draw her sexy in a way that was acceptable for Captain Marvel. It is however much better drawn. Though I can't figure out how that passed when she is yellow.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T13:08:28-07:00","id":241633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorwen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=241595#post241595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah! Okay. It was the one people were showing on some other boards when talk about Ms/Captain Marvel. I've always been indifferent one way or another to her comics though I do like her as a character. I just can't bring myself to read current Marvel (or DC) comics. Right now to me they signify all that is wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the sake of clarity, I should admit I phrased my description a bit sloppily. I don't mean that each and every comic book series gets rebooted simultaneously, like DC's Nu52; I mean when a given book's arc ends, so does the book. For instance, last year Wolverine got a new series in which he lost his healing factor. When that story ended, the book ended, and a new book with the same title (and same writer, and possibly the same artist but don't quote me on that one) got a #1 issue in which he's running around in Iron Man armor with guns and a team of mercenaries, murdering dudes for no adequately explained reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T13:16:30-07:00","id":241641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=241633#post241633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the sake of clarity, I should admit I phrased my description a bit sloppily. I don't mean that each and every comic book series gets rebooted simultaneously, like DC's Nu52; I mean when a given book's arc ends, so does the book. For instance, last year Wolverine got a new series in which he lost his healing factor. When that story ended, the book ended, and a new book with the same title (and same writer, and possibly the same artist but don't quote me on that one) got a #1 issue in which he's running around in Iron Man armor with guns and a team of mercenaries, murdering dudes for no adequately explained reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok. Some how that seems even more bizarre to me than just resetting every time. That's even more confusing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T01:56:54-07:00","id":243784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=240661#post240661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get what you're saying, but if you'll forgive me for taking your words literally for the sake of making a point: no, I don't. I don't have to expect that. I don't have to expect a weird, two-dimensional woman with no upper left arm presenting her ass like an open bun to lay a hotdog in, because as you say, it doesn't have words, but it <i>may as well</i> have a voice balloon reading, &quot;Hey guys! You can spank to this!&quot; No thank you, Marvel, and I'm disappointed that after books like <b>Ms. Marvel</b> and <b>Captain Marvel</b>, you haven't yet learned that I don't need or want those things in a book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really. really. I'm a gay dude. I like looking at hot bods. I'm not going to be a hypocrite about this. I don't get why people are up in arms about this. Look at teen wolf look at supernatural. Have you seen those shows they objectify men for the gratification of women. No one judges them because it's something women like. Look at soap operas and Arrow as well. They have huge Female viewratings because the guys in there are hot and they interact with other guys. Why is it okay when it's guys getting objectified but not women. This is a double standard.<br /> <br /> (Editing my overly hostile response a bit) I don't like Captain Marvel. Frankly I find that it's characters are as poor as it's plot. I can understand that on some level it appeals to you but I don't think that should be treated as a standard. Ms. Marvel is a little better but the people really aren't characters yet. There's also an annoying level of memes being used to be more &quot;hip&quot;. What I'm trying to say is that both can exist. You really shouldn't condemn something without reading it. I think the book is going to be trash because of who's writing it, his trackrecord, and his previous books but I don't think it's cover says everything about it. I don't think you should look at it and go this is trash because that's what you're doing right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 08-29-2014, 05:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T04:34:45-07:00","id":243819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=243784#post243784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really. Really. I'm a gay dude. I like looking at hot bods. I'm not going to be a hypocrite about this. I don't get why people are up in arms about this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not understand how your sexual orientation is relevant to this discussion. Does it confer upon you some kind of authority we straight men lack?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=243784#post243784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look at <b>Teen Wolf</b>; look at <b>Supernatural</b>. Have you seen those shows? They objectify men for the gratification of women.</div> </div> </div> </div>The last two times I had discussions about this in this community, I lost friends. A lot of friends. People I like and respect were driven away from the community forever because they couldn't abide to be part of a group that differs from their own opinion on what constitutes sexism. I am not getting into that again, but I will let you know that I am not at all impressed by your attempt to declare I may not complain about one, specific comic book in a thread about comic books unless I also complain in a thread for comic books about completely unrelated televisions programs I haven't even seen (except for <b>Supernatural</b>, which I've watched pretty thoroughly and cannot think of any examples of the objectification you speak of).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=243784#post243784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like Captain Marvel.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know you don't. You are posting in this thread about her (or possibly it; I can't tell if you're talking about the character or the book), and the only reason you ever post about anything in this thread is because you hate it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=243784#post243784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You really shouldn't condemn something without reading it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not have to read a book to have an opinion about its cover.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=243784#post243784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the book is going to be trash because of who's writing it, his trackrecord, and his previous books but I don't think its cover says everything about it. I don't think you should look at it and go this is trash because that's what you're doing right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Epimetheus, please look more closely at the two sentences I just quoted, because the first one tells me I'm wrong to describe the book as trash (which I haven't done, but never mind) without reading it, and in the very next sentence, <i>you call the book trash without reading it</i>. I will thank you to get your own fucking house in order before you tell me how to handle my affairs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":271,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","user":"JimB","date":". 08-29-2014, 07:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T04:46:25-07:00","id":243821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=243819#post243819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Epimetheus, please look more closely at the two sentences I just quoted, because the first one tells me I'm wrong to describe the book as trash (which I haven't done, but never mind) without reading it, and in the very next sentence, <i>you call the book trash without reading it</i>. I will thank you to get your own fucking house in order before you tell me how to handle my affairs.</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to be decrying the book for it's cover without any other previous assumptions. I on the other hand am familiar with hopeless work in the form of his current book Avengers underground and the previous title avengers arena. I suppose we'll have difference of opinions but I don't see the point of having a trivial issue when there are bigger issues. Interior arts going to be worse because it's by Greg &quot; Literally traces from Porn&quot; Land.<br /> <br /> I'm just too lazy to quote from here on out but the supernatural just has a lot of nods to the fanbase which is powered by slash fanfiction. My reference to sexual orientation is just because a few times I've had this conversation people have called me a cis, straight white male. It's rather an annoying because I'm hispanic and gay and people try to shut my opinion because X, Y, Z mannerisms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 08-29-2014, 07:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T04:53:52-07:00","id":243827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=243821#post243821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose we'll have difference of opinions but I don't see the point of having a trivial issue when there are bigger issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whatever, dude. I don't have it in me to keep doing this with you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":271,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","user":"JimB","date":". 08-29-2014, 07:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271