id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T06:06:21-07:00","id":258938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=258915#post258915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A while back II had an idea about doing Superman as a period piece set in the 30's or 40's and doing it in Black &amp; White. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>And there we could see the old boy scout theme fitting right in, along with the tag, Truth, justice and the American Way\u2122<br /> <br /> Except the one problem which I'm sure you already saw; WWII, and all that entails. There would have to be a Nazi supervillain to keep him occupied throughout the war.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T06:56:16-07:00","id":258947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=258915#post258915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Loved that one!</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing I love most about it is that it shows Superman having a crisis of ideals and how he deals with it. It is handled 1000 times better than Man of Steel.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, All Star Superman was pretty good. Not sure it'd work for a live action movie, but it was still great. </div> </div> </div>I thought it was a good one, but too negative for me. Bittersweet isn't my thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A while back II had an idea about doing Superman as a period piece set in the 30's or 40's and doing it in Black &amp; White. :P </div> </div> </div>That would be cool. I think there was a Justice League movie that did that, but wasn't black and white and of course was more than Superman.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T11:33:03-07:00","id":259071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=258938#post258938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And there we could see the old boy scout theme fitting right in, along with the tag, Truth, justice and the American Way\u2122<br /> <br /> Except the one problem which I'm sure you already saw; WWII, and all that entails. There would have to be a Nazi supervillain to keep him occupied throughout the war.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, back during the forties, his tagline was &quot;Truth, tolerance, and justice.&quot; It wasn't until the fifties or sixties that it got changed to that one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorwen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=258947#post258947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought [<b>All-Star Superman</b>] was a good one, but too negative for me. Bittersweet isn't my thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you talking about the book or the movie? Because if you think the book is bittersweet, reread the final page of the chapter about the Chronovore.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T18:04:15-07:00","id":259399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=258938#post258938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And there we could see the old boy scout theme fitting right in, along with the tag, Truth, justice and the American Way\u2122<br /> <br /> Except the one problem which I'm sure you already saw; WWII, and all that entails. There would have to be a Nazi supervillain to keep him occupied throughout the war.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh man, that would be awesome. Yea, WWII might be a slight issue, but we could always draw some inspiration from the comics of the time.<br /> <br /> And I think we could get away with telling his origin in the first 10 or 15 minutes. No need to make the whole an origin story. Hell, everyone knows it already...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorwen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=258947#post258947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing I love most about it is that it shows Superman having a crisis of ideals and how he deals with it. It is handled 1000 times better than Man of Steel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally with you. I love how they handled it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorwen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=258947#post258947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought it was a good one, but too negative for me. Bittersweet isn't my thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was alittle...but just enough for me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorwen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=258947#post258947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be cool. I think there was a Justice League movie that did that, but wasn't black and white and of course was more than Superman.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, it was called Justice League New Frontier. Its pretty awesome too!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T14:07:40-07:00","id":260071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=259071#post259071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you talking about the book or the movie? Because if you think the book is bittersweet, reread the final page of the chapter about the Chronovore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Movie. When I watched the movie I didn't know the two were the same. I had skipped reading the book because I didn't know about it till after and heard about the ending. Though I didn't know about any difference in the last of it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T15:12:43-07:00","id":260131,"title":"","content":"The movie is...okay. It cuts about half the book's content (though to be fair, it is quite faithful to the material preserved), and the one about the Chronovore is absolutely essential.<br /> <br /> Also, <a href=\"http://spicy-tempura.tumblr.com/post/37623222068/superman-prevents-a-suicide-in-all-star\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> is a page from the book that didn't make it into the movie and that always makes me cry. Go read the book. Grant Morrison is a self-indulgent weirdo, but if there's one thing in this world he fucking nails, it's Superman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T11:38:43-07:00","id":260803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=260131#post260131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The movie is...okay. It cuts about half the book's content (though to be fair, it is quite faithful to the material preserved), and the one about the Chronovore is absolutely essential.<br /> <br /> Also, <a href=\"http://spicy-tempura.tumblr.com/post/37623222068/superman-prevents-a-suicide-in-all-star\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> is a page from the book that didn't make it into the movie and that always makes me cry. Go read the book. Grant Morrison is a self-indulgent weirdo, but if there's one thing in this world he fucking nails, it's Superman.</div> </div> </div> </div>GM is a great writer, but he has also written some of the stuff I hate the most in comics. It is hard for me not to cringe when I hear his name.<br /> <br /> Still I might check it out then.<br /> <br /> Edit: Cool read as well as the link from there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":787,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","user":"Sorwen","date":". 09-19-2014, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T00:30:44-07:00","id":291845,"title":"","content":"Oh my, Marvel is doing an anti-bullying campaign featuring Earth (i.e America) Mightiest Hero, excuse me, but from what I have seen aren't they the biggest bulliest in the Marvel universe ?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T09:14:45-07:00","id":292086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=291845#post291845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh my, Marvel is doing an anti-bullying campaign featuring Earth (i.e America) Mightiest Hero, excuse me, but from what I have seen aren't they the biggest bulliest in the Marvel universe ?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>They can be sometimes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> BTW, speaking of bullies, whats this rumbling I'm hearing about Marvel canceling Fantastic 4? I mean, I'm no fan of the book, but the rumor I'm hearing is because they're pissed about the upcoming movie or some such. Plus, I heard something about them not wanting to do any new X-Men characters, and might be on the verge of ending that too? Again, I'm no X-Men fan these days, but that sounds a little petty if true...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T09:47:25-07:00","id":292113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=292086#post292086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They can be sometimes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know what happen in their own book, but when they feature in other series it mostly involve being all high and mighty sticking their nose into other people business, saying &quot;you are under arrested for breaking the law/being a danger to everyone&quot; when you have the freaking Hulk and the Scarlet Witch as member is just............urrggh.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> BTW, speaking of bullies, whats this rumbling I'm hearing about Marvel canceling Fantastic 4? I mean, I'm no fan of the book, but the rumor I'm hearing is because they're pissed about the upcoming movie or some such. Plus, I heard something about them not wanting to do any new X-Men characters, and might be on the verge of ending that too? Again, I'm no X-Men fan these days, but that sounds a little petty if true... </div> </div> </div>In New Warriors one of the Inhuman flat out said that &quot;This is an Inhuman world now, mutant&quot;, the writer for the Inhuman even said that they want to made them to be more like the X-Men. And their anniversary cover don't have any of the X-Men or F4 but it does have the lovely Avenger and GotG, oh hey, the two franchise that Marvel has the right to.<br /> <br /> Sure look like petty revenge to me :'P<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T11:36:41-07:00","id":292260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=292086#post292086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rumor I'm hearing is because they're pissed about the upcoming movie or some such.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly. Marvel sold the movie rights to many of its properties when it was in bankruptcy, and the production studios used Marvel's weak position to leverage certain considerations. I don't know the exact benefits the studios granted themselves, but they include a piece of the profits of any product (I think non-comic products, so figurines, action figures, posters, shit like that) Marvel makes featuring the licensed characters, because the studios claim part of the characters' fame is based on the exposure granted by the movies. Marvel and Disney want to stop paying those fees and to get the movie rights back, so they are paring down appearances and even canceling titles whose characters are licensed to other movie studios in an attempt to try to reduce the studios' profit until it would no longer be worth it for them to keep paying to renew the licenses.<br /> <br /> I don't know why they aren't doing this to Spider-Man, except to guess that Marvel cannot get rid of their single most beloved and iconic character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T11:45:51-07:00","id":292272,"title":"","content":"I think it is because Sony/Disney has a better relationship than Fox/Disney ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T12:12:25-07:00","id":292306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=292113#post292113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know what happen in their own book, but when they feature in other series it mostly involve being all high and mighty sticking their nose into other people business, saying &quot;you are under arrested for breaking the law/being a danger to everyone&quot; when you have the freaking Hulk and the Scarlet Witch as member is just............urrggh.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In New Warriors one of the Inhuman flat out said that &quot;This is an Inhuman world now, mutant&quot;, the writer for the Inhuman even said that they want to made them to be more like the X-Men. And their anniversary cover don't have any of the X-Men or F4 but it does have the lovely Avenger and GotG, oh hey, the two franchise that Marvel has the right to.<br /> <br /> Sure look like petty revenge to me :'P<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Too bad inhumans trying to be X-men is even worse than X-men these days (Technically not quality wise on some of the books because bendis can't write anything that isn't spiderman for the life of him) like 30k for a mainstream title is pretty bad. That's actually close to cancellation. It's not going to work. Which I feel kind of bad about because X-men was one of my favorites but at the same time I feel like they need to get rid of every writer they currently have except the ones working on niche x-books and replace them. However, inhumans has been terribly obvious and I'm glad no ones really fallen for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T12:22:24-07:00","id":293118,"title":"","content":"<i>Batman: City of Crime</i> might be one of the best Batman stories I have ever read, though it is dark. It features impressive writing and narration, and is excellent at making Gotham City feel like a character of its own, terrible though that character may be. I recommend it to anyone who enjoys the darker Batman stories.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> From the airport, her gleaming towers offer the promise of excitement and possibility. They flock to her. Six million and growing. They don\u2019t see her like this. No one sees her like this until it\u2019s too late. Until they have been stabbed, beaten, or raped. Until their hopes and dreams have been ground to dust, their spirits broken, and their thoughts turn black. Until they are hopelessly trapped in the snarled recesses of their own minds\u2014Just one more layer of cankered rot that feeds this great Metropolis known as Gotham city. City of fear. City of crime.<br /> <br /> The madwoman\u2019s eyes gleam and spin. She smiles a toothless smile. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T14:14:38-07:00","id":296164,"title":"","content":"Hey, Omicron, would you recommend <i>Elric: the Ruby Throne</i>? I know you mentioned it back before it was translated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T13:12:42-07:00","id":297430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=296164#post296164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, Omicron, would you recommend <i>Elric: the Ruby Throne</i>? I know you mentioned it back before it was translated.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might just be a bit too excessive for my tastes - the rather sober 70s prose of the original books had left me with a picture of Elric's setting that was less flamboyant, more down to earth - but it's gorgeous and, yeah, I think pretty good. You're in for naked slaves and human sacrifices, but I think amping up the decadent and monumental atmosphere is a good bet when operating in a visual medium that can't convey as much through text and narrative, so...<br /> <br /> All in all, yeah, I'd definitely recommend it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T15:21:49-07:00","id":298500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=292113#post292113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In New Warriors one of the Inhuman flat out said that &quot;This is an Inhuman world now, mutant&quot;, the writer for the Inhuman even said that they want to made them to be more like the X-Men. And their anniversary cover don't have any of the X-Men or F4 but it does have the lovely Avenger and GotG, oh hey, the two franchise that Marvel has the right to.<br /> <br /> Sure look like petty revenge to me :'P<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=292260#post292260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not exactly. Marvel sold the movie rights to many of its properties when it was in bankruptcy, and the production studios used Marvel's weak position to leverage certain considerations. I don't know the exact benefits the studios granted themselves, but they include a piece of the profits of any product (I think non-comic products, so figurines, action figures, posters, shit like that) Marvel makes featuring the licensed characters, because the studios claim part of the characters' fame is based on the exposure granted by the movies. Marvel and Disney want to stop paying those fees and to get the movie rights back, so they are paring down appearances and even canceling titles whose characters are licensed to other movie studios in an attempt to try to reduce the studios' profit until it would no longer be worth it for them to keep paying to renew the licenses.<br /> <br /> I don't know why they aren't doing this to Spider-Man, except to guess that Marvel cannot get rid of their single most beloved and iconic character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah...thats all kind of sad really.<br /> <br /> It'd be nice of they could work a licensing deal for the movies...but alas..<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T22:07:01-08:00","id":304193,"title":"","content":"So an inverted Iron Man is a huge selfish douchebag.............Marvel really think that Tony is some kind of Asshole with a Heart Gold, aren't they ? Do they forget who started Civil War in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T22:16:39-08:00","id":304198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=304193#post304193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do they forget who started Civil War in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>They didn't quite forget, but they view it as him being the heroic person doing the right thing. Though it may be worth noting -he- forgot about the Civil War, since he didn't back up his memory.<br /> <br /> To be fair, realistically, the registration act makes sense. But, in the Marvel Universe? After 50+ years of heroes overcoming odds, mutants spotlighted fighting for their own rights and obscene levels of government corruption and so forth, it doesn't really fit. And the way they went about it with capekiller squads and Prison 42, turning kids into trained killers and creating mad clones of gods? I don't see how they'd think Iron Man would be seen as the 'good guy.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-06-2014, 01:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T06:52:47-08:00","id":304537,"title":"","content":"They have to do something since Iron Man was such a dick in the comics, but such a cool bad ass in the movies.<br /> <br /> I think those of us who read the comics first and movies second are all having a bit of trouble with them trying to convert him from Howard Hugh(es) Hefner into Robert Downey Jr.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T06:56:14-08:00","id":304541,"title":"","content":"The Registration Act did make sense.<br /> Nitro blowing up a few city blocks and killing hundreds of people was a wake up call to the public that there were costumed vigilantes that had zero accountability when it came to innocent death and collateral damage. The public (as it was written) seemed at times blas\u00e9 or indifferent, or perhaps they saw the damaged done as a price to pay. After Nitro's little act the issue was politicized and the Act was made into law. Had Cap's refusal of leading enforcement of the Act been made public, no one would have seen IM as the good guy. After Cap's assassination, Stark said the Act wasn't worth it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T13:17:20-08:00","id":306876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=292260#post292260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know why they aren't doing this to Spider-Man, except to guess that Marvel cannot get rid of their single most beloved and iconic character.</div> </div> </div> </div>The funny thing was, he was already &quot;gone&quot;, in the sense that Peter Parker was essentially dead and Doc Ock had taken over the role as the Superior Spider-Man...which was a VERY entertaining run, now that I've read some of it! <br /> <br /> The strange thing is that they brought Peter back, prematurely ending SSM, according to the writer, because Amazing Spider Man 2 came out, and they apparently wanted the people who had just seen that movie to be able to go into comic book stores and read about the guy they had just seen the movie about.<br /> <br /> Does that EVER actually happen? Do comics stores actually see an increase of sales to non-regular readers after a comic-based movie comes out? Maybe a little, but not enough to justify killing an interesting storyline/character, ESP when they are literally dozens of neatly collected back issues in trade paperback form for curious customers to be directed to! Ugh...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T13:23:00-08:00","id":306878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=304541#post304541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Registration Act did make sense.<br /> Nitro blowing up a few city blocks and killing hundreds of people was a wake up call to the public that there were costumed vigilantes that had zero accountability when it came to innocent death and collateral damage. The public (as it was written) seemed at times blas\u00e9 or indifferent, or perhaps they saw the damaged done as a price to pay. After Nitro's little act the issue was politicized and the Act was made into law. Had Cap's refusal of leading enforcement of the Act been made public, no one would have seen IM as the good guy. After Cap's assassination, Stark said the Act wasn't worth it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, the Registration Act totally made sense. And if superhumans ever showed up in RL, not only would we quickly adopt something like it, but I would support doing so myself! <br /> <br /> The major problem with it is that it highlights the contrast between the escapism fantasy of superhero fiction with needs of recent fiction (across many media) to be more &quot;realistic&quot;. Personally, I see this trend towards &quot;realism&quot; to be more destructive than anything, as it leads to things like Man of Steel...<br /> <br /> Anyway, where does the Registration Act and the Fifty State Initiation stand now? I pretty much stopped reading after the Skrull Invasion, so I'm unclear on how things stand. Did they repeal those, or simply reform them into something more positive?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T13:25:05-08:00","id":306879,"title":"","content":"The one Marvel comic I'm reading now, and totally recommend, is Loki: Agent of Asgard! Witty, surprising, inventive...and the author is clearly a Doctor Who fan! Check it out...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T18:33:02-08:00","id":307055,"title":"","content":"Registration Act was repealed after Steve Rogers was resurrected and Thor rejoined the Avengers with Rogers leading the team. (as far as I know)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/m