beating them in that department.</a><br /> <br /> At least Marvel is putting out some kickass movies on a regular basis, DC's just skimming along on brand power now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I totally agree. Doesn't make theirs any less though. Just makes DC's especially sad.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T15:41:25-08:00","id":310601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=308805#post308805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure how good are Arrow and Flash <b>aside from having pretty male</b>, but on Marvel's side, I can confirm that Agents of SHIELD is just atrocious, the acting can only be described as.....pure narm, thinking about that show give me goose bump.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arrow has one of most diverse casts in the history of modern television, in my opinion. I remember reading a few articles that brought up the amazing diversity on the show. Not saying you're wrong, or trying to argue. Just an FYI.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T08:17:59-08:00","id":311289,"title":"","content":"Yes, but they're all still <i>very pretty</i> diverse people.<br /> <br /> But, hey, it's TV! They're all like that!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T09:38:12-08:00","id":311378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=308970#post308970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I quite like the current season of <b>Marvel's Agents of SHIELD</b>. I was weirdly bummed out when there was no new episode last week on account of the midterms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of which, after having watched this week's episode, anyone else think they know where they're going with this?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">So, over at Disney/Marvel, they're trying to let fall the properties that had to get sold off when Marvel was trying to keep afloat, mainly the Fantastic Four and X-Men/Factor/Force/Mutants in general. Obviously Spider-Man can't falter much as he's their flagship character (it would be like Disney letting Mickey Mouse be forgotten), but the box office on <b>Amazing Spider-Man 2</b> seems to have done a good job of that on it's own, plus their star (whom I think made a pretty damn good Peter Park &amp; Spider-Man) bowing out might get the rights back over to them soon enough.<br /> <br /> To fill the void left by the mutants, they're pushing the Inhumans out into the spotlight. This also means they are having to throw light into some of the darker corner of the Marvel Universe mythologies. For those of you who don't know, the Inhumans gain their powers from the Terrigen Mists, which was created and left behind by the Kree experimenting on primitive humans. This is one of the reasons why they took the risk of putting out the <b>Guardians of the Galaxy</b> movie, so they could introduce the larger world of Marvel and the (multiple) alien influences that are ultimately responsible for a lot of the superhumans on Earth.<br /> <br /> On <b>Agents of SHIELD</b>, they've got these people who have been injected with (what I assume to be) Kree blood and they've been drawing/carving these symbols to make something and, until last night, no one was really sure what it was. Now they've shown that it was a map of a city, and they stated they need to find it.<br /> <br /> Am I the only one who thinks it looked like it could be a map of Attilan, the Inhuman capital city?<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T10:01:27-08:00","id":311405,"title":"","content":"That's the prevailing theory I've been hearing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-30T12:29:06-08:00","id":326210,"title":"","content":"Due to the combination of immense nearly-invincible cosmic power and equally immense cosmic angst attached to a serious personality, I have always found the Silver Surfer pretty boring. So it was quite a surprise when I a friend showed me a few issues of his most recent book and I found it considerably entertaining. Pairing him up with a quirky, brave and at times unexpectedly resourceful but otherwise normal human was a good choice, and the execution is nailing it so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T07:50:59-08:00","id":335184,"title":"","content":"If you're not reading Low, you should be. One of the best comics of the year, if not the best.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T21:24:33-08:00","id":336727,"title":"","content":"So in the newest Avenger/X-men: AXIS issue, The Scarlet Witch just use a &quot;hit all my family with a 1d6 magic arrow&quot; spell, it injures Quicksilver but not Magneto, and Wanda mumbles about Magneto not being her father.<br /> <br /> I smell an incoming recon, the next issue will probably just come right out and say that she's an Inhuman so the comic will align neatly with the movie.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T11:11:39-08:00","id":337224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=336727#post336727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in the newest Avenger/X-men: AXIS issue, The Scarlet Witch just use a &quot;hit all my family with a 1d6 magic arrow&quot; spell, it injures Quicksilver but not Magneto, and Wanda mumbles about Magneto not being her father.<br /> <br /> I smell an incoming recon, the next issue will probably just come right out and say that she's an Inhuman so the comic will align neatly with the movie.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I'm going to throw up.....again.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T16:11:32-08:00","id":337475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorwen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=337224#post337224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I'm going to throw up.....again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Deep breaths and go read, like...Astro City, Death Vigil, or something else good ^__^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T20:34:26-08:00","id":337677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=336727#post336727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in the newest Avenger/X-men: AXIS issue, The Scarlet Witch just use a &quot;hit all my family with a 1d6 magic arrow&quot; spell, it injures Quicksilver but not Magneto, and Wanda mumbles about Magneto not being her father.<br /> <br /> I smell an incoming recon, the next issue will probably just come right out and say that she's an Inhuman so the comic will align neatly with the movie.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, at least it would explain why neither of their powers have ANY similatities to their father's.<br /> <br /> Every Jean + Scott kid has her powers. Kurt looks a little like mom and dad, plus his powers. Logan's kid and clone have healing powers, right?<br /> <br /> Master of Magnetism produces a reality warper and a speedster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T13:12:21-08:00","id":342163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=337677#post337677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, at least it would explain why neither of their powers have ANY similatities to their father's.<br /> <br /> Every Jean + Scott kid has her powers. Kurt looks a little like mom and dad, plus his powers. Logan's kid and clone have healing powers, right?<br /> <br /> Master of Magnetism produces a reality warper and a speedster.</div> </div> </div> </div>They were back when there are more than a few examples of children/siblings/etc had totally different powers. It would be a convenient excuse to use if they wouldn't have taken so many pains to build the Magneto link in the first place. They have even used it before, but I can't remember if that was 616 or an alternate universe thing. They never explored if Magda had any latent powers or not which would be an easier explanation of why. Nor did they ever say what would have happened if an Elder God hadn't interfered when Wanda was born. Her and Magik both kind of ended up with powers outside of normal mutants because of magic manipulation.<br /> <br /> To me it would be just as saying Cable wasn't really Scott's and Madelyne's kid or Rachel wasn't really Scott's and Jean's(alternate universe). So either the switch wasn't a switch and Bova lied about lying or they totally ignore it and make something else up. Or another Phoenix Jean/Xorn Jean setup which would make it that much more special. Whatever way they go it is sounding like the setup to a plot worthy of a soap opera writer or one that would make even them cringe. I'm not surprised because of how well they've been treating a lot of the history lately(even by Marvel standards). They can't even stay consistent within their own writing at times. There has been a lot of simple mistakes, ones that should have easily been caught, in the editing of All-New X-Men at least.<br /> <br /> It is a move worthy of Sony.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T03:07:58-08:00","id":342748,"title":"","content":"I was recently given an Star Wars comic to read by my friend and co-GM. I have never read any Star Wars stuff (only seen the movies) but he said it was a great story so I gave it a try.<br /> <br /> The comic is called &quot;Darth Vader and the Ghost Prison&quot;.<br /> <br /> Go read it now, it's awesome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T06:52:51-08:00","id":342888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorwen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=342163#post342163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They were back when there are more than a few examples of children/siblings/etc had totally different powers. It would be a convenient excuse to use if they wouldn't have taken so many pains to build the Magneto link in the first place. They have even used it before, but I can't remember if that was 616 or an alternate universe thing. They never explored if Magda had any latent powers or not which would be an easier explanation of why. Nor did they ever say what would have happened if an Elder God hadn't interfered when Wanda was born. Her and Magik both kind of ended up with powers outside of normal mutants because of magic manipulation.<br /> <br /> To me it would be just as saying Cable wasn't really Scott's and Madelyne's kid or Rachel wasn't really Scott's and Jean's(alternate universe). So either the switch wasn't a switch and Bova lied about lying or they totally ignore it and make something else up. Or another Phoenix Jean/Xorn Jean setup which would make it that much more special. Whatever way they go it is sounding like the setup to a plot worthy of a soap opera writer or one that would make even them cringe. I'm not surprised because of how well they've been treating a lot of the history lately(even by Marvel standards). They can't even stay consistent within their own writing at times. There has been a lot of simple mistakes, ones that should have easily been caught, in the editing of All-New X-Men at least.<br /> <br /> It is a move worthy of Sony.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, and that's the even crazier thing: they can make it look like it was planned all along.<br /> <br /> Wanda and Pietro have history of being away somewhere in the hands of the High Evolutionary. They've (recently) established that there are people out there with Inhuman heritage. The twins didn't even know Magneto was their father until well after their time with the Brotherhood. Wanda's powers have always waffled back and forth between &quot;true&quot; magic and reality-warping superpowers (what's the friggin' difference? I have no idea!). They've also established that Polaris IS the child of Magneto (which they kept playing with for years), so he has a kid that DID inherit his powers, like most mutants do, and who ALSO has history with the High Evolutionary. The High Evolutionary has tricks, tips, skills, etc gained from mutants AND Inhumans.<br /> <br /> There's a thousand little things that can all add up to Wanda and Pietro being Inhumans instead of mutants and there are explanations for every little discrepancy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T07:48:42-08:00","id":342906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=342888#post342888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> See, and that's the even crazier thing: they can make it look like it was planned all along.<br /> <br /> Wanda and Pietro have history of being away somewhere in the hands of the High Evolutionary. They've (recently) established that there are people out there with Inhuman heritage. The twins didn't even know Magneto was their father until well after their time with the Brotherhood. Wanda's powers have always waffled back and forth between &quot;true&quot; magic and reality-warping superpowers (what's the friggin' difference? I have no idea!). They've also established that Polaris IS the child of Magneto (which they kept playing with for years), so he has a kid that DID inherit his powers, like most mutants do, and who ALSO has history with the High Evolutionary. The High Evolutionary has tricks, tips, skills, etc gained from mutants AND Inhumans.<br /> <br /> There's a thousand little things that can all add up to Wanda and Pietro being Inhumans instead of mutants and there are explanations for every little discrepancy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't disagree that it is plausible, just as I said a plot worthy of a soap opera writer or one that would make even them cringe because of the history of the characters. On top of I could swear they had tried to pull that already with the High Evolutionary. Though as I said it could have been an alternate universe run I'm thinking of. It was so long ago I read all of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T07:54:20-08:00","id":342909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorwen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=342906#post342906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't disagree that it is plausible, just as I said a plot worthy of a soap opera writer or one that would make even them cringe because of the history of the characters. On top of I could swear they had tried to pull that already with the High Evolutionary. Though as I said it could have been an alternate universe run I'm thinking of. It was so long ago I read all of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I'm not disagreeing that it's a move that would even make soap opera writers exclaim &quot;Really? That's weak!&quot;....just expanding on the amazing pile of nonsense they could use to justify the entire thing and I'm sure NONE OF IT was written <i>just </i>for that purpose (except maybe the part about Inhumans having been breeding amongst humanity secretly for a few generations) AND YET they could claim the whole thing to have been self-apparent and support the claim with previous evidence.<br /> <br /> It's incredible the ground work they managed to lay down BY ACCIDENT.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 12-17-2014, 11:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T10:11:01-08:00","id":343065,"title":"","content":"From what I remember the High Evolutionary lived in Wundagore for a time, experimenting on animals and the like. Magda (mother of twins) gave her newborn babes to him (specifically Bova) to care for since she feared Magnus' uncertain temper. I don't remember if the Evolutionary did anything to the twins. I just recall an old particular panel showing Bova with the babes, Pietro and Wanda.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T12:04:32-08:00","id":343130,"title":"","content":"Could be this one:<br /> <img src=\"http://3.bp.blogspot.com/_NZvrpYQgDqo/S-cuF5hC22I/AAAAAAAAAlc/mtBFqu2xJZg/s1600/bova-magda-twins.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Or this one:<br /> <img src=\"http://www.marvunapp.com/Appendix2/bovanewmen1.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Or this one:<br /> <img src=\"http://goodcomics.comicbookresources.com/wp-content/uploads/2011/12/whizzer4.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> As you might gather, they've done this story a lot.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T13:40:11-08:00","id":343161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=336727#post336727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in the newest Avenger/X-men: AXIS issue, The Scarlet Witch just use a &quot;hit all my family with a 1d6 magic arrow&quot; spell, it injures Quicksilver but not Magneto, and Wanda mumbles about Magneto not being her father.<br /> <br /> I smell an incoming recon, the next issue will probably just come right out and say that she's an Inhuman so the comic will align neatly with the movie.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably, It doesn't stop it from being terrible, the book not the twist, which I haven't at all enjoyed the event in the main storyline. The tie-ins have a lot of gems though. If you actually look back on their history, Wanda and Pietro had no actual connection to Magneto in any way, shape or form. However, this was back when marvel had bought a few characters and were trying to tie them to. I can't even remember their names but the point is, it wasn't originally the plan it happened after a while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T16:16:52-08:00","id":343436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=343130#post343130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As you might gather, they've done this story a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah those bottom two were the ones I read.<br /> After the Cthon thing that the Witch got possessed by, it seemed to me that Marvel didn't know exactly where she fit in.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T15:40:33-08:00","id":346197,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://postimage.org/\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://s13.postimg.org/l68kjz8kn/h55_FB3_F29.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> <br /> So, apparently Spider-Woman is getting a new uniform. <a href=\"http://www.usatoday.com/story/life/2014/12/18/spider-woman-new-costume-exclusive/20574271/\" target=\"_blank\">According the editor for the Spider titles</a>, he was already planning it before the Milo Manara debacle, but I'm not entirely sure I buy it.<br /> <br /> Anyway, from that same link:<br /> <br /> &quot;As a woman myself who loves games and comics, I love to see thatfunctional, cool stylish look. It's like a jacket I would want to wear daily,&quot; says Tatiana Nahai, product manager for Gameloft.<br /> <br /> On another place I read it being called a more practical new costume.<br /> <br /> My sentiment is similar to when the same sort of stuff was said of the new Batgirl costume: Leather jackets are <b>not </b>more practical than spandex for agility-focused superheroes. Nobody is gonna see gymnasts wearing leather jackets while competing on the Olympics. I was actually especially annoyed at trading lenses on a cowl for easily-fall-from-your-face glasses, but in the link I posted it shows that they turn into a mask at the tap of a button, so I don't mind it anymore.<br /> <br /> In Batgirl case it was both better (because it was an emergency costume due to her losing her costumes in a fire or something. Though by now she should probably have being able to replace it), and worse (for me, personally), because someone I know kept arguing that the jacket was more protective when her previous costume was quite freaking armored and made of advanced materials.<br /> <br /> I recognize that Spider-Woman's new costume capacity to turn from street clothes to super-hero uniform quickly <b>is</b> functional and practical, but not more practical than wearing something that doesn't hinder your movements when the Rhino is trying to gore you.<br /> <br /> (Also, I should probably mention I'm biased against it, as I dislike it and fear it might become a trend because I <i>really </i>don't like superheroes in street clothes, especially more &quot;urban&quot; stuff, to the point I refuse to read anything with the jeans and T-shirt version of Superboy in it and nearly couldn't watch Young Justice for the same reason)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T16:26:21-08:00","id":346229,"title":"","content":"My own argument is against the changes purely for nostalgic reasons.<br /> But most clothing isn't going to hinder any one able to bench press tons. It's just going to look very beaten and torn after a day or two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T07:27:26-08:00","id":346648,"title":"","content":"As I've said elsewhere, my criteria for what makes a good superhero costume is that it should be giving the reader visual clues as to the hero's identity and powers. For instance, despite it being dated, I quite liked Hawkeye's costume:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://classicmarvelforever.com/images/hawkeye.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> It's littered with instances of the letter H, suggesting &quot;Hawk;&quot; the otherwise superfluous teardrop eye flairs draw attention to the eyes, suggesting eye. The flared boots and loincloth make one think of medieval characters like Robin Hood, and the bracers on his wrist are clearly an archer's bracers, both suggesting he probably uses a bow. I like it.<br /> <br /> I never liked Spider-Woman's costume because I don't think it gives any particular indication as to her identity or power. The yellow hourglass might evoke a garden spider's patterning, I guess...sort of...but what there indicates her power to manipulate people by excreting pheromones? What suggests her energy blasts? What suggests her ability to glide or to fly? Nothing. It's just a bodysuit, and the only suggestion as to her identity is that her mask's eyes look like Spider-Man's. If you know Spider-Man's costume, you might guess this person is Spider-Woman. The costume has style without any substance, and that's why I'm glad to see someone change it...<br /> <br /> ...into another costume with exactly the same problems and failures as the first. Crap.<br /> <br /> Nothing about this new outfit gives me anything about Spider-Woman. It's the same lack of substance with a new, updated flash. That's it. I kinda like the lines on the jacket, but that's a very superficial compliment. If I didn't already know this was Spider-Woman, I wouldn't know it by looking at her, or even guess it.<br /> <br /> My original comparison to Hawkeye was deliberately chosen because I think Spider-Woman's costume reminds me of Hawkeye's current look, which of course is based on the movie version. The movie version is not, by my standards, good...but I do wonder sometimes if my standards are outdated. Looking like an archer might be of secondary importance to looking like a character from one of the biggest money-making movies ever; being familiar with Jeremy Renner is probably much more likely than being able to piece together the visual clues of the purple spandex. Still, though, while I can use that argument for Hawkeye, Spider-Woman doesn't even have that defense.<br /> <br /> In the end, her new look is disposable to me. It's slightly neat, but mostly meh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":271,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","user":"JimB","date":". 12-21-2014, 10:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T11:05:54-08:00","id":346848,"title":"","content":"Not a fan of Spider-Woman's new costume. And yes, I was a huge fan of her previous one. <br /> <br /> Sigh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T12:30:38-08:00","id":346886,"title":"","content":"I liked her web-wings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T01:22:40-08:00","id":347257,"title":"","content":"I like the new look. I remember seeing the original outfit long ago when I was a kid in my older brother's room. He was not terribly into comics, and I am guessing picked it up because of spider woman's... assets. I remember being somewhat shocked by it. It seemed then and still seems now to be a very provacative outfit. I was actually surprised to learn that she was a super<i>hero</i> rather than a villain.<br /> <br /> I do like the new outfit... the ability to change into street clothes is a really neat idea, and I think she looks more like a hero somehow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T06:56:25-08:00","id":347364,"title":"","content":"They've also reduced said assets, made her look like she's barely into her 20s (which will make the movie casting easier) and given the costume designer of the next Avengers movie something to work with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T08:55:30-08:00","id":347464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=347364#post347364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They've also reduced said assets, made her look like she's barely into her 20s (which will make the movie casting easier) and g<b>iven the costume designer of the next Avengers movie something to work with.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Black Widow's costume was pretty similar in nature to Spider-Woman's costume and they didn't seem to have a problem putting it to film. Not a fan of her looking younger, either. If they're going to completely change the nature of the character(not saying they are...yet), why not just create a new character? <br /> <br /> I guess I just didn't see the need for a change, nor do I think it's a positive one. Of course, I'm certainly not speaking for everyone when I say these things. Regardless, as long as the stories are good, it won't matter too much in the long run.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T10:07:28-08:00","id":347507,"title":"","content":"I decided to get into again into Franco-Belgian comics and decided to marathon one series by one.<br /> <br /> My first on the list is XIII. Then I'll probably marathon Thorgal. I had interest int the premise of Red Knight but unable to find a version in any language I can read.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T07:40:54-08:00","id":348313,"title":"","content":"I've always found it difficult to get into comics. I often want to, as the graphic storytelling medium is something I have a great deal of curiosity about, but I find it really hard to get invested into any of the more mainstream super-hero titles, just due to the insane continuity snarl (it's a guy, who is significant if you've read this totally unrelated title, but if you haven't they won't help by explaining anything! And Hero X is angsty about something, which again only makes sense if you've read this other title [and who stopped numbering comics sequentially, instead going with this volume shit!? Makes it impossible for newcomers to get any idea about what's going on]! Oh, and what you thought you knew and were relying on to give a foundation to this idea is wrong because they changed it last reboot, which they had to do because the story got too ludicrously convoluted, which worked for like three issues because they ended up bringing all the old stuff back - I really didn't expect that to go so long. My apologies). So I've limited myself to more-or-less self-contained stories, like Sandman (refers to other stuff, but you don't need to know it), or Hellblazer, or stories that I know the background to fairly well, like the Buffy/Angel comic continuations, mostly Angel. Or the occasional established hero/villain, but a standalone volume, like The Killing Joke.<br /> <br /> Sometimes I look into getting into a particular heros stories, but that doesn't seem feasible. I remember about a year ago I looked into reading The Hulk, but that seemed just waaay too intimidating to work out what I was supposed to read, in what order, and what &quot;counted&quot; and what didn't and when. On the one had, it's sad, because there's this whole group of mythology I'm missing out on. On the other, I find it really hard to convince myself that it's worth the - quite significant - effort.<br /> <br /> I'm sure when you work that stuff out, the payoff is great. Just way too high a learning curve for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T08:20:56-08:00","id":348345,"title":"","content":"Realtalk, I limit myself to reading Silver Age covers at various sites since they are crazy in hilarious way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T12:56:03-08:00","id":348483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=348313#post348313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> like the Buffy/Angel comic continuations, mostly Angel. Or the occasional established hero/villain, but a standalone volume, like The Killing Joke.</div> </div> </div> </div>I give you one jar of Warren. It's true because I wrote it in the Vampyr book.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ortam + Malkavia makes a Requiem fun.<br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Posts in this colour are Persuasion.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">Posts in this colour are Seduction.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this colour are Intimidation.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/57-solomon-birch","name":"solomon birch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar57_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T23:12:06-08:00","id":348828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solomon birch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=348483#post348483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I give you one jar of Warren. It's true because I wrote it in the Vampyr book.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I get the feeling you're making a point, but I'm a bit confused as to what that is. Is it that I shouldn't be confused by the number of books in comics and just magically know which of the ten thousand comic lines called 'Iron Man' I should be able to effortlessly sort them out? Because that seems a silly, and thus unlikely, point to make. Is it that I complain about not knowing background, but can read these stories that require a lot of background? That'd be valid, but my point was that I already do know that background, so I can get into those much easier. And the background of Angel or Buffy is a hell of a lot simpler than that of The Hulk or Spiderman.<br /> <br /> So, yeah. Confused.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T23:49:37-08:00","id":348861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=348313#post348313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always found it difficult to get into comics. I often want to, as the graphic storytelling medium is something I have a great deal of curiosity about, but I find it really hard to get invested into any of the more mainstream super-hero titles, just due to the insane continuity snarl...<br /> <br /> ...So I've limited myself to more-or-less self-contained stories, like Sandman (refers to other stuff, but you don't need to know it), or Hellblazer, or stories that I know the background to fairly well, like the Buffy/Angel comic continuations, mostly Angel. Or the occasional established hero/villain, but a standalone volume, like The Killing Joke...<br /> <br /> ...I'm sure when you work that stuff out, the payoff is great. Just way too high a learning curve for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>some suggestions from some favourites of mine:<br /> <br /> <b>-</b> <b>Astro City</b>: Both the older stories and the current ones. Even the worst of it (dark ages) is reasonably decent, and pretty much all the rest goes from good to &quot;among the best comics of all time&quot; quality. Not exactly traditional superhero comics, because it is a superhero comic but it has its own style of storytelling that is atypical for the genre, but I can't recommend it enough. Currently published by DC, but has no relation at all with the DC universe, being completely self-contained. Besides, covers and a good deal of the character design are done by the phenomenal Alex Ross<br /> <br /> <b>- Superman: Peace on Earth</b><br /> <b>- Batman: War on Crime</b><br /> <b>- Wonder Woman: The Spirit of Truth</b><br /> <b>- Shazam: The Power of Hope</b><br /> These four are a collection of very well-written stories that really <i>get </i>the essence of each of these characters. You can read any of those that interests you in any order, they are not connected. They don't really require much knowledge about continuity and stuff. Perhaps you will not be familiar enough with the basics of Captain Marvel's mythos, but <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Captain_Marvel_%28DC_Comics%29\" target=\"_blank\">a short read on wikipedia </a> can fix that (section 1.1.1, section 1.1.2, and section 2 only up to the second paragraph after the powers table, are sufficient. About 2 pages or so of text). I imagine you are probably familiar enough with Batman and Superman to read theirs with no problem, and from what I recall Wonder Woman's doesn't really require knowing nearly anything about her either.<br /> <br /> Despite being independent stories, I put them together because the same creative team did all of them. Oh, and all of them are <i>entirely </i>illustrated by the Alex Ross who is, as I already said, phenomenal.<br /> <br /> <b>- Death Vigil</b>: urban fantasy comic featuring dead people being recruited to the vigil, an ancient organization that fights against eldritch abominations. Written and illustrated by the great <a href=\"http://nebezial.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">Stjepan Sejic</a> (you can see many examples of his excellent owrk and his humor in the various folders to the left of the gallery). His artwork is fantastic, and his characterization and humor are top notch. Since you like Buffy/Angel I suspect you'd enjoy this one. It is quite a recent publication, so you can get on board before there is much on which to catch on. Only 5 issues so far. And, since he is a cool dude, <a href=\"http://nebezial.deviantart.com/art/death-vigil-1-full-issue-cuz-it-s-a-good-day-496921638\" target=\"_blank\">he has made a .pdf of the first issue available for free!</a><br /> <br /> <b>- Invincible</b>: this one is more &quot;normal&quot; superhero stuff, except that, being creator owned stuff from Image, it is not shackled by continuity snafus (and, at less than 120 issues, there simply isn't SO much continuity) and the forever-return-to-status-quo syndrome that afflicts DC and Marvel. Instead, the author is not afraid to pretty much blow up the status quo very often. Never a boring issue on this one. The tagline of &quot;The ONLY Superhero comic you will ever need&quot; and the former one of &quot;The best superhero comic book in the universe&quot; are exaggerated, of course, but in my opinion not as much as one might think, because it is a <i>really </i>good comic book. Just a reads up, though, the fights can get <i>very </i>violent and gory. That actually usually detracts from my enjoyment, but I keep reading because the book is just too good to pass up.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T00:28:04-08:00","id":348874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=348861#post348861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">snip</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooh, thankee kindly. I'll check those out <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T06:33:50-08:00","id":348996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=348828#post348828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get the feeling you're making a point, but I'm a bit confused as to what that is. .</div> </div> </div> </div>There was no point or intent to confuse. I just referenced the current plots of the Angel and Buffy comics.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ortam + Malkavia makes a Requiem fun.<br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Posts in this colour are Persuasion.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">Posts in this colour are Seduction.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this colour are Intimidation.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/57-solomon-birch","name":"solomon birch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar57_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T06:45:16-08:00","id":348999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solomon birch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=348996#post348996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was no point or intent to confuse. I just referenced the current plots of the Angel and Buffy comics.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh. Well, I stopped reading them a while back (Buffy was a barely tolerable character at the best of times and steadily got worse over Season 8, and the interesting side characters were becoming less prominent and less interesting; stopped with Angel after Connor's interaction with that cult that turned him into a literal god), so no wonder it went over my head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T07:07:34-08:00","id":349035,"title":"","content":"I know I'm a late comer to the whole thing, but I finished Locke &amp; Key a few weeks ago and I've been getting into Fables now, up to Volume 5.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.idwpublishing.com/lockekey/\" target=\"_blank\">Locke &amp; Key</a> was a great story, and the layers just kept unfolding, which was one of the things that makes it great.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.vertigocomics.com/browse?content_type=comic&amp;keyword=FABLES\" target=\"_blank\">Fables</a>, I'm still waffling on because, while it's an interesting concept, I'm just not sure where it's going and if it's worth the trip.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T07:13:40-08:00","id":349036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=348874#post348874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oooh, thankee kindly. I'll check those out <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>independents are some of the best sources for self contained stories. My recommendation is to read by author. You will get consistently better books and enjoy them more regardless of who they are writing for or what book it is. Some of my favorites are:Jack Kirby, Warren Ellis, Garth Ennis, Jason Aaron, Grant Morrison, Neil Gaiman, Brian Wood. I know I'm forgetting a few but those authors will give you consistently good books, most of them for audiences that are more mature and sometimes reaching into academia and philosophy (Grant Morrisons Animal Man and Warren Ellis' Transmetropolitan come to mind)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T11:38:52-08:00","id":349183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=348313#post348313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometimes I look into getting into a particular heros stories, but that doesn't seem feasible. I remember about a year ago I looked into reading The Hulk, but that seemed just waaay too intimidating to work out what I was supposed to read, in what order, and what &quot;counted&quot; and what didn't and when. On the one had, it's sad, because there's this whole group of mythology I'm missing out on. On the other, I find it really hard to convince myself that it's worth the - quite significant - effort.<br /> <br /> I'm sure when you work that stuff out, the payoff is great. Just way too high a learning curve for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are looking for superheroes you might want to look at Top ten and Tom Strong. Watchmen revolutionized the Genre unforunately it was a step back. Miracle man and Authority are pretty much much more grittier and dark versions of the Genre. If you just want normal Comics, Lucifer, Books of magic, Sandman all by Neil Gaiman. The Last Man. Man, I have a lot of recommendations. Mostly I would recommend you look far away from the big two except for specific stand alone stories. Getting invested in such a payoff is actually BAD.<br /> <br /> Look at Cosmic marvel. From 2007-2010, there was a series of interconnecting comics. It was easy for anyone to follow because it was small. IT was an amazing Space opera. It had Highs and Lows (Never REad Wraith). Then the movie was announced Bendis took Over and RUINED the Guardians of the Galaxy. It's completely unrecognizable. That's the problem with the Big Two. They give good things to bad writers while the Good writers struggle to sell. Invitably the longer you stay in the more you start to despise what's happening to characters you love because it's not even done well. Granted, sometimes Good writers make really good works. New Ghost Rider, New Warriors, Blue Beetle before the reboot. That are just fantastic but get cancelled because of sales. It's just a Roller Coaster and I have problems getting on anymore. It's much better to stick to limited projects with set runs. At least then, if you liked it you know that the quality won't change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T18:53:13-08:00","id":349449,"title":"","content":"Neil Gaiman is a genius. I own pretty much all of Sandman. I've also read Transmetropolitan, didn't really do much for me. Y the Last Man I did enjoy, as I did Watchmen. <br /> <br /> I'll check out those others <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T19:07:32-08:00","id":349451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=349449#post349449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neil Gaiman is a genius. I own pretty much all of Sandman. I've also read Transmetropolitan, didn't really do much for me. Y the Last Man I did enjoy, as I did Watchmen.<br /> <br /> I'll check out those others <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><b>Northalnders</b>, <b>Gravel</b> (Gravel is all lovecraftian horror mixed with Mage), <b>The Invisibles</b>, <b>No Hero</b>, <b>Crossed</b> (this book is super fucked up is kind of a zombie apocalypse book but the zombies are essentially just humans with nothing but psychotic madmen who follow their primal whims at any and every turn) <b>Jack Kirby's New Gods</b> (this run is older and a bit campy but fucking fantastic), <b>Preacher</b>, <b>Punisher MAX by Garth Ennis</b> (best punisher run in years), <b>303</b> by Garth Ennis, <b>Streets of Glory</b>, <b>The Boys</b> (truly dark comedy that parodies big super heroes [ notbatman dies fucking the moon because he thinks its &quot;not Robin&quot; IIRC]), <b>Orbiter</b> (fantastic graphic novel about humans adventuring beyond the moon for the first time ever), <b>Black Gas</b> (really good weird apoc story), <b>Doktor Sleepless</b> (Holy fuck this book is good. Its about a cyberpunk future that mixes in lovecraftian horror transhumanism and the idolatry of pop icons), <b>Animal Man </b>(breaks fourth wall only read the Grant Morrison run. Mostly about a hero with rather substandard powers into someone truly great and fun to read)<br /> <br /> Thats all I can think of now. titles are bolded<br /> <br /> Punisher Max, The Boys and Crossed are not for the faint of heart at all. All 3 could trigger someone who has been physically or sexually assaulted. None of the books, however, make light of that subject or turn it into a joke (the closest to that would be The Boys where the new girl on the NOT Justice League is forced to perform sexual favors for the leaders. However the author does not try to make it into a joke. There is a short book where they kill a huge amount of Supes. what The Boys call superheroes, at a giant orgy.) Pretty much all the books I recommended are for 18+ readers if not for language than for content or simply because they require a bit of that wisdom that comes with an extra year or two past age 15.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","user":"cerealkiller","date":".  Clarification and explanations. 12-29-2014, 09:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T20:30:17-08:00","id":353399,"title":"","content":"I second <b>Preacher</b>. There were some things I didn't like about it, but plenty to enjoy. It was a great read.<br /> <br /> <b>Dylan Dog</b> was interesting, and I am almost halfway through reading the various <b>Hellboy</b> volumes. I love <b>American Vampire</b> and <b>Saga</b> is pretty good too (although I am a bit behind on that one, and I hear it is causing some controversy).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T04:58:07-08:00","id":353602,"title":"","content":"Lotta horror(-ish) in your picks, Storyteller. That a coincidence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T11:32:12-08:00","id":353925,"title":"","content":"As to Superhero looks. You have the start of many where they were trying to at least some what distance them from the every day. When you get to the 80's and 90's they kept to that line for the most part but adding in things that would update. Which often came from the more every day. Still trying to meet the expectations of the reader though and separate that this is a SUPERhero. You of course got new heroes that didn't go that line but the reason for that was more due to the expectations of that heroes universe. Too, many of those are really comic heroes rather than superheroes which is an important distinction some are failing to see. That isn't a quality distinction, but a distinction of category. I've never seen people get their undergarments more in a bunch then when you try to say that their favorite hero really isn't a SUPERhero.<br /> <br /> The problem for me in comics as a whole is that now you have more artists in charge so you get whatever they want shoved down your throat. The mentality has changed from trying to get the reader in and enjoy to the expectation that the reader has to enjoy whatever you put out there. Accompanied by the ever popular comforting thought that if you don't succeed it is because &quot;they just don't understand you&quot;. For me it seems it is because there is no longer the balance for that artistic temperament. The greatest things of my generation came out of that balance, that need that both sides had to argue to get what they wanted. Anytime one totally overrules the other is usually when bad things happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T16:02:02-08:00","id":354151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorwen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=353925#post353925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to Superhero looks. You have the start of many where they were trying to at least some what distance them from the every day. When you get to the 80's and 90's they kept to that line for the most part but adding in things that would update. Which often came from the more every day. Still trying to meet the expectations of the reader though and separate that this is a SUPERhero. You of course got new heroes that didn't go that line but the reason for that was more due to the expectations of that heroes universe. Too, many of those are really comic heroes rather than superheroes which is an important distinction some are failing to see. That isn't a quality distinction, but a distinction of category. I've never seen people get their undergarments more in a bunch then when you try to say that their favorite hero really isn't a SUPERhero.</div> </div> </div> </div>With the understanding it's a categorical difference, not an implication of quality, what would you say is the difference between a comic hero and a super hero?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T20:00:55-08:00","id":354332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=353602#post353602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lotta horror(-ish) in your picks, Storyteller. That a coincidence?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Horror has always held a dark little place in my lifeless heart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T09:42:31-08:00","id":355820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=354151#post354151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With the understanding it's a categorical difference, not an implication of quality, what would you say is the difference between a comic hero and a super hero?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a genre like anything else. That doesn't mean that it can only be that, but people are coming to it looking for an experience. While people expectations will differ some you still have a mean to work from. If half way through Inspector Gadget the Claw starts ripping out people's entrails and hanging them by them you stepped far afield a comedy(yes extreme example). If Batman runs around defeating villains in a baseball cap and trench coat your kind of loosing that Superhero identity. That might be good for a noir run or side story, but isn't good for a new sole focus identity. Just wearing a jacket doesn't really do that but it starts stepping in that direction.<br /> <br /> Spandex(just to simplify the example) is part of the uniform of the Superhero like a policeman or Fire Fighter has a uniform. They can still be that without the uniform, but their identity is in large part wrapped up in that. The difference between the two is that a Superhero is supposed to be a beacon(that isn't to say hero vs anit-hero or Superman vs Batman vs Spawn) and that outfit helps that identification, helps them stand out in that needed way. I wouldn't want to see Constantine in spandex. It might be as cheesy as the white hat/black hat in old westerns, but that is part of the experience. The Superhero is wrapped up in that identity created by the outfit.<br /> <br /> <br /> In this specific case theres more a why bother. It acomplishes even less than Clark Kent taking off his glasses to become Superman. The line from the link in danelsan's post kind encapsulates all of this for me.<br /> <br /> &quot;To operate on the level she wants to, she needs something that can pass for semi-normal and she can turn it on to crazy if she needs to.&quot;<br /> <br /> First in the aknowledgement that a superhero should &quot;turn it to crazy&quot; and second in the oblivious mindset that closing her jacket and extending her shades does &quot;turn it to crazy&quot;. Seriously? That is like say a banana pepper and a hobniario are just as hot.<br /> <br /> The other one that got to me was: &quot;She's sexy but not in a spandex way \u2014 in a modern, unique way.&quot; More like in a 90's biker wannabe kind of way. I'm at a loss how it is unique or modern. I can picture them sitting around at a Marvel roundtable discussing this and patting themselves on the back about how visionary and &quot;hip&quot; this is going to be. It would be like sitting in the eye of a hurricane saying how nice the weather is today. Its being oblivious to anything else going on around it.<br /> <br /> What they seem to say they are expecting and what they've created are at totally opposite ends of the spectrum. So to be a detective she had to loose the outfit, her figure, and her age? Its more like they were looking to make something like Batgirl and decided Spider-Woman was the way to do that rather than try and make a new character or use some of the characters tailor made to already do that. She looks more like some 16 year old Spider-Girl. It would be like trying to turn Superman into Superboy and say it is the natural progression of the character.<br /> <br /> It feels like its what too many of these failed movies have tried to do. They think the existing fans are some type of safety net. Its possible as it has worked before, but it has never done anything for the longevity of the franchise they do that to. The novelty will wear off and usually by the time it does the fans that have allowed it to carry are gone by then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T20:34:14-08:00","id":356196,"title":"","content":"If anyone liked the first issue of Death Vigil in the link I posted before, Stjepan Sejic has now <a href=\"http://nebezial.deviantart.com/art/death-vigil-2-full-issue-happy-new-year-503835860\" target=\"_blank\">released the second issue for free</a>. I already have all 5 current issues, but if you are still in the fence after issue #1, try this one and see if it turns you over ^__^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T04:05:14-08:00","id":367193,"title":"","content":"I can't add another comic book to my reading list currently, but at some point I have to at least buy the trade of Amazing Spider-Man in which the spiderverse storyline makes the Japanese Spider-Man* from the 70's part of comic book canon<br /> <br /> <br /> *You know, the one who introduced himself as &quot;the emissary of hell&quot; and was the first Tokusatsu hero to have a Giant Robot","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T09:06:33-08:00","id":371100,"title":"","content":"Since we're in a recommending mood right now I'd like to suggest <b>Hexed</b>. It's the story of Lucifer, a woman who acts as a sort of occult-oriented Catwoman, without the body suit or cleavage. The characters first appearance was way back in the fantastic <b>Fall of Cthulhu</b> series, then she had her own 4 issue mini, called <b>Hexed</b>, back in 2009 where she was hired to steal an angels wings back for it and we were introduced to her patron, a woman with a mysterious past who is also heavily involved with the occult. Recently she's got an ongoing, also called <b>Hexed</b>, where she's dealing with the fallout of some of the things that happened in the four issue mini and her patron's new intern, who was sort of shanghai'd into the occult underworld without knowing anything about it.<br /> <br /> For fans of American Vampire, they're trying to ride on the success of that with <b>Wolf Moon</b>, a comic about golems. No, of course not, it's about werewolves. Sort of. The mythology behind them isn't like that of World of Darkness. I don't believe it's as good as American Vampire, personally, I think they made an error focusing more on the werewolf hunter than the werewolf itself, but that does sort of get explained (and changed) later. But if you're a werewolf fan it might be your thing. The werewolf is a particularly monstrous and violent thing.<br /> <br /> I'll also second <b>Crossed</b>, specifically recommending <b>Badlands</b> (which is sort of a series of different stories by different writers and artists about the same 'world') and <b>Wish You Were Here </b>(which is just one story). Alan Moore's currently doing an interesting short series in the Crossed universe right now, showing the future of humanity without the civilization we currently have. And I'll suggest <b>Stitched</b>, which apparently spawned from Garth Ennis' first film, and starts an interesting story.<br /> <br /> Oh, and<b> Sam &amp; Twitch</b>. It's about a pair of detectives and while it Spawned from a superhero-ish comic, said antihero only appears in, I think, two frames throughout the entirety of the series, though, and it sticks to mostly down to earth detective stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-15-2015, 12:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T11:42:39-08:00","id":372769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=371100#post371100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and<b> Sam &amp; Twitch</b>. It's about a pair of detectives and while it Spawned from a superhero-ish comic...</div> </div> </div> </div>Terrible pun is terrible.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T17:56:08-08:00","id":384656,"title":"","content":"Any wrestling (the WWE kind) fans around? I just learned of an amusing development: CM Punk is gonna write a story for the next Thor Annual ^_^<br /> <a href=\"http://marvel.com/news/comics/23636/welcome_to_marvel_cm_punk_-_hope_you_survive_the_experience\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a> is an interview about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T20:32:37-08:00","id":387944,"title":"","content":"I've been reading Cthulhu Tales lately. For those that are unfamiliar, they take the Cthulhu mythos and apply it in different ways: an SVU-style murder mystery (with zombies), classic horror, romance, etc.<br /> <br /> Pretty well done, by and large.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T15:55:53-08:00","id":405229,"title":"","content":"Any girls around? Men are free to comment as well, of course, but I'm particularly interested in the perspective of women here. I'm wondering if I can get some opinions about these pages:<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://postimage.org/\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://s21.postimg.org/cb0k402uv/1423674682114.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://postimage.org/\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://s21.postimg.org/wrbkm8d4n/1423674769863.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> <br /> From my perspective, it looks like blatant pandering and using the comic as a soapbox by turning characters into author's mouthpieces, completely disregarding their characterization <span style=\"font-size:10px\">(not that this is anything new. Happens considerably more often than I would like)</span>. I mean, characterization in comics can be almost as inconsistent as powers, but Titania surrendering because...some sort feminism/girl-power enthusiasm, I guess? Did she somehow forget all the times she fought <i>She-Hulk</i>?<br /> <br /> Is <i>that </i>how they intend to build up her heat? By making it all about how she is a woman, instead of, you know, her actual super-heroism?<br /> <br /> For instance, when she defeated a bunch of Ice Giants by using the Hammer in a way Original Recipe Thor never did, I found that pretty cool. But when a villainess surrenders out of honoring how hard it is to be a woman, despite never having done so before with other heroines (even another one who is also a distaff counterpart of a male hero), not so much.<br /> <br /> So, opinions: is there some angle I'm missing, or is it just bad writing?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">(as an aside, the art is pretty good. I like the combination of clean lines and soft coloring. But Titania is looking kinda under-muscled from the way she is usually depicted, especially her arms)</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T18:19:17-08:00","id":405370,"title":"","content":"I don't know the characters in question, but is it possible that the writers were trying to avoid accusations of blatant fanservice-through-catfight? I mean, they haven't worried about it before, and arguably what they've done here is <i>worse</i>, but at least that'd give partial points for intent?<br /> <br /> Just a thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T20:59:04-08:00","id":405440,"title":"","content":"I like new Thor, and I find Titania being written out of character there. On the previous page Carl Creel, the man Titania hits, her husband, says some remarks that are probably similar to something the writer's heard in response to the change to a woman Thor.<br /> <br /> As for the pushing a character they like, it's no different from Batman hugging Tim Drake in Robin and saying Tim's going to be better than him one day, and urging him to ignore Cassandra Cain, she's just crazy. Or all the Avengers agreeing that Spider-man is going to be a smarter and better hero than all of them when he matures. Or after Tony Stark's memory got erased, Thor offering him access to the treasures of Asgard to become rich again. Or Quentin Quire, the 'world's worst terrorist,' being handed over to Wolverine so he can go to school with other mutants like him and become the star of the comic.<br /> <br /> In regards to dealing with real issues, there's nothing wrong with comics getting into that, especially when something is as topical as women in comics. It would be nice if it was handled more subtly or in character but that doesn't always happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T21:11:16-08:00","id":405445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=405229#post405229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm wondering if I can get some opinions about these pages:</div> </div> </div> </div>Way to settle the camera on Titania's half-bare bubble butt. No dissonance between art and writing there, no sir.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=405229#post405229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, characterization in comics can be almost as inconsistent as powers, but Titania surrendering because...some sort feminism/girl-power enthusiasm, I guess? Did she somehow forget all the times she fought <i>She-Hulk</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know anything about Titania, but I'm guess it's related to that bit about Thor's name. As in, Thor is her own identity and not a female variant on the <i>real</i> deal...like She-Hulk, for instance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=405229#post405229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is <i>that </i>how they intend to build up her heat? By making it all about how she is a woman, instead of, you know, her actual super-heroism?</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you read the previous four issues? I think they're allowed one issue out of five to show the world reacting to her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T06:44:09-08:00","id":405749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=405445#post405445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you read the previous four issues? I think they're allowed one issue out of five to show the world reacting to her.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, my displeasure with those pages led me to exaggerate how prevalent the thing actually is. Still, I hope they don't make that much of a big deal about her name from now on, and I <b>definitively</b> don't want to see other villainesses surrendering just to give her props for it.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">(By the way, why the hell did she punch out a surrendered opponent? If she is going to jail willingly, what is the point?)</span><br /> <br /> Speaking of characterization, Odin has been depicted before as an authoritative jerk, but was he as much of a sexist before? I'm not a big Thor reader, but I don't recall him being portrayed like that.<br /> <br /> On another subject, the whole Spider-Verse thing has been immensely amusing. Both the Broadway and the electric company versions of Spider-Man are now canon, for instance. There are various Spider-Men that &quot;look like&quot; the actor that portrayed them on film. Japanse Spider-Man with a giant mecha is also canon. May Parker. Spider-Gwen. I just love that whole thing ^__^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T06:50:30-08:00","id":405754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=405749#post405749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, why the hell did she punch out a surrendered opponent? If she is going to jail willingly, what is the point?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that pisses me off too. You don't hit a surrendered enemy, you dick. I guess part and parcel of being worthy of a weapon is being willing to use that weapon, but still.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=405749#post405749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of characterization, Odin has been depicted before as an authoritative jerk, but was he as much of a sexist before?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've misfiled some of my comics, so I can't check and am really asking: Is Odin that much of a sexist? I remember him calling Thor a witch a lot, but I'm less sure that's intended to condemn her vagina than to condemn her supposed sorcery she used to steal Mjolnir.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=405749#post405749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On another subject, the whole Spider-Verse thing has been immensely amusing.</div> </div> </div> </div>To each his own. I personally got so bored by the endless repetition of nearly nameless superheroes being slaughtered in job lots by invincible bad guys that I had the comic shop take the book off my pull. We'll see if I care after this is over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T08:03:11-08:00","id":405804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=405754#post405754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've misfiled some of my comics, so I can't check and am really asking: Is Odin that much of a sexist? I remember him calling Thor a witch a lot, but I'm less sure that's intended to condemn her vagina than to condemn her supposed sorcery she used to steal Mjolnir.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had in my mind more how he talks to his wife in issue #1<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T09:19:26-08:00","id":405840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=405754#post405754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To each his own. I personally got so bored by the endless repetition of nearly nameless superheroes being slaughtered in job lots by invincible bad guys that I had the comic shop take the book off my pull. We'll see if I care after this is over.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't the world ending, again, shortly after spider-verse is over ?<br /> <br /> I follow all the comic book tv shows right now and watch some youtube revisions of episodes and it came to my attention, that Marvel will end the 616-continuity and the UU-continuity (which is the only one I read from Marvel - but I am behind since the German issues are about 6 to 10 months later then the US issues) and revamp everything - probably with some more focus on similarities to the MCU and the properties they own. Which sucks for FOX, since they don't have an understanding like Marvel reached with SONY for incorporation Spider-Man into the MCU. Could mean less X-Men and less Fantastic Four in the future...<br /> <br /> At least that's what I heard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T14:15:10-08:00","id":406100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=405840#post405840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't the world ending, again, shortly after spider-verse is over ?<br /> <br /> I follow all the comic book tv shows right now and watch some youtube revisions of episodes and it came to my attention, that Marvel will end the 616-continuity and the UU-continuity (which is the only one I read from Marvel - but I am behind since the German issues are about 6 to 10 months later then the US issues) and revamp everything - probably with some more focus on similarities to the MCU and the properties they own. Which sucks for FOX, since they don't have an understanding like Marvel reached with SONY for incorporation Spider-Man into the MCU. Could mean less X-Men and less Fantastic Four in the future...<br /> <br /> At least that's what I heard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, I heard that too. Something about a big company wide crossover(again, sigh) with Secret Wars(and new mini series to go along with it) and then they'll blow it all up and replace it something called Battle world? I'm honestly having a hard time following or understanding the news about what they're doing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.newsarama.com/22828-marvel-release-full-map-of-secret-wars-battleworld.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.newsarama.com/22828-marvel-release-full-map-of-secret-wars-battleworld.html\" target=\"_blank\"> Newsarama </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.newsarama.com/22828-marvel-release-full-map-of-secret-wars-battleworld.html\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.newsarama.com/22828-marvel-release-full-map-of-secret-wars-battleworld.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.geekrex.com/2014/12/breaking-down-battle-world-in-marvels.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.geekrex.com/2014/12/breaking-down-battle-world-in-marvels.html\" target=\"_blank\"> Just a moment... </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.geekrex.com/2014/12/breaking-down-battle-world-in-marvels.html\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.geekrex.com/2014/12/breaking-down-battle-world-in-marvels.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.geeksofdoom.com/2015/01/26/marvel-ends-universe-secret-wars\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.geeksofdoom.com/GoD/img/spacer.gif\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.geeksofdoom.com/2015/01/26/marvel-ends-universe-secret-wars\" target=\"_blank\"> Marvel Ends The Universe With &lsquo;Secret Wars&rsquo; </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.geeksofdoom.com/2015/01/26/marvel-ends-universe-secret-wars\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.geeksofdoom.com/2015/01/26/marvel-ends-universe-secret-wars </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T16:22:33-08:00","id":406184,"title":"","content":"As far as I understood it, all marvel universes form a single realm and it somehow is determined who will be part of the new marvel universe and who won't.<br /> Anyways, it will be the end of the UU and therefore probably the end of me reading a ongoing series...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T18:02:18-08:00","id":406206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=406184#post406184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I understood it, all marvel universes form a single realm and it somehow is determined who will be part of the new marvel universe and who won't.<br /> Anyways, it will be the end of the UU and therefore probably the end of me reading a ongoing series...</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't read a series from Marvel in years now. I gave up during Civil War. Just got tired of mega crossovers screwing my subscriptions.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Battle World is part of this whole Secret Wars thing? I thought Battle World was what was coming after Secret Wars? Their news for this is too confusing...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T18:51:38-08:00","id":406216,"title":"","content":"It seems like it's Marvel's version of Crisis of Infinite Earths. The result is that all the extraneous parallel worlds will be destroyed, or at least forgotten until discovered again, and everyone will work off one format, and it's possible the Mutants or Fantastic Four will have their own universe, and be a separate part of things.<br /> <br /> They might merge some of the Ultimate stuff over, but it might just be the appearances of certain characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T07:31:56-08:00","id":406685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=405804#post405804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had in my mind more how he talks to his wife in issue #1.</div> </div> </div> </div>I found my comics and actually had to do a page-by-page analysis of them elsewhere, so I now say with complete confidence: yeah, Odin is a bit of a pig, but it seems clear to me at least half of that is wounded pride and outrage that the universe had the bad taste to get on without him while he was gone, and he seems to be just lashing out at any and every perceived challenge to his authority.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T07:33:53-08:00","id":407710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=406206#post406206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I haven't read a series from Marvel in years now. I gave up during Civil War. Just got tired of mega crossovers screwing my subscriptions.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Battle World is part of this whole Secret Wars thing? I thought Battle World was what was coming after Secret Wars? Their news for this is too confusing...</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, Battle World is a part of the Secret Wars. There are some interesting cross overs between titles. Age of Ultron vs Marvel Zombies being one of the real out theres. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Secret Wars starts on free comic day with a free Issue Zero. I'm thinking about picking up Marvel for this at least. I was really disappointed with how they treated All-New X-Men, but knowing this is going to be a mess any way might make it fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T16:18:11-08:00","id":408283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan;n405229<br /> <br /> From my perspective, it looks like blatant pandering and using the comic as a soapbox by turning characters into author's mouthpieces, completely disregarding their characterization [SIZE=10px</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">(not that this is anything new. Happens considerably more often than I would like)[/SIZE]. I mean, characterization in comics can be almost as inconsistent as powers, but Titania surrendering because...some sort feminism/girl-power enthusiasm, I guess? Did she somehow forget all the times she fought <i>She-Hulk</i>?<br /> <br /> Is <i>that </i>how they intend to build up her heat? By making it all about how she is a woman, instead of, you know, her actual super-heroism?<br /> <br /> For instance, when she defeated a bunch of Ice Giants by using the Hammer in a way Original Recipe Thor never did, I found that pretty cool. But when a villainess surrenders out of honoring how hard it is to be a woman, despite never having done so before with other heroines (even another one who is also a distaff counterpart of a male hero), not so much.<br /> <br /> So, opinions: is there some angle I'm missing, or is it just bad writing?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">(as an aside, the art is pretty good. I like the combination of clean lines and soft coloring. But Titania is looking kinda under-muscled from the way she is usually depicted, especially her arms)</span></div> </div> </div> </div>It's blatant pandering and bad writing. This is the Writer trying to grab up as many readers as they can by trying to go for a nishe audience. That and/or what you said. Titania was horribly characterized here. This is the woman who hates She Hulk because She Hulk is stronger than her. Unless she thought Thor was weaker than her there's no way she'd say or do something like that. She'd go after Thor harder than her husband for petty reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T16:42:54-08:00","id":408318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=408283#post408283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She'd go after Thor harder than her husband for petty reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>She might be going easy on Thor because Thor helped her and her husband when she had cancer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T17:44:12-08:00","id":408362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=408283#post408283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's blatant pandering and bad writing.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to Loxosceles, Titania has done this before and has been doing it for decades. She has surrendered to She-Hulk without a fight to show solidarity for her struggle to replace Ben Grimm in the Fantastic Four, says he, and that Absorbing Man surrendered to Eric Masterson out of respect for giving him a good fight once after Creel had just beaten the Avengers and the Fantastic Four unconscious single-handedly. He did not provide me with titles and issue numbers, but I am inclined to believe him. You may assign to this however much credibility you choose.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=408283#post408283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Titania was horribly characterized here. This is the woman who hates She-Hulk because She-Hulk is stronger than her.</div> </div> </div> </div>Loxosceles also mentioned that during the same period, She-Hulk and Titania have had bonding moments (in the middle of fights, but still) over the similarities they share. Again, however much credibility you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":271,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","user":"JimB","date":". 02-16-2015, 08:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T18:34:28-08:00","id":408413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=408362#post408362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to Loxosceles, Titania has done this before and has been doing it for decades. She has surrendered to She-Hulk without a fight to show solidarity for her struggle to replace Ben Grimm in the Fantastic Four, says he, and that Absorbing Man surrendered to Eric Masterson out of respect for giving him a good fight once after Creel had just beaten the Avengers and the Fantastic Four unconscious single-handedly. He did not provide me with titles and issue numbers, but I am inclined to believe him. You may assign to this however much credibility you choose.<br /> <br /> <br /> Loxosceles also mentioned that during the same period, She-Hulk and Titania have had bonding moments (in the middle of fights, but still) over the similarities they share. Again, however much credibility you want.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's possible but I certainly don't remember that. Writers do have very different styles and caused characters to act different and I've read enough comics to know there are too many different writers that have changed the characters several times. It just didn't feel like the characters at all in this case and felt like this was just trying to inject the writers beliefs on to the character in a way that was just felt shallow. Like in a look at my new character, she's better than the old and everyone loves her for it, sort of way. This would have been more believable if they played it a little more realistic and a little less caustic like Absorbing man's unnecessary reference to something he probably wouldn't care about in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 02-16-2015, 09:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T18:44:48-08:00","id":408446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=408413#post408413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's possible but I certainly don't remember that.</div> </div> </div> </div>He didn't feel like going through his records for a casual conversation, and I don't feel like asking him to so I can use him to score points in an argument he isn't in. It was after Secret Wars and during the era She-Hulk was in the Fantastic Four; that's the best I can do for you.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T08:03:40-08:00","id":408977,"title":"","content":"anyone reading Unbeatable Squirrel Girl? I'm in the mood for more upbeat super-heroing, but I'm afraid it will amount to the same &quot;hur hur, this silly-named heroine is the most powerful being in the Marvel Universe&quot; joke over and over...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T09:57:41-08:00","id":409064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=408977#post408977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">anyone reading Unbeatable Squirrel Girl? I'm in the mood for more upbeat super-heroing, but I'm afraid it will amount to the same &quot;hur hur, this silly-named heroine is the most powerful being in the Marvel Universe&quot; joke over and over...</div> </div> </div> </div>I looked at the art and decided not to bother. It's pretty bad. Especially considering we could have gotten the people who did the power pack minis a few years ago to draw it. I much rather preferred GLA back.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T12:35:43-08:00","id":409221,"title":"","content":"The art style is very different from what I've seen (there are previews online if you want to look) and the story seems to focus more on her and her life than the repeating joke.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T14:37:33-08:00","id":409336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorwen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=407710#post407710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, Battle World is a part of the Secret Wars. There are some interesting cross overs between titles. Age of Ultron vs Marvel Zombies being one of the real out theres. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Secret Wars starts on free comic day with a free Issue Zero. I'm thinking about picking up Marvel for this at least. I was really disappointed with how they treated All-New X-Men, but knowing this is going to be a mess any way might make it fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats still confusing to me. The Secret Wars Crossover creates Battle World? Or The crossover is Battle World? In which case, why is it called Secret Wars? Maybe I'm just being dense...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T14:50:51-08:00","id":409345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=409064#post409064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I looked at the art and decided not to bother. It's pretty bad. Especially considering we could have gotten the people who did the power pack minis a few years ago to draw it. I much rather preferred GLA back.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh. Art got me out of the She-Hulk book. I loved the premise, I liked the way the story was going, I really liked that they were setting her up in a new location with and developing a supporting cast and other decisions I favored. The comic was doing a lot of things the way I wanted some comic to do. But. The art is <b><i>horrible</i></b>. I tried to keep reading, but I couldn't. The artwork ruined the book for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T14:57:23-08:00","id":409352,"title":"","content":"I think Gotham Academy has pretty good art. It's sort of a newish style, there's definitely some anime influence, but it's all keeping in tone with the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T16:05:18-08:00","id":409390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=409352#post409352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Gotham Academy has pretty good art. It's sort of a newish style, there's definitely some anime influence, but it's all keeping in tone with the story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm...the artwork does look good, and the premise is somewhat intriguing. I think I'll give that one a shot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T18:47:08-08:00","id":409487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=409345#post409345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Heh. Art got me out of the She-Hulk book. I loved the premise, I liked the way the story was going, I really liked that they were setting her up in a new location with and developing a supporting cast and other decisions I favored. The comic was doing a lot of things the way I wanted some comic to do. But. The art is <b><i>horrible</i></b>. I tried to keep reading, but I couldn't. The artwork ruined the book for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah it's a very visual medium so when part of it sucks no matter how good the writing is it completely sucks but if you want cute comics I'd suggest the power pack miniseries by Gurihiru Studios they did some of the airbender comics and had concept art for the new squirrel girl series.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T07:46:40-08:00","id":416494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=409336#post409336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thats still confusing to me. The Secret Wars Crossover creates Battle World? Or The crossover is Battle World? In which case, why is it called Secret Wars? Maybe I'm just being dense...</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I understand it is the multivers is colliding and parts of the various Earths merge, one of the two is actually destroyed, or both are destroyed. At the start they are all there as they show on their map as a quasi single world. As to the name they kind of hint that, like before, this whole thing is being orcastrated by something. Really everything I've seen has been vague with heavy hints to this or that. They seem to be saving any real answers for Issue #0.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T16:26:44-07:00","id":509292,"title":"","content":"I'm bummed that Death Vigil is unlikely to continue past the first arc. Too bad. It has amazing art, good characters, good dialogue, barely any flaws. Pretty much all the reviews highly praise it too, everybody I have seem comment about it found it fantastic...and yet sales are tanking and it will probably end in issue 8. I hope in the future Nebezial (Stjepan Sejic) finds a way to continue it, and manages to make it an ongoing as he wanted, or at least gets to tell the first 3 arcs he had initially planned.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://nebezial.deviantart.com/journal/f-k-it-it-s-death-vigil-for-EVERYONE-531698214\" target=\"_blank\">He is posting issues for free on his Deviantart page under the reasoning that, in this age of Kickstarters and Patreons, people are willing to fund things based on teasers...how about having the whole thing?</a> Go read it, issues one to four are already available. If you like it, buy it! Then shove it in your friends faces and make them buy it too! Heck, preorder the trade paperback as well! It is a long shot, but maybe things can still be turned around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T16:36:21-07:00","id":509297,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't say it was flawless, though either did you. I'd certainly be willing to throw some money at a Kickstarter, their art has always been beautiful. But just getting it for free is nice too. He's got Sunstone available for purchase, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-09-2015, 09:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T21:08:55-07:00","id":509560,"title":"","content":"Just finished reading Secret Wars #1. Wow. Both the writing and the art were amazing. Hickman certainly knows how to spin an exciting story. Beware, however: you might be lost if you haven't read any of his Avengers work in the last year or so.<br /> <br /> Such an excellent start to the crossover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T00:15:11-07:00","id":509689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=509297#post509297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't say it was flawless, though either did you. I'd certainly be willing to throw some money at a Kickstarter, their art has always been beautiful. But just getting it for free is nice too. He's got Sunstone available for purchase, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately he said he doesn't have the patience and focus needed for a Kickstarter (and with how many projects he already juggles, I don't think he would have the time, especially considering all the rewards for various milestones that are part of the process). So it is a step short of a pay-what-you-want comic now, a pay-if-you-want one.<br /> <br /> As for sunstone, yes the first volume is available. Though, of course, every page also gets posted for free on his Shiniez deviantart account and once it is all done, he already said he will post for free the versions used for the print runs, with updated art and text (mostly corrections to his many typos).<br /> <br /> Also, I'm hoping one of his other projects, Teen Witchblade, gets off the ground and works out better than Death Vigil. It looks like it would be just as entertaining and possibly funnier, and hopefully having name recognition will make it sell better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T01:31:07-07:00","id":509732,"title":"","content":"Every few years I try, but I can never get into Witchblade. I managed to follow the Darkness for a long while before I got tired of it. I was hoping the new-ish Artifacts series would get me into it but I keep finding other things to read instead.<br /> <br /> No idea what Teen Witchblade would be like, though it makes me think of <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sabrina_the_Teenage_Witch\" target=\"_blank\">Sabrina</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T02:49:52-07:00","id":509756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=509732#post509732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every few years I try, but I can never get into Witchblade. I managed to follow the Darkness for a long while before I got tired of it. I was hoping the new-ish Artifacts series would get me into it but I keep finding other things to read instead.<br /> <br /> No idea what Teen Witchblade would be like, though it makes me think of <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sabrina_the_Teenage_Witch\" target=\"_blank\">Sabrina</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>While long time Witchblade readers (not me, I just read the first few issues way back then) likely will get some particular enjoyment out of it, the series has a completely independent canon (think of it as one of those alternative reality things). Also, if you <i>want</i> an idea of what it would be like, <a href=\"http://nebezial.deviantart.com/gallery/42514070/twitch\" target=\"_blank\">check out his gallery for it</a>, which even includes the first 13 pages of issue one.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T12:50:49-07:00","id":510140,"title":"","content":"Still not pleased with the way the X-Men are being shuttled off world to a new planet because the Terrigen Mists kill mutants. I was really hoping Marvel would get the movie rights back after the shitty 3rd movie, but I'm liking the First Class series and wish Fox and Disney could work out a shared continuity.<br /> <br /> Wolverine will be reincarnated/resurrected as an Inhuman, I'm betting my money now. Whether it's literal or spiritual is up for debate, they've already retconned Scarlet Witch and Quicksilver.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T16:02:52-07:00","id":510219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=510140#post510140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still not pleased with the way the X-Men are being shuttled off world to a new planet because the Terrigen Mists kill mutants. I was really hoping Marvel would get the movie rights back after the shitty 3rd movie, but I'm liking the First Class series and wish Fox and Disney could work out a shared continuity.<br /> <br /> <b>Wolverine will be reincarnated/resurrected as an Inhuman, I'm betting my money now</b>. Whether it's literal or spiritual is up for debate, they've already retconned Scarlet Witch and Quicksilver.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll take that bet. PayPal?<br /> <br /> Wolverine will always and forever be a mutant. Retconning Wanda and Pietro's history simply made sense. Especially since their histories were so screwed up to begin with. They're not touching Polaris because she actually fits as Magneto's daughter.<br /> Also, Wanda and Pietro's popularity pales in comparison to Logan's.<br /> <br /> I agree with you on everything else. Sadly, everything Fox touches, they destroy. Fantastic Four is going to be a disaster of mammoth proportions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T16:05:11-07:00","id":510221,"title":"","content":"I'm usually not big on retcons, but this is one I am totally on board with. They're bringing back Mayday Parker! Oh, happy day!<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/CEng4K-UgAAe3UK.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/457-arcanus-dicere","name":"Arcanus Dicere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T17:09:53-07:00","id":510254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=510140#post510140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still not pleased with the way the X-Men are being shuttled off world to a new planet because the Terrigen Mists kill mutants. I was really hoping Marvel would get the movie rights back after the shitty 3rd movie, but I'm liking the First Class series and wish Fox and Disney could work out a shared continuity.<br /> <br /> Wolverine will be reincarnated/resurrected as an Inhuman, I'm betting my money now. Whether it's literal or spiritual is up for debate, they've already retconned Scarlet Witch and Quicksilver.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find it very frustrating the way they've been handling mutants, especially with their declarations of who is wrong and who is right. I'm not a big Marvel fan but X-men were one of the first comics I got into years and years ago and while I finally managed to appreciate them again with some mental tricks, I really think they're getting the shaft.<br /> <br /> Wolverine, who is so famous for killing people that, 'I'm the best there is at what I do,' is his motto and specifically refers to it, and he's probably got so many pictures of him standing on top of or surrounded by a pile of bodies he's created that you could fill an entire comic with it and still have some left over for a second issue, somehow has the moral high ground when telling Cyclops off for standing up for mutant rights and because he killed Professor X, while possessed by the Phoenix Force. Never mind how many times Wolverine has been possessed or mentally controlled by the Hand or Weapon X or even Apocalypse when he became Death.<br /> <br /> It seems like they really took Brevoorts words to heart with a lot of their writing.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://wac.450f.edgecastcdn.net/80450F/comicsalliance.com/files/2011/05/tom-brevoort.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> I'm not that big of an X-men fan to begin with, and outside of that circle there's a very few characters that I like consistently. But they're all set up to be drastically changed, with Medusa breaking up with Black Bolt to go for Johnny Storm, the X-men Academy kids completely forgotten in favor of pushing the boring Quentin Quire. Emma and Cyclops breaking up and after years of not going a month without someone telling Cyclops he's wrong, him just giving up for no reason and saying they're right.<br /> <br /> When they clearly are not.<br /> <br /> So I'm trolled out. Secret Wars is going to have a new start for X-men, I think they'll have a drastic change, such as not being in the same universe as the Avengers and probably cut down to just two comics. Whatever it is, I'll be missing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T14:27:08-07:00","id":512338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=510140#post510140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still not pleased with the way the X-Men are being shuttled off world to a new planet because the Terrigen Mists kill mutants. I was really hoping Marvel would get the movie rights back after the shitty 3rd movie, but I'm liking the First Class series and wish Fox and Disney could work out a shared continuity.<br /> <br /> Wolverine will be reincarnated/resurrected as an Inhuman, I'm betting my money now. Whether it's literal or spiritual is up for debate, they've already retconned Scarlet Witch and Quicksilver.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that Bendis ruined the X-men and GoTG and made the worst run that manages to make Chuck Austin's look Passable and Ultimatium, well no not as bad as ultimatium but still fucking awful. I really don't care myself. I also am not happy with slott either. Between that and Nu52 I've pretty much been forced to fucking stick to Indies and the series that get cancelled in 12 issues because Spiderman and the X-men could be the best portrayal of either series in a goddamn decade and it still sells sub-20K and dies quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T17:18:12-07:00","id":512403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=512338#post512338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Considering that Bendis ruined the X-men and GoTG and made the worst run that manages to make Chuck Austin's look Passable and Ultimatium, well no not as bad as ultimatium but still fucking awful. I really don't care myself. I also am not happy with slott either. Between that and Nu52 I've pretty much been forced to fucking stick to Indies and the series that get cancelled in 12 issues <b>because Spiderman and the X-men could be the best portrayal of either series in a goddamn decade and it still sells sub-20K and dies quickly.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>It sold 26k in the month of March, and that's just from comic shops alone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T17:28:45-07:00","id":512406,"title":"","content":"While it was nice seeing Julian Keller in a comic again, it did seem like the writer didn't know anything about him. Plus they cancelled thirty-two other comics because they're ending their universe and the whole concept might not fit in, as there may no longer be a school for younger mutants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T18:29:47-07:00","id":512440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=512403#post512403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It sold 26k in the month of March, and that's just from comic shops alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's still unfortunately low. It was an exaggeration but I was referring to things like X-factor and Legacy or the pre-52 Blue Beetle. Both DC and Marvel tend to have way better writers working on niche titles that fall off quickly while crap writers smear shit on the pages call it a day and still get 100K+ numbers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T20:19:57-07:00","id":512501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=512403#post512403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It sold 26k in the month of March, and that's just from comic shops alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>I gotta go with Epimetheus on that -- those are low numbers, even by today's market (which operates at about half the numbers from a couple or three decades ago). I also second the &quot;...better writers working on niche titles that fall off quickly while crap writers smear shit on the pages[,]call it a day and still get 100k+ numbers.&quot; I have several friends -- one of whom is a long-term comic collector/expert since he was kid in the 70's -- who are finally so sick to death of both Marvel and DC (in terms of comics-as-written vs. the broader concepts they have in the characters) that they officially stopped collecting as of this month, cancelling all their subscriptions -- some of which they had literally had for decades -- and washing their hands of the industry as a whole. I don't blame them. I only keep up every few months w/Wonder Woman (which I've read since the 70's) because my subscription is free (via a special review arrangement); if shit turns out this summer with her mild revamp (along with Superman, et al,) as I expect it to, I myself may sever the last direct contact I have with comics as an industry, as well. (I didn't even bother with FCBD this year, at all, and felt no compulsion to -- I'm that sick of it.)<br /> <br /> While comic book properties may be having a golden era in the movies (between the last and present decades), the published industry as a whole is sucking balls....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T08:35:54-07:00","id":512944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=512440#post512440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's still unfortunately low. It was an exaggeration but I was referring to things like X-factor and Legacy or the pre-52 Blue Beetle. Both DC and Marvel tend to have way better writers working on niche titles that fall off quickly while crap writers smear shit on the pages call it a day and still get 100K+ numbers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. Especially not today. There are only 4 titles that are regularly doing 100k plus. Two of them are Star Wars titles with fantastic creative teams. The other two are actually fun books, if not quick reads. Lower numbers today are a bit skewed, since Marvel and DC are both making good money on digital sales. Those weren't around 5-10 years ago. Not like today. The digital market is huge now.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not trying to argue with you, however. Just pointing out sales data.<br /> <br /> I do agree to a point that Marvel and DC have definitely dropped in quality over the last few years. Image and Dark Horse are pumping out better books on a monthly basis and it's not even close. Crossovers are one of the problems, but they're not likely to stop any time soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T12:05:49-07:00","id":513193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=512944#post512944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> since Marvel and DC are both making good money on digital sales. Those weren't around 5-10 years ago. Not like today. The digital market is huge now.</div> </div> </div> </div>(Just jumping back in...)<br /> <br /> Oh -- yes, that is true. My response after Ep's was more in line with the straight numbers of printed today vs. a decade or two ago -- digital absolutely makes a big difference in terms of offsetting the figures in that regard, no question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T12:50:26-07:00","id":513250,"title":"","content":"To be fair, there ARE a few excellent comics the Big 2 are currently putting out.<br /> <br /> If you're not reading Jason Aaron's Thor run, you're wrong. Yes, that includes his run with Female Thor(she's awesome). Hawkeye is a great book, as is Daredevil.<br /> <br /> Over at DC, Scott Snyder's Batman run has been fantastic. Also...I think that's about all I favor at DC. I'm admittedly more of a Marvel fan than DC. Always have been.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T15:09:47-07:00","id":513348,"title":"","content":"Batman &amp; Robin has been telling a very solid story, it helps that they've kept pretty much the same writer. Grayson is really popular. Gotham Academy and Gotham by Midnight, both good. Catwoman's taken a new twist that looks like it's lasting, though a comic about a mob boss isn't everyone's style.<br /> <br /> Voodoo could have been good. How I lament for the things that could have been, but it was cancelled years ago.<br /> <br /> Not one of the Big Two but Jem and the Holograms is a surprisingly good comic. Mike Costa has been consistently killing it with the Cobra side of GI Joe and I expect he'll keep doing it with Snake Eyes: Agent of Cobra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T13:07:53-07:00","id":514418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=513348#post513348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Jem and the Holograms is a surprisingly good comic. .</div> </div> </div> </div>I wanted to like it but they didn't keep it 80's and yeah I know there are people who wouldn't be able to get into it if it were dated as much as the original show was but come on if it's not set in the 80's then it's just not the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T04:52:07-07:00","id":515048,"title":"","content":"That trailer for &quot;Legends of Tomorrow&quot; looks impressive. &quot;Supergirl&quot; doesn't look so bad either.<br /> <br /> Legends of Tomorrow:<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4MubNoWQiSc\" data-code=\"4MubNoWQiSc\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/4MubNoWQiSc/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Supergirl:<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Lm46-envrHo\" data-code=\"Lm46-envrHo\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Lm46-envrHo/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","user":"Shadowflame","date":". 05-15-2015, 10:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"