e":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=521746#post521746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does anyone feel about the reveal of Thor's new identity? I'm personally in a &quot;enjoy the journey and don't worry about the destination&quot; kind of mind frame, but nevertheless, I'm disappointed that it was such an obvious choice for the writers to make.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I do think it is somewhat disappointing, at this point I don't really care. That comic turned out to be quite underwhelming for me, both in terms of writing and artwork, and have stopped reading it. Which is a bit surprising, considering I liked Jason Aaron's previous work on Thor well enough.<br /> <br /> Also, it remains to be seen how much it will even matter, since she may well not retain the super-heroic identity once the current ultra-mega-giga-event is done.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T16:33:31-07:00","id":526072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=521746#post521746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does anyone feel about the reveal of Thor's new identity? I'm personally in a &quot;enjoy the journey and don't worry about the destination&quot; kind of mind frame, but nevertheless, I'm disappointed that it was such an obvious choice for the writers to make.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah.... *sigh* It <i>is</i> a rather disappointing choice.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I wish it was agent Solomon. Would have pleased me much better. Actually, I think this issue has single handedly killed my desire to renew my subscription, while after the last issue, when I thought it was Solomon, I was really excited. Oh well.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":1041,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","user":"brjedi26","date":". 06-23-2015, 11:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T07:56:22-07:00","id":535581,"title":"","content":"I think just about everything since the All-New started and the gearing toward the Secret Wars has been a bunch of failed opportunities. All that build up with this as the pay off. Like finally getting to have sex with the woman of your dreams just for it to be the worst sex of your life. &quot;Ummm....I think it best we pretend this never happened.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T11:35:11-07:00","id":562112,"title":"","content":"So, comic book people, can anyone suggest an X-Men comic (preferably available on Comixology or similar) that spends its time focused on kid-teenage-young adult mutants and how they handle their lives ostracised from the rest of the world? Super action fights are fine if they are there but not really what I'm looking for, I'm interested in how they handle things like making and losing friends as their powers appear, making and breaking of relationships, how they integrate (or don't) with the mutant community, etc.<br /> <br /> Human drama with mutants basically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T13:27:18-07:00","id":562175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=562112#post562112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, comic book people, can anyone suggest an X-Men comic (preferably available on Comixology or similar) that spends its time focused on kid-teenage-young adult mutants and how they handle their lives ostracised from the rest of the world? Super action fights are fine if they are there but not really what I'm looking for, I'm interested in how they handle things like making and losing friends as their powers appear, making and breaking of relationships, how they integrate (or don't) with the mutant community, etc.<br /> <br /> Human drama with mutants basically.</div> </div> </div> </div>Runaways???","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T13:41:46-07:00","id":562179,"title":"","content":"What's that one about? Do you think it's good or just a matching premise?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T13:59:24-07:00","id":562189,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_X-Men\" target=\"_blank\">New X-men's Academy</a> springs to mind. I prefer it more than Runaways, though that's a good comic too.<br /> <br /> Basically it just follows a bunch of students at the X-men academy, most of the focus is on two squads, each having an advisor from the standard X-men, Hellion and the Hellions advised by Emma Frost, and the New Mutants advised by Mirage. There are fights but it's not really focused on that, outside of the little arguments they have with each other.<br /> <br /> It does get a bit dark at the end, unfortunately.<br /> <br /> Not a Marvel title, but under the same idea I'd have to really recommend <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Intimates\" target=\"_blank\">the Intimates</a>, which is just fantastic.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://40.media.tumblr.com/tumblr_lvyy7pSEPq1qacy2so1_1280.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Both have a school dance issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T14:17:23-07:00","id":562220,"title":"","content":"I was reading New X-Men with the Helions etc. but it seemed to just suddenly time skip to having grown up characters in issue 16 which left me just...confused and annoyed.<br /> <br /> Edit: I mean...time jump to cut out major parts of their development, likely some of the most formative years of their lives? Joining back in when they're essentially different characters making the first 15 issues largely irrelevant?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","user":"Scutarii","date":". 06-20-2015, 05:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T15:51:01-07:00","id":562283,"title":"","content":"Yes, there was a shift in the writing when they moved over. Intimates is all one writer, but it's only 12 issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T02:42:24-07:00","id":562764,"title":"","content":"Is it a complete/satisfying story in your opinion at 12 issues? I don't mind short, I just don't want to hit issue 12 and have it end in the middle of something interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T20:54:13-07:00","id":575993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=562220#post562220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was reading New X-Men with the Helions etc. but it seemed to just suddenly time skip to having grown up characters in issue 16 which left me just...confused and annoyed.<br /> <br /> Edit: I mean...time jump to cut out major parts of their development, likely some of the most formative years of their lives? Joining back in when they're essentially different characters making the first 15 issues largely irrelevant?</div> </div> </div> </div>New X-men starts at x-men academy to House of M than continues. House of M is one of many comic wide crossovers that falls out into new x-men. I would read new X-men until the run ends and then pretend it's over.<br /> <br /> The X-universe does a spiral into the trash heap outside of fringe titles like X-factor and Spiderman and the X-men. Utopia's okay but AVX and bendis and aaron basically destroy the universe. They don't like X-men they clearly don't other than a few characters and they don't care about continuity or backstories.<br /> <br /> <br /> The first two series of Runaways and Young avengers is fine. However 3rd series for both is awful and unnecessary. Young Justice is really nice but in the 90's before it turns into teen titans which has been Consistently one of the worst books DC has published in the last 20 years.<br /> <br /> I've heard decent things from Gotham Academy but haven't read it. Avengers academy isn't bad but does decline in quality by the end. Avengers undercover and the one before it is complete trash. Ignore them.<br /> <br /> Teen books are hard to do well and normally don't turn out well. There are some I'm forgetting but most of them suck. S<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T20:59:29-07:00","id":575997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=562764#post562764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it a complete/satisfying story in your opinion at 12 issues? I don't mind short, I just don't want to hit issue 12 and have it end in the middle of something interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for the late response. I think the whole story was complete, and there's a definite end but you might feel some stories weren't tied up, maybe.<br /> <br /> Gotham Academy's good but it's not really that far into the series. They're not super-powered or mutants. Well...at least it's not a big part of the story.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://retconpunchdotcom.files.wordpress.com/2015/06/grapple-gun-of-my-dreams.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-02-2015, 12:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T23:44:06-07:00","id":577109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=575993#post575993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New X-men starts at x-men academy to House of M than continues. House of M is one of many comic wide crossovers that falls out into new x-men. I would read new X-men until the run ends and then pretend it's over.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry I'm not sure I understand. They have a big crossover that completely changes a series, does the New X-men pick up from where it actually left off in issue 16 at some point or does it just switch over to being a different series entirely that just happens to have a few shared character names?<br /> <br /> You know. I kinda, sorta want to get into comics (as I have basically never read them before, just floated on the periphery watching things like the X-Men cartoons) but from the outside it seems a complicated impenetrable mess. People then say that you should just dive in, pick something and follow it to see if it's for you. Well, I did that and I quite liked it...until it just changes randomly on me into something else and all of a sudden I'm not enjoying it, I'm pissed I bothered in the first place. Now I learn it's not just bad writing, it's some external series bleeding over and ruining everything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sorry for the late response. I think the whole story was complete, and there's a definite end but you might feel some stories weren't tied up, maybe. </div> </div> </div>Thanks, I've been looking but can't find it on Comixology (which has a dreadful search function). Do you know of any other good (legitimate!) sites I can get it? I'm not really looking for a hard copy but will grab one if it's not exorbitant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T22:25:57-07:00","id":578225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=562112#post562112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, comic book people, can anyone suggest an X-Men comic (preferably available on Comixology or similar) that spends its time focused on kid-teenage-young adult mutants and how they handle their lives ostracised from the rest of the world?</div> </div> </div> </div>NYX, but it's not for the easily disgusted or scandalized.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T05:56:55-07:00","id":578643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=578225#post578225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> NYX, but it's not for the easily disgusted or scandalized.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty vague. Care to elaborate a bit, or would that require too many spoilers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T07:32:03-07:00","id":578741,"title":"","content":"The protagonist is a teenage prostitute who cuts herself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T10:30:30-07:00","id":578924,"title":"","content":"Kiden is the protagonist, most of the story is from her pov, not Laura. But yeah, there's a lot of unpleasantness like that in NYX, sort of to be expected as it's more or less about a small group of homeless, underage mutants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfo