kedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T16:48:18-07:00","id":593303,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yTNJuUYybtU\" target=\"_blank\">Vertigo announced</a> a 3-month weekly schedule of new releases, including a new Lucifer series.<br /> <br /> Taking the place of Fables, winding down in the summer, is Red Thorn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T23:16:17-07:00","id":633178,"title":"","content":"The second issue of the new Archie comic came out and I'm surprised to say, as someone who had very little interest in Archie except for the live-action reunion's promise of skin to an adolescent, it's actually pretty good. I suppose I shouldn't be so surprised as Mark Waid seems to have been nailing it with his output in the last few years. Anyways, I like it. Betty seems to have more depth to her and they've mercifully added several characters to the main cast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T12:36:01-07:00","id":673349,"title":"","content":"I know I'm way behind on this one, but I just read <b>Wanted </b>for the first time.<br /> <br /> <br /> I want my money back. What was the point of that, really? And someone thought it should be a <i>movie</i>, too? I don't get it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T13:26:02-07:00","id":673371,"title":"","content":"The movie has exactly zero to do with the comic. Which is probably for the better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T14:32:46-07:00","id":673436,"title":"","content":"Mark Millar decided he could write for movies so all his TPB-aimed books basically test the waters for possible film projects.<br /> <br /> I was pleasantly surprised to find that Image's Beauty has been continued. It was part of their Pilot Season thing where readers get to vote on a bunch of #1 issues to see which one gets continued. I don't follow Image that closely but I've always been interested in the pilot season winners, because they never seem to get their #2 issues, or if they do, it's years afterward. Beauty won the contest in 2011, for instance. I've never bothered to look into the whys and wherefores, I just find it interesting.<br /> <br /> A lot of the Pilot Season comics seem pretty good. Genius depicted a sort of tactical genius growing up in a bad neighborhood in LA and with her people sort of declaring war on the police. It won in 2008 and got it's second issue in the past year when the protests rose up in Baltimore. Beauty was about a sexually transmitted disease that, surprise, makes you gorgeous. The story picks up a while afterwards when sufferers start dying and the police investigating the matter find out there might be a conspiracy behind the disease, just in time for the male detective to find his wife has been cheating on him by waking up and seeing himself turned good-looking in the mirror. Twilight Guardian, I think, was probably the most noteworthy one, with a troubled girl who patrols the streets of her suburb at night as a would-be crime-stopper. That one got the rest of its series a while ago, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T16:23:09-07:00","id":673527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=673349#post673349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know I'm way behind on this one, but I just read <b>Wanted </b>for the first time.<br /> <br /> <br /> I want my money back. What was the point of that, really?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never read it, myself. Never wanted too. In the last five to ten years, writer Mark Millar has been kind of famously contemptuous of comic books and their fans; he thinks he's too good for them and resents the people who keep supporting him by buying his work. I heard a pretty convincing argument that <b>Kick-Ass</b> is actually a middle finger to the fans of comic books, using the world as an example of how juvenile and stupid comic books are and Kick-Ass himself as an example of how juvenile and stupid comic book fans are. This mindset was visible to me as far back as his run on <b>Ultimate X-Men</b>, when he couldn't resist throwing in occasional snipes at how stupid comic book violence is. Doesn't much make me want to support his work.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T17:43:09-07:00","id":685078,"title":"","content":"Tried out Midnighter at the request of a friend. Read the first issue. Then read the next 3. This is a fantastic series that everyone should be buying. I know it's under the radar, but seriously...give it a try. The writer Steve Orlando gets Midnighter like no other(except for Ellis/Millar).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T09:50:07-07:00","id":685860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=673527#post673527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never read it, myself. Never wanted too. In the last five to ten years, writer Mark Millar has been kind of famously contemptuous of comic books and their fans; he thinks he's too good for them and resents the people who keep supporting him by buying his work. I heard a pretty convincing argument that <b>Kick-Ass</b> is actually a middle finger to the fans of comic books, using the world as an example of how juvenile and stupid comic books are and Kick-Ass himself as an example of how juvenile and stupid comic book fans are. This mindset was visible to me as far back as his run on <b>Ultimate X-Men</b>, when he couldn't resist throwing in occasional snipes at how stupid comic book violence is. Doesn't much make me want to support his work.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That pretty much, the point of his work is point a finger at you and tell you &quot;you are stupid for reading super hero comic books&quot; there a palpable contempt in his last works toward the superhero genre (Kickass, wanted &amp; old man logan A.K.A Marvel`s wanted) its similar to Alan moore hate of the genre just that, Moore has the balls to actually go out and do non superhero work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T16:53:45-07:00","id":690607,"title":"","content":"So, I've been reading Iron Man lately, thoroughly enjoying it, and eagerly awaiting the next Invincible Iron Man volume. However, apparently it spins off Secret Wars. Now, I generally dislike crossovers, particularly with X-Men - no disrespect to people who like X-Men, but the continuity is waaay more complicated, just due to the sheer number of significant characters, while Iron Man has comparatively few and as such is easier to follow.<br /> <br /> Apparently Secret Wars involves universes colliding/fighting, and is a big ol' crossover with, near I can tell, nearly everyone. And, to my wildly inexpert eye, it looks... kind of silly.<br /> <br /> So, my question is, to anyone who has read/is reading Secret Wars: do I need to read it to understand Iron Man going forward? I know you can't say for sure because the next Iron Man isn't out yet, but is there some kind of significant stuff for Stark that I can't infer on my own?<br /> <br /> I'll read it if I have to, but I'm pretty sure I wouldn't like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T18:16:42-07:00","id":690670,"title":"","content":"It's a lousy event, one main comic and several other minis. The gist of it is 'ending' all the other, alternate universes and combining everything into one universe, presumably trying to keep the 'best' versions of certain characters. The core story is told in Secret Wars #1-#8.<br /> <br /> If you just want to read the Iron Man related stuff there's a, I believe, 5 issue mini called Armor Wars that focuses on Iron Man.<br /> <br /> If you want to skip the event entirely, Invincible Iron Man #1 and #2 should be coming out this month.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-05-2015, 09:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T19:54:17-07:00","id":690792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=690670#post690670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a lousy event, one main comic and several other minis. The gist of it is 'ending' all the other, alternate universes and combining everything into one universe, presumably trying to keep the 'best' versions of certain characters. The core story is told in Secret Wars #1-#8.<br /> <br /> If you just want to read the Iron Man related stuff there's a, I believe, 5 issue mini called Armor Wars that focuses on Iron Man.<br /> <br /> If you want to skip the event entirely, Invincible Iron Man #1 and #2 should be coming out this month.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like Infinite Crisis? <br /> <br /> Cool, I'll check out Armour Wars, thanks :-)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T21:09:16-07:00","id":690860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=690792#post690792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like Infinite Crisis?</div> </div> </div> </div>More like the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crisis_on_Infinite_Earths\" target=\"_blank\">Crisis on Infinite Earths</a>, with a dash of New 52, since there's essentially a universe-wide reboot with new comics to get new people interested.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Cool, I'll check out Armour Wars, thanks :-) </div> </div> </div>Let us know how you like it, I've heard very little about the entire crossover. There's an Illuminati comic coming out of it starring one of my favorite characters that I might start following.<br /> <br /> I'm reading some Lobster Johnson at the moment, always been an intriguing entity in the Hellboy mythos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-06-2015, 12:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T04:30:31-07:00","id":691030,"title":"","content":"My view of Armor Wars:<br /> <br /> Not really a fan. It's not <i>bad</i>, by any measure, but it was such a different context, and the characters were so different, that I found it difficult to get engaged with the story. The relationships weren't really handled very well, the 'twist' was eminently predictable, and because I didn't know the 'rules' of the world, the unexpected things I had no context with which to interpret or anticipate them.<br /> <br /> It was cool, and interesting, it just didn't work due to the lack of context or history.<br /> <br /> Maybe it would have made more sense if I'd read Secret Wars, but I doubt it, based on the intro-text.<br /> <br /> Just my opinion, for what it's worth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T11:26:09-07:00","id":691467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=690607#post690607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, my question is, to anyone who has read/is reading Secret Wars: do I need to read it to understand Iron Man going forward? I know you can't say for sure because the next Iron Man isn't out yet, but is there some kind of significant stuff for Stark that I can't infer on my own?<br /> <br /> I'll read it if I have to, but I'm pretty sure I wouldn't like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Secret Wars has been fantastic. Hickman is a master craftsman that's carried two years worth of side stories into a comic that I'm simply loving. Probably my favorite major crossover between the big two over the last 5 years. It's been extremely well-received on numerous sites like Kotaku, both for the strength of the main Secret Wars series(currently stuck on #5) and for some of the excellent mini series running at the same time.<br /> <br /> Planet Hulk, Hail Hydra, A-Force, Weird World, and Old Man Logan are just a few of the great titles currently still going.<br /> <br /> If I were you, however, I'd simply wait for this month's Invincible Iron Man #1. Should be a great jumping on point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":95,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","user":"Fat Larry","date":". 10-06-2015, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T15:54:55-07:00","id":691768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=691467#post691467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Secret Wars has been fantastic. Hickman is a master craftsman that's carried two years worth of side stories into a comic that I'm simply loving. Probably my favorite major crossover between the big two over the last 5 years. It's been extremely well-received on numerous sites like Kotaku, both for the strength of the main Secret Wars series(currently stuck on #5) and for some of the excellent mini series running at the same time.<br /> <br /> Planet Hulk, Hail Hydra, A-Force, Weird World, and Old Man Logan are just a few of the great titles currently still going.<br /> <br /> If I were you, however, I'd simply wait for this month's Invincible Iron Man #1. Should be a great jumping on point.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with crossovers is that unless you read all the titles involved, your knowledge of the context of the events is inevitably going to be lacking. Like the Axis crossover, I could follow the events, but a lot of the nuances of the characters interactions was totally lost on me, and I know nearly nothing about Red Skull himself.<br /> <br /> A well written one can minimize these issues (heh. Pun unintended), but they're kind of inevitable, and the difficulty in being involved grows exponentially with the more titles involved. And with a huge one like this... yeesh.<br /> <br /> Plus I'm not really a fan of the multiverse concept anyway. I get where it's coming from, but I'm not sure it works as an ongoing plot device.<br /> <br /> I'll let it pass for now. Hopefully the new Invincible Iron Man will either follow on from Superior reasonably linearly, or it's understandable in itself. Was kind of disappointed with how Superior ended, or rather didn't end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T16:37:37-07:00","id":691787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=691768#post691768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with crossovers is that unless you read all the titles involved, your knowledge of the context of the events is inevitably going to be lacking. .</div> </div> </div> </div>Lacking, yes. Doesn't mean you won't find it enjoyable. I didn't read Secret Avengers or New Avengers, and still find Secret Wars to be quite easy to follow. Then again, I'm a big fan of Hickman's writing, so I knew what to sort of expect going in.<br /> <br /> Marvel is actually kicking a lot of ass right now, in my opinion(and my wallet's opinion). Sure, I'd love the giant crossovers to stop, but until then, there are still a ton of titles that are separate with fantastic creative teams.<br /> <br /> DC/Vertigo's got a ton of good stuff on the horizon as well, which has me excited.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T23:24:35-07:00","id":692036,"title":"","content":"Wow, Marvel is really going to extremes to bring back Wolverine. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T06:53:14-07:00","id":692411,"title":"","content":"Based on Invincible Iron Man #1:<br /> <br /> OK, neither the comic itself or Armor Wars explained why Stark isn't evil anymore. It was a barely justified plotline, albeit one I enjoyed, but give it an actual ending!<br /> <br /> I'm going to have to read Secret Wars, aren't I? Damn, I just know I'm not going to enjoy it...<br /> <br /> Oh, an IIM was vaguely interesting. Need to see more before I come to an opinion, but it was a strong enough opening (although the twist seemed to rely on knowledge I just don't have for its impact, which was unfortunate).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","user":"Allan53","date":". 10-07-2015, 09:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T12:29:41-07:00","id":692847,"title":"","content":"The one, true Batgirl has returned. Long live Cassandra Cain.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately written by Scott Snyder who seems to want to entangle her romantically with Tim Drake.<br /> <br /> But still, it's really great to have her back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T17:51:49-07:00","id":696637,"title":"","content":"Hey she was romantically entangled with him before the Universe rebooted. Snyder's no Puckett and the Artist is no Scott, but the action scene with her vs that Assassin was pretty good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T23:54:28-07:00","id":696824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=696637#post696637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey she was romantically entangled with him before the Universe rebooted.</div> </div> </div> </div>They barely had appearances together, and there wasn't any romance between the two in any of them. Though there was some in an alternate universe, but she was also partnered off with Superman in an alternate universe for all that means.<br /> <br /> Big surprise at the end of the comic.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://insidepulse.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/10/Batman-and-Robin-Eternal-1-spoilers-review-5.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Batman with a gun is nothing new, and he's clearly been mind controlled, but he's one of the few big characters in the JLA to have mostly avoided mind control scenarios. Superman seems to get turned evil every few years, but Batman's usually portrayed as the one who fights it off. I've never been a fan of the Robins, seeing them as mostly useless, Damian's changed my mind on that front.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-11-2015, 03:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T11:44:12-07:00","id":697588,"title":"","content":"Doctor Strange #1 was quite possibly the best comic I've read this year. Fantastic story and art. And I'm not a big Bachalo fan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T12:04:49-07:00","id":697656,"title":"","content":"I like Bachalo a lot.<br /> <br /> Having finished up Lobster Johnson's run, I've been catching up on Nailbiter and Birthright. The former is about an 'interrogator' who is called to a small town after a friend of his, an investigator for the FBI, phones him late one night explaining he's found out why the town produces so many serial killers, including the most recent, the Nailbiter. It's an interesting mystery with colorful characters and, importantly, a colorful background. The Nailbiter was found not guilty for some reason, and is also living in town, where his high school love is the local sheriff. The latter starts with a father in a family looking for his kid, who seems to have wandered off during a day at the park. The kid goes missing, the man's life falls apart, his wife leaves him, everyone suspects him of having killed his son. Which is when he's called in by the FBI because they found some big, scary dude in the woods who seems to know about the lost son. When the family gathers there, they see it's more than that, as he claims to be their son, despite it being one year later and him clearly being like twenty years older. He claims he was taken by magical creatures to a strange magical land where he was destined to be the hero that would defeat the dark overlord, and now that that's done, he's back to kill some of the overlord's lieutenants, who reside on our world. Everyone thinks he's crazy, but the father is sure it's their son. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">And it turns out destiny was subverted.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Still liking Archie, I tried the new Jughead but found it to be pretty meh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 10-11-2015, 06:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T18:56:36-07:00","id":698285,"title":"","content":"Nailbiter sounds good. How's the violence? I understand it'll have some, but some of the things I've read that are kind of similar tend towards the unnecessary degree of gore, which turns me off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T19:37:29-07:00","id":698306,"title":"","content":"Like a horror movie that might appear in the theaters. R-rated, but it's not Crossed or Stitched. Violence is there but not really the main focus. Lots of 'startling' stumbling upon bodies or macabre scenes, though.<br /> <br /> <br /> A non-plot spoiling page, some of the strange citizens of Buckaroo, whose populace has a tendency to go slasher when they move away.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://1.bp.blogspot.com/-UlTSRHQEyBY/U_oBdajH5KI/AAAAAAAAJRU/gVJA4nzBagU/s1600/Nailbiter%2B002%2B(2014)%2B(Digital)%2B(Darkness-Empire)%2B020.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T05:57:36-07:00","id":698525,"title":"","content":"Ah, if that's representative, then I can handle that without too much drama.<br /> <br /> I'll check it out, thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T15:37:19-07:00","id":713102,"title":"","content":"So, I was happy to ignore him, but Dr Doom is coming up way too often in Iron Man for me to continue doing so. So, can someone explain to me what his goals are? Because it seems sometimes he's a bad guy for no readily apparent reason beyond &quot;wanting to destroy the Fantastic Four... for no readily apparent reason&quot;, other times he's almost a heroic figure, fighting to stop Red Skull and other major-league bad guys.<br /> <br /> What about Latveria? I've only seen it in bits, but generally it seems a nice-ish place to live, when it's not being ravaged by Asgardian entities or evil mentor figures. Doom has even noted that when he ruled it (after being deposed for like the 50th time by now, I'm guessing?), the people were healthy, and it seemed pretty functional as countries go.<br /> <br /> Even Doom's role in Secret Wars seems ambiguous at worst, but I don't have even 1% of the context to understand <i>anything</i> in that series, so I'm not at all confident in that appraisal.<br /> <br /> He's clever, resourceful, clearly capable of long-term planning and multiple redundancies (plus, if I read correctly, millions of years old?), and the one country he rules, albeit off-and-on, seems to do OK. And I'm fine with him being a complex figure, but the way everyone reacts to him when I do see him is like he's just always bad for badness sake.<br /> <br /> So, can someone give me the skinny on him? I read his entry on ComicVine, but it didn't really help very much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T15:56:41-07:00","id":713136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://kotaku.com/dr-doom-is-very-different-now-1737884609\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://kotaku.com/app/uploads/2025/07/kotaku-1200x900-1.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://kotaku.com/dr-doom-is-very-different-now-1737884609\" target=\"_blank\"> Dr. Doom Is Very Different Now - Kotaku </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://kotaku.com/dr-doom-is-very-different-now-1737884609\" target=\"_blank\"> http://kotaku.com/dr-doom-is-very-different-now-1737884609 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> At the end of the last version of the Marvel Universe, Dr. Doom became something like a hero. He snatched enough power from near-omnipotent beings to stop </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Doom and Stark have always been connected. The new Iron Man series(of which #2 just released today) goes into a bit of depth into how they work in current continuity. The above article is pretty good at giving some info.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T16:12:54-07:00","id":713150,"title":"","content":"Yes, I read the issue; enjoyed it. But that really raises more questions than answers about who Doom is: so far as I can tell, Tony's just a tool. Which much though I like him would hardly be out of character for him, but but again, lacking in knowing what is going on. I know they've clashed a lot in the past, but that tells me nearly nothing about who Doom is and why this is supposedly so wildly out of character for him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T16:19:06-07:00","id":713161,"title":"","content":"Dr. Doom is an egotistical tyrant who believes his way is the only way. He has never asked for help without an ulterior motive that <i>usually</i> leaves those who help him suffering while he comes out ahead. I can't think of a good example of it occurring with Iron Man, I don't read the character's solo stuff, but Dr. Strange and Dr Doom's Triumph and Torment depicted this very nicely, as did the Dr. Doom and the Masters of Evil comic. Stark even refers to a time when they went back in time and Doom abandoned Stark there.<br /> <br /> Add to that the fact that he's generally considered one of the smartest villains in comics, as well as having technological expertise comparable to Tony Stark, and magical expertise comparable to Dr. Strange, he's very much a threat. I can't even think of any actual appearances of him near others while choosing not to wear his armor, or at least his mask, which is also comparable if not more powerful than Tony Stark's Iron Man armor, so Stark's disbelief that the nicely dressed man asking for help is actually Dr. Doom is understandable.<br /> <br /> It's probably worth noting that while he's had many defeats and been overcome in many individual comics, writers tend to handwave those and claim, 'It was just a Doombot,' referring to the robots Dr. Doom occasionally sends in his stead, which could never match his level of genius, cunning and power.<br /> <br /> Odds are there is going to be a flashback or monologue that will explain it all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-21-2015, 07:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T16:46:53-07:00","id":713187,"title":"","content":"JLA seems to be taking off. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">First Batman becomes Bat-God, and now the rest are following. Superman has become the God of Strength, Batman the God of Knowledge, Flash the God of Death, having merged with the Black Racer, and Shazam the God of Gods. Lex Luthor, left to languish on Apokalips, has become the God of Apokalips.</div></div> </div> </div> I'm not a fan of Johns' writing and his run on Justice League hasn't changed that. Like a lot of Johns' work, there's a lot of big and flashy events but they don't have much of an impact or depth. If you aren't a fan of everything Johns is a fan of, they're pretty dull. He has a tendency to write around the League to get to the characters he really wants to write about. There's an entire issue where the only Leaguer is Cyborg who only appears for a few pages, standing in the darkness waiting for someone else to tell him a story.<br /> <br /> Gotham Academy is good as usual. I worry it's going to be hijacked by events but considering the characters and who and what they are, that doesn't have to be a bad thing. When some supervillain devastates Gotham, through the teenage students at the Academy and their teachers you can see the impact it has on the normal citizenry. The main protagonist, Olive, is very antagonistic towards the concept of the Dark Knight, and from her perspective it's easy to see why. But the book has really evolved to a more ensemble cast, and her best friend Maps is enamored with all things Bat-related. Even, perhaps, his son. This weeks issue the characters, having formally acknowledged themselves as 'teenage detectives,' of a sort, use the cover of an athletics competition to escape from their chaperones and do some field research, digging into the city hall of records. I've previously mentioned that Batman isn't a major character in this, and it's true, he doesn't actually show up much, but in this issue Red Robin, Tim Drake, does run into them while doing his own research for the Robin War.<br /> <br /> Batman &amp; Robin Eternal is solid, but it would be nice to have more answers. Almost everyone's together now, with Harper Row, Stephanie Brown and Cassandra Cain all at the Batcave with Dick Grayson, Jason Todd and Tim Drake, trying to dissect the mystery brought up by the previous comics. It's interesting to see their interactions, but they are pretty invested in the strange confession of Batman and their rising suspicions of how it ties into the latest threat to Gotham so they aren't exactly soap opera-ing yet. Considering how Batman Eternal came out, I expect more interesting scenes of bonding and rivalries blooming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T18:13:57-07:00","id":713350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=713161#post713161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dr. Doom is an egotistical tyrant who believes his way is the only way. He has never asked for help without an ulterior motive that <i>usually</i> leaves those who help him suffering while he comes out ahead. I can't think of a good example of it occurring with Iron Man, I don't read the character's solo stuff, but Dr. Strange and Dr Doom's Triumph and Torment depicted this very nicely, as did the Dr. Doom and the Masters of Evil comic. Stark even refers to a time when they went back in time and Doom abandoned Stark there.<br /> <br /> Add to that the fact that he's generally considered one of the smartest villains in comics, as well as having technological expertise comparable to Tony Stark, and magical expertise comparable to Dr. Strange, he's very much a threat. I can't even think of any actual appearances of him near others while choosing not to wear his armor, or at least his mask, which is also comparable if not more powerful than Tony Stark's Iron Man armor, so Stark's disbelief that the nicely dressed man asking for help is actually Dr. Doom is understandable.<br /> <br /> It's probably worth noting that while he's had many defeats and been overcome in many individual comics, writers tend to handwave those and claim, 'It was just a Doombot,' referring to the robots Dr. Doom occasionally sends in his stead, which could never match his level of genius, cunning and power.<br /> <br /> Odds are there is going to be a flashback or monologue that will explain it all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool, thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> What is Dooms goal? Just &quot;rule the world&quot; seems a bit... I don't want to say petty, but oddly limited for someone of his insight and capabilities.<br /> <br /> \u200bOr have I just misread the whole character?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T18:52:46-07:00","id":713416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=713350#post713350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool, thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> What is Dooms goal? Just &quot;rule the world&quot; seems a bit... I don't want to say petty, but oddly limited for someone of his insight and capabilities.<br /> <br /> \u200bOr have I just misread the whole character?</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically that was it. He believed he knew the only way to create a perfect utopia without starvation or need or violence or crime. Under Doom's fist. To be fair, in this world, anyone who perpetrated violence or crimes would be instantly executed. He believes that the superheroes of the Marvel universe are not going to reach the same result, it can only be reached through him. To Doom, Doom is the hero, the rest are pretty much false prophets.<br /> <br /> He has side interests, like showing up Reed Richards, especially as a father, and dealing with his mother issues.<br /> <br /> Arguably the Secret Wars event shows that, even with near omnipotence and unsurpassed loyalty, he can't exactly keep everything under control. It's possible that the Victor von Doom asking for Tony Stark's help is a changed man who is honestly reaching out for assistance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T19:23:21-07:00","id":713477,"title":"","content":"Interesting...<br /> <br /> I wonder if it's worth reading the Fantastic Four just to learn more about him...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T19:56:03-07:00","id":713554,"title":"","content":"That is just what I did.<br /> <br /> Not for the same reasons, but when I was getting back into comics I found the only things I really read in Marvel were X-men. A friend had a ton of FF and they had a sort of reboot in the 90s so I picked up from there. I am no longer interested in the Fantastic Four. There's some good stories there but if you just want Doom there's some Doom-oriented compilations you can grab, and I know he's had many series of his own, like the one I mentioned before and the Books of Doom. Triumph and Torment is a really good story, beautiful art too. I never got into the Kirby era stuff but I know his work with other comics and if you do decide to start from the beginning you should start there, rather than the reboot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T05:09:47-07:00","id":731948,"title":"","content":"OK, well, I've now read the <i>Books of Doom</i>, and <i>Triumph and Torment</i>, and while I strongly preferred <i>BoD</i> to <i>T&amp;T </i>(T&amp;T wasn't bad, by any measure, but it was clearly a product of times, while <i>BoD</i> was a more modern, and this more relatable from my perspective, take) I did come to one firm conclusion: Doom is <i>freaking awesome</i>!<br /> <br /> Hell, I'm still not convinced he's actually evil, per se - random stranglings aside (that was... weird). Extreme? To be sure. But, well, kind of necessary, in a way. I don't know much about the F4, but he certainly seems more engaging than them to me.<br /> <br /> 'He conquered Latveria!' Well, yes, but in fairness it kind <i>needed</i> conquering.<br /> <br /> Totally awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T15:24:37-07:00","id":735986,"title":"","content":"Yes, it's what makes him one of the most popular villains in Marvel. A vague description doesn't do him justice. And he's certainly more engaging than the Fantastic Four, who have lagged behind other groups in becoming relevant to modern times.<br /> <br /> He's also much better to have around in humorous circumstances.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://40.media.tumblr.com/tumblr_m2jz8jGx2E1qzizmho1_1280.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T18:58:52-08:00","id":750417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=713102#post713102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I was happy to ignore him, but Dr Doom is coming up way too often in Iron Man for me to continue doing so. So, can someone explain to me what his goals are? Because it seems sometimes he's a bad guy for no readily apparent reason beyond &quot;wanting to destroy the Fantastic Four... for no readily apparent reason&quot;, other times he's almost a heroic figure, fighting to stop Red Skull and other major-league bad guys.<br /> <br /> What about Latveria? I've only seen it in bits, but generally it seems a nice-ish place to live, when it's not being ravaged by Asgardian entities or evil mentor figures. Doom has even noted that when he ruled it (after being deposed for like the 50th time by now, I'm guessing?), the people were healthy, and it seemed pretty functional as countries go.<br /> <br /> Even Doom's role in Secret Wars seems ambiguous at worst, but I don't have even 1% of the context to understand <i>anything</i> in that series, so I'm not at all confident in that appraisal.<br /> <br /> He's clever, resourceful, clearly capable of long-term planning and multiple redundancies (plus, if I read correctly, millions of years old?), and the one country he rules, albeit off-and-on, seems to do OK. And I'm fine with him being a complex figure, but the way everyone reacts to him when I do see him is like he's just always bad for badness sake.<br /> <br /> So, can someone give me the skinny on him? I read his entry on ComicVine, but it didn't really help very much.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh man, I LOVE Doom. He's just so bombastic and over the top. While I like the Fantastic Four in theory just fine (and Kirby's early work on the series was stellar), the villains clearly outstrip the Four. I can't speak much to the context of his appearances in Iron Man (I've only seen some preview materials and am not a big Bendis fan. He tends to twist characters in inorganic ways to match his very narrow style) or recent events in the character's life (the recent big Marvel event, Secret Wars, got postponed, so there's a mystery of how that ended and how that gap effects the current comics), I can provide some context for his background.<br /> <br /> Doom is like a big dumb Bond villain. He's like Marvel's version of Dracula, sharply dressed and always screaming &quot;FOOLS!&quot; at his opponents. The central conceit is that he's so full of pride that he can't accept his own failures. He blames Reed Richards for his facial scars, and Richards has become sort of his white whale. Doom is a fierce egotist and blames Richards' meddling for most if not all of his failures. There's been strong hints throughout recent runs of the series that he's covetous of Reed's family. For the past few years, the Fantastic Four has largely been under the domain of writer Jonathan Hickman. He was at the center of the last event, where the infinite realities were facing imminent destruction, and Doom saved the few remaining worlds by cobbling them together into a strange patchwork planet where he ruled as god. In this rewritten reality he basically assumed Reed's role, taking his wife and child as his own. I think the implication (not fully realized since the event hasn't ended), is that having a family has changed Doom for the better. He understands the need for compassion outside of his own self interest, and Reed and Susan Richards are missing from this world. There seems to be a thread similar to that in Superman comics where, had Superman never existed, Lex Luthor would have been the savior of mankind.<br /> <br /> As for Latveria, it's a fascist Eastern European state ruled by an army of killer robots designed to look like Doctor Doom. It's exactly as delightfully goofy as it sounds, and it's pretty representative of everything about the character. That said, they seem to be moving away from that direction, which strikes me as a bit of a shame.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T19:03:48-08:00","id":750422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=713187#post713187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">JLA seems to be taking off. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">First Batman becomes Bat-God, and now the rest are following. Superman has become the God of Strength, Batman the God of Knowledge, Flash the God of Death, having merged with the Black Racer, and Shazam the God of Gods. Lex Luthor, left to languish on Apokalips, has become the God of Apokalips.</div></div> </div> </div> I'm not a fan of Johns' writing and his run on Justice League hasn't changed that. Like a lot of Johns' work, there's a lot of big and flashy events but they don't have much of an impact or depth. If you aren't a fan of everything Johns is a fan of, they're pretty dull. He has a tendency to write around the League to get to the characters he really wants to write about. There's an entire issue where the only Leaguer is Cyborg who only appears for a few pages, standing in the darkness waiting for someone else to tell him a story.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Johns is capable of being a good writer, but he hasn't really been hitting it in years and years.Lately it seems like he's performing a poor rendition of Grant Morrison's Greatest Hits. So many of the beats in his Justice League run feel like they've already been done. Grant Morrison teased the idea of the Justice League becoming New Gods in Final Crisis then seemed to pull back, realizing that it was a bit too on the nose. The prevalence of the Crime Society of America earlier in his JL story seemed like a pale shadow of how Morrison revived the characters and walked that thin line of goofiness and relevance. And now Johns has set up the idea of Batman facing Joe Chill, which Morrison already pulled off superbly in his Batman run.<br /> <br /> He's done it before. His whole &quot;War of the Light&quot; story in Green Lantern took a clever little Alan Moore story about the fall of the Lanterns and turned it into a Michael Bay style adventure about Rainbow Bright heroes. Modern day Johns just feels like a kid smashing together action figures and riffing off the ideas of stories that have already been told by better writers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T02:13:22-08:00","id":753453,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"http://i651.photobucket.com/albums/uu232/ilikemonkeys56/Iron%20Man%20High%20Five_zpsxbgsl1pk.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Ah, Tony, never stop being awesome <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","user":"Allan53","date":".  EDIT: Added link to picture per nofathers advice 11-04-2015, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T10:04:56-08:00","id":754364,"title":"","content":"Yeah, you can't upload pictures, you have to link to already existing ones using [img]link[/img]<br /> <br /> As someone who's never particularly liked Midnighter, though enjoyed his interactions with other characters I have liked, I've been keeping up with his new series. Nice, major surprise that is apparently causing some hubub, mostly from the <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">'Why can't my character be in a happy relationship?'</div></div> </div> </div> people. The return of an old, insidious villain who might be Midnighter's match and who happens to be one of my faves.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://img2.wikia.nocookie.net/__cb20110706142941/marvel_dc/images/6/6b/Prometheus_(New_Earth)_008.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-04-2015, 01:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T13:58:10-08:00","id":760920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=713102#post713102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about Latveria? I've only seen it in bits, but generally it seems a nice-ish place to live, when it's not being ravaged by Asgardian entities or evil mentor figures. Doom has even noted that when he ruled it (after being deposed for like the 50th time by now, I'm guessing?), the people were healthy, and it seemed pretty functional as countries go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ummmm.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://i2.wp.com/i37.photobucket.com/albums/e56/tbondurant/ff_084_p05.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> [img]https://i0.wp.com/i37.photobucket.com/albums/e56/tbondurant/ff_084_p06.jpg[img]</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T14:12:43-08:00","id":760935,"title":"","content":"1. Cool, we have a quote-notification feature now! That's going to be handy <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> 2. That's clearly from, what, the 60's or 70's? Not exactly the most nuanced portrayals, back then (generally speaking). I'm not dismissing it, but as comics have advanced, it seems their portrayals have gotten more complex.<br /> <br /> Also, he's a despot. OK, fair criticism. That doesn't inherently make him <i>wrong</i>, for all we know (based on that panel, my knowledge of Doom is what I could pull off Comicvine, Books of Doom and Triumph and Torment) Latervia was in a situation where they needed a despot - it's rare, but it happens. That doesn't mean his people aren't generally happy. We are a pretty free and safe society here in Australia, but we still have people rebelling against the 'tyranny' of psychologists or the 'genocide' of animals (their words).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T15:51:05-08:00","id":760994,"title":"","content":"Latveria is generally depicted as a country fairly well off but with bouts of extreme tyranny depending upon the whims of its ruler. There's generally two sides of the country shown. One where everyone is horribly oppressed all the time, and another where people celebrate the rulership of Doom openly when visitors come, then return to their mundane lives beyond that. It's a country where the 1% is one person, and the 99% is everyone else.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/hPs4BeC.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Everyone who is well off there is well off directly as a result of Doom making them that way. And every citizen is a potential subject in one of his experiments. The only other option is death, and since he is a master of the dark arts, even that may not be an escape.<br /> <br /> There was a story arc where he confronted the Wakandan Panther God, who sought to determine whether his motives were pure. And while it is true Doom has good intentions for everyone, and best intentions for himself, his specifications for a utopia are close-mindedly specific. There is no crime because people who consider crime are killed by Doom. He considers himself a good ruler, when compared to every tyrant and despot in history. Everyone will be united, under Doom, and there will be no exception.<br /> <br /> As I said before, Doomworld, arguably, shows the flaws in his beliefs, or at least the bad side of it. Given the most power in the universe he uses it to torment his old enemies, and bumps people like Apocalypse and Mister Sinister to his dukes, ruling smaller 'nations' in his stead however they desire, providing they follow his commandments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-08-2015, 06:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T16:00:01-08:00","id":761001,"title":"","content":"Interesting ideas. I'll spend a few brain-cycles on it and get back to you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm particularly intrigued by the 'doombot-poverty' bit...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T16:02:31-08:00","id":761005,"title":"","content":"He's the 1%. He's a master of magic and science, he could turn the whole place into a paradise if he wanted, but a paradise wouldn't serve him. It's the mix between his code of honor and purity of belief, as well as his ruthlessness and self-centeredness that make him such a good character. If he was more one or two dimensional he wouldn't be nearly as interesting.<br /> <br /> Of course as of now he's not a ruler and they may or may not have changed his personality, similar to how the only Reed Richards in the world is the Ultimate one who turned evil because Sue Storm dumped him. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://p.dreamwidth.org/d8a4e4e4f2ea/-/i60.tinypic.com/dos8ps.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So this may be a new Dr Doom entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-08-2015, 07:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T16:52:03-08:00","id":761043,"title":"","content":"Sorry, I'm going to need some context for the Richards/Storm bit there - seems like she's breaking up with him for... no clearly explained reason (within that one page, of course)?<br /> <br /> Personally, I liked the idea in Books of Doom, where the hatred of him was a result of his deal with Mephisto to fight for his mothers freedom. No idea how well supported that is generally, but I find it appeals to me.<br /> <br /> And could he &quot;fix&quot; Latveria? I'm just thinking, aren't most super-geniuses in comics kind of known for having little impact on the world beyond their fancy machines - the Reed Richards is Useless trope? Don't know how well-founded that idea is, just seems relevant. So holding Doom to not &quot;fixing&quot; Latveria kind of opens a door to making most of the supposed 'heroes' kind of terrible too, by the same standard?<br /> <br /> Been re-reading Superior Iron Man lately. Apart from the kind of silly initial setup, and the lack of an ending, thoroughly enjoying it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T17:23:06-08:00","id":761059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=761043#post761043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, I'm going to need some context for the Richards/Storm bit there - seems like she's breaking up with him for... no clearly explained reason (within that one page, of course)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think she explained her reasons there, actually. But that's about it. It was the Ultimate universe where characters were viewed more on the most common perceptions of them, so Captain America was stuck in an uber-patriotic WW2 mindset, Reed Richards more of a genius who actually changed things, and Sue Storm more 'Mrs Fantastic' than anything else. Until she went her own way, and hooked up with Ben Grimm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And could he &quot;fix&quot; Latveria? I'm just thinking, aren't most super-geniuses in comics kind of known for having little impact on the world beyond their fancy machines - the Reed Richards is Useless trope? Don't know how well-founded that idea is, just seems relevant. So holding Doom to not &quot;fixing&quot; Latveria kind of opens a door to making most of the supposed 'heroes' kind of terrible too, by the same standard? </div> </div> </div>Yes, he could. Generally the world-at-large is considered static, it can't change much. Outside of side universes, the United States is going to stay the United States. The Ultimate Universe had a massive change that divided the US into three or four different 'countries.' But made-up nations like <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Latveria\" target=\"_blank\">Latveria</a> and <a href=\"http://dc.wikia.com/wiki/Gamorra_Island\" target=\"_blank\">Gamorra</a> and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Madripoor\" target=\"_blank\">Madripoor</a> and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kahndaq\" target=\"_blank\">Kahndaq</a> can and do change, often. Latveria overthrew their tyrant, for instance, and its not the first time Doom has been deposed. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pokolistan\" target=\"_blank\">Pokolistan </a>was ruled by General Zod in a similar fashion, he improved the land and gave everyone everything they needed and wanted, except freedom.<br /> <br /> All that said, Richards is said to have done a lot of work, but it's mostly wrapped up in testing or other things. I think his most widespread invention is the unstable molecules that the Fantastic Four and their allies often use to make up their outfits. That was before the reboot, however, and now Reed Richards seems to make monsters.<br /> <br /> I'm glad you're liking Superior Iron Man. Superior Spider-Man takes a similar approach. Doctor Octopus manages to possess Peter Parker and acts as Spider-man. While there were some people who disliked it, it had a surprisingly large and vocal fandom. Or Iron Man's side of the Civil War.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-08-2015, 08:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T13:32:47-08:00","id":764347,"title":"","content":"This came out before this week but I didn't see it until the other day. I've mentioned my issue with the way Marvel was taking mutants and their portrayal of Cyclops as incorrect in managing the X-men and how others were being touted as right. In a horrible fashion.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://i.newsarama.com/images/i/000/104/466/original/UncannyAvengers5Havok_02.jpg?1367019589\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> The writer of this caught a lot of flak from people for its view of how minorities should act but his response was that anyone who had a problem with it should do something with 'hobo piss.'</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> But issue 600 of the Uncanny X-men came out. Brian Michael Bendis is the writer and a lot of people don't like him. I've never had a problem with his work, and I believe I've mentioned I think his work on Sam &amp; Twitch is probably the greatest cop series in comics, and Powers doesn't come far behind. I'm a big Bat-fan so this is directly competing with the award winning Gotham Central comics. Anyways, he wrapped up, not everything, but Cyclops' war against authority by staging a peaceful 'Million Mutant March' of sorts with mutant heroes and villains and civilians to show that, they may be different, but they want the same things everyone else does. Magneto even made a show.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://comicsverse.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/11/ss-2015-11-04-at-10.30.36.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> And Beast was sort of shunned by the community for his misdeeds and trying to deflect matters on Cyclops. So that was cool.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately it's sort of a light week for comics. For me, at least. Bruce Wayne is getting married, so some poor woman is going to die. Batman &amp; Robin Eternal is going good but it's still scratching the surface of a mystery. It turns out Tim Drake's Marty Stu'ness may have an in-world explanation. Birthright, a comic I previously mentioned here, is going well, and GI Joe: a Real American Hero is going strong and headfirst into the Cobra World Order event which should be interesting, even if its not the newer GI Joe that's thrilled me the past few years. Speaking of newer GI Joe, Transformers vs GI Joe is an insane trip and I have to recommend it to anyone who might be interested in either franchise. It helps that it's using the old Kirby style and are just running with the craziness of the animated series'.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://comicsalliance.com/files/2014/12/TFJ06.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I mentioned Vertigo was coming out with some new lines a while back. So far I've been unimpressed but Slash &amp; Burn came out yesterday and I'm going to keep my eye on it. It seemed a little too disjointed, but the story is appealing. It's about a woman who's chosen to become a firefighter to make up for her pyromaniac younger years, as well as to help cope with her disorder.<br /> <br /> Because of the X-men thing I was quick to jump on a comic that was coming out that I wanted to read but was avoiding. A few years ago Marvel came out with the Illuminati comic, basically a bunch of the 'leaders' of Marvel people came together with some of the more arrogant heroes and decided that they would decide on things to influence and problems to tackle 'in the name of Earth' without regard for what other heroes thought. It wasn't nearly as cynical as I make it out, but pretty much every 'good intention' ended in death and danger. A new Illuminati comic was announced in Marvel's 'All New, All Different' reboot, with a different focus. <br /> <br /> This one was about <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hood_(comics)\" target=\"_blank\">the Hood</a>, one of my favorites over in Marvel, and his gathering of supervillains to, once again, create a sort of crime syndicate. He had done this before, with the backing of supernatural powers, basically creating a supervillain union. If a hero was bothering you, other members of the union would help you deal with it. If you didn't have the manpower or technology needed for a certain crime, you now had the connections to find what was necessary. If you were caught and sent to jail, you had dozens of teleporters or other powered individuals who could break you out. All you had to do was agree to play by the rules and kick some money into the pot. Organization isn't cheap. This, I think, helped explain some things in the world such as villains constantly breaking out or appearing with weapons and science beyond their capability for no reason. Due to matters beyond his control, things sort of fell apart, but since the reboot he's setting it back up and already has some members.<br /> <br /> I wanted to mention this because as I was reading it, I kept thinking of this thread. See, it focuses on his attempt to recruit one villain in particular. Titania. I know the hullaballoo of the She-Thor thing was all over the internet but I didn't care at the time. Or now, really. But I always found Titania and her relationship with the Absorbing Man pretty interesting, which was why it drew my attention when <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=405229#post405229\">it popped up on this thread</a>. And the Illuminati comic starts out with Absorbing Man in prison and talking with his wife before being sent to what sounds like a worse, more high security prison, He wants to break out and go back to crime, she wants to go straight. And she tries, but the first part of the book shows how hard it is for an ex-con, especially one who is sort of an equivalent to a terrorist, to live a normal life, especially in the same city as heroes that keep bumping into her and expecting the worst. Anyways, despite the retread of ideas, it was a good comic showing things from a villains point of view.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://p.dreamwidth.org/5db1bfa964ee/-/abload.de/img/illuminati2015-001-00e6rwl.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T17:14:20-08:00","id":764538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=761059#post761059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm glad you're liking Superior Iron Man. Superior Spider-Man takes a similar approach. Doctor Octopus manages to possess Peter Parker and acts as Spider-man. While there were some people who disliked it, it had a surprisingly large and vocal fandom. Or Iron Man's side of the Civil War.</div> </div> </div> </div>I heard about the Spider-man story. Not having read it, it sounds pretty different though? Superior Iron Man is a side of Tony that is a legitimate, if usually controlled / suppressed, part of him. Whereas someone coming in and mind controlling is a pretty different kettle of fish? Not saying it can't be good, but I'm not seeing the mapping over between them thematically?<br /> <br /> What is really appealing to me about SIM is that this was always a possibility with Tony. He's always been kind of megalomaniac, and a compulsive fiddler who wants to help people. It's really just been his moral code and that of his friends that has kept him from doing something like this. The charging money and other specifics are more clearly wrong, but the near forcible 'upgrading' of the people around him? Intriguing, philosophically speaking. <br /> <br /> And that's why I like it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T17:25:55-08:00","id":764549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=764538#post764538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I heard about the Spider-man story. Not having read it, it sounds pretty different though? Superior Iron Man is a side of Tony that is a legitimate, if usually controlled / suppressed, part of him. Whereas someone coming in and mind controlling is a pretty different kettle of fish? Not saying it can't be good, but I'm not seeing the mapping over between them thematically?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's fair to say they were a usually controlled or suppressed part of him so much as they were a minor part of him, they really didn't need to be suppressed or controlled because of that. The AXIS event inverted things, what was minor became major, what was major became minor. Tony Stark is completely capable of being a dick on his own, but that leads to more things like the road to Civil War or his repeated attempts to create the Illuminati. Superior Iron Man was basically wearing a helm of opposite alignment, having been magically altered.<br /> <br /> In either case you have a character who is ordinarily a hero being subverted by an outside force bent on twisting it. The issue with Otto, who possessed the dead Spider-man, was that he was affected by Spider-man's own memories, which arguably corrupted him into being more of a hero. So the subversion was two-fold. I was just throwing it out there.<br /> <br /> Hobgoblin was apparently the big standout in the AXIS event.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-12-2015, 08:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T18:15:08-08:00","id":764581,"title":"","content":"Two thoughts occur to me. First, while I can see where you're coming from, I'm going to have to respectfully disagree with your interpretation of the inversion event. If it was a major/minor-minor/major thing, then we'd see other signs of it - major traits would become much less prevalent. One of Tony's defining characteristics is his belief in the future and the ability of people to create it through technology. However, his actions in SIM can be seen as a continuation of that, albeit in a somewhat twisted form. They\u2019re really more remiscient of a Tony who has simply had his \u2018limitations\u2019 removed if you will, which seems to line up with how we saw it affect the other inverted characters; traditionally heroic types spoke a lot about being free of their previous limitations, while usually villainous types focussed more on how they now find their previous actions repulsive and terrible. Modelling it more as a simple \u2018morality switch\u2019, as silly as that notion is (and part of why I try to ignore the AXIS as much as possible) fits better. Even fits with the original intent of the spell; if you accept Xavier as purely or nearly-purely good (which seems to be how they spoke about him; I don\u2019t know X-men well enough to definitively comment) and Red Skull as purely or nearly-purely evil (again, consistent with how they spoke of him during the event which is my main benchmark), then flipping the good/bad switch fits, albeit not perfectly.<br /> <br /> If it was a major/minor thing, then I would more expect Tony to lose his interest in technology and the future \u2013 sure, we see a bit of that with him drinking and partying, but he\u2019s still interested in studying Teen Abomination, constructed a better suit and even built on Extremis 3.0. Twisted, to be sure, but reasonably consistent with his interest in technology and the future. Just more self-interested than usual. And control has often been a part of his character; look at what it took him to end up entrusting Pepper to run his company, and she\u2019s shown herself to be trustworthy and capable many, <i>many</i> times over. Even with the Most Wanted storyline, he did as much as he possibly could himself, relying on even those he trusted most as little as possible. I vaguely remember some side comment when he was building Resilient and the swarm and such that there were some questions about privacy or something. Plus there's the whole Illuminati storyline, which I'm not terribly familiar with so I shan't comment further beyond saying it sounds more like he's gone from subtle control to overt.<br /> <br /> The second point is that I try to ignore the \u2018external event twisting his mind\u2019 aspect of the story as much as possible, as hypocritical as that is. It just strikes me as kind of silly; morality is way too complex to be subject to a simple switch like that, so I try to ignore the origin of his new state and just view it as a result of some kind of trauma and him going overboard to compensate \u2013 again, consistent with past portrayal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T19:04:38-08:00","id":764611,"title":"","content":"I'd say the very fact that it's an inversion in the first place suggests its their major characteristics, and point out that Tony's magnanimity, bravery and heroism are the major parts that were inverted. Though I wouldn't use the terms good or evil, especially in Marvel. But that's just me and you've, honestly, probably read more of Iron Man than myself now so you've probably got a better handle on him.<br /> <br /> And I can fully appreciate the ignoring the external event part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T20:08:05-08:00","id":764658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=764581#post764581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if you accept Xavier as purely or nearly-purely good (which seems to be how they spoke about him</div> </div> </div> </div>Xavier is usually presented as a cross between Ghandi and Martin Luther King.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=764581#post764581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Red Skull as purely or nearly-purely evil</div> </div> </div> </div>Literally a Nazi. Describing him as a cross between Hitler and Skelator is almost disturbingly accurate.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=764581#post764581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It just strikes me as kind of silly; morality is way too complex to be subject to a simple switch like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you played Mage: the Awakening? When an Archmaster decides to play switcheroo with your Virtue and Vice, your moral compass gets pretty messed up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":6138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","user":"Mangle77","date":". 11-13-2015, 12:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T20:39:13-08:00","id":764691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=764658#post764658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have your played Mage: the Awakening? When an Archmaster decides to play switcheroo with your Virtue and Vice, your moral compass gets pretty messed up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have. I generally find it fairly silly, as well as the whole 'virtue/vice' system in more general. Much more in favour of the revised version, or the CWoD nature/demeanor system. I mean, it's always going to be flawed and imperfect, but at least it allows a greater degree of flexibility in description.<br /> <br /> And I personally wouldn't view something Archmasters are capable of as any kind of barometer - their power and role is usually pretty poorly defined. Even in the book meant for them it's not hugely coherent. They're really more intended as plot devices than something the players can meaningfully interact with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T20:41:03-08:00","id":764692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=764611#post764611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say the very fact that it's an inversion in the first place suggests its their major characteristics, and point out that Tony's magnanimity, bravery and heroism are the major parts that were inverted. Though I wouldn't use the terms good or evil, especially in Marvel. But that's just me and you've, honestly, probably read more of Iron Man than myself now so you've probably got a better handle on him.<br /> <br /> And I can fully appreciate the ignoring the external event part.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a fair amount of subjectivity - we are talking about interpretations, after all.<br /> <br /> In terms of what I've read, pretty much most things involving Iron Man since Extremis. Except most of the Secret Wars stuff - I tried, I did, I just didn't have nearly the context for any of it to make much sense to me. Which in no way makes me a superior interpreter, particularly since different writers have their own interpretations on top of our inevitable subjectivity <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T02:58:54-08:00","id":769835,"title":"","content":"So, to my shame, I've gotten a bit twitchy without my regular dose of Iron Man. Rather, with regular infusions of something interesting to read. So can anyone recommend something interesting, ideally that either I can pick up the beginning of easily or that doesn't require ten years of catching up? I didn't mind doing it with Iron Man, but I was already intrigued by the character in a way none of the other characters I've seen (except Doom, but I think I've read all there really is of him as a central character).<br /> <br /> EDIT: How about Thor? I confess this is probably be being manipulated, but the recent story about the new Thor being sick with cancer intrigues me; the idea of human fragility and godly power being combined sounds potentially interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","user":"Allan53","date":". 11-20-2015, 06:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T18:10:42-08:00","id":775715,"title":"","content":"Well, I read the new Thor, and while there was a bit of context missing - most notably why Odin has gone all Big Brother and why Thor is an outlaw - it was generally solid and enjoyable. Not sure how it'll go on, since Loki is still around and my past experience has not been kind to any story involving Loki, but the central premise seems solid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T19:04:18-08:00","id":775734,"title":"","content":"No idea, myself. I stopped reading Loki when she turned back into a guy, around the end of the Dark Avengers stuff when Hood disappeared.<br /> <br /> I've started reading Rumble, from Image comics. Only 9 issues in and it's a nice story but I don't want to get too invested as it doesn't seem like one that's going to go very far. It makes me think of Kill Six Billion Demons, but backwards. Basically, long ago, gods roamed the Earth. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://www.adventuresinpoortaste.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/02/rumble-3-slanjau-war-hound.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div> And thousands of years later, well, they still do, just not nearly as common. And Rathraq, seen above, has found a new body to inhabit after eons of...not. With his new body he's befriended poor Bobby, who's sort of just trying to keep his head down, run his father's bar and maybe get laid. Bobby's other, human friend is far more into the idea and wants to go around kicking ass while not really seeing anything beyond the glamour of a warriors life. Bobby's got an idea of it, presumably of his father who died in a mysterious fashion. Anyways, good art, catchy story.<br /> <br /> Bunch of good comics this week, though a lot of the reveals were more sad than anything. Ladytron's still in Grayson, though, so that's cool. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://1.bp.blogspot.com/-yD_d0UK3cIY/VjKoofgThWI/AAAAAAAANII/9mTQyYQ51Fc/s1600/Grayson%2B%252313%2B%25282015%2529%2B-%2BPage%2B23.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T23:13:36-08:00","id":775819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=769835#post769835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, to my shame, I've gotten a bit twitchy without my regular dose of Iron Man. Rather, with regular infusions of something interesting to read. So can anyone recommend something interesting, ideally that either I can pick up the beginning of easily or that doesn't require ten years of catching up? I didn't mind doing it with Iron Man, but I was already intrigued by the character in a way none of the other characters I've seen (except Doom, but I think I've read all there really is of him as a central character).<br /> <br /> EDIT: How about Thor? I confess this is probably be being manipulated, but the recent story about the new Thor being sick with cancer intrigues me; the idea of human fragility and godly power being combined sounds potentially interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of my experience leans towards the modern, so don't take it as a survey of the best stories in the characters' history, but...<br /> <br /> I really liked Matt Fraction's Iron Man. It's been a while since I've read it, but I recall it being pretty easy to get into (I didn't possess a particularly extensive knowledge of Marvel lore when I got into it). The only context you need to know is that it takes place after Civil War. Tony Stark waged a war against his fellow superheroes under the pretext of trying to implement a superhuman registration act. When the story begins, he's recently lost the struggle and is filled with regrets, and his attempts to finally address his flaws and overcome them is the driving force behind the series. The entire run spans about 60 issues and is collected as Invincible Iron Man.<br /> <br /> As for Thor, I haven't read the new stuff involving the female Thor, but I've read some of the stories that preceded it (also written by Jason Aaron), and they're pretty great. It frequently alternates and loops together different versions of Thor (himself as a young buck god, his modern incarnation, and a version of him in a bleak future where he's taken the throne of his father) to really strong effect. There's a good mix of heavy metal inspiration, classic mythology, and Kirbyesque weirdness blended together.<br /> <br /> That said, the best thing to come out of the Thor corner of the universe has been Kieron Gillen's take on Loki. He was writing a book for a while called Journey to Mystery about Loki (de-aged to a child. I can't even begin to explain) trying to not be such an evil sonuvabitch while still being a sneaky little bastard that was a lot of fun. Gillen then moved to a book called Loki, Agent of Asgard that cast him in a really delightful spy thriller.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 11-28-2015, 02:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T23:21:26-08:00","id":775820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=764658#post764658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Literally a Nazi. Describing him as a cross between Hitler and Skelator is almost disturbingly accurate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always been fond of the Red Skull being portrayed as a ruthless opportunist. He doesn't really believe in Nazism. Who cares about the &quot;Master Race&quot; when your only interest is yourself? Racism and nationalism are a means to an end for him.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> In my head he's less Hitler and Stalin, more Ayn Rand and Donald Trump.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T00:01:12-08:00","id":775831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=775819#post775819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Most of my experience leans towards the modern, so don't take it as a survey of the best stories in the characters' history, but...<br /> <br /> I really liked Matt Fraction's Iron Man. It's been a while since I've read it, but I recall it being pretty easy to get into (I didn't possess a particularly extensive knowledge of Marvel lore when I got into it). The only context you need to know is that it takes place after Civil War. Tony Stark waged a war against his fellow superheroes under the pretext of trying to implement a superhuman registration act. When the story begins, he's recently lost the struggle and is filled with regrets, and his attempts to finally address his flaws and overcome them is the driving force behind the series. The entire run spans about 60 issues and is collected as Invincible Iron Man.<br /> <br /> As for Thor, I haven't read the new stuff involving the female Thor, but I've read some of the stories that preceded it (also written by Jason Aaron), and they're pretty great. It frequently alternates and loops together different versions of Thor (himself as a young buck god, his modern incarnation, and a version of him in a bleak future where he's taken the throne of his father) to really strong effect. There's a good mix of heavy metal inspiration, classic mythology, and Kirbyesque weirdness blended together.<br /> <br /> That said, the best thing to come out of the Thor corner of the universe has been Kieron Gillen's take on Loki. He was writing a book for a while called Journey to Mystery about Loki (de-aged to a child. I can't even begin to explain) trying to not be such an evil sonuvabitch while still being a sneaky little bastard that was a lot of fun. Gillen then moved to a book called Loki, Agent of Asgard that cast him in a really delightful spy thriller.</div> </div> </div> </div>Read IIM, throughly enjoyed it. Honestly, it was part of what <i>really</i> drew me into Iron Man - Extremis was good, don't get me wrong, but IIM tended to show so much complexity to the character, and drew you into this pre-existing world without requiring the encyclopaedic knowledge some stories do.<br /> <br /> Thor, I've really only read two parts. The first couple dozen issues of Thor v1, up to the Hela/Dsir arc, and the newest issue with Jane Foster. I liked the new issue, not so much the older stuff - I got the feeling they were going for epic, but the characters just really failed for me. Baldur just failed and moped, Thor was ... strange, Tyr I also couldn't get a bead on, and Loki was so obviously evil that I found it amazing that the other gods hadn't killed/imprisoned him just on general principles. Made it really hard to get invested, at least for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T04:51:25-08:00","id":778925,"title":"","content":"So, I've recently been reading through She-Hulk, volumes 1 and 2. And before I say any more, I do enjoy it. The campy tone mixed with the serious moments, the self-aware nature of it, and the surprisingly complex portrayal of Jennifer Walters and She-Hulk and the examination of the line between them leading to questions of identity, it's really good and even with its problems well worth a read in my opinion. But... well, no series is without problems, and She-Hulk is no exception to this rule.<br /> <br /> I've spoken before of my lack of fondness for crossovers, and my opinion on that has not changed. However, She-Hulk, near I can tell, does something worse: it has crossovers, but doesn't really explain that it has, or really even note that they existed, yet allows them to have an impact on the story. Like She-Hulk <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">suddenly having destroyed a town, or having become a bounty hunter with a Skrull</span>, (colour-censored for spoilers) all of a sudden the whole context is different, and I have no idea why. The covers don't tell me &quot;This story is continued in Avengers #227&quot; or even do that asterix-thing where it tells you what it's referring to (OK, it does it sometimes, but not as a rule).Characters appear and disappear at semi-random, and I don't know if they're just off somewhere not doing anything, or if the author just doesn't like them, or if they're dead/an alien god/on a world of ducks. Which would be fine, it's just me needing to do a bit of legwork - sloppy, but can be addressed easily. Except they also have changes and stories which they deliberately don't tell for plot reasons, like where Jennifer Walters got the gamma-changer or whatever.So are they setting up potential plot, or is this the result of a crossover, or is this just bad writing? And when they do resolve the conflicts set up, like She-Hulk regaining the ability to shift between the forms (that doesn't count as a spoiler, it happens so often), it's not often done well - &quot;WHY DOES DOING A U-TURN BETWEEN UNIVERSES FIX HER MENTAL BLOCKS WHICH HAVE BEEN REPEATEDLY STATED TO BE ENTIRELY PSYCHOLOGICAL IN NATURE!?&quot;<br /> <br /> I <i>do</i> like She-Hulk, I do. I just want to like her more, and while she's not a badly written character, I'm tempted to say she's a badly <i>handled</i> character, if that makes sense. If you're looking for well-woven narratives, not really your friend. If you're looking for genuinely interesting characters with a lot of laughs, it's pretty much right on the money.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T13:52:47-08:00","id":779239,"title":"","content":"Batman v Superman trailer was pretty terrible. I'm not sure I can pinpoint all the reasons I feel this way, but I'm quite sure the movie will be a train wreck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T11:10:08-08:00","id":780629,"title":"","content":"Aside from Superman pulling Batman's cowl off so hard he takes the eye makeup with it I liked the trailer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T12:07:05-08:00","id":780651,"title":"","content":"It had some classic Clark and Bruce trash-talk.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i345.photobucket.com/albums/p388/proteus_lives/Scan11180.jpg~original\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> The parademons are an interesting new twist, implying some Darkseid involvement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T16:40:23-08:00","id":780773,"title":"","content":"Is Lois Lane meant to be Hispanic? Every now and then, I see her speaking Spanish; and in the books where she does, she has a darker skin tone colored in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T16:55:04-08:00","id":780785,"title":"","content":"I always put that down to her being a good reporter, and doesn't something like a third of the US speak Spanish as a first language? So it'd be a useful skill for her.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Sorry, according to Wikipedia it's more like an eighth, but hugely non-evenly distributed. Given that Metropolis is in the north-east (apparently), which isn't hugely Hispanophonic, then my conclusion isn't really supported.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","user":"Allan53","date":". 12-05-2015, 07:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T17:08:00-08:00","id":780791,"title":"","content":"Yeah, and she was an army brat so she'd probably have more exposure than an average American.<br /> <br /> Apparently she was originally modeled on a Joanne Kovacs, who was a model that the creators of Superman and Lois Lane hired. The writer later married her.<br /> <br /> It says she was Hungarian, but various changes were made over time, like her hairstyle changing to look more like Teri Hatcher during the Lois &amp; Clark series, and her violet eye color from the animated Superman series from the 90s.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://static.comicvine.com/uploads/scale_super/10/103530/4293328-3909518891-14194.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> There's a new comic out that looks pretty good, Sheriff of Babylon. Hard to tell how well it will do but it reminds me of the concept behind The Kingdom, namely, 'what would a murder investigation look like on Mars?' They dropped things down to a more terrestrial bent and put it in the Middle East. The main characters seem to be a police officer turned military contractor, trying to train a police force in Iran in 2003, and Sofia, an enigmatic power broker. The sheriff starts investigating things that may have him butt heads with Sofia when some of his trainees turn up dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-05-2015, 08:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T11:19:41-08:00","id":781219,"title":"","content":"Dr. Strange and Totally Awesome Hulk are simply fantastic books. Strange is on issue 3 right now, while TAH just started.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T16:46:03-08:00","id":781385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=781219#post781219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dr. Strange and Totally Awesome Hulk are simply fantastic books. Strange is on issue 3 right now, while TAH just started.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking as someone who's always looking for something good, why is Strange so good? I know the broad strokes of the character - doctor who mastered the mystic arts under the Ancient One, arguably the most mystically capable individual in the Marvel universe - but not much about the personality and types of stories and such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T17:12:11-08:00","id":781399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=781385#post781385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking as someone who's always looking for something good, why is Strange so good?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>(Scene: Doctor Strange #2. A mortal woman, Zelma Stanton, has come to Doctor Strange's Sanctum Santorum to have mystical parasites removed from her skull. They escape, forcing the Doctor to guide her through his home on a hunt for them.)</i><br /> <br /> <b>Zelma:</b> Um...are there supposed to be snakes on your coffee table?<br /> <b>Snake 1:</b> Hey girl. What's up?<br /> <b>Snake 2:</b> What's your hurry?<br /> <b>Doctor Strange:</b> Please do not talk to the snakes.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> That is why you should read this book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T17:13:45-08:00","id":781401,"title":"","content":"He's one of the harder characters to write for for Marvel, apparently. Generally he's a nice guy who sort of wavers between the more mellow 'nice guy with powers and responsibility' and more severe and stern 'you don't understand the powers you are dealing with!' type of attitude. Having read the first issues of both the new Dr. Strange, which admittedly has great art, I didn't see anything that particularly stood out in the story. And the new Hulk stood out even less. As much as I like Amadeus Cho, I found that tacking the powers of the strongest thing in the Marvel universe onto one of the smartest people on Earth managed to make him one of the most trite people in the Marvel universe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=781399#post781399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is why you should read this book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, did you like the Darkness? I never read past the first story arc.<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://static.comicvine.com/uploads/original/2/25521/1242184-thedarkness24pg09gl5.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-06-2015, 08:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T19:42:32-08:00","id":781493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=781401#post781401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh, did you like <b>the Darkness</b>?</div> </div> </div> </div>Never read it. Saw some of the pages in <b>Wizard Magazine</b> and even at that age, the book seemed a tad juvenile to me (when you make a plot point out of him being unable to fuck, I start looking at you funny).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T20:53:49-08:00","id":781520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=781385#post781385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking as someone who's always looking for something good, why is Strange so good? I know the broad strokes of the character - doctor who mastered the mystic arts under the Ancient One, arguably the most mystically capable individual in the Marvel universe - but not much about the personality and types of stories and such.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's some reviews of it so you can see for yourself:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.comicbookresources.com/comic-review/doctor-strange-1-marvel-comics\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.comicbookresources.com/comic-review/doctor-strange-1-marvel-comics\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.comicbookresources.com/comic-review/doctor-strange-1-marvel-comics\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.comicbookresources.com/comic-review/doctor-strange-1-marvel-comics </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.ign.com/articles/2015/10/06/doctor-strange-1-review\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.ign.com/articles/2015/10/06/doctor-strange-1-review\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.ign.com/articles/2015/10/06/doctor-strange-1-review\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.ign.com/articles/2015/10/06/doctor-strange-1-review </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.newsarama.com/26709-best-shots-reviews-dr-strange-2-green-lantern-46-nova-1.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.newsarama.com/26709-best-shots-reviews-dr-strange-2-green-lantern-46-nova-1.html\" target=\"_blank\"> Newsarama </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.newsarama.com/26709-best-shots-reviews-dr-strange-2-green-lantern-46-nova-1.html\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.newsarama.com/26709-best-shots-reviews-dr-strange-2-green-lantern-46-nova-1.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The book is already critically acclaimed and is generally one of the highest rated books of the month across all publishers.<br /> <br /> Give it a try. Doctor Strange is awesome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T20:58:02-08:00","id":781524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=781401#post781401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I found that tacking the powers of the strongest thing in the Marvel universe onto one of the smartest people on Earth managed to make him one of the most trite people in the Marvel universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the one thing I do agree with you on, as we've seen a Hulk that was this powerful and this intelligent before. However, with Cho being a 19 year old kid, I still feel it manages to feel a bit fresh and the art by Frank Cho doesn't get much better.<br /> <br /> Granted, it's only one issue in, but with all the reviews pouring in, I'd have to agree with most of them which say how good of a start it's off to.<br /> <br /> I'm just worried that Cho won't be able to keep up with the schedule as he's notoriously slow. We'll see...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T21:21:00-08:00","id":781536,"title":"","content":"Ok, just heard something cool at work I wanted to share with you guys. I work for a printing company, mostly magazines and periodicals. Well, just found out starting tomorrow we will start printing most or all the comics for Marvel.<br /> <br /> I jst thought that was cool. However, it's not on any machine I work on","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T22:31:12-08:00","id":781564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=781399#post781399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>(Scene: Doctor Strange #2. A mortal woman, Zelma Stanton, has come to Doctor Strange's Sanctum Santorum to have mystical parasites removed from her skull. They escape, forcing the Doctor to guide her through his home on a hunt for them.)</i><br /> <br /> <b>Zelma:</b> Um...are there supposed to be snakes on your coffee table?<br /> <b>Snake 1:</b> Hey girl. What's up?<br /> <b>Snake 2:</b> What's your hurry?<br /> <b>Doctor Strange:</b> Please do not talk to the snakes.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> That is why you should read this book.</div> </div> </div> </div>... that was possibly the most effective thing you could possibly have ever said to get me into the series. Like, I think even offering me money wouldn't have worked as well. Although in the name of science maybe we should give it a try? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=781493#post781493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Never read it. Saw some of the pages in <b>Wizard Magazine</b> and even at that age, the book seemed a tad juvenile to me (when you make a plot point out of him being unable to fuck, I start looking at you funny).</div> </div> </div> </div>I read the first arc, enjoyed it (if, yes, a tad juvenile). Read the next, not so much, since it was immediately following a crossover with Witchblade, which I had only the slightest understanding of and it totally contradicted what I understood as the Darkness/Angelus dynamic. The third was intensely boring. So in my opinion, while the darklings are totally hilarious, I don't feel I've missed out by not continuing. And if I feel like I need a darkling fix, I'll just watch Gremlins.<br /> <br /> Technically, he <i>can</i> fuck, he just risks dying if he impregnates the woman. Even condoms and such aren't totally 100%, and he likes living. But, yeah...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=781536#post781536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, just heard something cool at work I wanted to share with you guys. I work for a printing company, mostly magazines and periodicals. Well, just found out starting tomorrow we will start printing most or all the comics for Marvel.<br /> <br /> I jst thought that was cool. However, it's not on any machine I work on</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, even if it's not on your machine or anything, that's still pretty damn awesome <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T08:29:45-08:00","id":781703,"title":"","content":"Anyone reading Invincible or the current Star Wars/Darth Vader comics?<br /> <br /> Invincible has a time travel reboot storyling going right now that I can't really talk about because it's so spoiler heavy.<br /> <br /> Star Wars/Darth Vader are crossing over in &quot;Vader Down&quot;, where the eponymous Sith Lord finds himself largely alone against an army of rebel scum, and one of the two sides is horribly outmatched and knows it. There's the following two exchanges from the end of Vader Down #1 and Darth Vader #13 are pretty good.<br /> <br /> Vader stands in a valley on a planet he crash landed on.after taking out a flight of Y-Wings while on foot.<br /> Rebel Scum #0057: DARTH VADER! LAY DOWN YOUR WEAPONS! YOU ARE SURROUNDED!<br /> *camera pulls back, revealing an army of rebel soldiers and tanks and hovercraft surrounding the Sith Lord*<br /> *Darth Vader ignites his lightsaber*<br /> Darth Vader: All I am surrounded by is fear. And dead men.<br /> <br /> Rebel Scum #0057: Darth Vader-- Enough! SURRENDER! NOW!<br /> Darth Vader: Very well.<br /> Rebel Scum #0241: *whispering* force be praised.<br /> Darth Vader: Lower your weapons. You will not be harmed.<br /> <br /> I also haven't read the thread. Anyone reading The Wicked + The Divine?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9258-col","name":"CoL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T08:37:32-08:00","id":781705,"title":"","content":"Invincible's pretty good, though I feel like they're sort of lost when it comes what to do next.<br /> <br /> I liked the first couple story arcs in The Wicked + The Divine but after that it seems like they're trying to stretch the story out unnecessarily so I ceased reading it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-07-2015, 11:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T10:21:16-08:00","id":781745,"title":"","content":"So. Comics. I finally decided to try and get into them.<br /> <br /> Which isn't to say I have never read comics. Hell, I was even writing one for a time. I loved Sandman, Transmetropolitan, Watchmen, Preacher (never read it through, though), Dark Knight Returns, stuff like that. Classics would be the best way to describe them, I guess. Walking Dead too, though that's not yet a classic. But I never really kept track of the ongoing superhero stuff.<br /> <br /> Back when New 52 came out, I tried getting into it. Felt like a good jumping-on point. Animal Man was FANTASTIC, read about 10-15 issues and then kinda drifted away. Detective Comics seemed really awesome with the face-getting-cut-off Joker storyline but after a short while the story seemed to completely forget about that and I lost interest. And that's about it. Now, Marvel is resetting their stuff and I looked into Doctor Strange first - read just the first issue and I love it. There's something in there that shares Animal Man's DNA, I think. Which is similar to Image's Witch Doctor DNA. I'll stick with it, they're doing something awesome there.<br /> <br /> So, hopefully I'll start keeping track of the superhero stuff a lot more but I'm looking for some pointers from knowledgeable people. There's a crapload of comics out there and it ain't cheap buying all of 'em (though significantly easier to track down now, thanks to Comixology) so any help finding worthwhile ones would be much appreciated. I'm mainly interested in new Marvel and post-New 52 DC (though I have no idea what's going on with them after the initial #1 issues started appearing).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2050-dawngreeter","name":"Dawngreeter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2050_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T14:07:29-08:00","id":781832,"title":"","content":"You might like the new Constantine: the Hellblazer. Seems to wiggle him into the DCU without making him a superhero, a problem with the earlier line.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://40.media.tumblr.com/a9e4f7e631303716fb86c264372aaba7/tumblr_nyrhzvyB9H1two7n9o1_1280.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://41.media.tumblr.com/23206e87ca33a824818f94bb2fbb82bd/tumblr_nyri1li8pK1two7n9o1_1280.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://41.media.tumblr.com/0b46235c15a1bb0ab72eea5fa83181d5/tumblr_nxohsheJ2p1u6jvtzo1_1280.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> I've really enjoyed Batman &amp; Robin and it's new line, Robin: Son of Batman. But based on your preferences I'd suggest you check out Rumble, from Image Comics. Hexed, too, which is over with and so can be read without worrying about new issues coming and wrecking everything. Scott Snyder has a Wytches series but I haven't read past the first issue, which was good.<br /> <br /> Karnak's a solid comic from Marvel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-07-2015, 05:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T17:18:04-08:00","id":781955,"title":"","content":"Can anyone think of a Batman story involving a Joker-copycat killer? The closest I know of is one written by Kevin Smith, where Maxie Zeus turned Joker Venom into a rave drug.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T17:25:20-08:00","id":781959,"title":"","content":"In The Joker: Devil's Advocate someone attempts to use Joker's toxin to kill others and frame him. They succeed to an extent. Also, arguably, Joker's daughter and Last Laugh, where he 'Jokerizes' most of the supervillains in DC. I'm pretty sure it's come up in smaller story arcs as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T17:53:18-08:00","id":781977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dawngreeter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=781745#post781745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So. Comics. I finally decided to try and get into them.<br /> <br /> Which isn't to say I have never read comics. Hell, I was even writing one for a time. I loved Sandman, Transmetropolitan, Watchmen, Preacher (never read it through, though), Dark Knight Returns, stuff like that. Classics would be the best way to describe them, I guess. Walking Dead too, though that's not yet a classic. But I never really kept track of the ongoing superhero stuff.<br /> <br /> Back when New 52 came out, I tried getting into it. Felt like a good jumping-on point. Animal Man was FANTASTIC, read about 10-15 issues and then kinda drifted away. Detective Comics seemed really awesome with the face-getting-cut-off Joker storyline but after a short while the story seemed to completely forget about that and I lost interest. And that's about it. Now, Marvel is resetting their stuff and I looked into Doctor Strange first - read just the first issue and I love it. There's something in there that shares Animal Man's DNA, I think. Which is similar to Image's Witch Doctor DNA. I'll stick with it, they're doing something awesome there.<br /> <br /> So, hopefully I'll start keeping track of the superhero stuff a lot more but I'm looking for some pointers from knowledgeable people. There's a crapload of comics out there and it ain't cheap buying all of 'em (though significantly easier to track down now, thanks to Comixology) so any help finding worthwhile ones would be much appreciated. I'm mainly interested in new Marvel and post-New 52 DC (though I have no idea what's going on with them after the initial #1 issues started appearing).</div> </div> </div> </div>Iron Man Extremis is a 6 issue run that is pretty good as a jumping in point, plus Iron Man is awesome as a character. Give it a look, it's easy enough to get.<br /> <br /> Alias is also very solid. Not a superhero comic per se, it follows ex superhero Jessica Jones as she tries to make a living as a private detective. I'm told it's similar to the Netflix series, but I haven't seen it so I can't comment. Check out the first couple issues, see what you think.<br /> <br /> She-Hulk is good for a laugh and a pretty interesting character, but YMMV how long you want to stick with it. Slott's run is well worth a look (I think it's called Single Green Female, but not certain. Ran in 2004).<br /> <br /> Comicvine is immensely useful as a resource with following what comes after what, which can be difficult - just in case you don't already know it.<br /> <br /> Hope that's helpful :-)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T05:10:51-08:00","id":782234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=781399#post781399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>(Scene: Doctor Strange #2. A mortal woman, Zelma Stanton, has come to Doctor Strange's Sanctum Santorum to have mystical parasites removed from her skull. They escape, forcing the Doctor to guide her through his home on a hunt for them.)</i><br /> <br /> <b>Zelma:</b> Um...are there supposed to be snakes on your coffee table?<br /> <b>Snake 1:</b> Hey girl. What's up?<br /> <b>Snake 2:</b> What's your hurry?<br /> <b>Doctor Strange:</b> Please do not talk to the snakes.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> That is why you should read this book.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I've been reading Doctor Strange. Not complete, but from what I can tell the 'highlights'; Beginnings and Endings, Sorcerers Apprentice, The Oath, Defenders: Indefensible, and some of the Illuminati/World War Hulk stuff. And while it's good, no argument about that, I'm really getting the impression he's not a hugely continuity-intensive guy? Like, I haven't really gotten the feeling at any point that I've had to draw on past knowledge to really understand what's going on in any of those books.<br /> <br /> Which is by no means a bad thing, don't get me wrong. Just, well, like if you're reading Superior Iron Man, you're going to need to draw on Extremis, Stark Disassembled, and suchforth just to understand what's going on - which can make it really hard to get into, but it also provides a certain... richness? You've seen this character grow and learn over time, but I've never really gotten the feeling that Strange has really grown all that much over the stories.<br /> <br /> (Oh, and the Illuminati bit where all these great heroes are sitting around a table complaining about their relationships? Hilarious <i>and</i> heart-warming, all at once.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T06:39:51-08:00","id":782265,"title":"","content":"I am only a casual fan of Doctor Strange, so I can't say. I do notice his origin gets retold a lot, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T09:31:37-08:00","id":782345,"title":"","content":"First off, thanks for the advice, all. Read through the three Doctor Strange issues that have been published so far and I'll go through recommendations for the next one to read.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=782234#post782234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't really gotten the feeling at any point that I've had to draw on past knowledge to really understand what's going on in any of those books.<br /> <br /> Which is by no means a bad thing, don't get me wrong. Just, well, like if you're reading Superior Iron Man, you're going to need to draw on Extremis, Stark Disassembled, and suchforth just to understand what's going on - which can make it really hard to get into, but it also provides a certain... richness?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe this is one of the reasons why I fell for Doctor Strange? I don't know. But usually, as someone who wasn't up to date on the ongoing superhero developments in comics, reading a comic can be frustrating and confusing. For example, I wanted to read the Secret Wars so I Googled what I should read in order to fully understand it. I found a list of probably two hundred comics over past 30 years, or some such silliness. So I just figured I'd let it go and hop on the Marvel train after the reboot (which isn't really a reboot after all, apparently, so what the hell?!).<br /> <br /> But I have been enjoying knowing everything about the Marvel cinematic universe, and all the shows and subplots and so forth, which is why I decided it's a worthwhile investment to actually get to know the comics. So, yeah. I can understand the richness argument, I just have trouble getting to the point where I see it myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2050-dawngreeter","name":"Dawngreeter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2050_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T16:51:07-08:00","id":782553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dawngreeter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=782345#post782345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe this is one of the reasons why I fell for Doctor Strange? I don't know. But usually, as someone who wasn't up to date on the ongoing superhero developments in comics, reading a comic can be frustrating and confusing. For example, I wanted to read the Secret Wars so I Googled what I should read in order to fully understand it. I found a list of probably two hundred comics over past 30 years, or some such silliness. So I just figured I'd let it go and hop on the Marvel train after the reboot (which isn't really a reboot after all, apparently, so what the hell?!).<br /> <br /> But I have been enjoying knowing everything about the Marvel cinematic universe, and all the shows and subplots and so forth, which is why I decided it's a worthwhile investment to actually get to know the comics. So, yeah. I can understand the richness argument, I just have trouble getting to the point where I see it myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the building thing is <i>certainly</i> not without problems either, and can get more than a little silly in many cases.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T20:45:18-08:00","id":782597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dawngreeter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=782345#post782345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First off, thanks for the advice, all. Read through the three Doctor Strange issues that have been published so far and I'll go through recommendations for the next one to read.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Maybe this is one of the reasons why I fell for Doctor Strange? I don't know. But usually, as someone who wasn't up to date on the ongoing superhero developments in comics, reading a comic can be frustrating and confusing. For example, I wanted to read the Secret Wars so I Googled what I should read in order to fully understand it. I found a list of probably two hundred comics over past 30 years, or some such silliness. So I just figured I'd let it go and hop on the Marvel train after the reboot (which isn't really a reboot after all, apparently, so what the hell?!).<br /> <br /> But I have been enjoying knowing everything about the Marvel cinematic universe, and all the shows and subplots and so forth, which is why I decided it's a worthwhile investment to actually get to know the comics. So, yeah. I can understand the richness argument, I just have trouble getting to the point where I see it myself.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Marvel has clearly had a problem, throughout the entire of their publishing history, of knowing what to do with Doctor Strange. He doesn't fit cleanly into most of the superhero tropes, his power level makes him hard to match with reasonable threats, and he doesn't really possess that compelling internal conflict that the best Marvel characters have. This has turned out to be both a good and a bad thing. There aren't a whole lot of Doc Strange solo books, and the character drama can often be fairly shallow. OTOH, this makes him stand alone pretty well. For me, the appeal of Doctor Strange has always been in the visuals. I'm of the opinion that Chris Bachalo really knocks the new book out of the park, but if you like Strange, you should definitely try to dig up a collection of the original Strange Tales series drawn by Steve Ditko. It's stunningly beautiful in ways that we rarely see in comics, even today.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T08:21:02-08:00","id":782815,"title":"","content":"I think the nature of magic in the Marvel Universe also has something to do with it. I have thought about it a lot, and it's very hard for me to imagine how to tell a Doctor Strange story well, because the boundaries of magic are so unclear; I've read several stories of his that involve him not knowing how to do a thing, but then he goes to his library and reads books and then he knows how to do the thing that makes him win, which is...not a terrifically compelling formula. I didn't like it in Buffy and I don't care for it here. But you can't open each book with a concrete spell list to define his powers because that's basically apologizing for the premise, so...what do you do?<br /> <br /> Well, the first thing you do is have snakes flirt with a girl in a way that makes me hear them being voiced by Keegan-Michael Key and Jordan Peele. That is a great place to start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T08:50:47-08:00","id":782832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=782815#post782815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the nature of magic in the Marvel Universe also has something to do with it. I have thought about it a lot, and it's very hard for me to imagine how to tell a Doctor Strange story well, because the boundaries of magic are so unclear; I've read several stories of his that involve him not knowing how to do a thing, but then he goes to his library and reads books and then he knows how to do the thing that makes him win, which is...not a terrifically compelling formula. I didn't like it in Buffy and I don't care for it here. But you can't open each book with a concrete spell list to define his powers because that's basically apologizing for the premise, so...what do you do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sanderson had some interesting thoughts on how magic should work in fiction. Essentially, either magic has rules that you must explain to the audience before your character is allowed to exploit any exceptions, or magic has no rules and is essentially useless for resolving plot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T10:01:00-08:00","id":782886,"title":"","content":"I was as unimpressed by Sanderson's lectures about magic as I am by his novels, but if anyone's interested there's <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zwb7b9Ks0VE\" target=\"_blank\">videos</a> and <a href=\"http://brandonsanderson.com/sandersons-first-law/\" target=\"_blank\">blogs</a>.<br /> <br /> The problem with Dr. Strange is really one that extends to all magic heroes and, occasionally, villains. JimB has it right, for plot reasons a magician can't instantly solve a problem, but once the problem is mostly explored and the reader sees it for what it is, they happen to have a spell that allows them to do it. What bugs me is that while this is seen as an issue with magic characters, it's really something that comes up in all comics. Things like super strength and durability and even speed vary depending upon the writer, with someone like Spider-man able to lift a bus, but his punches not being able to utterly destroy a human in a costume in one shot. How often has a villain pointed out their physical superiority at the end only to have the hero say something like, 'Yeah, but now it's personal' or 'Now I'm mad,' leading to a trouncing of said villain. And technology heroes can be awful about it, with their science often just being magic with pseudo-scientific terms, and that last-minute gadget they've whipped up or 'reversing the polarity' being the equivalent of that spell Dr. Strange or Dr. Fate picks up.<br /> <br /> Still, interesting stories are told with these other characters, while somehow it becomes a roadblock with magic heroes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T12:01:16-08:00","id":782971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=782886#post782886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was as unimpressed by Sanderson's lectures about magic as I am by his novels, but if anyone's interested there's <a href=\"http://&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zwb7b9Ks0VE&quot;\" target=\"_blank\">videos</a> and <a href=\"http://&quot;http://brandonsanderson.com/sandersons-first-law/&quot;\" target=\"_blank\">blogs</a>.<br /> <br /> The problem with Dr. Strange is really one that extends to all magic heroes and, occasionally, villains. JimB has it right, for plot reasons a magician can't instantly solve a problem, but once the problem is mostly explored and the reader sees it for what it is, they happen to have a spell that allows them to do it. What bugs me is that while this is seen as an issue with magic characters, it's really something that comes up in all comics. Things like super strength and durability and even speed vary depending upon the writer, with someone like Spider-man able to lift a bus, but his punches not being able to utterly destroy a human in a costume in one shot. How often has a villain pointed out their physical superiority at the end only to have the hero say something like, 'Yeah, but now it's personal' or 'Now I'm mad,' leading to a trouncing of said villain. And technology heroes can be awful about it, with their science often just being magic with pseudo-scientific terms, and that last-minute gadget they've whipped up or 'reversing the polarity' being the equivalent of that spell Dr. Strange or Dr. Fate picks up.<br /> <br /> Still, interesting stories are told with these other characters, while somehow it becomes a roadblock with magic heroes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's particularly egregious in how Marvel handles mystical characters. Doctor Strange is typically used in one of two ways. He's either a deus ex machina where his powers suit whatever is convenient for the story, or he's essentially just another superhero with levitation subbing for flight, arcane bolts subbing for laser eyes, etc. Other characters like Scarlet Witch have the same problem. I think it can be seen in more tech based characters as well, but writers are getting better at making it natural within the context of the setting. There tend to be more underlying roles to Marvel pseudo-science than Marvel mysticism.<br /> <br /> I don't think it has to be that way though. DC has (possibly had?) a pretty robust mystical setting in part because of Vertigo's popularity in the 80s and 90s and in part because they continued to foster that little corner of the universe (Michael Moorcock famously wrote a &quot;magic bible&quot; that was the anchor for their core line mystic books), and the result is a lot of interlocking and interesting mythologies. I think the problem is that Marvel has never really supported many books with magical characters.<br /> <br /> I mean, regular readers can generally understand the style and some of the underlying roles of Tony Stark tech or Reed Richards tech, but I don't think Doc Strange has had the space to develop a signature to his magic.<br /> <br /> tl;dr: Whether you're talking about magic or pseudo-science, a setting is only as developed as the space it's given, and it takes time and effort to develop the internal logic of a character's world. Strange unfortunately doesn't have that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 12-09-2015, 03:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T13:05:35-08:00","id":783023,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think the past has shown that you can have sort of ruleless or rules-lite magic characters who are both engaging and not walking deux ex machinas. And I've read interviews where the editors have said their big hesitance in making another Dr. Strange comic is they haven't found a 'magic system' they like.<br /> <br /> Another problem with Strange is that he's the Sorcerer Supreme, basically the most powerful magical force in the entire dimension, and his duty is, more or less, to defend it. In the case of Dr. Strange losing, the entire dimension ends or at least changes so drastically you wouldn't recognize it. The X-men have this problem with Apocalypse, whose 'win condition' requires an entire spinoff alternate universe. And while Age of Apocalypse is cool, because it's the only thing that could happen if Apocalypse wins you know when he's showing up he's not usually going to conquer the entire world, enslave humanity and pit mutants against one another. Just like you know when Dr. Strange goes up against Shuma-Gorath or Dormammu, Dr. Strange isn't going to lose and turn the Marvel Universe into the Dormammu Universe. Which is a meta way of thinking, I admit, but Hellblazer focused on John Constantine and really got readers engaged in his flaws and weaknesses, and Sandman and Lucifer focused on characters with boundless power but the stories were told on a mythic scale. Dr. Strange really hits a weird medium for that, because he's got his flaws, but he's also the Sorcerer Supreme so he has some level of purity about him. And he's really powerful, but as a heroic figure he can't go around just wrecking peoples lives.<br /> <br /> And the support network. Dr. Strange has some allies, but they exist in a weird untouchable state as well. Wong the eternal manservant, even when suffering illness of his own. Clea, another Sorcerer Supreme. They've tried getting Strange hooked up with plucky girl apprentices, something that, looking back, seems to be weirdly common for magic comics, but they stop at really engaging them fully with Dr. Strange, and they usually don't last. I'm a big believer in support and background characters doing a lot of the work in fleshing out the world of the main character. Paul Dini is great for that.<br /> <br /> All that said, it's why he's pretty good as a back-up in other comics. During Civil War and afterwards he was a tired mentor who had a lot of impact on the Marvel Universe while, as far as I can recall, not even having his own comic. He supported Captain America's side and kept their Avengers concealed from Capekiller squads, he used forbidden magics to try and put down the Hulk in World War Hulk, lost the title of Sorcerer Supreme and guided the Avengers against Dormammu's acolytes, acted as an adviser to Magik and Pixie. He gives characters some room for development with a sense of the Marvel Universe at large, while not just zipping in and solving all their problems.<br /> <br /> Maybe this current run will manage it, the first issue didn't really interest me much but I'll try again once the first couple story arcs are complete. I always want to like magic comics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-09-2015, 04:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T15:26:06-08:00","id":783086,"title":"","content":"Recently picked up the first issue of <b>Insexts</b>. If you're going to Google that title, then for god's sake remember that S at the end, because searching for &quot;insext&quot; will take you to websites you do not want to go to and teach you things you did not want to learn. I was promised a book about Victorian lesbians taking revenge on the world and becoming bug monsters, and frankly, Victorian lesbians are a weirdly specific fetish of mine (don't judge), so I thought hey.<br /> <br /> Alas, Victorian lesbians engaging in Skinemax-levels of sex can't take me through the book. It feels so rushed: The abusive husband is introduced and murdered so fast I don't even consider this a spoiler, the protagonist and her lover/maid are already deep in a relationship at the start of the book so there's no establishing of why they even like each other (unless a shared sexual preference and a good bed life are reason enough to be willing to kill for one another, which hey, maybe they are), and the maid already got her magical insect powers off-camera before the book began by...talking to another woman's maid who was in Burma?<br /> <br /> I usually give a book two issues to impress me, but I'm kinda thinkin' screw this.<br /> <br /> I also picked up <b>Scarlet Witch #1</b>. Haven't got to it yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T15:44:14-08:00","id":783093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=782886#post782886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with Dr. Strange is really one that extends to all magic heroes and, occasionally, villains. JimB has it right, for plot reasons a magician can't instantly solve a problem, but once the problem is mostly explored and the reader sees it for what it is, they happen to have a spell that allows them to do it. What bugs me is that while this is seen as an issue with magic characters, it's really something that comes up in all comics. Things like super strength and durability and even speed vary depending upon the writer, with someone like Spider-man able to lift a bus, but his punches not being able to utterly destroy a human in a costume in one shot. How often has a villain pointed out their physical superiority at the end only to have the hero say something like, 'Yeah, but now it's personal' or 'Now I'm mad,' leading to a trouncing of said villain. And technology heroes can be awful about it, with their science often just being magic with pseudo-scientific terms, and that last-minute gadget they've whipped up or 'reversing the polarity' being the equivalent of that spell Dr. Strange or Dr. Fate picks up.<br /> <br /> Still, interesting stories are told with these other characters, while somehow it becomes a roadblock with magic heroes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it comes down to the antagonists. Spider-man and Stark and such tend to fight humans - enhanced humans, or humans using funky tech, but ultimately humans, and killing carries a certain moral weight there. While Strange tends to fight inhuman - usually demonic - entities, which apart from often being Chaotic Evil more or less by definition, just don't carry the same moral weight with readers. If Spider-man killed Doc Ock, then that would be crossing a moral line that just isn't the case if Strange were to kill Dormammu. Also, the undefined nature of the magic comes into play: Spider-man can't really do much if he can't physically touch the opponent, while Strange just has so many more options that it starts to strain belief that he can't figure out a way to bind Dormammu or Nightmare to a rock and keep it in his attic.<br /> <br /> Well-done magic characters like Constantine I think work because they emphasise the cost of doing certain things, or the limitations of the character. Constantine saves the world in the short-term, but in the long term is arguably doing more harm, and his means aren't exactly moral either, so there's an edge, a conflict there. While Strange (based on very limited reading) basically waves his hands, maybe says an incantation, and problem fixed, with no greater cost than <i>maybe</i> he's a little tired. Maybe. It's just really, really hard to get engaged with a character who is fairly bland as characters go, and is so rarely challenged.<br /> <br /> That's my view, anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T19:24:10-08:00","id":783858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=783086#post783086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Recently picked up the first issue of <b>Insexts</b>. If you're going to Google that title, then for god's sake remember that S at the end, because searching for &quot;insext&quot; will take you to websites you do not want to go to and teach you things you did not want to learn. I was promised a book about Victorian lesbians taking revenge on the world and becoming bug monsters, and frankly, Victorian lesbians are a weirdly specific fetish of mine (don't judge), so I thought hey.</div> </div> </div> </div>You might try Monstress. It's up to issue two, and there's some implied lesbianism but no explicit sex. There's very few male characters. Taking place in a fantasy world after a war between two civilizations, one made of 'arcanics,' who have a more natural bond to nature and mysticism, and another human civilization which seems ruled over by an authoritarian order of warrior-sorceress-assassin nun-nobles called the Cumaea. It's clearly got some inspirations from manga, and the art style and concepts resembles Kim Hyung-Tae. It seems good so far.<br /> <br 