l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=783858#post783858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might try <b>Monstress</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>For personal reasons I'd rather not get into, I'm staying away from this book, but I appreciate the recommendation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T06:08:23-08:00","id":784105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=783858#post783858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You might try Monstress. It's up to issue two, and there's some implied lesbianism but no explicit sex. There's very few male characters. Taking place in a fantasy world after a war between two civilizations, one made of 'arcanics,' who have a more natural bond to nature and mysticism, and another human civilization which seems ruled over by an authoritarian order of warrior-sorceress-assassin nun-nobles called the Cumaea. It's clearly got some inspirations from manga, and the art style and concepts resembles Kim Hyung-Tae. It seems good so far.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://imagecomics.com/uploads/releases/Monstress1_PreviewPage3.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>I picked up the first issue and was surprised at how good it was. I'm not really a Marjorie Lui fan, but her writing was acceptable on the book, and Takeda's art is amazing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T06:44:43-08:00","id":784131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=784105#post784105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I picked up the first issue and was surprised at how good it was. I'm not really a Marjorie Lui fan, but her writing was acceptable on the book, and Takeda's art is amazing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, I hated her handling of X-23 and Wolverine. Some writers do way better on original characters and universes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T02:44:57-08:00","id":792063,"title":"","content":"So, how do you guys find new series to read?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T03:13:43-08:00","id":792075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dawngreeter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=781745#post781745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, hopefully I'll start keeping track of the superhero stuff a lot more but I'm looking for some pointers from knowledgeable people. There's a crapload of comics out there and it ain't cheap buying all of 'em (though significantly easier to track down now, thanks to Comixology) so any help finding worthwhile ones would be much appreciated. I'm mainly interested in new Marvel and post-New 52 DC (though I have no idea what's going on with them after the initial #1 issues started appearing).</div> </div> </div> </div>I would recommend new 52 wonder woman, pretty much self contained and surprisingly a good Scion story.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=783093#post783093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well-done magic characters like Constantine I think work because they emphasise the cost of doing certain things, or the limitations of the character. Constantine saves the world in the short-term, but in the long term is arguably doing more harm, and his means aren't exactly moral either, so there's an edge, a conflict there. While Strange (based on very limited reading) basically waves his hands, maybe says an incantation, and problem fixed, with no greater cost than <i>maybe</i> he's a little tired. Maybe. It's just really, really hard to get engaged with a character who is fairly bland as characters go, and is so rarely challenged.<br /> <br /> That's my view, anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always put Kid Loki`s run in Journey into mystery as good twist on how to use magic on a history. Because they recognize it as plot device and narrative tool in-setting and the fun is seeing how the everything works out in the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 12-24-2015, 06:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T13:57:29-08:00","id":792351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=792063#post792063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, how do you guys find new series to read?</div> </div> </div> </div>I never really resorted to the various blogs and comic news sites, so when I tended to find new comics it was just because I happened to see them at shops. It's how I found the old and fantastic Hellraiser comics, as well as the mediocre Citizen Pain, and various other oddities. Sometimes you get lucky and see an ad for something that looks interesting, but really I get tuned into things by chance or if they're related to something I'm already pulling.<br /> <br /> This week was an understandably slow week for comics, at least to me. Nothing that good from the big two so I looked around and saw a few comics that seemed somewhat interesting and I picked up the #1s for them. Hellbreak is a muddy story about a militarily-trained team that works for an organization who sends them to hell to find the souls of those trapped there while their bodies are possessed by demons. I thought it would be about a jailbreak from hell and this premise isn't nearly as interesting, plus the characters are pretty bland. Outcast was another, basically a supernatural mystery with some guy who's had an awful past and seems to be sort of the epicenter of a demon-possessing epidemic. To make things worse, either demons like him, or can't stand him, because while drawn to him he can cause them pain by touching their hosts and kick them out. It seems better than Hellbreak but it's also going really slow. They were both started within a few months of each other and I'm trying to think back and remember if demon possession was in the news back then. I also picked up the first issue of Grant Morrison's Nameless, which looks like it's going to be a solid read.<br /> <br /> So, basically, check your local comic book store, or even bookstore for comics and tpbs you wouldn't normally look for. Big stores like Barnes and Noble tend to have some comics, but they usually have a huge trade paperback section and you can sometimes find gems there. Otherwise I'm sure there's some news sites that're really good at talking about comics out you've probably never heard of but I couldn't tell you which ones are good or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T20:33:06-08:00","id":792516,"title":"","content":"Picked up and read the first two issues of Jacked, a new series from Vertigo.<br /> <br /> Holy crap.<br /> <br /> Not only is it well written and fantastically drawn, but it is the PERFECT material for a Pentex-themed campaign centered around Magadon Pharmaceuticals. <br /> <br /> Loser of a husband/father/overall human being, ends up taking these pills that make him better. Stronger, faster, etc. etc. But at what cost? I highly recommend it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T23:45:47-08:00","id":792626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=792516#post792516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Picked up and read the first two issues of Jacked, a new series from Vertigo.<br /> <br /> Holy crap.<br /> <br /> Not only is it well written and fantastically drawn, but it is the PERFECT material for a Pentex-themed campaign centered around Magadon Pharmaceuticals.<br /> <br /> Loser of a husband/father/overall human being, ends up taking these pills that make him better. Stronger, faster, etc. etc. But at what cost? I highly recommend it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I liked what I've read. Good recommendation <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T19:01:43-08:00","id":813090,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I checked out the first issue of <b>InSeXts</b>, and I agree with JimB's assessment: the idea behind it is potentially really good, but the pacing is all wonky. It doesn't build worth a damn, just stuff happening with little impact or meaning. The characters are flat, with little attempt to endear them to the reader - I think we're just supposed to be engaged with them because they're ladies in Victorian times, who've allegedly had a hard time of it. I say 'allegedly' because the reader is never actually shown any evidence of it. They discuss it, which is normally fine, but what we actually see is the abusive husband is maybe kind of a tool, and... that's it. Which means the events of the book are flat at best, or at worst the protagonists come off as homicidal maniacs. Which is, again, not inherently bad, but I'm pretty sure we're supposed to like these characters.<br /> <br /> However, <b>Super Zero</b> looks potentially interesting. Essentially it follows a girl of dubious sanity who wants to be a super-hero, but to be a super-hero she has to have an origin story, so she keeps trying to set one up. Art's pretty good, characters are well-developed, and I'm interested to see where this goes.<br /> <br /> <b>The Secret</b> is also pretty good. Essentially, the main character gets invited to a party where a bunch of kids are playing a silly game where they call random numbers, and tell the person who answers &quot;I know your secret&quot;, and things go pretty wrong from there. The art's intriguing, does that kind-of-blurry watercolour style which I normally don't like but here it kind of works. Story's well-told, and you really get emotionally drawn in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","user":"Allan53","date":". 01-21-2016, 01:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T10:29:54-08:00","id":816235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=792075#post792075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would recommend new 52 wonder woman, pretty much self contained and surprisingly a good Scion story.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would only recommend WW during Azz's run then it goes down hill from here.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T15:09:41-08:00","id":816449,"title":"","content":"So what did y'all think about Secret Wars?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T16:23:39-08:00","id":816495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=816449#post816449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what did y'all think about Secret Wars?</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't read all of it, but what I did read didn't really impress me. But then I'm not a fan of crossovers and know basically nothing about the Ultimate universe apart from it being more 'modern' or something. I wanted to like the latter part, with Doom (because Doom is awesome), but again, the lack of context was a real problem in grasping what was happening.<br /> <br /> I read Armor Wars, because I like Iron Man, but that similarly left me cold. The story was flat and predictable, and it didn't really go anywhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T03:28:01-08:00","id":816760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=816235#post816235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would only recommend WW during Azz's run then it goes down hill from here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah i was willing to give it a chance even though i dislike David Finch but.....ugh. Well, it was fun to like WW while it lasted <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T11:46:34-08:00","id":817029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=816760#post816760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah i was willing to give it a chance even though i dislike David Finch but.....ugh. Well, it was fun to like WW while it lasted <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>WW is pretty much cursed almost as cursed as TT. I get how WW is still around but why has TT been going for 20 years while being complete shit for that entire time.<br /> <br /> In other news I'm going to be really sad when Midnighter gets cancelled it looks like it's going to after prez.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T13:26:00-08:00","id":817104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=816449#post816449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what did y'all think about Secret Wars?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spun its wheels a fair bit, there was no need for the looooong delays when the same story could have been told over 6 issues rather than 9 and actually finished up before some of the rebooted Marvel Universe titles had 5 months of publication. Still, the overall story holds together pretty well (something I never expected from Hickman), and a lot of tributary miniseries were very interesting and brought new ideas to the MU.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T13:30:58-08:00","id":817109,"title":"","content":"Think she and her writers are just too wrapped up in the past. WW2 was almost a hundred years ago, as horrible as it was, Nazis are way overdone, and most people can see women taking powerful roles, leading Wonder Woman to combat strange social ills that seem unnecessary for a superhero. There's a lot they can do to contemporize her but they're pretty drastic moves.<br /> <br /> It's been a good past couple weeks for my comics, Batman stuff has been solid, especially Snyder's work and even the different writers on Robin, Son of Batman and Gotham Academy were a nice change, rather than an out of character snorefest. Legends of the Dark Knight finished up its wild and creepy Six Fingers story arc. As much as I like the 'epic' stories in the more mainstream comics, LotDK really manages to capture the more traditional 'Batman as a detective in Gotham' vibe the way most comics don't, with their focus on other aspects. Plus Six Fingers had the memorable scenes of him getting bones broken and beaten up by an untrained teenage girl. Illuminati maintains good story but should probably amp things up soon. The various new Vertigo works seem to be doing well, but I'm way behind on them.<br /> <br /> I've really been liking Midnighter, but it does seem to need more. They should either bite the bullet and use it to help flesh out an international espionage community or something, bouncing back and forth between superheroics and other stuff without really having an impact is getting tiring.<br /> <br /> Broken Moon finished up its four issue run, and I'm left thinking the same thing I thought when I read the first issue, 'Why?' It's a decent story, but seems to be part of a larger event, and doesn't really give you anything to get you into any of the characters unless you're a genre fan who just likes vampires, werewolves or Frankensteins. And even then you can give us something more than a royal rumble.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how long ago I posted, we've been really busy here, so I apologize if I already mentioned it, but I read Scott Snyder's Wytches, which was a good, solid horror comic. Really looking forward to part two.<br /> <br /> Right now I'm trying to summon up the time and energy to read the Woods and Morning Glories, two comics I've been wanting to read for years but never had the time to.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://1.bp.blogspot.com/-qO0sRe_6s8U/Vm9zdjJXdhI/AAAAAAAT4fA/QcNexauv3jY/s1600/44_15.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Oh yeah. And the huge Court of Owls reveal.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://insidepulse.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/01/Robin-War-2-spoilers-Dick-Grayson-Robin-Nightwing-Court-of-Owls-9.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-26-2016, 11:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T21:04:24-08:00","id":817385,"title":"","content":"Have you been reading midnighter without grayson because they heavily crossover almost to the point of both of them them being in both books almost half the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T21:07:31-08:00","id":817386,"title":"","content":"Yeah, and they do go so well together, but Grayson's done a lot of work to build up the international espionage community and Midnighter needs to get in on that. Grayson being Grayson is like the best thing that could have happened to the character. They're both good comics, I just think Midnighter needs something more to get some wider appeal.<br /> <br /> It does look like something is in the works for both of them, though. Midnighter's often been teamed up with other characters so I could easily see him sharing headlines with someone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-27-2016, 12:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T02:29:12-08:00","id":817479,"title":"","content":"If a series gets cancelled, how much notice is typical?<br /> <br /> I'm almost certainly overreacting, but I saw the release date for the next <b>Jacked</b> has changed to TBD, and the only time I have seen this was when Superior Iron Man ended. Jacked is a comic still in the early stages of it's run... I'm paranoid.<br /> <br /> Note: I'm legitimately interested in the notice-cancel question. The rest is more in the nature of context. I'm pretty sure the next Jacked (which I see is now #4 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) has a release date, so it's unlikely to be cancelled before then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","user":"Allan53","date":". 01-27-2016, 05:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T06:32:30-08:00","id":817554,"title":"","content":"I'd think it would depend on why. If something is under-performing badly, or is actively hurting the sales of other lines (by virtue of people objecting to it or it's content for example), or ran into legal issues then it'd probably be suspended very quickly with a side possibility of retooling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T07:39:25-08:00","id":817582,"title":"","content":"Sites that have future solicitations usually will have warning when a comic isn't being renewed, as it won't be in the solicitations for a few months from now.<br /> <br /> Most writers and artists have twitter or some other social media front, and they tend to be pretty open about what's happening, so if they haven't announced it there, you can just ask them.<br /> <br /> If you've subscribed to a comic they don't generally give you much warning and will tend to fill out the rest of your subscription with another comic they deem related.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-27-2016, 11:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T12:57:07-08:00","id":817868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=817029#post817029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WW is pretty much cursed almost as cursed as TT. I get how WW is still around but why has TT been going for 20 years while being complete shit for that entire time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah i agree, recently i read the &quot;Deathstroke&quot; first arc and i was blown away of how good it was. The ending was excellent and Deathstroke was an actual character instead of a mary sue like now.<br /> <br /> But yeah, TT has being going pretty badly. I started when Red Devil was part of the titans and i love the line up and all the plot that were coming buuuut them they proceed to abort those plots and it was just a mess <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T22:00:24-08:00","id":820742,"title":"","content":"So, on a whim, I picked up a copy of <b>The Question: The Five Books of Blood</b> over the weekend. I read it. Then I went and read <b>Gotham Central</b>. Then I started <b>52</b>.<br /> <br /> Renee Montoya is awesome, in short. And Gotham Central is so amazing how did I never know it was a thing. It follows the lives of the Major Crimes Unit in Gotham as they do their damndest to be good cops in a horrendously corrupt city filled with maniacs and Batman, and you really get to see how frustrating it is for them, and understand how Batman, while important to Gotham, really is a mixed blessing at best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T16:34:42-08:00","id":821298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=820742#post820742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, on a whim, I picked up a copy of <b>The Question: The Five Books of Blood</b> over the weekend. I read it. Then I went and read <b>Gotham Central</b>. Then I started <b>52</b>.<br /> <br /> Renee Montoya is awesome, in short. And Gotham Central is so amazing how did I never know it was a thing. It follows the lives of the Major Crimes Unit in Gotham as they do their damndest to be good cops in a horrendously corrupt city filled with maniacs and Batman, and you really get to see how frustrating it is for them, and understand how Batman, while important to Gotham, really is a mixed blessing at best.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotham the tv series is loosely based off of it. It really has more fun with the concept than GCPD did, though, putting in a lot of over-the-top silliness.<br /> <br /> As for Renee, congratulations on meeting Greg Rucka's 'The Woman.'<br /> <br /> He's a great writer, though I'm not a fan of his novels. But he almost always writes about 'The Woman.' He had a few while he was working for DC Comics. Renee Montoya, Sasha Bordeaux, and Katherine Kane. When he went to Marvel he brought her to the Punisher in the form of Rachel Cole, and she's appeared in his various non-Big Two works. While it's not fair to label them like that, they share so many characteristics and are in so much of his work it's something I find hard to do. I can appreciate them as separate characters, I love Renee, Sasha and Rachel but am was not a fan of Kane until he stopped writing her, basically she tends to be red haired, from a disciplined background, very focused but usually willing to be a loose cannon and play by her own set of rules. Army woman. It's basically a female version of a stereotypical action hero. And he often makes her ineligible to more stereotypical romances, which I think is because female characters, especially side characters like Renee, are often expected to become the romantic interest of a primary protagonist.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/2f/RachelColeAlves.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/11/Sasha_Bordeaux.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>]<img src=\"http://www.writeups.org/img/fiche/4851q.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><img src=\"http://static.comicvine.com/uploads/original/0/40/651932-carriebw.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Honestly I imagine he had a crush on some fantasy version of her and he's doing what he can to put her into his work. The readers benefit, thankfully.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://io9.com/5912366/why-i-write-strong-female-characters\" target=\"_blank\">Here's an article he wrote about writing them.</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-01-2016, 07:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T23:33:31-08:00","id":821462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=821298#post821298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Gotham the tv series is loosely based off of it. It really has more fun with the concept than GCPD did, though, putting in a lot of over-the-top silliness.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I tried to watch Gotham, but it seemed more concerned with setting up the Batman mythos than focussing on the issues of Gotham. I did see it sort of explore that with Gordon, but... I dunno. Seemed different somehow.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=821298#post821298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for Renee, congratulations on meeting Greg Rucka's 'The Woman.'<br /> <br /> He's a great writer, though I'm not a fan of his novels. But he almost always writes about 'The Woman.' He had a few while he was working for DC Comics. Renee Montoya, Sasha Bordeaux, and Katherine Kane. When he went to Marvel he brought her to the Punisher in the form of Rachel Cole, and she's appeared in his various non-Big Two works. While it's not fair to label them like that, they share so many characteristics and are in so much of his work it's something I find hard to do. I can appreciate them as separate characters, I love Renee, Sasha and Rachel but am was not a fan of Kane until he stopped writing her, basically she tends to be red haired, from a disciplined background, very focused but usually willing to be a loose cannon and play by her own set of rules. Army woman. It's basically a female version of a stereotypical action hero. And he often makes her ineligible to more stereotypical romances, which I think is because female characters, especially side characters like Renee, are often expected to become the romantic interest of a primary protagonist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's unfortunate in a way I cannot rationally, clearly articulate. I suppose I should be grateful that at least it's more interesting than those writers who feel the need to not only write decent female characters (which is totally, entirely fine), but to shove it in your face that their characters are the absolute embodiment of perfect feminist ideals. Nobody likes 'message pieces', they're preachy and dull.<br /> <br /> But, based entirely on what I've read so far, which isn't much, he seems to have avoided that. So, yay! I can take a bit of lacking flexibility in character concepts if it means we get cool characters <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T11:11:45-08:00","id":821743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=821462#post821462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tried to watch Gotham, but it seemed more concerned with setting up the Batman mythos than focussing on the issues of Gotham. I did see it sort of explore that with Gordon, but... I dunno. Seemed different somehow.</div> </div> </div> </div>It starts off with a lot of focus on Bruce but the show is really, clearly, about Jim Gordon and his war on corruption. Arguably Jim and Penguin become the main characters at some point. The idea of Batman doesn't really come up, but the show does a good job showing off how the death of the Waynes was a tipping point in a tremendously corrupt city. There's shades of the 99%'er movement there, with people just sick and tired of being ground between the corrupt government and business and organized crime and just doing something about it. Which is the type of situation that led to Gotham's vigilantism. At the worst, it's a fun and occasionally over-the-top police procedural with interesting characters that takes a lot from a healthy setting that's had over seventy years of creativity poured into it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, that's unfortunate in a way I cannot rationally, clearly articulate. I suppose I should be grateful that at least it's more interesting than those writers who feel the need to not only write decent female characters (which is totally, entirely fine), but to shove it in your face that their characters are the absolute embodiment of perfect feminist ideals. Nobody likes 'message pieces', they're preachy and dull.<br /> <br /> But, based entirely on what I've read so far, which isn't much, he seems to have avoided that. So, yay! I can take a bit of lacking flexibility in character concepts if it means we get cool characters <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>Yeah he really doesn't shove your face in it, but it's...there. And like I said, all the characters are different and stand on their own. I'd really suggest reading Whiteout for an interesting crime story, but Rucka's run on Punisher was good too.<br /> <br /> Have you ever read <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Planetary_(comics)\" target=\"_blank\">Planetary</a>, by Warren Ellis?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T16:56:39-08:00","id":821973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=821743#post821743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It starts off with a lot of focus on Bruce but the show is really, clearly, about Jim Gordon and his war on corruption. Arguably Jim and Penguin become the main characters at some point. The idea of Batman doesn't really come up, but the show does a good job showing off how the death of the Waynes was a tipping point in a tremendously corrupt city. There's shades of the 99%'er movement there, with people just sick and tired of being ground between the corrupt government and business and organized crime and just doing something about it. Which is the type of situation that led to Gotham's vigilantism. At the worst, it's a fun and occasionally over-the-top police procedural with interesting characters that takes a lot from a healthy setting that's had over seventy years of creativity poured into it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, fair enough. I really only watched the first few episodes, didn't really like it, so I stopped. I think I stopped after the episode with the kids being kidnapped by someone, and it turns out one of them is Selina Kyle (I think, it was a while ago). If it gets better I'll give it another look.<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=821743#post821743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Have you ever read <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Planetary_(comics)\" target=\"_blank\">Planetary</a>, by Warren Ellis?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have not. Is it good?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T17:10:22-08:00","id":821983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=821973#post821973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have not. Is it good?</div> </div> </div> </div>Very good. It has a lot of nods towards other comic book franchises, as the protagonists run into variants of them in their explorations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T18:33:27-08:00","id":822032,"title":"","content":"Sort-of-tangentially-comic-related-digression: nofather, is it weird that whenever I see your username I hear it pronounced in Laufey's voice from the first Thor movie?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T06:31:15-08:00","id":822323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=822032#post822032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sort-of-tangentially-comic-related-digression: nofather, is it weird that whenever I see your username I hear it pronounced in Laufey's voice from the first Thor movie?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not, I'm sure my namesake would have approved, even if he was more heated about it and fictional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T07:19:26-08:00","id":823319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=821973#post821973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have not. Is it good?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you like the sort of meta-fictional narrative that talks about the medium while in the medium - as I do - it's the best thing ever. The story follows a group of &quot;crypto-archaeologists&quot; who research the secret history of the world, which is based of tropes of pop culture over the years - from the pulp heroes in the African jungle of the early 20s through the 90s staple of profanity-spewing, countercultural British antiheroes, in additional to Multiversal theorizing (Ellis is very good at it) and references to iconic characters of the comic book culture (For example, one issue deals with whatever happened to this universe's version of Superman, Wonder Woman and Green Lantern).<br /> <br /> It's pure gold. Have a go at it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1578-patricl_gleason","name":"Patricl_Gleason","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1578_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T15:49:14-08:00","id":825133,"title":"","content":"So I read the first two issues of <b>Mystery Girl</b>. Basically, Trine, for reasons she's blanked on, has acquired the ability to instantly answer any question she encounters, excepting why she can do this. She makes a living answering questions in her &quot;sidewalk detective&quot; stand, from &quot;where's the most recent copy of my father's will&quot; to &quot;where is the evidence needed to convict this guy for the murder he committed&quot;. One day, a woman comes to her asking her to answer the question of the location of a particularly well-preserved woolly mammoth. Out of boredom and a desire to see the mammoth, Trine says she will only <i>show</i> them, not <i>tell</i> them. Meanwhile, there's a serial killer around who has fixated on Trine.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if I'd recommend this or not. The characters are decent if stereotypical, but Trine's ability - which the whole narrative is built around - has the potential to be story-breaking, or exposition-dumping. There's been a few points where the details are lacking polish already, which doesn't inspire confidence. The art is nice, but every five or so pages there's random nudity, never for any readily apparent reason. It really does come off as &quot;oh, I need to show boobs every few pages. I haven't done that in a few pages. Aaand random shower scene.&quot; The pacing could be better in places as well - her travelling to Siberia has gone for several pages already, with none of them having seemingly plot-relevant stuff, but not enough detail to be doing the &quot;Trine going travelling and shaking out of her rut&quot; thing. More than anything else, it <i>almost</i> reads like &quot;hey, these are things I heard Russians do, like stop the train so every man on board can pee in a row, and drink vodka, and boast about how they're strong in broken English!&quot; And yet, there's no sign of anybody finding Trine, a black woman, at all a novelty - I don't want to comment on nowadays, but I vaguely remember black people in Russia were pretty damn unusual sight a couple decades ago? No background characters staring at her or anything.<br /> <br /> It's not <i>bad</i>, by any measure. But I'm not confident in saying it's good, either. The quality will depend entirely on the execution of this rather tricky idea, and the writer has not yet shown that kind of finesse, so my hopes are not high.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T21:25:21-08:00","id":829103,"title":"","content":"So I finally read the Woods. It was alright, but underwhelming. I think if I hadn't read a similar story dozens of times before it would have more appeal but as it is, I have, so it doesn't. It's not badly written, just kind of predictable, and I don't trust the writers to really pull off the big mystery well. It seems that a lot of writers have caught Lost fever, and decide to just have some crazy mystery with no intention of really resolving it, or at least no idea how to, until they absolutely have to. I'll check on the Woods again when it's finished.<br /> <br /> Oh right, what it's about. A high school gets taken to another world. Like, the entire school building and everyone in it, and the world is shrouded in strange, alien forests full of creepy monsters. The other inhabitants are also Earthlings who have been taken from their world, though so far we've only seen signs of Mayans, Australian Aborigines, an English village and anachronistic Japanese Army. Others were said to have existed but fell, as some of the people seem to think the moon they're on is some sort of testing ground or competition. It seems like each group gets dropped in front of a black obelisk that touches at least one person in the group, granting them control over the flora and fauna and security systems of the planet while also leading them to 'the Black City.' So it's one part Lost in Space, another part Historical Fantasy, and another part Saved By The Bell. There's probably a more modern and relevant teenage high school show but I can't think of one off the top of my head.<br /> <br /> Fortunately I also had \u00dcber, which was really good. It's just finished up its first 'chapter,' and the next stage is '\u00dcber: Invasion.' <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=88113#post88113\">Aranis</a> called it out years ago in this thread. It's basically an alternate history where the question is asked, 'What if Nazi Germany got the atomic bomb first?' But instead of an atomic bomb, they got 'superheroes.' Though I use the term incredibly loosely. They're soldiers with super powers, really. The writers seem to have really thought over the limits of the abilities, and how they work and how they're gained, and they utterly dominate the battlefield. Fortunately for the Allies, there was a deeply entrenched British spy working in the German program, and she managed to escape with enough important information and resources for the Allies to recreate the superbeings. Unfortunately, Germany has a really big headstart, and the guy behind the program had some tricks up his sleeves as well that no one else was aware of. Even though the superhumans weren't revealed until the last possible moments, as Hitler was in his bunker, they've come back with a vengeance. And in the Pacific Theater, it turns out the man with the plan had arranged for another Axis power to gain the benefits of the program, really stifling the American movements there.<br /> <br /> It's a great story, really riveting though I imagine if you're not into history or the military it would get tedious. Surprisingly gory for the writer, but I think it's pretty appropriate, many of the 'battleship' class \u00dcbers are unstable and have been driven to extremes by their changes and duties and being used, basically, as nothing but weapons of mass destruction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T17:09:38-08:00","id":834139,"title":"","content":"So I read the first few issues of <b>Planetary</b>. I'll get to it in a minute, but first I want to talk about the X-Files.<br /> <br /> The X-Files was, and remains, one of my favourite shows. It had serious issues - most notably the appearance of an overarching plot which totally failed to deliver for a very long time - but the main draw of the show, the atmosphere of mystery and paranoia and the relationship between Mulder and Scully, made for very compelling watching. But the weakest parts of the shows were where it tried to build up the conspiracy, but they hadn't yet worked out what, exactly, was going on. As a result, the allegedly all-knowing and all-powerful conspiracy really came off as conspicuously smoke and mirrors, with no more substance than that, doing whatever was the most mysterious regardless for basic logic. Once they'd worked out what was going on, with the alien colonists and what the conspiracy actually was doing, they tended to be much more cohesive.<br /> <br /> Planetary strikes me as the early conspiracy X-Files episodes. The mystery-of-the-week stuff is cool-ish, but the total lack of answers or payoff is frustrating. And it would be fine if it felt like it was building towards something, but it doesn't - it's just &quot;hey, there's this ghost cop, and suddenly an alien thingy under the pavement! Which the next issue will promptly ignore&quot;. And &quot;we have this guy born on this seemingly significant date for no clear reason, and he's immortal! And has ice powers... sometimes!&quot; And &quot;we have this guy without a proper name who has exposition-powers, for no clear reason!&quot; And so on and so on. I <i>want</i> to like the series, I do - mystery alien magic dimensional stuff is compelling. But I can't tell the difference between inconsequential monster-of-the-week, and story-building. And the general reluctance to give any kind of answer to any question is immensely frustrating. I get they're a mystery thing, and they're building mystery. But the every issue I've read so far goes: &quot;cool yet incompletely explored setup, action scene, big reveal (usually of uncertain significance), end of issue&quot;. What happened to the reality-computer? Did they destroy it? Did they put it in a warehouse, Indiana Jones style? Are they going to use it? Is it going to be a glorified paper-weight? How did it get a sheet over it if everyone but the cripple was dead after the fight?<br /> <br /> You don't even really learn anything about the characters. So far as I've read, you know no more about them in issue #8 then you knew about them in issue #1. Jakita is your standard Action Girl, The Drummer is and has remained vaguely annoying with exposition powers, and Elijah Snow is gruff and old, with occasional ice powers. We don't know their likes and dislikes, their favourite drink, what they do in their downtime, whether they <i>have</i> downtime, how they were recruited to Planetary, do they have relationships, or anything beyond their initial characterisations. They're... I don't know the technical name, but &quot;Plot Puppets&quot; seems as good as any - they aren't people, they're devices to move the plot - such as it is - along. And I find that very flat.<br /> <br /> I <i>want</i> to like the series, I do. But it asks way too many questions, and its often clumsy handling of individual issues gives me no confidence that there's a worked out overarching plot with actual answers. And I'm reasonably patient, but you can only tease the reader for so long before they stop expecting any kind of payoff. Particularly with characters you seemingly make no effort to make engaging or remotely relatable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T21:43:00-08:00","id":834256,"title":"","content":"They get more into them. Meeting Jakita's father and stuff. Also the overall plot is about them dealing with the evil Fantastic Four.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T05:16:43-08:00","id":834378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=834139#post834139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I read the first few issues of <b>Planetary</b><br /> Planetary strikes me as the early conspiracy X-Files episodes. The mystery-of-the-week stuff is cool-ish, but the total lack of answers or payoff is frustrating. And it would be fine if it felt like it was building towards something, but it doesn't - it's just &quot;hey, there's this ghost cop, and suddenly an alien thingy under the pavement! Which the next issue will promptly ignore&quot;. And &quot;we have this guy born on this seemingly significant date for no clear reason, and he's immortal! And has ice powers... sometimes!&quot; And &quot;we have this guy without a proper name who has exposition-powers, for no clear reason!&quot; And so on and so on. I <i>want</i> to like the series, I do - mystery alien magic dimensional stuff is compelling. But I can't tell the difference between inconsequential monster-of-the-week, and story-building. And the general reluctance to give any kind of answer to any question is immensely frustrating. I get they're a mystery thing, and they're building mystery. But the every issue I've read so far goes: &quot;cool yet incompletely explored setup, action scene, big reveal (usually of uncertain significance), end of issue&quot;. What happened to the reality-computer? Did they destroy it? Did they put it in a warehouse, Indiana Jones style? Are they going to use it? Is it going to be a glorified paper-weight? How did it get a sheet over it if everyone but the cripple was dead after the fight?<br /> <br /> You don't even really learn anything about the characters. So far as I've read, you know no more about them in issue #8 then you knew about them in issue #1. Jakita is your standard Action Girl, The Drummer is and has remained vaguely annoying with exposition powers, and Elijah Snow is gruff and old, with occasional ice powers. We don't know their likes and dislikes, their favourite drink, what they do in their downtime, whether they <i>have</i> downtime, how they were recruited to Planetary, do they have relationships, or anything beyond their initial characterisations. They're... I don't know the technical name, but &quot;Plot Puppets&quot; seems as good as any - they aren't people, they're devices to move the plot - such as it is - along. And I find that very flat.<br /> <br /> I <i>want</i> to like the series, I do. But it asks way too many questions, and its often clumsy handling of individual issues gives me no confidence that there's a worked out overarching plot with actual answers. And I'm reasonably patient, but you can only tease the reader for so long before they stop expecting any kind of payoff. Particularly with characters you seemingly make no effort to make engaging or remotely relatable.</div> </div> </div> </div>You should read it all. It actually ties itself very well, and most things you have seen as throwaways will actually tie in together by the end of the story. The concept of the thing is that the series is self contained and that each story is an exploration of thematic and stylistic elements of different kind of fiction. They tie together on a meta level through a story that's going in the background, but the key is in the Fourth Man and why he actually made Planetary.<br /> <br /> With Planetary it's quite critical that you are aware of what each episode is actually talking about. Each of them nalysyes a movie, a comic book style, a literary style. They all have their own tone, and once you have seen enough of it, you will notice the pattern and key behind it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T01:54:00-08:00","id":838542,"title":"","content":"So, I've read three comics lately that I want to talk about.<br /> <br /> The first was <b>Supergirl</b>, specifically the first volume of her New 52 incarnation (issues #1-#7, I believe). Basically, Kara Zor-El/Supergirl arrives on Earth several years later than Superman for reasons not yet explained, and is totally disoriented and has no idea what's going on, a situation that is only exacerbated when her first contact is the henchmen of a powerful, morally-ambiguous-at-best businessman who is <i>not</i> Lex Luthor. The interaction goes about as well as you'd expect when a bunch of henchmen attempt to arrest a disoriented teenage girl who is suddenly manifesting superpowers and has basically no control over them. The volume mostly follows Kara's attempt to orient herself on her new world, and interacting with a bunch of bad guys.<br /> <br /> It's not <i>bad</i>, but by the end I didn't really know anything more about Kara as a character. She spent most of her time screaming, punching or crying (or all three), and being expositioned at. Maybe further issues flesh that out, but as it stands it was fun, but some more character information would have been nice. I'll keep my eyes out to see if this changes, but in itself I was kind of disappointed. Maybe if I knew the character better it'd have worked better *shrug*.<br /> <br /> Second is <b>Clean Room</b>. This one is legitimately interesting. Basically a woman's fiance kills himself after being exposed to a self-help group/cult, and she is investigating it to find out why. Along the way she encounters the mythology surrounding the &quot;Clean Room&quot;, a mysterious room within the organisations headquarters. Periodically she hallucinates (or they're real, still not sure) demons, and the head of the group is certainly suspicious. I've only read the first two issues, but I'm intrigued enough to keep my eyes on this one.<br /> <br /> It's hard to explain why this works for me in a way Planetary or other mystery series don't. It's mysterious as hell, gives basically no answers, but it does give the impression that there are answers coming. The art is fine if unremarkable, and the characters are a bit flat, but that could be because we haven't, at this point, spent much time with any of them, and it has so far focussed on setting up the mystery than informing the characters. Chloe (the woman with the dead fiance) is driven but human - she's been broken by her fiance's death, and she's on a crusade largely in a probably futile attempt to put herself back together. The way the group members talk is very much as you'd expect the members of the group to talk - describing her in jargon that is meaningless to outsiders yet clearly meant to indicate some sort of perceived &quot;fault&quot; of hers that the group can &quot;fix&quot;. The leader of the group, Astrid Mueller, is powerful, controlled, and (possibly) magical. She clearly has an agenda, and that agenda involves accumulating as much power as possible.<br /> <br /> <b>Unfollow</b> is another slow-build series. Basically the setup is the creator of a Twitter expy is dying, and sets it up so that upon his death, his billions will be split between 140 people distributed over the world, or however many are alive at the time of his death. It is clearly setting up a &quot;humans are animals who will kill each other for selfish reasons&quot; kind of story, from both the premise and how the characters talk. I can't really talk about the story beyond that because at the end of the second issue we're <i>still</i> gathering the characters. I'm starting to suspect they intend to introduce every single one of the 140 characters (no, I did not come up with that pun. It's explicitly made, several times, in the series).<br /> <br /> I'm honestly baffled as to whether I like this or not. The art is good, but there's just way too many characters: a special-forces whacko who believes God talks to him, a Japanese author who for some unclear reason cut his own legs off (either in protest of something or for artistic reasons, it's unclear), a female nature documentarian who has a habit of being victimised by men who I am starting to rather gloomily doubt is our &quot;main&quot; protagonist, since she's one of the few who we've seen multiple times, and a black youth from Harlem with gang issues and a sister (no, that's not me being racist: that's literally all we know about him). I suspect the long-term success of this will depend on 1. how long it takes to actually get to telling the story, and 2. how much I end up hating our &quot;main&quot; characters. I'm in for the ride for the moment, but if I don't see something solid in the next couple issues then I'll probably drop it. I want to see it succeed because I like the premise. The art is interesting, doing a king of semi-realistic semi-cartoonish thing which I find nice to look at, and the fauxlosophising is entertaining rather than painful, largely because I can see actual people who would talk like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T16:50:16-07:00","id":899544,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"http://www.rantlifestyle.com/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/Captain-America-Issue-1.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Turns out he was faking it the whole time.<br /> <br /> Apparently ABC is looking at Unfollow as a tv show.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T17:18:40-07:00","id":899568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=899544#post899544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><img src=\"http://www.rantlifestyle.com/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/Captain-America-Issue-1.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Turns out he was faking it the whole time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the &quot;Cap is and always was secretly a Hydra agent&quot; it is clearly a ridiculous gimmick to create outrage-driven buzz to drive up sales. Either it involves some stupid twist about being some alternate version of Cap or some idiocy like that, or it will be retconned as as soon as that writer is out.<br /> <br /> That said, it is a tremendous offense to the memory of the character's creators and the circumstances in which he was created (by Jewish people, as an answer to Nazi Germany, at a point in which the US had yet to enter the war, and there were enough people in the US actually sympathetic to the Nazi cause that it led to the offices of Timely Comics being picketed by protestors).<br /> <br /> Not only that but...well, I'm not even from the US, so I probably shouldn't be saying anything about your presidential candidates (it is not like the clusterfuck here in Brazil will help me save face XD), but even if I think Trump is a horrible person, I think trying to make a comic with a political bent and then putting the viewpoint opposing your own in the mouth of the freaking <i>Red Skull</i> is not how it should be done. That is not clever political commentary, it is literally calling your opposition super-nazis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T17:43:35-07:00","id":899581,"title":"","content":"I've never been the biggest Captain American fan(though I seriously love what they've done with the movies)...but this whole &quot;Cap is and always was secretly a Hydra agent&quot; is pretty offensive to me. What the hell are they thinking?<br /> <br /> Granted, I stepped away from Marvel when they did the giant Civil War event(after two or more other huge crossovers), so I don't have much stake in this. But this news makes me really glad I stepped away...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T18:15:27-07:00","id":899608,"title":"","content":"Hey Everyone:<br /> I\u2019m new to the boards and came across this topic, and I do pick up a lot of comics. And as it\u2019s Wednesday I do have my pulled stack already read I\u2019ll go over what I get when I get them. So after a six pack and a few shots, here we go..<br /> <br /> Tokyo Ghost #7 Still Really solid, now that the final issue is in the future this seems to be setting up the final fight between to two ex lovers. Still a cool book, kind of bummed it\u2019s ending in a few months.<br /> <br /> Superman #52 The Superman of the \u2018New 52\u2019 Universe finally dies, but it doesn\u2019t matter as the main Superman has always been here..Too long to explain the whole story<br /> <br /> Squarriors: Summer #1 The next story arch of the AWESOME story where Secret of Nimh meets Game of Thrones with a dash of Walking dead. I\u2019m a sucker for uplifted animals taking over the world. The art is great so is the dialog. Favorite book of the week<br /> <br /> Justice League #50 Darkseid wars arc is still going and it ties into the Rebirth event that also started this week. Like three people die and a group of super heroes are coming to the DC universe from an old Alan Moore series that and somehow its really kind of cool.<br /> <br /> Flash #52 Nothing special, last issue before Flash Rebirth. Just ending this series with a Ho Hum story<br /> <br /> Extraordinary X-Men #10: Their part in this Apocalypse War Event, (if you really want to call it an event.) The Story is ok, not the greatest X-Men book out now, but not the worst.<br /> <br /> Deathstroke #18: Ok issue, Slades got his kids back, he still has one eye, eh it\u2019s ok. Feels like things might be in a rush to end for Deathstrokes Rebirth in a few months.<br /> <br /> Daredevil #7: Electra had a kid, she looking for it. The kid might be Daredevils, answers lead to more questions.<br /> <br /> Carnage #8: I really liked Carnage when it first came out, not feeling it so much now. Eight issues in, traveled across the world and back and still on the same arc..just isn\u2019t progressing like it should.<br /> <br /> Bloodshot Reborn #13: We wrap up the Analog man story and..wow. I really love a lot of Valiant comics. This story was a fun read and segways to the next story nicely. I think Lemire has done this telling of Blooshot really well.<br /> <br /> Aliens: Defiance #2: Love the are and feel of this story. Always loved Dark Horse take on Aliens and this is no exception.<br /> <br /> DC Rebirth #1: Honestly, I thought it was really good. The book is really big for only 3 bucks. This is really the only issue for this story as the rest of the event is just told in the books you\u2019d already picked up. We see pre 52 Wally West again in a way that was kind of touching, (if you know about a lot of stuff in DC comics you\u2019d understand and don\u2019t want to spoil it.) I have really been rooting for DC comics but have been left underwhelmed with past events, this one is different. This is really a decent story and ties into a lot of what has been going on in other titles nicely. Looking forward to next week.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11846-atomichammer","name":"AtomicHammer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11846_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T13:39:02-07:00","id":903752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=899568#post899568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, it is a tremendous offense to the memory of the character's creators and the circumstances in which he was created (by Jewish people, as an answer to Nazi Germany, at a point in which the US had yet to enter the war, and there were enough people in the US actually sympathetic to the Nazi cause that it led to the offices of Timely Comics being picketed by protestors).</div> </div> </div> </div>I gotta say, I don't know Joe Simon OR Jack Kirby, but I've read enough of their work and know enough of how comics were written at the time to say, with some confidence, that neither of them would've given much of a fuck. Much like how, Gerber, Busiek and a few million different writers (lots of them, having written Cap) also don't really give a fuck.<br /> <br /> People have been doing this kind of ridiculous twist as long as comics have been around. Literally the only people who have a bug up their arse about it are MCU band wagon jumpers and recreationally offended social justice warriors.<br /> <br /> The real outrage is how many old guard creators are getting shit from these groups because they were anything less than horror struck by it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T15:23:57-07:00","id":903802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=903752#post903752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People have been doing this kind of ridiculous twist as long as comics have been around. Literally the only people who have a bug up their arse about it are MCU band wagon jumpers and recreationally offended social justice warriors.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I can tell, these &quot;MCU band wagon jumpers&quot; seem to be doing a lot to breath some life into the industry. Hell, I got into comics initially because I liked the Iron Man movies (well, the first two) so much. I'd eyeballed them before, of course, but it was the movies that pushed me over the edge. So I'd say they're as legitimate fans as anything else.<br /> <br /> That said, I do agree with you that it's a stupid ploy to garner publicity and readers. It'll turn out he's been brainwashed or it's a clone or whatever and we'll all pretend it never happened, like Superboy punching reality for DC fans, or the story where Superman stopped some aliens settling in some small town as a weird metaphor for illegal immigration. It's happened before, it'll happen again, and it'll be just as dumb then. It's just that long-time comic book people have been around to see enough of this bullshit to just ignore it for the short-term thing that it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T15:27:36-07:00","id":903805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=903752#post903752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I gotta say, I don't know Joe Simon OR Jack Kirby, but I've read enough of their work and know enough of how comics were written at the time to say, with some confidence, that neither of them would've given much of a fuck.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that's accurate, Kirby was in World War 2, he probably wouldn't enjoy the character he was originally going to name Super American to turn out to be a Nazi..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> People have been doing this kind of ridiculous twist as long as comics have been around. Literally the only people who have a bug up their arse about it are MCU band wagon jumpers and recreationally offended social justice warriors. </div> </div> </div>It's got nothing to do with social justice. It's the same kind of thing that has people getting pissy when Superman kills Zod. It's seen, accurately, as a betrayal of the character for the sake of twitter trending and outrage purchases.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=903802#post903802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, I do agree with you that it's a stupid ploy to garner publicity and readers. It'll turn out he's been brainwashed or it's a clone or whatever and we'll all pretend it never happened,</div> </div> </div> </div>They've already said it's not a clone or mind control or anything like that. It's 'real' Captain America. The comic itself backs it up, at least to an extent, it shows him being recruited before the super soldier serum program.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-30-2016, 06:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T18:02:54-07:00","id":903878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=903752#post903752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Literally the only people who have a bug up their arse about it are MCU band wagon jumpers and recreationally offended <b>social justice warriors</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny that the writer, Nick Spencer, is someone who has identified as such in the past, and is extremely liberal and progressive in his politics throughout ALL of his written work.<br /> <br /> I think some older fans(like myself) are slightly annoyed by this story for many reasons.<br /> <br /> I know people like to bring up the notion that Cap has done something like this before. Except, when he did, he was BRAINWASHED. Pretty different from announcing he has been &quot;Hydra&quot; the entire team. Very different, actually.<br /> <br /> By the way, I'm not giving you crap, I'm just trying to bring in a different perspective. Brainwashing story 5 decades ago is one thing; announcing the character has been Hydra all along is pretty shitty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T04:50:57-07:00","id":904090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=903805#post903805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They've already said it's not a clone or mind control or anything like that. It's 'real' Captain America. The comic itself backs it up, at least to an extent, it shows him being recruited before the super soldier serum program.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it remains true in a year, then I'll believe it. Until then, I deem sufficient cause to be skeptical.<br /> <br /> I suppose they could be going for a &quot;was bad, but now overcoming ones badness&quot; storyline? If the writer is a self-described SJW, then I could see that as a possibility. It's dumb and dull, but not the dumbest/dullest thing in existence.<br /> <br /> But I remain skeptical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T05:20:03-07:00","id":904096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=903805#post903805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think that's accurate, Kirby was in World War 2, he probably wouldn't enjoy the character he was originally going to name Super American to turn out to be a Nazi..</div> </div> </div> </div>He worked during the Silver Age, which is pretty much where this kind of trope came from. Probably wouldn't have liked it during WWII, because there's a WAR on man. But, we kinda won and it's ancient history.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's got nothing to do with social justice. It's the same kind of thing that has people getting pissy when Superman kills Zod. It's seen, accurately, as a betrayal of the character for the sake of twitter trending and outrage purchases. </div> </div> </div>I really hate to break this to you. But this is like, the third time he's done it. I don't like it when he kills anyone, but if he's gotta kill somebody, Zod has precedent.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They've already said it's not a clone or mind control or anything like that. It's 'real' Captain America. The comic itself backs it up, at least to an extent, it shows him being recruited before the super soldier serum program. </div> </div> </div>So you're saying it's &quot;Not a Hoax! Not a dream! Not an Imaginary Tale!&quot;<br /> <br /> I mean, shit bro. There IS a universe in Marvel where the Nazis won WWII, maybe HydraCap comes from that one. Maybe Red Skull's pulling some other kind of bullshit, maybe, Steve is playing a stupidly convoluted long game. I don't know. Don't really care either, this kind of thing lost it's luster the umpteenth time I saw it on a Superdickery page.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T05:46:14-07:00","id":904105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=903802#post903802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I can tell, these &quot;MCU band wagon jumpers&quot; seem to be doing a lot to breath some life into the industry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quantitatively, sure. Granted. Qualitatively? I've been in too many threads about the latest Marvel or WB/DC movie devolving into an out and out company war to honestly believe that.<br /> <br /> But more to my original point, they don't know the various tropes like this, because Hollywood refuses to take those tropes seriously. Or just can't display them because they really don't gel with a movie. Whichever reason you end up with a significant fanbase that's harassing Kurt Busiek for saying Helmut Zemo is not a Nazi*.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hell, I got into comics initially because I liked the Iron Man movies (well, the first two) so much. I'd eyeballed them before, of course, but it was the movies that pushed me over the edge. So I'd say they're as legitimate fans as anything else. </div> </div> </div>You're not unique in that regard. I think the vast majority of comic fans become comic fans because of the secondary media. Batman's popular because holy shit, a few dozen successful live action movies, cartoons, video games and all that jazz.. Superman's has a few Live Action shows, a few cartoons, that one Radio Show and the Iconic movies from the seventies.<br /> <br /> Thing is, the vast majority of them are going to die off when the gravy train stops rolling, whenever that happens. And in my limited experience those same people are making it very hard to have a civilized discussion about comics and comic related media because they're too busy flinging shit at each other about reviews, box office performances, and a few other asinine aspects. So I can't say I'll be said to see them gone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T06:00:06-07:00","id":904113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=903878#post903878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Funny that the writer, Nick Spencer, is someone who has identified as such in the past, and is extremely liberal and progressive in his politics throughout ALL of his written work.</div> </div> </div> </div>SJWs are not a united front or this one big happy family. They are like sharks. They follow the blood and take a bite out of whatever they find bleeding. Whedon was a feminist and they crucified him over twitter over his rendition of Black Widow.<br /> A webcomic artist known as Thunt was driven to near permanent hiatus due to their harassing. He was raised as a feminist his entire life. But that didn't mean a thing.<br /> <br /> Being an SJW is not a guarantee of protection against the more militant SJWs. Strange as it sounds it puts you under greater risk of being attacked, sort of like the Party in 1984. It's why the sanest thing a progressive liberal can do is avoid them at all costs. Nothing worse than a &quot;righteous&quot; extremist.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T07:08:20-07:00","id":904125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=904096#post904096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really hate to break this to you. But this is like, the third time he's done it. I don't like it when he kills anyone, but if he's gotta kill somebody, Zod has precedent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering more recent depictions of Superman have had him increasingly acting more 'boy scout,' him killing him, particularly by snapping his neck, was seen as unnecessarily brutal for the character, however justified the act was. Perhaps it was a bad example, though, because there was no precedent for Steve Rogers to be a member of Hydra since the early 1900s until now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So you're saying it's &quot;Not a Hoax! Not a dream! Not an Imaginary Tale!&quot; </div> </div> </div>I didn't say that at all. I said that 'they' said that. The writer and editor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nick Spencer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">SPENCER: Issue 2 will lay a lot of our cards on the table in terms of what the new status quo is, but the one thing we can say unequivocally is: This is not a clone, not an imposter, not mind control, not someone else acting through Steve. This really is Steve Rogers, Captain America himself.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>USA Today</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Marvel executive editor Tom Brevoort confirms that it\u2019s really Steve Rogers and not some clone, shapeshifting Skrull, Life Model Decoy or a Cap from an alternate universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get that you don't like social justice warriors, not being one I don't particularly care. But you seem to be fine acknowledging it's just a gimmick, you just don't think it's a gimmick in poor taste?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=904090#post904090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it remains true in a year, then I'll believe it. Until then, I deem sufficient cause to be skeptical.<br /> <br /> I suppose they could be going for a &quot;was bad, but now overcoming ones badness&quot; storyline? If the writer is a self-described SJW, then I could see that as a possibility. It's dumb and dull, but not the dumbest/dullest thing in existence.<br /> <br /> But I remain skeptical.</div> </div> </div> </div>As above. I think rather than changing the writing, since 'there's no such thing as bad press,' they'll just reboot it or retcon it later on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-31-2016, 10:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T08:52:34-07:00","id":904203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=904113#post904113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">SJWs are not a united front or this one big happy family. They are like sharks. They follow the blood and take a bite out of whatever they find bleeding. Whedon was a feminist and they crucified him over twitter over his rendition of Black Widow.<br /> A webcomic artist known as Thunt was driven to near permanent hiatus due to their harassing. He was raised as a feminist his entire life. But that didn't mean a thing.<br /> <br /> Being an SJW is not a guarantee of protection against the more militant SJWs. Strange as it sounds it puts you under greater risk of being attacked, sort of like the Party in 1984. It's why the sanest thing a progressive liberal can do is avoid them at all costs. Nothing worse than a &quot;righteous&quot; extremist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes sense. And I can agree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T14:32:56-07:00","id":904453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=904125#post904125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Considering more recent depictions of Superman have had him increasingly acting more 'boy scout,' him killing him, particularly by snapping his neck, was seen as unnecessarily brutal for the character, however justified the act was. Perhaps it was a bad example, though, because there was no precedent for Steve Rogers to be a member of Hydra since the early 1900s until now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cape Comics have been around for 78 Years. Believe me, there IS. At this moment I cannot quite think of it, I'm afraid. Closest I can get to is Terra's infiltration of the New Teen Titans, but even that doesn't quite fit.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I didn't say that at all. I said that 'they' said that. The writer and editor. </div> </div> </div>And they've been saying it since the fifties, nofather.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But you seem to be fine acknowledging it's just a gimmick, you just don't think it's a gimmick in poor taste? </div> </div> </div>On that mark, I'm going to reserve judgement until this whole thing is done. Some very brilliant stories came of this sort of nonsense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T15:05:36-07:00","id":904485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=904453#post904453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cape Comics have been around for 78 Years. Believe me, there IS. At this moment I cannot quite think of it, I'm afraid. Closest I can get to is Terra's infiltration of the New Teen Titans, but even that doesn't quite fit.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no precedent for Captain America being a member of Hydra. There are crazy twists all the time, but usually they have some reason behind them. This is probably the writer's attempt to paint patriotism out as a form of fascism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And they've been saying it since the fifties, nofather. </div> </div> </div>So you seem to think it's a gimmick and the writer and editor are lying about it and you still don't think it's in poor taste? In even more poor taste in that case?<br /> <br /> Incidentally, the idea that the only people who a problem with it are '<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">MCU band wagon jumpers and recreationally offended social justice warriors,' is just wrong. You may enjoy it, or just not care, that doesn't mean that people who do are 'less real fans' or some sort of social clique you don't approve of.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-31-2016, 06:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T15:22:41-07:00","id":904497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=904105#post904105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quantitatively, sure. Granted. Qualitatively? I've been in too many threads about the latest Marvel or WB/DC movie devolving into an out and out company war to honestly believe that.<br /> <br /> But more to my original point, they don't know the various tropes like this, because Hollywood refuses to take those tropes seriously. Or just can't display them because they really don't gel with a movie. Whichever reason you end up with a significant fanbase that's harassing Kurt Busiek for saying Helmut Zemo is not a Nazi*.<br /> <br /> You're not unique in that regard. I think the vast majority of comic fans become comic fans because of the secondary media. Batman's popular because holy shit, a few dozen successful live action movies, cartoons, video games and all that jazz.. Superman's has a few Live Action shows, a few cartoons, that one Radio Show and the Iconic movies from the seventies.<br /> <br /> Thing is, the vast majority of them are going to die off when the gravy train stops rolling, whenever that happens. And in my limited experience those same people are making it very hard to have a civilized discussion about comics and comic related media because they're too busy flinging shit at each other about reviews, box office performances, and a few other asinine aspects. So I can't say I'll be said to see them gone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's true of any hobby/past-time, really. It's quite common to get into something through something else, and most people start a hobby then drop off after a while. And unfortunately, some people are really annoying during that time. They're certainly ignorant, because they're new.<br /> <br /> But given that readership of comics has been dropping since, well, a long time, and artistically it's been somewhat circular for a while, I'd say some new eyes/readers is a good thing. Yeah, they're going to be idiots for a while. But maybe the long-timers are too set on how things are, so they are more likely to see any change as idiotic. From the inside, the other side always looks wrong.<br /> <br /> Just to use Iron Man as an example, the movies have legitimately affected the comics - for the better, in my eyes, but I'm a comparative newbie. And now it's far more accessible to whatever new people are coming along, since they can draw on a couple of 90-minute movies rather than having to slog through dozens or hundreds of issues. Will there be differences? Sure. But they can grasp the &quot;essence&quot; of what's going on, and I'd say most people are willing to put in the work if they have what they feel is a starting point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=904113#post904113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">SJWs are not a united front or this one big happy family. They are like sharks. They follow the blood and take a bite out of whatever they find bleeding. Whedon was a feminist and they crucified him over twitter over his rendition of Black Widow.<br /> A webcomic artist known as Thunt was driven to near permanent hiatus due to their harassing. He was raised as a feminist his entire life. But that didn't mean a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say piranhas is a better analogy. If they're alone, they're damaging, sure, but it's when they swarm which the real terror begins. Plus groups are their natural state of being. A quick google search says that some species are in fact cannibals, so that works too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T19:46:12-07:00","id":904661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=904485#post904485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no precedent for Captain America being a member of Hydra. There are crazy twists all the time, but usually they have some reason behind them. This is probably the writer's attempt to paint patriotism out as a form of fascism.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sort of story's been done quite a few times in Captain America. One of the most celebrated Captain America speeches is him talking to a mob on the actions and policies of a false Captain America who's trying to manipulate people's patriotism towards fascism. Or at least white supremacy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So you seem to think it's a gimmick and the writer and editor are lying about it and you still don't think it's in poor taste? In even more poor taste in that case? </div> </div> </div>Again. Reserving judgement until the entire thing plays out. If it's a bad story, it'll be forgotten and phased out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Incidentally, the idea that the only people who a problem with it are '<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">MCU band wagon jumpers and recreationally offended social justice warriors,' is just wrong. </span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Enlighten me. Correct me. If not them, then who?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","user":"The Revenge of TV Head","date":". 05-31-2016, 10:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T20:20:08-07:00","id":904677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=904661#post904661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">That sort of story's been done quite a few times in Captain America. One of the most celebrated Captain America speeches is him talking to a mob on the actions and policies of a false Captain America who's trying to manipulate people's patriotism towards fascism. Or at least white supremacy.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Except that 'true' Captain America was a fascist the whole time now.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again. Reserving judgement until the entire thing plays out. If it's a bad story, it'll be forgotten and phased out. </div> </div> </div>That seems more avoiding the question. You seem very intent in believing that the people behind it are lying to their customers, is that fine if it's a good story?<br /> <br /> Besides, it's going to be phased out anyways since <a href=\"http://www.newsarama.com/29524-marvel-now-and-again-this-is-the-world-we-live-in.html\" target=\"_blank\">Marvel is switching to a yearly reboot system.</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Enlighten me. Correct me. If not them, then who? </div> </div> </div>Comic fans who don't like bad writing and the sacrificing of a characters' history for some gimmick or political statement by a writer. Basically anyone with taste or an, I admit, devotion to canon or continuity. I don't even know where you got the idea, but we were talking about comics and no one's brought up these social justice issues you have a problem with or don't have a problem with. And your posts have been dismissing anyone who has a problem with it, ignoring it and just talking about your problems with social justice warriors, which seems deserving of its own thread unless you want to swing it back to comics. Green Arrow is a social justice warrior for instance, and the awful webcomics of Dave Willis seem to fit the description.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/HxuZH0y.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> From the new Green Arrow, sort of going back to his roots.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-31-2016, 11:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T21:52:11-07:00","id":904715,"title":"","content":"For me, back in the day (early-mid 80s) i started getting into Action force (The uk version of GI joe), The UK version of Transformers (which imo had MORE to it than the stateside version), and Via the Transformers UK comics, i got into several others... Such as Strike force Morituri, Machineman, Machine man 2020, Visionaries, Zoids, and even Inhumanoids.. <br /> After that, i started getting into the X series of comics, starting with Xmen, Xman, Uncanny X, Xfactor, Xforce, Cable, Gen X, and then branched out a little into the Avengers and such. Mostly for the crossover stuff. Sometime right around the 2nd coming of Onslaught/Operation Zero tolerance neck of the woods, i stopped getting them.<br /> I also did a little for DC comics, centering around and just after the death of Superman..<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T22:36:43-07:00","id":904729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=904677#post904677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Except that 'true' Captain America was a fascist the whole time now.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Seemingly, yes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That seems more avoiding the question. You seem very intent in believing that the people behind it are lying to their customers, is that fine if it's a good story? </div> </div> </div>What's the difference between a good story and a well constructed lie?<br /> <br /> Of course they lie. We pay to buy them. That doesn't mean we can't be cognizant that they're still lies. Or that we should embitter ourselves about it either. Superman and Lois didn't marry eachother in that one issue way back in the Silver Age, but that doesn't mean you can't tell interesting stories with Van Zee and his wife. Or that doing it was specifically wrong or somehow unethical.<br /> I, for one, will not pass judgement on this particular lie, this story, until the story is done. Call it morbid curiosity, maybe I'm a bit too jaded or complacent. But I just don't see the point in getting riled up over a weird twist in a comic book. Certainly not in harassing older writers and artists who for not joining in on the rage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Comic fans who don't like bad writing and the sacrificing of a characters' history for some gimmick or political statement by a writer. Basically anyone with taste or an, I admit, devotion to canon or continuity. </div> </div> </div>I look at the figures that are being harassed and cannot say they're anyone that someone who is devoted to canon and continuity.<br /> Spencer getting shit is one thing. Steve Gerber? Ed Brubaker? Busiek?<br /> Those three at least, are NOT getting shit from comic book fans who enjoy the long, crazy, history of in universe comics. Because they're either devoted fans of it or MADE THAT HISTORY.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't even know where you got the idea, but we were talking about comics and no one's brought up these social justice issues you have a problem with or don't have a problem with. </div> </div> </div>p the people who are complaining and harassing other people based on their complaints. Larry noted that Spencer shares a lot in common with the people who are bothering him, I explained why this is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And your posts have been dismissing anyone who has a problem with it </div> </div> </div>Well, I can't slap people through the internet, so this is my only recourse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T22:47:13-07:00","id":904734,"title":"","content":"Me personally? I'm tired of the &quot;comic x's new story has ruined my childhood and the writer should be fired immediately&quot; bullshit. Which usually comes before the story has gotten past its first chapter. People cry that comics just retread the same ground over and over again, then get insanely offended when they don't. Did I say I think that's bullshit yet? Oh yeah, I believe I did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T22:55:05-07:00","id":904739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=904677#post904677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Except that 'true' Captain America was a fascist the whole time now.</span></span></span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It'll be true until it's not. Hence why there's no need to get angry, because comics make a lot of noise but things rarely change in any fundamental way, and very rarely for any length of time - at least once they've settled into their groove. The next writer or editor or whatever will retcon it.<br /> <br /> Is it dumb? Sure. Would it piss me off if I were a Cap fan? Probably. It's just a gimmick and cash grab - maybe poor taste, maybe not, I'm not in a place to judge. But it <i>is</i> stupid, and if I got angry every time someone did something stupid I'd never get any work done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T22:56:02-07:00","id":904740,"title":"","content":"And Oh my FUCKING god, I finally thought of a retcon that actually approaches Cap being a fascist all along!<br /> <br /> Okay, this was mercifully before your time, but there was this supervillain, kind of a harmless idiot called &quot;Dr. Light&quot;, his superpower was bending light about. He was a jobber bad guy for the Justice League, Teen Titans and possibly the third Flash, Wally West.<br /> <br /> In the 2004 DC limited series, Identity Crisis, it was revealed that the reason he was so lame was because he was brainwashed. By several members of the Justice League.<br /> That is, Ray Palmer, Dinah Lance, Carter Hall, Hal Jordan, Barry Allen and Zatanna (who actually performed the brainwashing via magic). These are Heroes that basically defined the Silver and Bronze Ages of comics. And not only did they brainwash Dr. Light, who had, moments before raped Elongated Man's wife*, but Batman, because Batman walked in on the proceedings and raised a number of objections.<br /> Even the fan reactions to it is reminiscent of some of today's outrage.<br /> <br /> Hell I was about as mad about it then as you seem to be about Cap now. So I guess there might be something to what you're saying.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *THE ARISTOCRATS! Identity Crisis was horrible**.<br /> Edit: **However, a number of great stories came along because of Identity Crisis. ReadingRalph's sections of 52 were far more rewarding knowing what he goes through in Identity Crisis. Pretty much the only time I'd suggest reading it is if you're prepping yourself to read 52. Which I cannot gush enough about. It's an inspiring thing about comics, even the bad stories can be re-purposed into telling good ones. Another reason why I don't really get mad if a story turns out to be poor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","user":"The Revenge of TV Head","date":". 06-01-2016, 02:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T04:51:56-07:00","id":904862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=904740#post904740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the difference between a good story and a well constructed lie?<br /> <br /> Of course they lie. We pay to buy them. That doesn't mean we can't be cognizant that they're still lies. Or that we should embitter ourselves about it either. Superman and Lois didn't marry eachother in that one issue way back in the Silver Age, but that doesn't mean you can't tell interesting stories with Van Zee and his wife. Or that doing it was specifically wrong or somehow unethical.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't believe there's a difference between a story and an interview with USA Today, or any other piece of media?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And Oh my FUCKING god, I finally thought of a retcon that actually approaches Cap being a fascist all along!<br /> <br /> Okay, this was mercifully before your time, but there was this supervillain, kind of a harmless idiot called &quot;Dr. Light&quot;, his superpower was bending light about. He was a jobber bad guy for the Justice League, Teen Titans and possibly the third Flash, Wally West.<br /> <br /> In the 2004 DC limited series, Identity Crisis, it was revealed that the reason he was so lame was because he was brainwashed. By several members of the Justice League.<br /> That is, Ray Palmer, Dinah Lance, Carter Hall, Hal Jordan, Barry Allen and Zatanna (who actually performed the brainwashing via magic). These are Heroes that basically defined the Silver and Bronze Ages of comics. And not only did they brainwash Dr. Light, who had, moments before raped Elongated Man's wife*, but Batman, because Batman walked in on the proceedings and raised a number of objections.<br /> Even the fan reactions to it is reminiscent of some of today's outrage.<br /> <br /> Hell I was about as mad about it then as you seem to be about Cap now. So I guess there might be something to what you're saying. </div> </div> </div>Identity Crisis wasn't 'before my time,' as just because I'm not a social justice warrior or new to the hobby doesn't mean I'm some comic bandwagon jumper. Besides, that actually had some merit, because Dr. Light was a more serious villain before he started being a joke to the Teen Titans, just like Catwoman was a more serious villain before she became an antihero. And Carter Hall and Oliver Queen, who was also there, have always taken an alternative route to their heroics. The story was used to explain changes in characters personalities over the years.<br /> <br /> You assume a lot and between that you being a loudmouth, you're really acting like an ass. But who cares.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=904739#post904739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It'll be true until it's not. Hence why there's no need to get angry, because comics make a lot of noise but things rarely change in any fundamental way, and very rarely for any length of time - at least once they've settled into their groove. The next writer or editor or whatever will retcon it.<br /> <br /> Is it dumb? Sure. Would it piss me off if I were a Cap fan? Probably. It's just a gimmick and cash grab - maybe poor taste, maybe not, I'm not in a place to judge. But it <i>is</i> stupid, and if I got angry every time someone did something stupid I'd never get any work done.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure whether it's a good thing comic fandom is so used to this stuff they just wait till it's over, or a bad thing that they're so resigned but keep supporting it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-01-2016, 08:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T05:26:16-07:00","id":904873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=904661#post904661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Enlighten me. Correct me. If not them,<b> then who?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm in NO WAY a social justice _______. Not in the least. I'm also a huge comic fan of 30+ years. And I don't like what they're doing with Cap. I'm not in outrage over it, but I'm certainly not a fan of it. Though to be fair, I'm also not a fan of Nick Spencer(the writer).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T05:30:52-07:00","id":904875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=904873#post904873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though to be fair, I'm also not a fan of Nick Spencer(the writer).</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you read Morning Glories? Apparently he wrote it, and it's gotten good reviews but I've never gotten around to getting past the first issue.<br /> <br /> Thief of Thieves was a letdown, and I've only read a couple issues of his Marvel comics. People raved over Ant-Man but I found it pretty boring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T07:10:44-07:00","id":904939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=904875#post904875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Have you read <b>Morning Glories</b>? Apparently he wrote it, and it's gotten good reviews but I've never gotten around to getting past the first issue.<br /> <br /> Thief of Thieves was a letdown, and I've only read a couple issues of his Marvel comics. People raved over Ant-Man but I found it pretty boring.</div> </div> </div> </div>Haven't read it yet, but I've heard decent things about it. I've heard some good things about The Fix(which I think he is currently writing, too). But I've sampled his work, and I'm not a fan of writers injecting their own political views into their work. I mean, I guess if it's subtle(and minor) I can usually look past it. But not when it becomes a major part of the story. I read a few issues of Frank Tieri's Catwoman, and noticed a ton of references to being anti-police. Not anti-bad cop, but anti-law enforcement. As someone with cops in my family, it was a huge turn off.<br /> <br /> Same reason I'm not a huge fan of Mage the Ascension(although I respect Phil as he's a great writer) or any of David Hill's work. There's a number of Marvel writers that are similar.<br /> <br /> I'm just not good enough to separate the author's political views and their work. Especially when I can SEE it in their writing. Character flaw, I guess.<br /> <br /> I wish I could turn it off or simply not care, but I can't.<br /> <br /> Antman was AMAZING under Robert Kirkman. I wish he were still writing it, but I still get my Kirkman fix with Invincible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":95,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","user":"Fat Larry","date":". 06-01-2016, 10:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T13:19:03-07:00","id":905136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=904862#post904862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't believe there's a difference between a story and an interview with USA Today, or any other piece of media?</div> </div> </div> </div>When you're going to be spewing half truths either way? Not really. I don't get pissed when I find out the ocean is wet either. Getting pissed about something you can't change is just a waste of energy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Identity Crisis wasn't 'before my time, </div> </div> </div>2004. Iron Man came out in 2008. Then again, Identity Crisis did sell a lot of trades, commercially it was a pretty big success. Anger sells I guess.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ' as just because I'm not a social justice warrior or new to the hobby doesn't mean I'm some comic bandwagon jumper. Besides, that actually had some merit, because Dr. Light was a more serious villain before he started being a joke to the Teen Titans, just like Catwoman was a more serious villain before she became an antihero. And Carter Hall and Oliver Queen, who was also there, have always taken an alternative route to their heroics. The story was used to explain changes in characters personalities over the years. </div> </div> </div>And it was fucking terrible. Raped and murdered Sue, Retconned Jean Loring into a deranged killer and Batman into an unapproachable lunatic until 52. And retconned a number of great heroes to the Silver Age into the kind of people who'd brainwash not just an enemy, but an ally.<br /> <br /> But it had merit because you see, Dr. Light wasn't as intimidating in one book as he was in another.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You assume a lot and between that you being a loudmouth, you're really acting like an ass. </div> </div> </div>You're breaking my heart, kid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T16:48:20-07:00","id":905262,"title":"","content":"Back again and unfortunately sober this week. Just going over what I got and read. Or is everyone finally ready to jump on the Hydra bandwagon? Steve Rodgers did!<br /> <br /> Civil War II #1 I didn\u2019t like the first Civil War, (no, not the one in 1861,) This one starts off ok. This event has Minority Report written all over the premise and I hated that story. At least Thanos wacks a couple of heroes. Yeah I was excited he wacked to characters that I had no emotional attachment too and the story gave me not a lot of reason to mourn their loss. Where\u2019s Captain America to say \u201cHail Hydra\u201d when you need him to?<br /> <br /> 4001 AD #2 Valiant is so under rated, Might be the best read for the summer for me. <br /> <br /> Army of Darkness: Furious Road #4 Let\u2019s be honest, its not going to win any Eisner awards. It\u2019s full of clich\u00e9s from the movies, and not original, but it\u2019s an ok read.<br /> <br /> Batman Rebirth: I\u2019m not sure what I just read. The whole issue takes place over a year, and Calendar Man crawls out of his own body through his mouth. It was just an odd \u2018set up\u2019 for the new on-going series.<br /> <br /> Green Arrow Rebirth: Pretty decent. The art is hit or miss sometimes. This feels a lot more like the Pre 52 Arrow but with the new 52 history.<br /> <br /> Green Lanterns Rebirth: Hal leaves Jessica and Baz to watch Earth as he looks for the Corps? (Thought Baz was with the Corps when they vanished?) I swear they have different colorist doing the same book, that\u2019s so annoying! Decent set up book if you\u2019re into \u201cC Lister\u201d Green Lantern Corps<br /> <br /> Moon Knight #3 I\u2019m not to sure if Moon Knight is actually crazy or really being chased by ancient Egyptian devils. But I feel we need definite answers soon or we are just spinning our wheels. Moon Knight is still fun to read thus far.<br /> <br /> Predator: Life and Death #4 Last issue but not the last issue..<br /> <br /> Punisher #2 Still love the Punisher after all these years. Becky Cloonan and Steve Dillion doing a good job writing, but the art can be a turn off for me at times. Tim Bradstreet please come back to do the covers.<br /> <br /> Superman Rebirth: Another set up issue but was a decent read explaining the difference between the two Supermen and reminds us all stuff in comics are never truly forever..even death<br /> <br /> Superman: Coming of Supermen #5: When this Miniseries was announced I was real excited. I was a big fan of Neal Adams art in the day, now I can\u2019t wait until this story is over. I don\u2019t know if Neal\u2019s art is being rushed or he lost his touch doing too much acid back in the day. In a few panels it looks like one guy is Marty Feldman looking in two different directions at the same time, like he\u2019s gone full derp.<br /> <br /> Walking Dead #155 The book has been this set up for \u2018All Out War\u2019 part 2 for a while now, will if finally start next issue?<br /> <br /> What did everyone else get?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11846-atomichammer","name":"AtomicHammer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11846_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T21:16:57-07:00","id":905393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AtomicHammer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=905262#post905262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What did everyone else get?</div> </div> </div> </div>Aside from the usual, tried out Interceptor 1-2. Seems good so far. Sort of post-post vampire apocalypse. Humanity left to another planet to inhabit, Palus, and tried to forget the fact that they were running away from the vampires controlling the Earth, which they nuked upon leaving. A long time later and the president of the new planet is informed that nuking the Earth didn't kill the vampires and apparently they've got at least the basics of a space program as some of them have been found on Palus.<br /> <br /> The story is mostly about the incredibly well-armed super soldier they sent back to Earth to ensure the vampires are destroyed, who has found that not only did vampires survive and thrive, but so did the previously unknown human resistance that was left behind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T16:07:56-07:00","id":906772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=905393#post905393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aside from the usual,</div> </div> </div> </div>Whats your usual stuff?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11846-atomichammer","name":"AtomicHammer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11846_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T16:51:35-07:00","id":906804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AtomicHammer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=906772#post906772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whats your usual stuff?</div> </div> </div> </div>Batman, in this case Rebirth. Agree with you sort of weird but seems to be a special issue with a nod to Watchmen and the new continuity. Otherwise this week Injustice, Nailbiter, Providence, and Knights of the Dinner Table. I'll probably grab Dr. Fate at some point but not a regular reader.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T19:52:44-07:00","id":906908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=905136#post905136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And it was fucking terrible. Raped and murdered Sue, Retconned Jean Loring into a deranged killer and Batman into an unapproachable lunatic until 52. And retconned a number of great heroes to the Silver Age into the kind of people who'd brainwash not just an enemy, but an ally.<br /> <br /> But it had merit because you see, Dr. Light wasn't as intimidating in one book as he was in another.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, it started or solidify a trend of masturbating deathstroke/batman because they can take on the whole JLA single handedly without preparation.<br /> <br /> Reading the original titans Dr Light wasnt *that* kind of a joke. He was fairly competent but i always felt that &quot;was a joke villan all that time&quot; was because identity crisis told me so not because of any kind of previous reading but that could just be me.<br /> <br /> And it kinda backfire it. Dr Light didnt became any more threatening by replace 90% of his dialogues with the word rape.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AtomicHammer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=905262#post905262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What did everyone else get?</div> </div> </div> </div>Finally got around to read power man &amp; Iron Fist. Good stuff, i get a good 70s vibe from it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AtomicHammer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=905262#post905262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Civil War II #1 I didn\u2019t like the first Civil War, (no, not the one in 1861,) This one starts off ok. This event has Minority Report written all over the premise and I hated that story. At least Thanos wacks a couple of heroes. Yeah I was excited he wacked to characters that I had no emotional attachment too and the story gave me not a lot of reason to mourn their loss. Where\u2019s Captain America to say \u201cHail Hydra\u201d when you need him to?</div> </div> </div> </div>I really dislike it. It could have worked but they drop the ball the moment thanos appeared any kind of moral ambiguity and question about the use of power went out of the window.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T00:20:32-07:00","id":907012,"title":"","content":"Picked up Old Man Logan(which was good), Green Lantern Rebirth(also, good), Green Arrow Rebirth(which was horrible), and The Punisher(also horrible).<br /> <br /> 50% success rate. Not too bad. <br /> <br /> I also skipped Moon Knight which, after skimming through it at the store, is taking far TOO LONG to actually go anywhere. Sad I wasted 10 bucks on the first two issues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T16:01:41-07:00","id":907314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=906908#post906908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really dislike it. It could have worked but they drop the ball the moment thanos appeared any kind of moral ambiguity and question about the use of power went out of the window.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasnt a fan of the first Civil War and it feels Bendis is just doing shock writing to gain response, but it was the first issue i will see how it ends","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11846-atomichammer","name":"AtomicHammer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11846_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T17:57:35-07:00","id":907348,"title":"","content":"I've long since abandoned Marvel, so I can't comment on that side of things. I <i>had</i> abandoned DC back in 2011 when New 52 came online, and only got back into it last year(?) when Morrison's <i>Multiversity</i> was released. I was figuring that I'd get <i>Multiversity</i> and then pull out again; but then <i>Convergence</i> came along, followed a few months later by <i>Titans Hunt</i> and <i>Lois and Clark</i> \u2014 and now <i>Rebirth</i>. I now have <i>Action</i>, <i>Detective</i>, and <i>Titans</i> on my pull list, and I picked up <i>Superman: Rebirth</i> and <i>Batman: Rebirth</i> this week. I'm also going to be looking at <i>Batgirl and the Birds of Prey</i> and [b]Super Sons[/i] when they come out, and will be keeping an eye out for the returns of the Justice Society, the Legion of Superheroes, and the Shazam family to see how DC is going to handle them going forward. <br /> <br /> Overall, I'm happy with the <i>Rebirth</i> initiative, despite a few seeming missteps*. I like that they're <i>not</i> dumping the world of New 52, they're just adding back in elements that <i>it</i> dumped. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:gray\">* most notably the killing of post-Flashpoint Superman and substituting in pre-Flashpoint Superman; I'm a fan of the latter version, but I think I would have preferred the former sticking around but being tweaked to incorporate elements of the latter).</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T17:59:49-07:00","id":907351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=906908#post906908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really dislike it. It could have worked but they drop the ball the moment thanos appeared any kind of moral ambiguity and question about the use of power went out of the window.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure it'll go bad, but so far I think they've done pretty well at making all sides reasonable. Yes, there are clear cases, but since 90-odd% of visions are not going to fall within that bound, just following them blindly seems unwise. Also, they have no reason to trust this Inhuman - sure, we know he's on the level, but how do they? For all they know he's a Skrull messing with them - not the first time that's happened. Or one of the several dozen other entities capable of such manipulations.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, they are capable individuals and it'd be idiotic of them to ignore information this potentially valuable. And someone manifesting this power isn't exactly an impossibility - it's been seen before, although specific examples elude me at the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T19:04:22-07:00","id":907379,"title":"","content":"Hydra Cap isn't a cash grab, it's Nick Spencer saying &quot;FUCK YOU!!&quot; to fans who wanted Steve Rogers back in action. &quot;Here you go, here's your blonde-haired, blue-eyed white superhero. BTW, he's Hydra now, and SOMEHOW, HE ALWAYS WAS!! ENJOY!&quot; The fact that editorial is defending this crap is why I don't support the actual comics anymore","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T23:21:34-07:00","id":907476,"title":"","content":"It wouldn't surprise me; I've seen comic book creators pull some very childish stunts. Google \u201cDidio and Herald\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T20:47:44-07:00","id":908083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=907351#post907351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure it'll go bad, but so far I think they've done pretty well at making all sides reasonable. Yes, there are clear cases, but since 90-odd% of visions are not going to fall within that bound, just following them blindly seems unwise. Also, they have no reason to trust this Inhuman - sure, we know he's on the level, but how do they? For all they know he's a Skrull messing with them - not the first time that's happened. Or one of the several dozen other entities capable of such manipulations.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, they are capable individuals and it'd be idiotic of them to ignore information this potentially valuable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally i dont think they made Captain Marvel side reasonable. Iron man quite reasonable says &quot;hey, we should analyse this kid power and take it easy because this could potentially lead to abuse of power&quot; and her response is &quot;i dont care as long as the world is running&quot;. <br /> <br /> Seems like a very strawman argument. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=907351#post907351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And someone manifesting this power isn't exactly an impossibility - it's been seen before, although specific examples elude me at the moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Blindfold, Destiny and Madame Web both of them. But they made a point that unlike all of them nobody can read the new guy mind.<br /> <br /> Like you said there is the foundation of a good conflict there but the case that spark the conflict *was* a clear one, Thanos, it doesnt get more black and white than the guy who wants to kill everything as gift to death. So the heroes following the vision of the inhuman and Warmachine dying was the best possible scenario because otherwise Thanos would have do what he wanted and that never ever is good.<br /> <br /> They should have use an sparking incident with the same result (same heroes dying) that wasnt clear whether it would have gone the same way or not had they intervene. Hell if they gonna re-hash civil war, making the inhuman guy having a vision of a superhuman fight causing another Stamford causing Captain marvel`s team to intervene and leaving it ambiguously both whether the fight was gonna go the way of Stamford and thus Warmachine`s death was in vain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 06-05-2016, 11:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T21:13:33-07:00","id":908098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=908083#post908083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally i dont think they made Captain Marvel side reasonable. Iron man quite reasonable says &quot;hey, we should analyse this kid power and take it easy because this could potentially lead to abuse of power&quot; and her response is &quot;i dont care as long as the world is running&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assumed that it made sense if you've read Captain Marvel (I don't). I got the feeling she's been dealing with a lot of bad stuff lately that this kind of information would have helped with - they kind of hinted at it in Issue #0. Anyone who reads that series want to weigh in?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=908083#post908083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like you said there is the foundation of a good conflict there but the case that spark the conflict *was* a clear one, Thanos, it doesnt get more black and white than the guy who wants to kill everything as gift to death. So the heroes following the vision of the inhuman and Warmachine dying was the best possible scenario because otherwise Thanos would have do what he wanted and that never ever is good.<br /> <br /> They should have use an sparking incident with the same result (same heroes dying) that wasnt clear whether it would have gone the same way or not had they intervene. Hell if they gonna re-hash civil war, making the inhuman guy having a vision of a superhuman fight causing another Stamford causing Captain marvel`s team to intervene and leaving it ambiguously both whether the fight was gonna go the way of Stamford and thus Warmachine`s death was in vain.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no counter-argument for this. That could have been handled better, true.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Just read the FCBD issue - while I still agree it could have been handled much better, the timing of the Thanos vision does cast a degree of suspicion on the legitimacy of the visions. At least, if I were some manipulative bad guy, I would have led with a couple unambiguous things first, especially if they run a good chance of taking out a couple heroes in the process.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","user":"Allan53","date":". 06-08-2016, 03:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T19:12:56-07:00","id":912043,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the delay, but I\u2019m wasted on Kraken Rum so here we go!<br /> <br /> Legends of Tomorrow #4: I\u2019m forced to pay 8 bucks for a mediocre Firestorm story. The idea is keen, the execution for the book is subpar.<br /> <br /> Green Lantern Corps: Edge of Oblivion #6: Still wondering why all the GLC miniseries this past year and no ongoing. Story was OK, last issue in the mini.<br /> <br /> Prometheus: Life and Death #1: The continuation of the for mentioned Predator story. At least we get to see a Promethean smash a dudes head with his bare hands. Always a Polaroid moment.<br /> <br /> Ninjak #16 Still solid! Why don\u2019t more people read Valiant?<br /> <br /> 4001AD Bloodshot one shot: Pretty cool tie it as Blood shot is like just a Frankenstein head on a nano-swarm. It\u2019s not just cool, it\u2019s like Frankenstein cool.<br /> <br /> Action Comics #957: Finally back t original numbering. My Sorting boxes will thank me later, plus Doomsday and Lex Luther as Superman!<br /> <br /> Daredevil #8 Ok, this issue did throw me for a loop. We went from Matt Murdock DA for New York, to international man of mystery ala James Bond?<br /> <br /> Aquaman Rebirth: I honestly liked the set up here. I am a Aquaman fan and the story and art was decent.<br /> <br /> Detective Comics # 934: So Clayface is joining the Bat-family? Sometimes you wonder if the family just gets too big.<br /> <br /> Flash Rebirth: It was ok, felt like a retelling of the main DCU Rebirth issue with Barry\u2019s own issues.<br /> <br /> So what else did everyone get? What did I miss?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11846-atomichammer","name":"AtomicHammer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11846_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T19:17:53-07:00","id":912044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=907012#post907012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">, and The Punisher(also horrible).</div> </div> </div> </div>To each their own, I have liked it so far. The art may be off putting at times, but dig the story. I just hop they bring out the ol weaponsmith Punisher where he made traps and all that good stuff","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11846-atomichammer","name":"AtomicHammer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11846_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T19:50:05-07:00","id":912048,"title":"","content":"Injection is going well. A Warren Ellis story, basically a think-tank was created in the UK to predict the future of the UK and the world and see what they could do with it. They all predicted a sort of technological flatline with no real advances for a long time. One of the members is a 'cunning man' and after great reluctance decides to help them inject something into the system that should keep things from going stale. Everyone involved regrets it. Very interesting story, but Ellis is good at that, sort of out there at points. There's unfortunately going to be a hiatus for a while, presumably they'll be gathering the issues into a TPB.<br /> <br /> I liked Detective Comics, which was surprising to me because I don't like some of the main characters. Batwoman and Tim Drake. Unsure about new Spoiler and Cassandra, as well. But the mystery and plot seemed like it would be pretty engaging. Wonder if Clayface will find a way to swing with the rest of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T06:35:00-07:00","id":912214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=912048#post912048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I liked Detective Comics, which was surprising to me because I don't like some of the main characters. Batwoman and Tim Drake. Unsure about new Spoiler and Cassandra, as well. But the mystery and plot seemed like it would be pretty engaging. Wonder if Clayface will find a way to swing with the rest of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same here. Not a Batfan in the least, but I enjoyed Detective Comics a little too much. Clayface rules.<br /> <br /> So far, this is my Rebirth tally:<br /> <br /> Green Arrow: Sucks.<br /> Green Lantern: Awesome.<br /> Detective Comics: Awesome.<br /> Action Comics: Sucks. <br /> Batman: Sucks. <br /> The Flash: Awesome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T12:40:11-07:00","id":912384,"title":"","content":"So is anyone The Wicked + The Divine? I recently picked up the third collected volume and while the art and worldbuilding is still great, I find myself less and less hooked by the characters and plot. I'm still reading it because it's gorgeous, but it seems to have lost its initial spark to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T10:13:09-07:00","id":912847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=912384#post912384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So is anyone The Wicked + The Divine? I recently picked up the third collected volume and while the art and worldbuilding is still great, I find myself less and less hooked by the characters and plot. I'm still reading it because it's gorgeous, but it seems to have lost its initial spark to me.</div> </div> </div> </div> I haven't, but thats not due to me not liking it as that I already just get so much a week to read, (plus RPG book and novels,) I have never checked it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11846-atomichammer","name":"AtomicHammer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11846_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T10:49:26-07:00","id":912860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=912384#post912384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find myself less and less hooked by the characters and plot. I'm still reading it because it's gorgeous, but it seems to have lost its initial spark to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something like that here, too. Nice setting building and introduction but after a while the story seemed like it was being dragged out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T11:15:12-07:00","id":912875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=912860#post912860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Something like that here, too. Nice setting building and introduction but after a while the story seemed like it was being dragged out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it's absolutely fucking gorgeous, but the writing just isn't there to back it up anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T20:43:46-07:00","id":915341,"title":"","content":"Some nice comics this week. Crossed is amping up well, just wish they could get a better artist. Batman #1 was solid and fun introduction. Thought the animal death in Superman #1 was a bit unnecessary, same thing happened in Batman &amp; Robin with Damian, though the reason was different. Maybe that was the point, maybe it was incidental.<br /> <br /> I found the Last Crusade to be pretty fun as well, even as someone who doesn't like Jason Todd.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/suxf60W.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T16:43:24-07:00","id":916487,"title":"","content":"So I've started reading <b>Captain Marvel</b> (starting with the 2012 collection), mostly to get a sense for the character. And I've only read 7 or so issues, but so far? Not particularly impressed. Not to say it's <i>bad</i>, by no means would I say that; I'm re-leafing through <i>The Darkness</i>, and <i>that's</i> bad. Captain Marvel, I don't know, just seems to be... trying too hard? Maybe this works if you're more familiar with her, but so far I've read through a time-travel adventure/backstory (which was fine, if somewhat pointless, since it didn't really tell me anything they didn't cover in their one-page summary of her backstory except she was friends/hero-worship with some other female pilot back in the day), and all that really did was make me think &quot;yeah, it was hard being a woman in the military in the 40s and around&quot;. Which I knew. At no point did it really help me get a sense of the character, since she spent most of the time scowling and punching. Oh, and her friend is dying, but that doesn't really tie into the story in any kind of significant way.<br /> <br /> Apparently the current arc will also help me get a sense of the character, so we'll see how that goes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","user":"Allan53","date":". 06-17-2016, 07:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T18:17:31-07:00","id":916523,"title":"","content":"I remember when I tried to give Captain Marvel a chance. This was before that run, technically she was still Ms. Marvel, but I'll spoiler it anyways. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">It was during or after the Civil War, and she thought a captured Skrull on a SHIELD helicarrier had some information about her boyfriend. It wanted to be let out of its power-dampening cell in order to give her the answer. It was against regulations and, if I recall correctly, others on board said absolutely not. She went off and did something else, then came back and pulled the Skrull out and demanded the information.<br /> <br /> The Skrull blew up, causing the helicarrier to blow up. Workers fall and die graphically, and it was over a town, no one was able to act to save it in time so they just had to clean up the wreckage afterwards. Captain Marvel was sad about what happened. So the next night she went to Wonder Man's apartment, explained it, then they had sex and she was better and went to help the Avengers. It was the end of the story.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I just didn't get it. I mean, I get that Marvel, at least some of it, tries to make characters who are people first, heroes second. But it seemed so surreal. She had even backed Tony's side in the Civil War.<br /> <br /> Anyways, writing female protagonists seems to be a near-insurmountable issue for most writers. When I was getting back into comics I asked around and I'd hear things like, 'So-and-so is great! But don't read issues 1-200, just read 201-206 and don't read the next fifty.' Which didn't give me much confidence in the characters.<br /> <br /> All that said, I really enjoyed Batgirl's entire run. That's Cassandra Cain, who had the first Batgirl ongoing. The ending was a bummer but I thought it was written well, even if it got jerked around by events. And Madame Xanadu's Vertigo run, though I'm not sure if that would count. There must be more, I just can't think of them at the moment.<br /> <br /> People have been raving about Gwenpool and Kamala Khan, though it's not my thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-17-2016, 10:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T07:11:46-07:00","id":917328,"title":"","content":"Damn, I\u2019m late again with what I picked up.<br /> <br /> Astonishing Ant-Man#9: Still doing the foreshadowing Scott going to prison again, but still don\u2019t know why? They need to wrap that up soon as I\u2019m starting not to care.<br /> <br /> Batman #1: Good issue, good art. We get introduced to new characters Gotham and Gotham Girl, (more like this generation\u2019s version of Gangbuster.) Don\u2019t see them lasting in ten years.<br /> <br /> Civil War II #2: A set up issue to define the battle lines a little more. Best moment, the Hulk, (not Cho,) is coming back to kill them all, Thank God!<br /> <br /> X-Men Civil War II #1: Storms Extraordinary X-Men face off against Magnetos Uncanny X-Men that feels more like a simple disagreement than true conflict. Plus Nightcrawler jumps ship to Magnetos side, so a little added drama there.<br /> <br /> Dark Knight Return-Last Crusade: The intermission tale for DK3, that takes place before The Dark Knight Returns and focuses on Joker and how he killed the previous Robin in Frank Millers Batman Universe. It\u2019s a cool story, but not necessary if you read The Dark Knight Returns you already know what will happen, but still nice to have.<br /> <br /> Descender #12: The sad song of Tim-22. I see a lot of issues like this lately where we get full issues dedicated to antagonist of why they are doing these horrible things. I guess to build sympathy for the bad guy? We saw it with Negan from the Walking Dead and a few other books. Just interrupts the flow of the main story.<br /> <br /> Devolution #5: Mini finally ends and..just went down left field and not sure how they were trying to end this.<br /> <br /> Green Arrow #1: Wasn\u2019t too bad really.<br /> <br /> Green Lanterns #1: The Reds are back, but still wondering why they had Larfleeze on the cover.<br /> <br /> Justice League #51: Where in a rush to get to #52 So we can get back to #1 so We will tell a little tale of Robin working with the League.<br /> <br /> Superman #1: Superman\u2019s kid maybe teaming up with pops. I\u2019m curious, pretty good story.<br /> <br /> Swamp Thing #6: This Mini finally ends, and the villain was who we all though he was is reviled. Poor Mathew, (same one from Sandman,) just can\u2019t catch a break. But all is set right again with this issue. I love Swamp Thing, but this wasn\u2019t his greatest story. So my hope for a decent ongoing Swamp Thing book is dwindling.<br /> <br /> Titans Rebirth: Setting things right again and it feels good.<br /> <br /> Uncanny X-Men #8: Still my favorite X-Men book. The story is still fun to read even though the Event as a whole sucks.<br /> <br /> Side Note..Is anyone else following the Apocalypse War Event? Is it even an Event? It just feels like each X-Book has their own little \u201cFlavor of Apocalypse\u201d story but don\u2019t see the connection to ALL the books. And I hate Hopless\u2019s All New X-Men so I don\u2019t even read that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11846-atomichammer","name":"AtomicHammer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11846_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T08:35:19-07:00","id":917369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AtomicHammer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=917328#post917328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Civil War II #2: A set up issue to define the battle lines a little more. Best moment, the Hulk, (not Cho,) is coming back to kill them all, Thank God!<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, I don't think that's going to happen.<br /> <br /> I think Marvel is going to put Bruce Banner to rest for a long, long time(2-3 years, maybe).<br /> <br /> If you know what I mean...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T09:34:22-07:00","id":917397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=917369#post917369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unfortunately, I don't think that's going to happen.<br /> <br /> I think Marvel is going to put Bruce Banner to rest for a long, long time(2-3 years, maybe).<br /> <br /> If you know what I mean...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In favor for Amadeus? Maybe, but I was hoping they would bring back more of the the Hulk attitude from World War Hulk and tie it in as being pissed his cousin got killed last issue, (if thats not brought up then this will be poorly written.)<br /> <br /> But I can see Bendis doing that too as that's what Bendis does. He can't write a story unless he's killing someone, turning heroes into villians or retconing someones past in a fucked up out of character way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11846,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11846-atomichammer","user":"AtomicHammer","date":". 06-19-2016, 01:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11846-atomichammer","name":"AtomicHammer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11846_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T12:44:09-07:00","id":917503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AtomicHammer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=917397#post917397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> In favor for Amadeus? Maybe, but I was hoping they would <b>bring back more of the the Hulk attitude from World War Hulk and tie it in as being pissed his cousin got killed last issue</b>, (if thats not brought up then this will be poorly written.)<br /> <br /> But I can see Bendis doing that too as that's what Bendis does. He can't write a story unless he's killing someone, turning heroes into villians or retconing someones past in a fucked up out of character way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wish. But nah, I don't see it. I see Bruce dying, I see Cho taking over, and I see She-Hulk waking up from her coma at the end of the event(where SHE will be pissed). <br /> <br /> Bendis used to be so good. Unfortunately, he's fallen hard over the last five or so years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T18:51:52-07:00","id":919436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=917503#post917503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bendis used to be so good. Unfortunately, he's fallen hard over the last five or so years.</div> </div> </div> </div>When was this? <br /> <br /> Now to serious business....<br /> <br /> Ok everyone, It\u2019s Wednesday, I\u2019m drinking Kraken, Rockin out to Perurbator, Frankincense burning, and this is what I got this week in comics.<br /> <br /> Action Comics #958: Doomsdays back. I know a lot of people cringe about 90\u2019s comics, but I missed Doomsday. Hope they don\u2019t Nerf this villain.<br /> <br /> Aquaman #1: I like Aquaman, a lot of people stereotype the character without really knowing much about him. Mantas back causing mayhem, but why was Ocean Master on the cover?<br /> <br /> Autumlands #11: Awesome Sci Fi Fantasy setting, big fan of the series. This issue we are introduced to another aspect to this world Busiek created.<br /> <br /> Black Road #3: This was a character building issue, we get more Magnus and how he thinks and plans. The march to Rome continues.<br /> <br /> Carnage #9: The only Marvel book I got this week and it\u2019s a filler issue. Carnage was hardly in the book.<br /> <br /> Deathstroke #19: Love the character, but this arc stopped like two issues ago for me. Let\u2019s move on.<br /> <br /> Detective Comics #935: With all that\u2019s going on in this book with all the Bat Family, it still flows like a fine wine. Seriously awesome book.<br /> <br /> Drifter #12: Abram still missing and some shit is about to go down. Anyone else read this Sci Fi Western?<br /> <br /> Flash #1: Was ok, not bad<br /> <br /> Justice League #52: One shot all for Lex Luther taking up the now dead New 52 Superman\u2019s cause,(cape and all.)<br /> <br /> Rai #14: A 4001AD tie in, and a little confusing, more of a side note issue.<br /> <br /> Robin-Son of Batman #13: Think this was the last issue, good run. Not sure why it had to end.<br /> <br /> What did everyone else get?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11846-atomichammer","name":"AtomicHammer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11846_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T19:01:22-07:00","id":919443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AtomicHammer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=919436#post919436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>When was this?</b><br /> <br /> Now to serious business....<br /> <br /> <br /> Action Comics #958: Doomsdays back. I know a lot of people cringe about 90\u2019s comics, but<b> I missed Doomsday</b>. Hope they don\u2019t Nerf this villain.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>What did everyone else get</b>?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1. His run on Daredevil is legendary. Powers was excellent. That's...all I got.<br /> <br /> 2. Doomsday shows up around twice a year. I don't get a chance to miss him like you, unfortunately since he's used so damn much.<br /> <br /> 3. Detective Comics, Thor, Action Comics, and Nighthawk for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T19:14:39-07:00","id":919446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=919443#post919443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> 1. His run on Daredevil is legendary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I know a lot of people go to Daredevil for Bendis. It just felt like he was trying to catch that Miller magic that Frank forgot how to conjure. Didn't feel like anything new to me. It was good dont get me wrong, but didn't feel ground breaking.<br /> <br /> But to each their own, he sells books so people like him.<br /> <br /> And Doomsday twice a year? Where I havent seen him in any books for awhile. At least in Superman that I know of. The Last year was the whole Superman depowered facing Wraith and That Haxor virus dude that were all tied to Vandal Savage and before that it was that story with that Ulyseeses dude and that Solar Flair power<br /> <br /> Then the new 52 superman died","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11846,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11846-atomichammer","user":"AtomicHammer","date":". 06-22-2016, 10:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11846-atomichammer","name":"AtomicHammer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11846_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T21:07:26-07:00","id":919495,"title":"","content":"Bendis' run on Sam &amp; Twitch was fantastic, as well.<br /> <br /> It does sort of suck that Robin, Son of Batman ended, seems like they could have just aged him between issues or something. Better yet have a few issues showing what he does over the years, sort of like the Long Halloween. I'm mostly reassured because he's going to be a main character in two more comics and a supporting character in at least one other.<br /> <br /> While I did like Detective Comics, over the past few years long-term fans have been a bit annoyed how the comic has left the 'Detective' part in the dust. It seems like they could have had a more investigative method of training, rather than fighting a bunch of faux-Jokers. I can't deny it was a good comic, though, even disliking some of the main characters.<br /> <br /> In case you didn't read Deathstroke, <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">he and his children are now members of the League of Assassins. I expect them to show up a lot in Teen Titans now, but hopefully they won't pull the same old stuff. Great art but the story was pretty meh.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T21:35:37-07:00","id":920145,"title":"","content":"So I gave <b>She-Wolf</b>, an Image comic allegedly about a girl reacting to a werewolf bite, a try. I say allegedly, because honestly if I didn't read the blurb I'd be totally baffled as to what was supposed to be going on and what was real and what wasn't. Now, that can work, but I get less \u201cexistential horror\u201d and more \u201cseriously, what the hell is even going on?\u201d.<br /> <br /> This can be illustrated more clearly by example than explanation. This is two pages, one occurring directly after another. Context doesn\u2019t really help.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"http://i651.photobucket.com/albums/uu232/ilikemonkeys56/She-Wolf_zpsstp7laic.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Is the girl in the bed the same as the girl who was scratched? Is that the same as the girl by the window, now magically dressed? There are parts of semi-coherent narrative, but it doesn\u2019t take long before it flips back to just weirdness. And they rarely establish much. We don\u2019t know the character, we don\u2019t know the situation, and we don\u2019t know who the werewolf was (her boyfriend? A friend? Some innocent recipient who she cursed for unknown reasons?) Why is it presented this way? It\u2019s just frustrating and artsy for the sake of being artsy. There\u2019s innovative, and then there\u2019s just bad storytelling. Later on she spontaneously turns into a werewolf in front of people, and they seem shocked, but the next panel people are just talking to her as normal, with no transition.<br /> <br /> So, yeah. Like the idea, very poor execution.<br /> <br /> <b>Project: Nemesis</b> recently finished. I\u2019m\u2026 not sure whether I like this or not. It doesn\u2019t really give us many answers, and the ones we do get <i>tend</i> to more undermine the story than help it, but it does a really good job of making us feel how the characters do \u2013 there\u2019s a big monster rampaging and there\u2019s basically nothing they can do about it. They\u2019re totally out of their depth, and desperately trying to stay alive.<br /> <br /> The last issue does tie up the plot threads, and it\u2019s not a bad plot as they go, but, I dunno, it seemed a bit ham-handed/smultsy to me.<br /> <br /> The art is pretty much always gorgeous, and I do like the characters \u2013 each has a consistent and clear motivation (mostly variants on the theme of \u201cstay alive\u201d), and the basic idea was potentially very interesting. Worth a look, I\u2019d say, but that\u2019s just me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T21:44:19-07:00","id":920153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=920145#post920145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Project: Nemesis</b> recently finished. I\u2019m\u2026 not sure whether I like this or not. It doesn\u2019t really give us many answers, and the ones we do get <i>tend</i> to more undermine the story than help it, but it does a really good job of making us feel how the characters do \u2013 there\u2019s a big monster rampaging and there\u2019s basically nothing they can do about it. They\u2019re totally out of their depth, and desperately trying to stay alive.<br /> <br /> The last issue does tie up the plot threads, and it\u2019s not a bad plot as they go, but, I dunno, it seemed a bit ham-handed/smultsy to me.<br /> <br /> The art is pretty much always gorgeous, and I do like the characters \u2013 each has a consistent and clear motivation (mostly variants on the theme of \u201cstay alive\u201d), and the basic idea was potentially very interesting. Worth a look, I\u2019d say, but that\u2019s just me.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's based on a book, with a number of sequels, which might be why answers are doled out so slowly. I haven't seen the comic, or finished the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T19:36:56-07:00","id":922996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=919495#post919495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bendis' run on Sam &amp; Twitch was fantastic, as well.<br /> <br /> In case you didn't read Deathstroke, <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">he and his children are now members of the League of Assassins. I expect them to show up a lot in Teen Titans now, but hopefully they won't pull the same old stuff. Great art but the story was pretty meh.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>I never read Sam &amp; Twitch so I can't comment. Obviously people like Bendis as he moves books, and thats cool. I just feel that he's more of a 'shock' writer from what I have read in the past. But thats just my opinion, if people like him and I don't it's cool.<br /> <br /> As for the Deathstroke spoiler, yeah maybe..It's just I get the feeling when they renumber Deathstroke, a lot of this past run may be forgotten. Now I can totally see that in Titans in some way, but not directly tied to this run. We'll see as the Deathstroke Annual is out this week.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11846-atomichammer","name":"AtomicHammer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11846_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T18:22:54-07:00","id":923607,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s Wednesday, and this weeks pull list is being brought to you by Stella Artois as I drank a 6 pack of it, (along with some Kraken Rum,) before giving you my list this week because\u2026\u2026<br /> <br /> X-O Manowar #47: Love the book, but bummed because my main dude at my local comic shop told me the book is ending at 50, and we are on the countdown to 50. X-O along with most of Valiant comics is just super awesome in my opinion. This book is Valiant s flagship in my opinion and will be sad to see it go.<br /> <br /> Bloodshot Reborn #14: We are waist deep in Bloodshot Island. I feel the idea of it is cool, but the execution was piss poor. The book is ok, but we are heading towards left field way to fast.<br /> <br /> Daredevil/Punisher #2: Good issue, great art, and I love both characters. It\u2019s a good story, the issues are 5 bucks a pop and I wonder why? But a fun ride so far even if this issue was late.<br /> <br /> Dark Knight 3 #5: I dig Frank Millers Batman Universe. Big Marketing moment in this issue, remember Batman in his power armor? Well Superman is in his Power Armor and how do you defeat an army of Kryptonians when you\u2019re a billionaire? Synthetic Kryptonite rain, and for some reason I really like it. So when you start to see the statues of Superman in power armor years from now..it started here.<br /> <br /> Deathstroke Annual #2: Most annuls suck, this was really good. Even if you don\u2019t collect Deathstroke, you can pick this up and enjoy the story. Single shot, great story, well worth the 5 bucks.<br /> <br /> Extraordinary X-Men #11: Decent, not the best X-men book out there.<br /> <br /> Uncanny X-Men #9: This is the BEST X-Men book out now. Love it, I know it\u2019s my opinion, but a great run so far even in the quasi- crossover.<br /> <br /> ..That\u2019s my pull. Don\u2019t be shy!! What did everyone else get?!?!?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11846-atomichammer","name":"AtomicHammer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11846_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T19:29:10-07:00","id":923636,"title":"","content":"Grayson's Annual was a nice sendoff, I liked Deathstroke's too. Teen Titans' Annual was lame but that is to be expected, unfortunately. Hoping the new run turns the title around with its rebranding of characters and new nemeses.<br /> <br /> Pizzazz came back strong in Jem and the Holograms, a line I've really found myself surprised to enjoy, since I never saw the cartoon. GI Joe vs Street Fighter was fun but heavy on the Street Fighter mythos this issue. And the last GI Joe vs Transformers was just another epic and bizarro take on the two franchises, great comic. Hillbilly #1 came out, nice story there too.<br /> <br /> I've always wanted to get into Valiant, but have no idea where to start, any suggestions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T09:21:57-07:00","id":923898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=923636#post923636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've always wanted to get into Valiant, but have no idea where to start, any suggestions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ninjak and Bloodshot are fantastic, from what I hear. Been meaning to check them out myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T18:12:34-07:00","id":924696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=923898#post923898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ninjak and Bloodshot are fantastic, from what I hear. Been meaning to check them out myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much what Larry said. I'd also say X-O manowar but if the series is really ending at 50 you only have a few issues left. X_O I always thought of the crown jewel of Valiant. I think stopping this title at 50 is a big mistake. Rai is also good, but it takes place in Valiant's future and that may not last as well.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11846-atomichammer","name":"AtomicHammer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11846_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T13:53:12-07:00","id":925027,"title":"","content":"Thank you, both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T19:23:58-07:00","id":927407,"title":"","content":"I honestly don\u2019t remember if I went over my pull list from last week, so if I missed it..whatever let\u2019s get drunk.<br /> <br /> Walking Dead #156: Going to be a big issue me thinks. Did Negan do what he did to help Rick or to help himself? People say he was the worst villain in Walking Dead, I disagree. The Governor from the comics was WAY more sadistic, (TV show didn\u2019t do the character any justice IMO,) and did things for his own perverse pleasure. Negan did things for a reason, mostly to set examples, and this issue proves that.<br /> <br /> Tokyo Ghost #8: The buildup is coming, will this end on a happy note?<br /> <br /> Superman: Coming of Supermen #6: Last issue, had a lot of hopes for this mini series. Didn\u2019t really live up to it. I\u2019d avoid this even in Trades unless you are a diehard Superman fan.<br /> <br /> Superman #2: We get the father son team up and it feels pretty good. Someone also makes a cameo at the end, the 90\u2019s are making a comeback.<br /> <br /> Silver Surfer #5: Always liked Surfer, but I just can\u2019t get into what Slott is doing. This issue pretty much is him admitting he didn\u2019t know the characters origin and thumbing his nose at what really made the Surfer the character he was.. Regret and Loneliness. That\u2019s right kids, it wasn\u2019t always about the Power Cosmic.<br /> <br /> The Punisher #3: Still like it, don\u2019t care what other people think.<br /> <br /> Moon Knight #4: I still like the series even though every issue ends in a plot twist. We need some foundation here.<br /> <br /> Justice League Rebirth: The Bad art from JLA meets a story of giant space ticks. Don\u2019t they know a movie is coming out in a few years?<br /> <br /> Green Lanterns #2: It was ok, Red Lanterns are on Earth spreading the Rage.<br /> <br /> 4001AD-Shadowman: Decent one shot story that really doesn\u2019t feel like a tie in to the event. If you like Shadowman, (or a concept of an alternate version of the character,) and don\u2019t want to invest on the whole event..this could be worth your 4 bucks.<br /> <br /> Aquaman #2: Good story, but Manta would so kill him, just sayin.<br /> <br /> Batman #2: Cool story, are they implying the new characters are Kryptonians? Anyway Hugo is bringing his Monster Men from Wagners stories.<br /> <br /> Civil War 2-X-Men #2: Not bad really, things continue to shift between the X-Teams. Lot of drama but little action.<br /> <br /> Daredevil/Punisher #3: Was ok, could be a lot worse<br /> <br /> Green Arrow #2: Honestly, this was really good.<br /> <br /> What did everyone else get?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11846-atomichammer","name":"AtomicHammer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11846_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T11:12:00-07:00","id":927693,"title":"","content":"Picked Ms Marvel #8, its a shame that otherwise solid books have to get dragged into Civil War II.<br /> <br /> However i suspect that either the writters are drunk or they just dont get the concept of &quot;morally ambiguous&quot; between Thanos in Civil Wars and this one is just jarring.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">So between the race and background of Ms Marvel i knew exactly how this comic was gonna go even before i open it. She was gonna side with Carol Danver but in the end she is gonna side with Iron man because profiling is wrong.<br /> <br /> However this comic deals with the first part of the formula. Kamala accepts one of the visions of Ullyses and her with a new team stopped a guy who was driving a stolen tank that was fated to blow up and kill lots of innocent.<br /> <br /> So then kamala goes home and gets a talk by her sister in law about how profiling is bad and if they charge that guy from a crime that he might do then crime would have to be redefined and something about &quot;though-on-crime&quot; that happened in greenville.<br /> <br /> Which is fine except....im pretty sure that stealing a TANK, driving said tank on the street and crushing cars parked are all crimes. Thats not arresting a guy for a crime that he might do, he was already doing lots of crimes.<br /> <br /> Which is even more confusing because next &quot;scene&quot; Ms marvel grabs a guy who, by the predictions, was gonna rob a grocery store. Which is a pretty good example of the previous issue. I mean if the grocery store robber scene was put before the &quot;talk&quot; then it would have drive the point home but as its stand im thinking someone confuse the order of the pages on this one.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The elements of a descent albeit incredible predictable story are there but the order of the events undermines it.<br /> <br /> Picked Silver Surfer #5 which hasnt been contaminated with Civil War II yet and it was pretty good. Its a funny heartwarming comic.<br /> <br /> Spiderwoman #9 which manage to tell one last story before been contaminated with Civil War II. Less pages about Carol and more with the wendigo case would have been great. However now it reads as an entirely pointless number.<br /> <br /> Vote for Loki #2. Fun but hate the artist.<br /> <br /> Captain America: Sam Wilson #9. Subtlety your name is not Sam Wilson. Faceless robot cops that oppress the minorities with police brutality called Americops? Seriously? Why not just make their leader Tumptron? Or put the wall between mexico and USA as a plot point? There is straw man arguments and then there is this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T20:53:43-07:00","id":927944,"title":"","content":"Green Lantern Rebirth #2 - Yeah. My hope for this title disappeared after one really good issue. The art is good. But that's about it.<br /> <br /> Superman Rebirth #2 - Loved it. Wasn't a fan of what happened last issue with the _______ being lasered, but this issue recovers nicely. Art is nice, too. <br /> <br /> Kingpin #1 - I paid 4.99 for this comic. All I wanted was a good Kingpin story. I didn't get one. And the art was poor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T23:25:45-07:00","id":927979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=927944#post927944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Superman Rebirth #2 - Loved it. Wasn't a fan of what happened last issue with the _______ being lasered, but this issue recovers nicely. Art is nice, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it was meant to be a parallel to Batman &amp; Robin.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://67.media.tumblr.com/196989fc7ab4f335b9e752b8050bd856/tumblr_mhh38pRlqC1qj182xo6_r1_500.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Damian had since mellowed out, but as you can see they handle the situation differently. Plus the usual kid not in control of his emotions stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T08:49:43-07:00","id":930367,"title":"","content":"I thought <a href=\"http://www.theouthousers.com/index.php/news/135760-thanks-to-rich-johnston-only-10-of-cbr-readers-excited-for-marvel-now.html\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> was amusing.<br /> <br /> Though I can't see how they could honestly believe their new books like 'Occupy Avengers,' grim and gritty Avengers, and 'Slapstick' would keep everyone hyped. I admit fifteen years ago a Solo title would have gotten me on board easy.<br /> <br /> New Super-Man was surprisingly good. I like the character, and the supporting cast so far. DC has had a good record of starting comics in international settings, even Batwing started good. Hoping it stays up.<br /> <br /> Detective Comics had a nice twist, too. If we're not getting simple detective work this looks like a suitable replacement. I'd still prefer not to have Tim Drake but he's not as omnipotent as he was depicted before.<br /> <br /> Nightwing: Rebirth was solid but I think sort of jumped the gun in killing a certain character. As good as it seemed, when a comic starts by eradicating aspects of the past often end up replacing it with something not as good.<br /> <br /> The Paybacks has a new series out, too, which is great. It's a comic about a world of superheroes and villains where, basically, a mysterious entity named Mr. Pierce acts as a moneylender for would-be superpeople, offering loans so they can build their death ray or support their crime-fighting lifestyle. If they default, however, they're legally obligated to join the Paybacks, Mr. Pierce's own team of meta-individuals who act as repo men. It's a fun comic, pretty unique though it obviously takes a lot of jabs at existing super universes. It's descended from another comic, Buzzkill, which was about an ex-superhero trying to go through AA after quitting the life, because his power involves him gaining special abilities when ingesting alcohol or other drugs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-14-2016, 10:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T10:54:45-07:00","id":941264,"title":"","content":"Last week's comics were pretty good. Kind of on the edge with Detective Comics this issue's sold me. Red Hood, normally a character I don't like, had a good first issue. Nightwing's keeping the energy from Grayson. GI Joe has a new twist, Jem and the Holograms has Pizzazz back in action and another car accident, they seem to have story arcs the way cartoon shows have episodes. Doctor Fate was good as well.<br /> <br /> I don't normally keep up with comic news but I do occasionally drop by Newsarama and found <a href=\"http://www.newsarama.com/30436-leaks-like-marvel-now-catalog-are-piracy-says-marvel-e-i-c.html\" target=\"_blank\">this interesting article</a> linking spoilers to piracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T19:31:22-07:00","id":967676,"title":"","content":"Hawkman still isn't a racist concept. Egyptians looked about as white as the average greek, they certainly portrayed nubians, but they're far more closely related to their middle eastern neighbors than anyone else.<br /> <br /> It's been a long ass time since JimB and I clashed on that matter. But it still annoys me and I'm sauced, so fuck it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T19:00:12-07:00","id":971662,"title":"","content":"I have not been keeping up with Marvel for a while, is the new Iron Heart character gonna be superheroing alongside Iron Man, or is Tony out of the action for now?<br /> <br /> Also, was Civil War II as bad, and everyone as out of character, as in Civil War?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T21:31:46-07:00","id":971752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=971662#post971662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, was Civil War II as bad, and everyone as out of character, as in Civil War?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know Captain Marvel very well, so I can't really say if she's out of character or not. I've tried, but she's just not that interesting to me. It <i>seems</i> as if she jumped on this potentially dangerous resource way too fast, and is remarkably hard-headed about pretty definitive evidence that it is, at best, imperfect (willing to imprison a woman indefinitely based on basically nothing; findings corroborated by Hank that the visions can't be perfectly accurate), but they did imply she's been being run pretty hard lately, so maybe that's what's driving it.<br /> <br /> Tony Stark seems more-or-less in character to me. He's encountered stuff like this before, and he's understandably skeptical about it.<br /> <br /> The story has its problems, I won't deny. The order of events to create what I'm <i>guessing</i> is the desired effect is all kinds of wonky, and I don't understand why someone with future-sight is suddenly such a game-changer when such powers have existed before - I can't quote sources, but I'm sure they have. Also, I hope you know a fair amount about the Inhumans, because they factor in here in a major way, and they make little attempt to get you up to speed. So far I've been treating them as narratively equivalent to the mutants, and that seems to be going pretty well, but i know I'm missing a lot on specific characters.<br /> <br /> By and large, I'd say it's a vast improvement over Civil War I. It's far from perfect, and I can see people thinking those problems are too bad to save the story as it is, but generally I don't think it's too bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T21:25:39-07:00","id":972339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=971662#post971662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have not been keeping up with Marvel for a while, is the new Iron Heart character gonna be superheroing alongside Iron Man, or is Tony out of the action for now?<br /> <br /> Also, was Civil War II as bad, and everyone as out of character, as in Civil War?</div> </div> </div> </div>Tony Stark is taking a sabbatical.<br /> <br /> It's Bendis. His name is synonymous with character assassination. He gives <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b><i><u>NO</u></i></b></span> fucks about any continuity but his own. So of course Carol/Captain Marvel is acting out of character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T21:50:41-07:00","id":972346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=971752#post971752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand why someone with future-sight is suddenly such a game-changer when such powers have existed before - I can't quote sources, but I'm sure they have.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are a few, most notably <a href=\"http://comicvine.gamespot.com/destiny/4005-43467/\" target=\"_blank\">Destiny. </a><br /> <br /> <br /> As for the <a href=\"http://comicvine.gamespot.com/inhumans/4060-11427/\" target=\"_blank\">Inhumans</a>; they are kind of like what mutants wish they could be, in that they've had a hidden society for longer than <i>Homo Sapiens</i> has walked upright. They are the result of genetic experiments by the alien <a href=\"http://comicvine.gamespot.com/kree-empire/4020-58192/\" target=\"_blank\">Kree Empire</a>, and unlike mutants, their unique abilities only manifest after a kind of triggered metamorphosis. called <a href=\"http://comicvine.gamespot.com/terrigenesis/4015-42287/\" target=\"_blank\">Terrigenesis</a>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T00:33:33-07:00","id":972380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=972339#post972339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tony Stark is taking a sabbatical.<br /> <br /> It's Bendis. His name is synonymous with character assassination. He gives <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b><i><u>NO</u></i></b></span> fucks about any continuity but his own. So of course Carol/Captain Marvel is acting out of character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Carol being a authoritarian, murderous crypto fascist is a return to form for her, actually. This is less Bendis performing a character assassination and more him ignoring KSD's character assassination.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T12:10:20-07:00","id":972630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=972380#post972380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Carol being a authoritarian, murderous crypto fascist is a return to form for her, actually. This is less Bendis performing a character assassination and more him ignoring KSD's character assassination.</div> </div> </div> </div> If you are referring to her behavior during and immediately after the first Civil War, that too was Carol been written to fit a story, rather than the story being written to fit the characters. This is the problem with Marvel's big events of the past decade; they only work if you ignore the history of the heroes involved. This is why I refuse to spend any money on Marvel's comics, at least until there's a MAJOR regime change. Are you enjoying a particular title? Have a favorite character? Too bad, here's a big event, that will bury the story you were enjoying, kill the your favorites, and ruin the reputations of any who survive.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T23:50:35-07:00","id":972966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=972630#post972630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you are referring to her behavior during and immediately after the first Civil War, that too was Carol been written to fit a story, rather than the story being written to fit the characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'm referring to the stories before that juncture too. Wherein she was also a depressed alcoholic mess that was too gutsy to hate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T05:31:07-07:00","id":973058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AtomicHammer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=927407#post927407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Batman #2: Cool story, are they implying the new characters are Kryptonians? Anyway Hugo is bringing his Monster Men from Wagners stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>How has this series been going since? And is it new-to-Batman friendly? I assume, like other Rebirth, I need to read the Rebirth story, but apart from that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","user":"Allan53","date":". 09-21-2016, 08:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T18:07:48-07:00","id":991635,"title":"","content":"So torn. On the one hand, Infamous Iron Man is the combination of my two favourite characters - Victor von Doom and Tony Stark. On the other hand, Bendis' writing lately has not impressed me, and that done badly is worse than not doing it at all.<br /> <br /> Similarly for the restart of Invincible Iron Man.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T20:29:19-07:00","id":995489,"title":"","content":"I have to wonder if Civil War II is some kind of complex scheme to sell more copies of Civil War I by making the latter seem Watchmen in comparison with the former.<br /> <br /> Civil War I has its problem and while some parts and reaction didnt make sense at least 80% of the verbal exchanges made sense. Civil Wars 6, though? No, just no. The exchanges are all wrong. Chit chat between character feels off, its like the uncanny valley of comic books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T02:45:12-07:00","id":995562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=995489#post995489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to wonder if Civil War II is some kind of complex scheme to sell more copies of Civil War I by making the latter seem Watchmen in comparison with the former.<br /> <br /> Civil War I has its problem and while some parts and reaction didnt make sense at least 80% of the verbal exchanges made sense. Civil Wars 6, though? No, just no. The exchanges are all wrong. Chit chat between character feels off, its like the uncanny valley of comic books.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Civil War 2 has its issues, I don't think anyone would seriously argue against that. But Civil War 1 was <i>way</i> worse. At least with this they've worked out what the topic of contention actually <i>is</i>, something that was never really done in CW1. The characters aren't <i>too</i> out of character, and people's choices, agree or disagree, tend to make some broad sense.<br /> <br /> In counter to that you argue that the dialogue is off in some vague and undefined way?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T05:26:35-07:00","id":995588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=995562#post995562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Civil War 2 has its issues, I don't think anyone would seriously argue against that. But Civil War 1 was <i>way</i> worse. At least with this they've worked out what the topic of contention actually <i>is</i>, something that was never really done in CW1. The characters aren't <i>too</i> out of character, and people's choices, agree or disagree, tend to make some broad sense.<br /> <br /> In counter to that you argue that the dialogue is off in some vague and undefined way?</div> </div> </div> </div>In both the point of contention is pretty clear. Goverment control vs individual freedom and profiling vs freedom, that both conflicts can only function is both sides are extremist dickheads is another matter. The characters in CWII are incredible out of character. Any X-men except the evil one (beast and Jean Grey) siding with Carol is completely out of character, specially Kitty Pride which has known 2 version of herself from totalitarians regimes. <br /> <br /> Carol reaction to the revelation of Ullyses not being accurate is the moment when they writers threw the whole character through the window and put a straw man argument against fascism/profiling.<br /> <br /> Example<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> When Tchalla switches side he gives a speech that boils down to, you should always trust blindly Captain America which is odd, later the character explains that he has seen to much shady deals from Carol which would have been a great if that was the initial dialogue but when you announce your switching side motivation, saying &quot;because captain america did it&quot; is off for the character.<br /> <br /> Same later when Carol is sitting with Storm, Peter Quill, Maria Hill and Jean Grey. Carol hugs Storm and says &quot;i cant believe how you were married to that man&quot; which is incredibly off. The guy was your team mate and a long time friend, he didnt left in violence he just bowed out when the moral question was arresting a child. The comment is unwarranted bitter and out of character for Carol and her relationship with Tchalla.<br /> <br /> Tonny Stark speech when they return to the base, he is basically jumping on joy that he was right when 3 numbers before he was saddened when he bring the proof that the preventive stuff wasnt 100% accurate and yes the saddened part happened after they blew up Star Tower. The fact that Tchalla reasoning to switching sides was that the has seen ullysses being wrong which was proven 3 number ago by Tony and confirmed by beast who is on Carol side.<br /> <br /> The speech Peter Quill gave to Carol that when he was king of Spartan he learned that if he could prevent something bad from happening they should. Not only didnt happen in Peter Quill short run as king but it come off from nowhere, Peter Quill would never agree with what Carol is doing unless it was 100% right (which by this point wasnt).<br /> <br /> Tony Stark is reduced to a child who just wants to feel validated that he is right, isntead of a man once again forced to fight his friends and it never weights on him that fact when it should.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T15:30:13-08:00","id":1005884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=967676#post967676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been a long ass time since JimB and I clashed on that matter. But it still annoys me and I'm sauced, so fuck it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry I upset you.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T19:56:26-08:00","id":1005946,"title":"","content":"Anyone read Lone Sloane Delirious by Phillipe Druillet? It was a ground breaking graphic novel from the early 70's. A trippy classic,<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://media.titan-comics.com/dynamic-images/comics/issues/Lone-Sloane-Delirius-Cover.jpg.size-600.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Apparently no 2 has been released but I haven't read it yet<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.bleedingcool.com/2015/12/10/20-years-later-lone-sloane-delirius-2-is-coming-back-thanks-to-titan-comics/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.bleedingcool.com/2015/12/...-titan-comics/</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12683-baghill","name":"Baghill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T12:36:53-08:00","id":1014886,"title":"","content":"If anyone is interested, Barnes &amp; Noble is having their yearly gra