r\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=1168319#post1168319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A double date 78 years in the making.<br /> <br /> Clark Kent and Lois Lane, and Bruce Wayne and Selina Kyle. Hard to believe they've never been on a date before, though it probably makes more sense considering the latters marriage was erased.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. Looks entertaining. What comic is that from?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-17T11:51:22-08:00","id":1168414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=1168382#post1168382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. Looks entertaining. What comic is that from?</div> </div> </div> </div>Batman #37, not out yet. Technically the story starts in #36 with Lois and Catwoman sort of urging them to contact one another after Batman's engagement.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T17:04:53-08:00","id":1172111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.spiked-online.com/spiked-review/article/comic-fans-take-on-identity-politics/#.Wkl-KfevDqC\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.spiked-online.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/netherlands-israel-palestine-protest-hamas-1536x864.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.spiked-online.com/spiked-review/article/comic-fans-take-on-identity-politics/#.Wkl-KfevDqC\" target=\"_blank\"> Long-reads Archives - spiked </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.spiked-online.com/spiked-review/article/comic-fans-take-on-identity-politics/#.Wkl-KfevDqC\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.spiked-online.com/spiked-review/article/comic-fans-take-on-identity-politics/#.Wkl-KfevDqC </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T17:22:35-08:00","id":1172115,"title":"","content":"It's sort of an interesting dynamic. Marvel went all out and made Amadeus Cho the Hulk, and he's not really representative of Koreans in anything but name and occasionally appearance. He might as well be Adam Jones.<br /> <br /> DC went with the New Super-Man with a Chinese character in China who works (worked) for the Chinese government. It's not exactly the best selling comic but it's very well written<br /> <br /> It's not just a matter of replacing the main character, as plenty of people seemed to like Dick Grayson as Batman. Plenty of others liked Otto Octavius possessing Peter Parker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T22:26:48-08:00","id":1172186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=1172115#post1172115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's sort of an interesting dynamic. Marvel went all out and made Amadeus Cho the Hulk, and he's not really representative of Koreans in anything but name and occasionally appearance. He might as well be Adam Jones.<br /> <br /> DC went with the New Super-Man with a Chinese character in China who works (worked) for the Chinese government. It's not exactly the best selling comic but it's very well written<br /> <br /> It's not just a matter of replacing the main character, as plenty of people seemed to like Dick Grayson as Batman. Plenty of others liked Otto Octavius possessing Peter Parker.</div> </div> </div> </div> The article really goes into why it went wrong, all the reasons, and you can extend it to other stuff like the all female ghostbusters, people are fine with diversity, they don't like people with a judgmental attitude and a cultural war agenda hijacking beloved IPs. <br /> <br /> Example with a good plot people could have gone on board with a female Thor, instead they had a female Thor throwing down lines like &quot;Cis Male Shitlord&quot; or something like that. People could deal with a female Thor for example, but they couldn't deal with taking a wrecking ball through the entire IP in a way that was over the top preachy, poorly done, with people who hated the fans, that was too far. I can deal with a female Thor, I can't deal with a female Thor who sounds like a women studies professor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T23:49:50-08:00","id":1172204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=1172186#post1172186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The article really goes into why it went wrong, all the reasons, and you can extend it to other stuff like the all female ghostbusters, people are fine with diversity, they don't like people with a judgmental attitude and a cultural war agenda hijacking beloved IPs.</div> </div> </div> </div>It certainly seems to be pointing at diversity as the big boogeyman that made Marvel comics bad but there is a bit more to it, and the article glosses over it in favor of its own agenda.<br /> <br /> For instance there's a couple points it brings up, 'black writer who has advocated for reparations for slavery and who had no previous comic-book writing experience.' And 'America Chavez is an alien who identifies as a Latina lesbian Feminist. She is written by Gabby Rivera, a Latina lesbian who (again) had no experience of comic-book writing before being given her own series.'<br /> <br /> There's pretty solid points there that go beyond writers with 'a judgmental attitude and a cultural war agenda.'<br /> <br /> There's also little mention of X-men comics, which have arguably been a posterchild for diversity and were thoroughly gutted for the past few years, killing off prized characters, turning others evil and vilifying them while also cutting merchandising for the entire franchise. That's something that only makes it into the article twice, tangentially, 'Iceman was gay,' and 'Wolverine and Hawkeye are women,' the latter of which doesn't mention that 'old' Wolverine is still out there with his own comic. No mention of pushing event after event, extending them more and more with delays, with haplessly jumping onto things like spinning off Deadshot's Mercs for Money into three series. Solo, Slapstick and Foolkiller, which all sold abysmally but at least two of which star straight white male characters (arguable with Slapstick).<br /> <br /> Simply put, this is how Marvel writing works. It's how it has worked for years. Before someone else became Iron Man you had Avengers World, you had Civil War, you had 'amnesia so no one blames him for Civil War.' Before adding Miles Morales there was Peter Parker making a deal with the devil. Before Iceman was outed by Jean Grey you had most of the class of X-men Academy blown up by rockets. Before then you had Ultimatum. Chuck Austen's X-men. It's a series of bad stories, and Marvel isn't even alone in making them. They just haven't corrected themselves yet and the diversity angle is a hot button issue for articles like the one you linked to get easy clicks off of.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Example with a good plot people could have gone on board with a female Thor, instead they had a female Thor throwing down lines like &quot;Cis Male Shitlord&quot; or something like that. People could deal with a female Thor for example, but they couldn't deal with taking a wrecking ball through the entire IP in a way that was over the top preachy, poorly done, with people who hated the fans, that was too far. I can deal with a female Thor, I can't deal with a female Thor who sounds like a women studies professor. </div> </div> </div>Considering the attitude of the fans towards the writers I can't really blame them if they did hate fans. I've disliked Marvel writers for their writing for a long time and if I was one I probably wouldn't like it either, that's before you throw in the fans who don't like them due to gender, skin color, orientation or other things that don't matter when reading a comic.<br /> <br /> But putting aside your dislike of womens studies professors, does this mean you're going to be getting your Thor comics again now that she's dying, then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T10:07:41-08:00","id":1172295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=1172204#post1172204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It certainly seems to be pointing at diversity as the big boogeyman that made Marvel comics bad but there is a bit more to it, and the article glosses over it in favor of its own agenda.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=xxW8AVLUCSo\" target=\"_blank\">I feel like Thorgi has thoughts on this</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> 