-09-25T18:49:34-07:00","id":1415494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimmi05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=1415485#post1415485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am looking for a new series to get into. Anybody got any good recommendations? Marvel, DC, or indie or whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about some web comics? <br /> <br /> Sword interval is nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T22:08:44-07:00","id":1415507,"title":"","content":"I like Supercrooks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T14:43:08-07:00","id":1415601,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12952\" data-vbnamecard=\"12952\">Accelerator</a> My days of reading webcomics are over but I will have to check it out.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4621_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4621\" data-vbnamecard=\"4621\">Nicolas Milioni</a> the one by Mark Millar? I will have to check out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T14:57:41-07:00","id":1415606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimmi05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=1415601#post1415601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12952\" data-vbnamecard=\"12952\">Accelerator</a> My days of reading webcomics are over but I will have to check it out.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>It has a truly excellent sub-plot and side-characte romance. Mutually supportive, loving, commited, clear communication... god, I can't believe I missed those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T15:16:17-07:00","id":1415608,"title":"","content":"I don't think I can help with recent print comics. I haven't been buying print comics for a couple years now. Probably my favorite from back when I could is probably <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giant_Days\" target=\"_blank\">Giant Days</a>, which ended not too long ago (tragically, I missed out on it; although it was always difficult getting issues for it back when I did). It's a great comedy slice-of-life, that ventured into magical realism a bit.<br /> <br /> <br /> If web comics count, I can offer a bit more suggestions:<ul><li><a href=\"https://www.devilscandycomic.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Devil's Candy</a>: Shonen manga style comic about devils in a devil society, attending devil school. Kind of like Disgaea 3, except without the obscene power levels (at least, at first). It follows soft boi cinnamon roll Kazu Decker, the frankenstein's monster girl he makes as a science project, and their various friends. Gorgeous, gothic, and grotesque art intersperses more typical manga character designs.</li> <li><a href=\"https://www.drugsandwires.fail/\" target=\"_blank\">Drugs &amp; Wires</a>: An alternate history cyberpunk early 90s, where despite having cyber limbs and brain-machine interfaces, it's still the 90s. Set in the former soviet bloc nation of Stradania, where a subculture of cyborgs combines brain implants with drugs to create vivid VR. Because the tech is so low-fi that the drugs are needed to boost the signal. Except some users aren't in it for the &quot;digital trips&quot;, so much as for the high. In comes our protagonist Dan, a proto-hipster junkie whose life has been on the downturn ever since his brain implant was hit by a deadly computer virus, whose effects continue to haunt him even when the machine is turned off. It's very much a different flavor of cyberpunk.</li> <li><a href=\"https://killsixbilliondemons.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Kill Six Billion Demons</a>: A series so Exalted that the Exalted forum on this very site has <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons\">a thread dedicated to it</a>. Allison, a normal college student on an Earth very much like our own, gets sucked across the time-space continuum into Throne, the center of a multiverse where the gods are dead, and the powerful Demiurges who took their place ruined the universe through their wars. Now Allison has a key inside her head that is the literal key to a power that could - and does - upset the delicate balance of the multiverse. It's got heavy East Asian inspiration, and combines philosophy with over-the-top kung fu. NSFW.</li> <li><a href=\"https://www.sleeplessdomain.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Sleepless Domain</a>: A reconstruction magical girl series, set in a self-contained city in a magical bubble. Knowledge of the outside world is scarce. And every night, the magical shields retract to around the buildings themselves, while monsters stalk the streets and try to break through. The people of the city are protected by a small army of magical girls, the heroines and celebrities of this society. This is the story of a few such magical girls, and their interpersonal lives playing out amidst the situation becoming unsustainable. Emotionally complex, intriguing, and occasionally romantic. Kind of like Madoka Magica, except playing out over a longer period.</li> <li><a href=\"https://www.howtobeawerewolf.com/\" target=\"_blank\">How To Be A Werewolf</a>: A story about a young woman who has lived a sheltered existence at her family home, ever since contracting lycanthropy as a child. Until she meets and befriends other werewolves (and mages), leading her on a path to coming out of her shell, embracing her shifter nature, and learning more about the origins of her new state. As the title suggests, it's a story about the protagonist learning how to be a self-actualized werewolf. A very <i>comfy</i> story, eschewing the typical werewolf tropes of mindless savagery and horror.</li> <li><a href=\"http://www.sssscomic.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Stand Still Stay Silent</a>: A post-apocalypse story that blends with Scandinavian folklore. A group of misfits venture out from mankind's Iceland refuge, years after a plague ended civilization, in order to scout the ruins of the world. Dodging monsters and getting in touch with magic that was once lost. I haven't been keeping up with this one, but it's really good.</li> <li><a href=\"https://www.lackadaisy.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Lackadaisy</a>: Also called Lackadaisy Cats. A <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/FunnyAnimal\" target=\"_blank\">funny animal</a> story set in the roaring 20s, except everyone is a cat. In the days of prohibition, a boot-legging crime gang is on its last legs after the death of its charismatic founder. But the selection of weirdos, lunatics, and haz-beens (or never weres) that this founder attracted continue pressing on, if for no reason than because they have no other prospects. Or out of a number of other personal motivations, that push the old timers and some new blood towards greater risks and deeper transgressions. The comic takes forever between updates, but those updates are always interesting, intrigue-building, and gorgeous to look at when they drop. The creator just crowd-funded an animated film adaptation.</li> <li><a href=\"https://girlgeniusonline.com/comic.php#.X2-64mhKjIV\" target=\"_blank\">Girl Genius</a>: The Ur steampunk webcomic about mad scientists. Set in an alternate universe Europe ravaged by the products of mad genius, and filled with the machines, monsters, and machinations they devised. The protagonist discovers herself the heir of a family of sometimes heroes, mostly tyrants and warlords. She must grow into her legacy, reclaim her birthright, navigate the dizzying political landscape (and accompanying forces trying to use her to their own ends), and decide what kind of mad scientist princess she will ultimately be. Oh, and figure out which of the many eligible bachelor madmen she wants to get with (if she doesn't decide to just assert her right as warlord and take them all as her harem). Going on for decades, and shows no sign of stopping or lagging in quality. Also, another extremely pretty comic.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T15:20:15-07:00","id":1415610,"title":"","content":"Dammit, I made a whole post recommending webcomics, but I either canceled the post by mistake or the forum ate it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T15:31:11-07:00","id":1415614,"title":"","content":"My original post included a paragraph explaining premise and what I like about them. But I'm just going to put out the list and links, and let you explore at your own pace.<ul><li><a href=\"https://www.devilscandycomic.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Devil's Candy</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://www.drugsandwires.fail/\" target=\"_blank\">Drugs &amp; Wires</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://www.sleeplessdomain.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Sleepless Domain</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://killsixbilliondemons.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Kill Six Billion Demons</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://www.howtobeawerewolf.com/\" target=\"_blank\">How To Be A Werewolf</a></li> <li><a href=\"http://www.sssscomic.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Stand Still Stay Silent</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://www.lackadaisy.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Lackadaisy</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://girlgeniusonline.com/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">Girl Genius</a></li> </ul>All of these are webcomics with long-term storylines, and all are continuously updating. (Though Lackadaisy goes a long time between pages. It's worth it, though). None of them are what you'd call &quot;comic strip&quot; style works, which is much different than what is found in print comics.<br /> <br /> Basically all of them have incredible art. The only exceptions could be argued for Drugs &amp; Wires (which is pretty typical most of the time, but gets spikes of visual appeal at times) and How To Be A Werewolf (whose creator started as an amateur and got better as the comic goes on). Everything else is fantastic in this regard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 09-26-2020, 06:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T17:20:52-07:00","id":1415623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/65267-let-s-talk-comics?p=1415614#post1415614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My original post included a paragraph explaining premise and what I like about them. But I'm just going to put out the list and links, and let you explore at your own pace.<ul><li><a href=\"https://www.devilscandycomic.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Devil's Candy</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://www.drugsandwires.fail/\" target=\"_blank\">Drugs &amp; Wires</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://www.sleeplessdomain.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Sleepless Domain</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://killsixbilliondemons.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Kill Six Billion Demons</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://www.howtobeawerewolf.com/\" target=\"_blank\">How To Be A Werewolf</a></li> <li><a href=\"http://www.sssscomic.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Stand Still Stay Silent</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://www.lackadaisy.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Lackadaisy</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://girlgeniusonline.com/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">Girl Genius</a></li> </ul>All of these are webcomics with long-term storylines, and all are continuously updating. (Though Lackadaisy goes a long time between pages. It's worth it, though). None of them are what you'd call &quot;comic strip&quot; style works, which is much different than what is found in print comics.<br /> <br /> Basically all of them have incredible art. The only exceptions could be argued for Drugs &amp; Wires (which is pretty typical most of the time, but gets spikes of visual appeal at times) and How To Be A Werewolf (whose creator started as an amateur and got better as the comic goes on). Everything else is fantastic in this regard.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember reading Girl Genius back in the day. I always loved the Foglio's work ever since there stuff for Mtg and What's new with Phil and Dixie. I think I stopped because to me the stories were just dragging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T17:54:57-07:00","id":1415629,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Grimmi. Supercrooks is Millar at his best. The characters in particular are pretty charismatic and charming","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-02T09:32:32-07:00","id":1479955,"title":"","content":"I find myself drifting away from standard superhero fare as I get older and found myself enjoying graphic novels like Prince Of Thieves, Geiger, Sherlock Holmes, and even stuff from Zenescope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}